42,27-84-4009,27,84,4009,,1984-12-30,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Bilsland Mobil Oil,615 E MAIN,MONMOUTH,97361,,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : Seton, Johnson and Odell ***",(Burgerville USA #25),"The following information was obtained from the Remediation Summary Report (Dudek 2020). 
In February 1984, the Bilsland Mobil gas station was demolished and 4 underground storage tanks along with contaminated soils were removed. Significant gasoline-related contamination was found in soil and groundwater.  

A groundwater treatment system was installed and a vapor protection system, including a 30-mil plastic barrier, perforated pipes, and a fan system were reportedly installed beneath the restaurant, but no as-builts or other confirmation have been found. Operating of the systems were shut down aorund 1994, when five monitoring wells were installed, and sampling happened between 1996 and 2001. 

In 2017, sampling occurred to evaluate conditions for adjacent road construction.  A sample of groundwater and free product was collected from the top of MW-1, near the northwestern corner of the Site, and two groundwater samples were collected from MW-3 and MW-5 near the south and center of the Site. A total of 13 soil samples and six groundwater samples were analyzed for gasoline and VOCs. Gasoline and naphthalene were in MW-1 at 32,700 micrograms per liter (µg/L) and 859 µg/L, exceeding the risk-based concentration (RBC) for direct contact to a construction worker. Soil samples collected along the western and southern sides of the restaurant contained concentrations of benzene and ethylbenzene above RBCs for vapor intrusion into occupational bldg.

In February 2018 ISCO injections occurred along the northern and western site boundaries, near MW-1, using calcium hydroxide and activated persulfate. Five quarters of groundwater sampling followed and showed concs decreasing. Still MW-1R had gas and naphthalene above construction worker RBCs.  Four soil vapor samples collected in July 2020 showed concentrations of gas and ethylbenzene above RBCs for occupational exposure in the MW1R area so indoor and outdoor air samples were collected in this area, and these results were negative, indicating despite the soil concentrations, indoor air was not impacted, possibly due to the vapor barrier that was reportedly installed.",24629.0,0.0,AFARRIS,2021-09-07 10:36:49.807
43,21-84-4010,21,84,4010,,1984-01-01,1999-03-18 13:49:10,MOBIL STATION,279 NW HWY 101,DEPOE BAY,97341,,False,,,3.0,ADMCLO,False,False,True,,False,,,,,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : NO PCS MANAGED. NO CONTAMINANTS PRESENT BY SIGHT/ODOR.  REPORTED ON A COMPLAINT...5/16/01 RPR ADMINISTRATIVELY CLOSED 5/16/01... NO APPARENT RELEASE...GAD 5/16/01. *** DENNIS MCKENZIE SOLD STATION TO JAMES WOODALL WITH EMPTY TANKS IN 1985.  JAMES WOODALL AND CONTRACTOR RON MILLER SENT IN LETTERS STATING 2 GASOLINE AND 1 WASTE OIL USTS WERE DECOM BY REMOVAL IN 1985.  THEY ALSO STATED THERE WAS NO SOIL CONTAMINATION,,,24630.0,,GDECK,2001-05-16 14:37:02.000
