46,36-85-4001,36,85,4001,,1985-10-14,1999-03-18 13:49:10,NEWS REGISTER,611 NE THIRD ST,MCMINNVILLE,97128,,False,1.0,,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,Pjt Mgr = JLP,,"The News Register leased/operated a parking and gasoline facility between 1981 and 1985.  Previous operation of the gasoline distribution operations had been controlled by the Fenton Estate. Anecdotal reports of a previous UST system filled in place in the 1970s were made. During this period of time area businesses (up to one block away) reported petroleum odors in their buildings. Petroleum contamination was discovered in 1985 during the investigation of a complaint from the City of McMinnville.  At that time an estimated 2,000 gallons of gasoline had been released from active UST system over several months. The second UST system was decommissioned in October of 1993.  The former USTs appear to have been located under what is currently a sidewalk on the east side of Ford Street. The former pump-island was located in the southwestern portion of the News Register (aka Oregon Lithoprint) builing, positioned diagonal to Ford and Third Streets (i.e. under the building footprint). Several phases of investigation were completed for soil, groundwater, and soil-gas or indoor air concerns. Characterization and risk-assessment of the remaining contmaination continues.  A pilot study to assess the ability and effectiveness of in-situ remediation and a ""Data-Gap"" investigation were completed in the summer of 2016. ",142411.0,0.0,iPMO#38,2016-10-14 15:09:19.400
