85,20-88-4067,20,88,4067,2283.0,1988-08-31,1999-03-18 13:49:10,DAN'S MUFFLER,409 S SIXTH STREET,COTTAGE GROVE,97424,(503)942-7868,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"The Dan’s Muffler site formerly operated as an auto repair facility. The property had been used for a fuel service station until 1982. Six USTs  were decommissioned by removal from the property in May 1988 by CSC Environmental. Approximately 40 cubic yards of petroleum-contaminated soil  was excavated from the two tank cavities and disposed of at Short Mountain Landfill in Lane County. According to CSC Environmental, soil contamination remained and a petroleum sheen was present on water that entered the excavations. Results of soil sampling in 2007 identified gasoline at 1,310 ppm in boring P2 from 5 to 6 feet bgs.  Boring P2 was placed next to the former tank cavity and repair shop building, and represented the same location as B1 from the 2002 site assessment by Geomax.  Groundwater samples were collected from each boring during the 2007 assessment.  Petroleum was detected at each sample location, with the highest concentrations at P2 (including gasoline at 14,300 ppb, benzene at 60.4 ppb, & naphthalene at 520 ppb). The site was granted closure in 2008 with conditions, including no groundwater wells and use of a health & safety plan to protect construction workers from contact with contaminated groundwater. DEQ was notified of a property transaction in 2015.
