158,07-82-0001,07,82,0001,,1982-01-01,1999-03-18 13:49:10,UNKNOWN,UNKNOWN ,PRINEVILLE,97754,,False,,,,,True,False,,,False,,,,,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : Owner of contaminated well:  John Owens  875 Madras Hwy., Prineville. Monitoring wells were installed (4) near PRP. Tanks tested at PRP, negative results. Product still being detected in GW. SHOULD HAVE BEEN LOGGED AS A COMPLAINT. *** ",,,24664.0,,SPAIKO,2000-11-20 08:38:13.000
159,18-89-0005,18,89,0005,4988.0,1989-04-01,1999-03-18 13:49:10,MAC'S STORE,12450 HWY 39,KLAMATH FALLS,97601,(503)884-4977,False,4.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,3.0,False,True,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : Approved State Contractor Work Plan LUST CORRESPONDS TO ECSI FILE #2785 ***,ECSI #2785,"The Mac’s Store site is an active convenience store, certified scale, and former retail fuel facility located south of the City of Klamath Falls.

In March 1989 ODOT noticed a gasoline smell within a trench they were digging along Highway 39, northeast of Klamath Falls and adjacent to Mac's Store. Two 1,000-gallon underground storage tanks (USTs) were subsequently decommissioned, removed and initial cleanup of the site began. In late 1989, the owner identified that he was unable to pay for investigation and cleanup.

DEQ sampled two domestic wells, including the shared Store/residence well and the Palmer well located downgradient of the site in October 2006 and June 2007. Many of the site’s monitoring wells were either destroyed or could not be located in the field.  The Store/residence well was sampled in October 2006 and in June 2007.  The downgradient Palmer well was only sampled in October 2006.  Concentrations of petroleum hydrocarbons and volatile organic compounds (VOCs) were not detected in water samples collected from either well. No impacts to drinking water wells have historically been observed.

On September 22, 2008, two soil borings (MW-4, MW-5) were installed by DEQ using DPT drilling. Groundwater monitoring of wells MW-1, MW-4, MW-5, and the Store/residential well was performed on September 24, 2009. 

As part of the Sept/ 2008 SI, a CSM was developed including defining of LOF, BWU, and LU.  Groundwater from the shallow aquifer is not used and unlikely to be used for beneficial purposes within or in the vicinity of the LOF.  

The site has been recommended for a Conditional NFA determination following a 30 day public comment period ending 8/31/09.  Additional information is located in the site document section of this database.

Deed notice recorded on property on 7/24/2009.",7922.0,0.0,DANDERS,2009-10-02 12:39:58.037
