174,34-87-0008,34,87,0008,729.0,1987-06-17,1999-03-18 13:49:10,BP OIL SITE #11037,12975 SW CANYON RD,BEAVERTON,97005,(503) 641-3444,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"This is a longtime cleanup and monitoring site. A release from UST system piping was reported in 1987.  Approximately 190 cubic yards of contaminated soil were removed following discovery. A remediation systm consisting of a GW recovery and treatment system, an SVE system located in the vicinity of the UST cavity and fuel dispener island, and an SVE system at the western portion of the site operated from 1990 to 1997.  The western VE system was tunrned off in 1997 and the remaining sytems were deactivated in 2000.  High concentrations of gasoline constituents are still detected in some wells.  According to the October 2008 monitoring report, free product was detected in monitoring well MW-4.  

Groundwater data collected from extraction wells E-4 and E-5 (near station building) have consistently exhibited benzene above occupational worker standards for vapor intrusion.  Immediately north of site is D&M Automotive Repair.  Based on historic groundwater flow, it was determined that impacted groundwater in the area of E-4 and E-5 has likely migrated beneath the off-site building for D&M Automotive.

Based on high gasoline/benzene levels in E-4 and E-5, and lack of monitoring wells in actual down-gradient direction, monitoring well MW-8 was installed in the D&M Automotive parking lot in December 2010.  Constituents detected in soil at levels above occuptional vapor intrusion RBC standards.  Subsequent monitiorng of MW-8 has revealed levels of gasoline TPH and benzene above occupational vapor intrusion RBC standards.  

In April 2012, following significant efforts to gain access, ARCADIS performed a soil-gas investigation of the site and adjacent D&M Automotive facility. Sub-slab sample from both buildings did not reveal detections above applicable RBCs.  Indoor air samples from D&M revealed constituent detections well above indoor air RBCs but are likely attributable to site operations and on-site sources.  In August 2013, ARCADIS installed additional monitoring wells MW-9 and MW-10 down-gradient of D& M Automotive to continue delineating the extent of contamination. Significant levels of gasoline and benzene remain in MW-8 in the parking lot for D&M Automotive. Based on elevated concentrations of gasoline and benzene in monitoring wells MW-9 and/or MW-10 in the right-of-way north of the D&M Automotive property, a soil-gas investigation was performed in in the sidewalk adjacent to residential and commercial properties down-gradient of SW Beaverdam Road in October 2014. There were no detections in the soil gas sample above reporting limits.

The final down-gradient delineation was performed in January 2018, when samples were collected from three temporary wells installed on nearby commercial properties.  Despite multiple attempts, DEQ never secured acess to a residential property north of the Tom's Pancake restaurant property.  There were no detections above reporting limits in the samples.

Although soil gas does not pose a risk to occupants of the D&M Automotive property, DEQ has concerns about future buildings on the site.  David Greer, owner of D&M entered into an agreement with BP in August 2017, in which he agreed to execute an E&ES requiring DEQ review of future development plans.  Draft E&ES language for D&M Automotive property was approved by BP in Fall 2019 and submitted to Mr. Greer in December 2019.  Attorney for Mr. Greer (Carson Bowler) provided comment on draft E&ES language in January 2020.

CMMP for D&M Automotive property was approved in September 2019

Next steps: get final agreement on E&ES language for D&M Automotive property via Mr. Greer's attorney. Concurrently, obtain agreement from site property owner on E&ES. Prepare Staff Memo recommending conditional NFA. Put conditional NFA proposal out for comment. Finalize and execute E&ES documents (JKS 2-6-20)

Sampling during an UST Piping upgrade in November 2020 contained low levels of Gx and BTEX. LUST/UST determined a new release does not need to be recorded (md 11/24/2020) ",,,2320.0,0.0,MDROUIN,2020-11-24 07:19:56.307
