201,04-88-0086,04,88,0086,3815.0,1988-11-08,1999-03-18 13:49:10,TONGUE POINT JOB CORPS CENTER,HWY 30,ASTORIA,97103,(503) 325-2131,False,4.0,GW,3.0,,True,False,False,,False,True,False,False,False,"The Tongue Point Naval Air Station site was used as a submarine and destroyer base (1921-1938), a naval air station (1938-1945), and a reserve shipyard (1946-1962) before being decommissioned.  A portion of the NAS was later redeveloped as a Job Corps Center.

Fuel was observed seeping into Cathlamet Bay in November 1988.  Soil and groundwater contamination was discovered at ""UST Site #1"" in December 1989, and the site was subsequently decommissioned in August 1990.  In April 1992, six 25,000-gallon aviation gasoline USTs were decommissioned and 1,302 cubic yards of PCS removed.  Quarterly groundwater monitoring was conducted from December 1993 to July 1997.  In July 2001 an additional 1,100 cubic yards of PCS were removed from the site, and 3,000 lbs of ORC were placed in the excavation.  Quarterly groundwater monitoring resumed in December 2002.

The most recent file information is from 2006.  A 200-ft section of 6"" aviation fuel pipeline was remvoed in February 2006.  A Conceptual Site Model and ecological assessment workplan were expected to be completed in the summer of 2006.  It appears several portions of the site have been remediated, but other portions may remain.  (3/15/10 KPD)

In 2006 Loren Garner was appointed as PM.  The RP has combined the planning for the cleanup under ECSI with the other cleanup issues.  There has been ongoing work submitted under ECSI file 171.  According to the ECSI file, the remedial investigation work in Fall 2008 showed relatively limited problems in most of the locations that were under review by the Environmental Cleanup program. 

UST Site 1 had an active release of sheen observed in October 2008 following record rainfall. Booms were placed in the river and sheen has reduced but is still observed from time to time. This area may be prioritized for an IRAM response. (LLC 10/16/2010)",ECSI #171,"This LUST site has been referred to the Cleanup Program, and is listed as ECSI 171.  The UST Cleanup program is working on the Cleanup team and the scope of the ECSI 171 site was expanded to include ""Multi-Sites"" which consist of other locations throughout the original property with remaining concerns, such as UST sites, etc. The remedial investigation work in Fall 2008 showed relatively limited problems in most locations. UST Site 1 had an active release of sheen observed in October 2008 following record rainfall. Booms were placed in the river and sheen has reduced but is still observed from time to time. This area may be prioritized for an IRAM response. Please review the ECSI files, for total site information including the LUST releases.",24674.0,0.0,LKENT,2010-12-13 12:00:28.617
