239,26-88-0078,26,88,0078,3105.0,1988-10-20,1999-03-18 13:49:10,STAFF JENNINGS INC,8240 SW MACADAM AVE,PORTLAND,97219,(503) 244-7505,False,4.0,GW,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,ECSI #5684 and ECSI #6056,"Staff Jennings, a marine craft sales facility, began operating at the site in 1940.  In October 1988 a petroleum release, primarily of gasoline, from a cracked pipe was discovered at the north end of the site.  The soil and groundwater contamination extended onto the adjacent property to the north and east to the Willamette River.  A 10,000-gallon gasoline UST and 4,000-gallon gasoline UST were decommissioned by removal in October 1994.

A groundwater pump-and-treat system was installed at the site in September 1997.  A dual-phase extraction system began operating in December 2000, and a network of 19 air sparging well points was added in October 2002.  The treatment system removed 8,148 lbs. of volatile organic compounds and treated 6,595,800 gallons of groundwater.  The treatment system was shut down for a year of compliance monitoring in February 2005.  DEQ issued a No Further Action letter for the cleanup in September 2006.

A 1,000-gallon UST was discovered at the site in February 2013 and decommissioned by removal in April 2013.  Three additional USTs were discovered in April and May 2015: a 1,000-gallon gasoline UST, a 340-gallon diesel UST, and a 110-gallon waste oil UST.  The tanks were removed along with about 1,670 tons of PCS.  A final UST (a 12,000-gallon tank divided into diesel and gasoline compartments) was removed in May 2016.",20075.0,0.0,KDANA,2018-04-17 07:58:05.910
