285,34-88-0059,34,88,0059,964.0,1988-09-20,1999-03-18 13:49:10,UNOCAL 4126,18520 SW T V HWY,ALOHA,97006,,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Four quarters of GW monitoring events have been completed with the data below the RBCs.  Comments solicited from Washington County and ODOT regarding contamination historically detected in rights of way adjacent to site.  ODOT and County have requested that a liability agreement be negotiated with Chevron concerning contamination in road.  Template agreement sent to parties in April 2009.  Draft EES in preparation.  Await confirmation of negotiation of agreements. (JS 07-08-09).  Letter dated July 15 received,informing that Arcadis is the new consultant.  Spoke with Melissa Blanchette on 7-17-09. Confirmed Chevron is negotiating liability agreements directly with ODOT/WA County.  They are working on a media management plan for site (JS 07-17-09).  Draft EE&S submitted to section hydrogeologist (JKS 8-25-09).  Draft EE&S submitted to owner (Hong Kim), Arcadis, Wohlers, and Ron Cain approximately 9-21-09 (JKS 9-23-09). Email dated October 9, 2009 indicated that owner would sign EES if DEQ, S&J Java LLC (purchaser under contract) and Cain Petroleum sign Assignment of Easement and Equitable Servitudes.  Based on advice from Charlie Landman, DEQ notified attorney for Cain Petroleum (Mary Ellen Farr) that it would be preferable to add those parties to theEE&S.  Email sent on October 13, 2009 - no response to date (JKS 10-20-09).  DEQ notified that liability agreements with ODOT and Washington County nearly completed.  Media management plan also nearly finalized.  Arcadis notifed that final version of media management plan must be received before draft E&ES can be submitted to Tanks Manager for initial approval (JKS 2-25-10).  DEQ received signed and recorded E&ES on April 15, 2010; Draft NFA being finalized (JKS 04-19-10)",,,18604.0,0.0,LKENT,2011-01-14 10:32:15.290
