364,23-89-0003,23,89,0003,6357.0,1989-10-12,1999-03-18 13:49:10,MADARIAGA CHEVRON,607 MAIN ST,JORDAN VALLEY,97910,,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,ECSI 3880,"[December 2010] The site is a former retail service station and motel.  Current site features include a service station, a service canopy, and a two story motel.  

In October 1989, four USTs, storing gasoline and diesel, were removed by Idaho Petroleum Equipment from a single excavation.  Petroleum-related soil and groundwater contamination, including the presence of free product, were noted during decommissioning activities. 

Additional assessment including the removal of the most recent USTs was performed in late 2009 and early 2010 with ARRA funding.  The SI report for these activities may be viewed in the site document section of this database.

Additional sub slab soil gas sampling was performed in March 2010. The report for these activities may be viewed in the site document section of this database.

To achieve regulatory closure, an Easement and Equitable Servitude (E&ES) will need to be recorded with Malheur County.  The E&ES will require placement of a vapor barrier or other engineering control beneath any new foundation (for new or expanded structures).  To maintain current conditions the following restrictions will also be included: 1) no single family residential use will be allowed on the property; 2) prohibit beneficial use of groundwater; and 3) require proper handling, characterization, and disposal of any contaminated media (soil, groundwater) encountered during any subsurface excavation.

A public comment period was held from August 1 to 31, 2010.  A notice was place in the Argus Observer on August 1 and in the August 2010 Secretary of the State Bulletin.  The notice was also posted around town by the city.  No comments were received.

The property has been abandoned and there is not a valid property owner to sign the E&ES documents.  Therefore, a CNFA can not be issued for the site until the property ownership has been resolved and the E&ES signed and recorded with the County.  A deed notice was filed with the County on December 13, 2010.  The notice was placed on the property to bring attention to the petroleum contamination remaining on the property as an interim measure.",55856.0,0.0,KROBERT,2013-12-04 14:54:05.747
