NON sent 11/13/2001.  Due Nov. 30, 2001.",Franko Oil/Midstate Petro,"The petroleum contamination at this site was initially reported to DEQ in 1989 apparently during or in preparation for decommissioning of the UST systems, No documentation of that activity was included in the file. In March 1997 the four USTs were decommissioned by removal followed by excavation of approximately 700 tons of petroleum contaminated soil.  In October 2003 four temporary boring were placed  to assess remaining impacts.  Although the 2003 work did not include the necessary QA/QC - COC, boring logs, written narrative, etc., a figure of the approximate boring locations was included with the lab results received by DEQ on October 28, 2003.  During this assessment the highest detection of petroleum contamination was observed near the SE corner of the former UST nest.  Chlorinated solvents were also detected in 3 of the 4 borings.  The PCE and other chlorinated solvent contamination detections may be associated with the former dry-cleaner located further to the SE of the site. On or around 10-30-13 additional assessment was performed to determine the areal extent of contamination.  On December 10, 2013 DEQ received a report of findings and a request for closure.  Based on the information provided in this report and the current and reasonably likely future use of the site, DEQ has determined that a conditional closure is appropriate for the property.",22084.0,0.0,JGLASS,2014-02-05 10:17:36.400
