2)  If new NFA date is issued, then this file must be processed out of the SRC BOX, spreadsheet lists, labels, etc.  File with new NFA date will go into SRC in future with new destruction date.  


4/25/19 JClaussen: Spoke w/Jeff Slater of BB Holdings (current property owner). Has had Phase 2 work done that has found soil & GW contamination. Requested copies of reports; may need to re-open site for evaluation of new data when received. Requested CRA.

Original FIR and Closed dates were 3/25/1992 (Soil Matrix closure).  Site reopened 5/28/2019 to evaluate new information indicatiing groundwater contamination.... gdeck Site re-opened on : 5/28/2019 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 3/25/1992.",,"A fuel station operated at this site from the 1950s through 1991 undergoing several ownership changes between Chevron, Franko and Texaco during this time. The site also operated as a Pacific Pride fuel station. 

DEQ issued a No Further Action on 7/2/21 after soliciting public comment from neighboring properties and the city in June 2021. Contamination in groundwater migrates off site beneath Newmark Avenue and to the north, but the the contamination is deep and not anticipated to be encountered or put people at risk..",22091.0,0.0,GDECK,2021-07-02 14:58:42.710
