892,34-90-0056,34,90,0056,188.0,1990-02-06,1999-03-18 13:49:10,HANEGAN'S SERVICE STATION,18970 SW BOONES FERRY ROAD,TUALATIN,97062,(503)692-4120,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : Six tanks decommissioned. Visit 20-MAR-90 by A. Pollock. *** PPA with City of Tualatin.  Facility closed, USTs to be decommissioned, soil remediated, and groundwater monitoring initiated as part of PPA.  Currently conducting groundwater monitoring LLC 7/19/2010.  DEQ letter dated 2-1-11 noted that PPA included provision that if, following four quarters of monitoring, levels of contaminants in groundwater exceeded applicable RBCs, DEQ could request an additional monitroring well.  Contaminant levels in MW-5 remain above RBCs.  DEQ feels the logical place for an additional well is near boring GP-24 (March 2005) which is on the adjacent property to the east.  CH2MHIll submitted a work plan in October 2011 that proposed two sets of remedial injection events to knock down levels of petroleum hydrodarbons in the area of the former USTs.  CH2MHill proposed a year of semi-annual monitoring following injection.  In letter dated 10-24-11, DEQ approved the work plan but informed the City of Tualatin that further investigation in the area of March 2005 boring GP-24 is needed (JKS 11-17-11). After two post-remedial monitoring events (6 and 12 months), contaminant levels in MW-5 have dropped by a factor of six.  Closure requested in report dated 3-29-13 (JKS 4-23-13).

DEQ commented on the risk-based report and requested information about water wells in the area and figures showing the extent of contamination.  Response from consultant received in December 2014.  Staff Memo prepared for internal review. (JKS 2-18-15)",,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : Six tanks decommissioned. Visit 20-MAR-90 by A. Pollock. *** PPA with City of Tualatin.  Facility closed, USTs to be decommissioned, soil remediated, and groundwater monitoring initiated as part of PPA.  Currently conducting groundwater monitoring LLC 7/19/2010.  DEQ letter dated 2-1-11 noted that PPA included provision that if, following four quarters of monitoring, levels of contaminants in groundwater exceeded applicable RBCs, DEQ could request an additional monitroring well.  Contaminant levels in MW-5 remain above RBCs.  DEQ feels the logical place for an additional well is near boring GP-24 (March 2005) which is on the adjacent property to the east.  CH2MHIll submitted a work plan in October 2011 that proposed two sets of remedial injection events to knock down levels of petroleum hydrodarbons in the area of the former USTs.  CH2MHill proposed a year of semi-annual monitoring following injection.  In letter dated 10-24-11, DEQ approved the work plan but informed the City of Tualatin that further investigation in the area of March 2005 boring GP-24 is needed (JKS 11-17-11). After two post-remedial monitoring events (6 and 12 months), contaminant levels in MW-5 have dropped by a factor of six.  Closure requested in report dated 3-29-13 (JKS 4-23-13).

DEQ commented on the risk-based report and requested information about water wells in the area and figures showing the extent of contamination.  Response from consultant received in December 2014.  Staff Memo prepared for internal review. (JKS 2-18-15)",9832.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2015-02-18 08:21:11.597
