905,34-90-0211,34,90,0211,10470.0,1990-06-12,1999-03-18 13:49:10,CADY PROPERTY,149 SE 3RD AVE,HILLSBORO,97123,(503) 681-8465,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Three USTs were removed from the site in June 1990: a 1,000-gallon UST from the center of the property, and two 350-gallon USTs from the sidewalk along 3rd Ave.  Gasoline and diesel fractions were detected in soil and shallow groundwater, mostly around the sidewalk USTs.  Sixty (60) cubic yards of PCS were excavated in July 1991 and stockpiled on-site for aeration treatment.  In Sept 1996, Tri-Met encountered additional PCS while installing a utility vault beneath 3rd Ave as part of the Westside Light Rail project.  About 180 tons of PCS were excavated in 1996-97 during utility installation, but more remained behind.  Removal of additional PCS may be difficult to impossible due to other utility lines, buildings, etc.  Current property owner Gene Zurbrugg of Zurbrugg Development Company thinks Tri-Met took care of everything, and that anything left is just typical urban corridor contamination that he shouldn't / can't be held responsible for.  (6/23/09 KPD)",,,9355.0,0.0,KDANA,2009-06-23 09:27:04.630
906,34-90-0081,34,90,0081,744.0,1990-02-27,1999-03-18 13:49:10,BP OIL #11042,10775 SW GREENBURG RD,TIGARD,97223,(503) 620-8747,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,LUST #34-91-0026 (duplicate) and #34-07-1489,"Mobil Oil constructed a service station at the site in 1972.  Contamination was discovered when the site was transferred to BP Oil in 1989.  In August 1991, six USTs (four gasoline, one heating oil, and one waste oil) were removed from the site, and over the next several months about 1,500 cubic yards of PCS were removed as the site was extensively excavated and reconstructed.  Eight on-site groundwater monitoring wells, four groundwater recovery wells, four air sparging wells, and three off-site groundwater wells were eventually installed at and near the site.  Extraction and treatment of both groundwater and soil vapors began in June 1993 and continued through December 1997.  Total VOC recovery was estimated at 2,235 lbs.  After a year of compliance monitoring, DEQ issued the NFA letter in March 1999.",2069.0,0.0,LLO,2016-03-25 13:41:14.430
