940,22-90-4209,22,90,4209,3576.0,1990-09-04,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Texaco-Lyons Street,330 LYON ST S,ALBANY,97321,(503)926-1955,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : ADDRESS ORIGINALLY REPORTED AS FOURTH AND LYONS. *** Pjt Mgr=C Rodda.,See Also: 22-90-4257,"The site is located in Albany at 330 South Lyon Street, and operated as a fuel service station from 1947 until August 1990.  The three gasoline USTs were located at the southern portion of the property in a single cavity.  Reports in the USTC file indicate that the gasoline tanks were removed from the site on August 24, 1990.  SSM Enterprises completed the UST removal and Cascade Earth Sciences (CES) collected four soil samples during the decommissioning.  The soil samples were analyzed for the presence of TPH  using the EPA 418.1 analytical method.  Only sample TL-S2 detected TPH at a concentration of 687 ppm .  Groundwater entered the UST excavation at approximately 15 feet bgs and sheen was observed.  

According to the family of the former station operator, a waste oil UST (#4) existed in the same tank nest as the gasoline USTs.  No other documentation of this waste oil tank or its removal, soil sampling, and other decommissioning activities exists in DEQ records.  

A second waste oil tank (#5) was decommissioned by removal in June 2008.  Five confirmation soil samples were collected from the excavation, with a maximum diesel concentration of 5,060 ppm at the east wall sample from 5 feet bgs.  This sample, E Wall 5’ also measured heavy oil at 4,130 ppm.  Gasoline was detected in N Wall 4.6’ at 940 ppm.
In June 2008, a second waste oil tank was decommissioned by removal from within a service building on the west side of the property.  The tank contained approximately 210 gallons of waste oil products, which were disposed of by Thermo Fluids.  The decommissioning subcontractor, Mid-Pacific Enterprises, transported and disposed of 6.32 tons of petroleum-contaminated soil excavated from the waste oil tank cavity.  The contaminated soil was removed to the extent practicable based on the building structure.",20398.0,0.0,CRODDA,2009-05-05 12:51:12.883
