982,03-90-0099,03,90,0099,805.0,1990-03-16,1999-03-18 13:49:10,BP 11004,896 MOLALLA AVE,OREGON CITY,97045,,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"1.3.2013:  Spoke with John Wilbur, owner of property.  They may rehab current building rather than raze and use whole lot for parking.  I indicated that is fine since the shallow soil gas results are acceptable (even if they were to construct a new commercial structure at grade).  RAH.

7.2012:  draft nfa in for manager review, still need CMMP from Arcadis. (RAH)


5.29.12:  Letters to impacted parties (City Oregon City and K&R Lube) sent.  comments due 9 July.  (RAH)-No comments received (7.23, RAH)

3.28.12:  CSM/closure request submitted in early march.  Site looks good for impacted party letter and subsequent closure (most likely occupational as grocery market is going to buy it & use for parking).  deciding whether or not to implement and restrictions/notices re: soil gas failing urb res at deeper levels, upper passes. (RAH)

1.30.2012:  discussed soil gas results w/arcadis and discussed some options for limited restrictions, depending on zoning.  they will be working on the risk evaluation/csm from here.  (RAH)


10/2011:  received confirmation soil and gw report.  QM finished at remaining 2 MWs (MW-2 and 3).  did some sg sampling too.  Full risk evaluation report estimated to be delivered end of November.

4/2001:  Approved confirmation sampling work plan (and 1 SG point).  We realized that work plan was not submitted after our meeting, hence the later approval.  work looks to be completed in April or may, pending any permit acquisitions.

1/2011:  Arcadis making adjustments to final conf. sampling  (soil, gw, and ~1 sg point) .(RAH)
Barring major issues, candidate for closure after conf. sampling and final reporting.

PCE downgradient (off-prop problem).  need work plan for soil sampling from UST removal around 2005. (RAH, 1/26/10).",,,2039.0,0.0,RHOOD,2013-01-03 09:59:44.097
