985,03-90-0178,03,90,0178,7980.0,1990-05-15,1999-03-18 13:49:10,CLAIRMONT SERVICE,1511 MOLALLA AVE,OREGON CITY,97045,(503) 657-8037,False,1.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Soil and groundwater contamination was encountered during sewer line installation in May 1990.  Additional off-site contamination was encountered in a utility vault and in line excavations in March-April 1991.  The tanks were replaced in June 1992 and over 2,000 tons of PCS was removed.  Groundwater monitoring (beginning in 1992) has gradually been reduced to annual monitoring of two wells.  The most recent results (from September 2017) showed gasoline in MW-4 at 8,400 ppb, along with benzene at 110 ppb.  No contaminants were detected in MW-5.  The next round of monitoring is scheduled for the Third Quarter of 2018.  The site operator (Susan Stein of Stein Oil Company) has not responded to previous requests to sign up for the LUST program, even though her consultant (Wohlers) argues that the site poses no risk.  (01/02/2018 KPD)

Further evaluation of residual impact in soils needs to be performed along with diesel analysis in groundwater.  The results need to be summarized in a conceptual site model and submitted to DEQ.  There is an old water well on-site that needs further evaluation.  These findings were sent to Stein Oil as part of the EPA grant for backlogged sites.",,,23397.0,0.0,ADESMON,2021-09-01 10:01:44.290
