1045,26-90-0088,26,90,0088,7515.0,1990-03-08,1999-03-18 13:49:10,LOMBARD BP STATION,5305 N LOMBARD ST,PORTLAND,97203,(503) 286-4303,False,7.0,MATRIX,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"A 10,000-gallon gasoline UST and two 8,000-gallon gasoline USTs were decommissioned in May 1990 and replaced by two 10,000-gallon gasoline USTs and one 8,000-gallon gasoline UST.  Soil samples collected around the UST nest found up to 2,000 ppm TPH.  A soil vapor extraction system was installed and began operating in December 1990.  The SVE system is known to have operated at least until June 1992 and reportedly operated until August 1999.

Two 500-gallon tanks, holding used oil and heating oil, were removed from the site in July 1999.  Soil samples collected around the site found gasoline beneath a dispenser (9,640 ppm) and in a separate stained soil area (4,210 ppm).  Approximately 17 tons of PCS were excavated and removed from the site.  Confirmation sampling found no detectable gasoline.

Confirmation sampling in the SVE treatment area in February 2016 found only 275 ppm heavy oil, below the Level 2 Soil Matrix Cleanup standard of 500 ppm.",7932.0,0.0,KDANA,2017-04-18 07:08:20.953
