1055,26-89-0073,26,89,0073,718.0,1990-04-26,1999-03-18 13:49:10,BP STATION #11033,425 NE BROADWAY,PORTLAND,97232,,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"A soil gas survey in April 1989 detected contamination at the site.  A total of 10 soil vapor extraction (SVE) wells were installed at the site from January to October 1991.  The service station was torn down and rebuilt in January 1992 and the five original USTs were removed, along with a reported 700 cubic yards of PCS.  Over 50 confirmation soil samples were collected, showing gasoline remaining in the soil in three locations.  A bi-level SVE system was installed in April 1993 and operated until July 1999, removing an estimated 144,700 pounds of VOCs.  Confirmation soil sampling in March 2004 showed remaining contamination below levels of concern.",2809.0,0.0,KDANA,2009-04-02 16:09:03.927
