1076,36-90-4229,36,90,4229,903.0,1990-10-02,1999-03-18 13:49:10,UNOCAL BULK PLANT 0524,700 N COLLEGE ST,NEWBERG,97132,(503)538-2513,False,,,,,True,False,,,False,,,,,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : RP TERMINATED VCR AGREEMENT AS OF 4/1/00. *** An E-mail was sent to Mike Anderson on this site on October 2, 1990.  The TCLP question is important here as the release is from above ground tanks and the mass of the contaminated media and product/waste is anticipated to be above 1000 kg.",Bob Alexander stopped VCR  4/1/00.  Subsequent time charged to UNOCAL.,,2623.0,,GDECK,2001-01-10 00:00:00.000
1077,24-90-4230,24,90,4230,7481.0,1990-08-14,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Silverton High School,807 JEFFERSON ST,SILVERTON,97381,(503)873-6331,False,2.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : SEE ALSO 24-93-4104 SILVERTON BUS BARNS. *** Pjt Mgr = JLG 3/9/04.,See Also: 24-93-4104 Silverton Bus Barns,,23068.0,0.0,GDECK,2007-07-13 15:28:12.813
1078,20-90-4228,20,90,4228,,1990-09-27,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Glausi Oil Bulk Plant,1830 HWY 101,FLORENCE,97439,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Site address of 1830 was contiguous with the other release at 1839.  Keep this Bulk Plant release address as 1830 to keep them distinct.  The bulk plant has since been cleaned up and redeveloped.... N Sawka and G Deck... 3/5/2020.,20-93-4199 Glausi Florence Chevron,"Groundwater and soil contamination have been found beneath the site due to past and current operations as a bulk petroleum storage facility and later as a cardlock. The bulk petroleum facility operated from about 1950-1990 on Tax Lots 5901, 5902 and 5903.  The bulk facility was demolished after 1990.  The first petroleum release was reported during demolition activities (LUST 20-90-4228) and about 3600 tons of PCS was removed. The south side of the site (Tax Lot 5900) was developed into a cardlock facility in 1991.  A petroleum release from a leaking valve was reported from the cardlock facility in 1993 (20-93-4199).  The valve was replaced and groundwater and soil vapor remediation was conducted between February and May 1994.  Intermittent groundwater monitoring has been completed at the site from 1991 through 2018.  Data shows that concentrations of petroleum contamination in the groundwater have significantly decreased over time.  DEQ has reviewed all of the site data to date and has determined that the remaining contamination in soil and groundwater no longer poses a risk as long as the following conditions are met: 1) property remains commercial, 2) DEQ be notified of any new building construction which could require some type of vapor mitigation controls, 3) no groundwater be used on the property, and 4) a contaminated media management plan be developed. These requirements have implemented through a deed restriction that was recorded on the property with the Lane County Clerk on July 30, 2020.  DEQ has proposed and plans to issue a No Further Action for the site once all administrative closure activities are complete.",24890.0,0.0,GDECK,2020-12-02 15:39:50.813
