1209,26-89-0181,26,89,0181,9400.0,1989-08-15,1999-03-18 13:49:10,CITY CENTER PARKING,632 SW PINE ST,PORTLAND,97205,(503) 221-1666,False,1.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Three 1,000-gallon gasoline USTs were removed from beneath the sidewalk along SW Pine Street in August 1989, and PCS was noted.  (No PCS was reported to have been removed, and no decommissioning report was ever received).  Three borings were advanced in December 1989 to determine the extent of contamination.  One soil sample showed 390 ppm TPH, and shallow groundwater had low levels of toluene and xylenes.  A soil vapor extraction system was proposed in 1990-91 but apparently never installed.  DEQ last heard from Greg Goodman and City Center Parking in 1993, saying they were waiting for an 1882 terra cotta combined sewer line beneath Pine Street to be replaced before doing any remediation.  Site has been backlogged since.  The site could probably receive an NFA after another round of confirmation sampling.  (7/6/09 KPD)",,,17602.0,0.0,KDANA,2009-07-06 09:04:11.297
