1277,34-89-0218,34,89,0218,67.0,1989-10-05,1999-03-18 13:49:10,"CARR CHEVROLET CO., INC.",11635 SW CANYON RD,BEAVERTON,97005,(503) 644-2161,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Two 650-gallon gasoline USTs were removed in October 1989, and petroleum was observed in the soil and groundwater.  Six monitoring wells were installed by March 1990.  A soil vapor extraction system was installed in December 1991 and operated from February 1992 until late 1994, when it was decided the system had been ineffective.  Nineteen borings were advanced around the site in August 1996 to delineate the extent of contamination.

Work resumed with additional sampling in 2002 and 2003.  GeoDesign submitted a CAP in September 2003.  The risks were determined to be vapor intrusion to indoor air, volatilization to outdoor air, and direct contact with groundwater.  GeoDesign essentially recommended a ""Hazard Notice"" for the groundwater, and suggested indoor and outdoor air sampling to confirm or eliminate those risks.  The file ends in October 2004 with discussions on soil vapor sampling locations.  The project apparently fell off the radar when Bart Bretherton and Rich Reiter left the program in 2004 and 2005.  (7/8/09 KPD)",,,1005.0,0.0,KDANA,2009-07-08 11:03:38.443
