1303,05-90-0458,05,90,0458,2832.0,1990-11-27,1999-03-18 13:49:10,CLATSKANIE MINI MART,260 COLUMBIA RIVER HWY,CLATSKANIE,97016,(503)728-2035,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,19907.0,0.0,LKENT,2011-10-26 14:49:49.873
1304,26-90-0359,26,90,0359,4258.0,1990-10-03,1999-03-18 13:49:10,RAY'S TRUCK SERVICE,6423 NW ST HELENS RD,PORTLAND,97204,(503) 283-1256,False,1.0,MATRIX,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Ray's Truck Service, founded by Ray Austad and later run by Larry Austad, began operating at the site in the 1950s.  Four underground storage tanks were removed from the site in 1990: a 4,000-gallon diesel UST, a 3,000-gallon gasoline UST, and two 1,000-gallon gasoline USTs.  Petroleum-contaminated soils (PCS) were encountered but left in-place.

Mike Fitz with Star Oil Company acquired the site in 1995.  In 1997, approximately 247 cubic yards of PCS were excavated and aerated on-site for about six weeks before being placed back into the excavation pit.  However, additional sampling around the site in 1999 revealed additional PCS, with gasoline concentrations up to 19,600 ppm.

Work resumed at the site in October 2016 with additional soil sampling and the installation of three groundwater monitoring wells.  Gasoline was detected in both the soil (up to 10,800 ppm) and groundwater (up to 276,000 ppb), along with volatile organic compounds (VOCs).  A fourth monitoring well was installed in November 2017, and groundwater was monitored quarterly for a year.  A report summarizing all of the sampling data was completed in June 2019.",,,20862.0,0.0,KDANA,2020-07-07 10:49:29.877
