1364,24-89-4066,24,89,4066,182.0,1989-06-27,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Marion Grocery,5848 STAYTON RD,MARION,97359,(503) 769-3869,False,1.0,,,NFA,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : Site cleaned to standards BDC ***

NFA letter issued 6/7/1991.  

Site reopened 2/26/2018 due to Phase 2 SA showing groundwater impacts.  Owner wants to sell and has provided CRA received 2/16/2018. Site re-opened on : 2/26/2018 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 6/7/1991.",,"The site was developed in 1958 and by 1967, three buildings including a home, independent utility shed, and the Marion Grocery & Deli Store were constructed on the property. Two 1,000-gallon underground storage tanks (USTs) were installed on April 11, 1971. In May 1989, both tanks were permanently decommissioned. During the May 1989 decommissioning activities, petroleum contaminated soil (PCS) was encountered. 119 tons of PCS was removed from the property and the release was reported to DEQ. LUST #24-89-4066 was created and DEQ issued a No Further Action (NFA) letter on June 7, 1991.

On October 25, 2017, Partner Engineering and Science, Inc completed a Transaction Screen Assessment Report. The DEQ reopened the site on February 26, 2018 due to the Partner Phase II SIR detecting groundwater impacts in the vicinity of the former UST. AEG advanced six soil borings and collected soil samples from each in January 2018; additionally, groundwater samples were collected from three of the six borings in February 2018. AEG collected water samples from the store tap and house tap onsite.  All samples were analyzed for petroleum range hydrocarbons as gasoline (NWTPHGX) and for petroleum related volatile organic compounds (VOCs). AEG completed four quarters of groundwater monitoring events in 2018 (February, May, August, and December). In addition, groundwater samples were also performed in March and August 2019; October 2020. The October 2020 groundwater sampling event analyzed samples using NWTPHGX, petroleum range hydrocarbons as diesel (NWTPHDX), petroleum related VOCs, and total lead. NWTPHGX was reported at concentrations of 131 µg/L in February 2018 and 116 µg/L in December 2018. The October 2020 sampling event detected NWTPHGX at 32.8 µg/L. The neighboring well at 14051 Marion Road SE was sampled in March and August 2019; the neighboring well at 14077 Duckflat Road was sampled in October 2020. These groundwater samples were analyzed for NWTPHGX, NWTPHDX, and RBDM VOCs. The sample results were below all applicable RBCs. The extent of contamination is limited to soil and groundwater west of the former UST excavation area. All residual petroleum contamination in soil and groundwater is below all applicable RBCs. 
",18038.0,0.0,ALEIDEL,2021-08-30 11:36:33.990
