1381,22-90-4034,22,90,4034,775.0,1990-02-16,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Courtesy Corner,1515 CALAPOOIA SW,ALBANY,97321,(503)928-8264,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"226 yd3 to short mt.3-90 GW impacts no quarterly reports 2-91 RS 5-93
Assigned to DRB.","EXXON Pacific Blvd., USTC #22-89-4182","The site is an active fuel service station, dispensing gasoline, diesel, and heating oil products. Historically, operations at the facility have included use of underground waste oil and heating oil tanks. The site is underlain by sands and gravels. Groundwater had been measured in site monitoring wells from 4 to 11 feet below ground surface. The facility has utilized at least nine underground tanks since 1952 when the service station began operation. At that time, four 10,000-gallon tanks for leaded and unleaded gasoline, diesel, and heating oil were installed. In 1974, a 4,000-gallon diesel tank was installed, and in 1980 two more tanks (one 1,000-gallon kerosene and one 10,000-gallon unleaded gasoline) were added to the inventory. The 500-gallon waste oil and heating oil tanks were located at the north end of the property and were decommissioned by removal in 1990. Quarterly and semi-annual groundwater monitoring has been conducted since May 1991. In October 2005, results showed significant decreases in gasoline constituents since the initial sampling, but still at elevated concentrations. DEQ asked for follow-up investigation in 2008 as part of a risk-based evaluation. Further investigation was requested based on the results of this April 2009 probe assessment, which identified off-site contamination above risk levels. Groundwater contamination was not delineated, and the highest concentration of gasoline was detected northeast and downgradient of the tank system on the property boundary at boring GP-C. Gasoline was detected at 139,000 ppb and benzene was 812 ppb. In addition, gasoline (132,000 ppb) and several VOCs (ie, benzene at 1,620 ppb) were detected at high concentrations in water from GP-D, located along Pacific Boulevard. More borings were installed in July 2012 to collect soil and groundwater samples. Soil contamination was minimal in these locations after excavations in 1994. Gasoline was found at 44,500 ppb in boring B-3, and benzene was 4,370 ppb in water from B-2. Off-site, contamination remains at levels that could pose a risk to workers who make contact with water during construction/excavation activities. A deed restriction (EES) was recorded by the property owner in January 2013, which prohibits use of groundwater for consumption, residential land use, and implementation of a health & safety plan for future excavation at the site.",13672.0,0.0,CRODDA,2013-02-05 13:30:15.240
1382,26-89-0042,26,89,0042,,1989-03-21,1999-03-18 13:49:10,ABE'S AUTO SERVICE,4934 SE STARK ,PORTLAND,97215,,False,7.0,MATRIX,,,True,False,,,False,,,,,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : NFA SENT SITE CLOSED *** ,,,24960.0,,MALBERT,1996-02-28 09:15:27.000
1383,26-89-0017,26,89,0017,724.0,1989-02-03,1999-03-18 13:49:10,BP OIL SITE #11036,6303 SW CAPITOL HWY,PORTLAND,97239,(503) 244-3104,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,,LUST #26-07-1499,"An estimated 2,800 gallons of super unleaded gasoline were released from a product line at this site on February 3, 1989.  Approximately 1,610 gallons of product were recovered from an adjacent tank cavity over the next few weeks.  A groundwater pump-and-treat system (using a recovery well in the tank cavity) and soil vapor extraction system began operating in June 1990 and continued until April 1993, when they were replaced by an air sparging system.

A total of five underground storage tanks (plus the recovery well) were removed from the site in September 1993.  Soil vapor extraction and groundwater monitoring continued until mid-1995, although little additional contamination was detected.",2054.0,0.0,KDANA,2010-04-06 16:32:05.277
