1386,26-89-0063,26,89,0063,5860.0,1989-04-12,1999-03-18 13:49:10,JAMES RIVER CORP.,2985 NORTH MARINE DRIVE,PORTLAND,97217,(503) 285-3621,False,4.0,GW,3.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : Referred to ECD 26-APR-89. *** referred to VCASA,,,541.0,0.0,RHOOD,2015-08-24 11:47:02.667
1387,26-89-0036,26,89,0036,9106.0,1989-03-10,1999-03-18 13:49:10,HARVESTER CO. (RAY'S SERVICE STATION),1715 SW SALMON ST,PORTLAND,97205,(503) 228-7063,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"No Further Action Letter issued for release in January 2000.

In 2004 GeoDesign performed a site assessment for due diligence purposes.  The current parking lot will be redveloped with a mixed-use building with one floor of sub-grade parking. Gasoline was detected in soil at a level above residential/urban residential RBCs near to the southwest corner of the property.  

In February 2018, additional assessment was performed at the the site related to a property transaction. Eleven borings were advanced to a depth of 32 feet bgs at the site. Groundwater was not encountered.  Soil samples collected from the site were generally consistent with or below conditions as known at the time of closure of the 1989 release.  One boring (DP-7 at 19-20 feet bgs) advanced in the eastern portion of the former service station building detected lead at 1,880 ppm.  TCLP testing of this sample and four others with detected lead > 100 ppm only revealed one exceedance. Due to the depth of the sample, it is not likely to be disturbed or encountered by site workers.  Also, historical testing of shallow perched groundwater did not reveal high levels of lead. 

Due to historical detections of gasoline and VOCs exceeding urban residential RBCs for the vapor intrusion pathway, GeoDesign collected five soil gas samples from the site.  No VOCs were detected above residential RBCs.  Due to the planned future use (i.e, residential apartments above commercial/retail space), the ventilation that will accompany future below-ground parking, and the soil gas testing results, future employees and residents are not at risk from vapor intrusion. The 2018 investigation did not reveal evidence for additonal releases.  As documented in a letter dated April 9, 2018, the NFA determination remains in force. (JKS 4-13-18)",,"No Further Action Letter issued for release in January 2000.

In 2004 GeoDesign performed a site assessment for due diligence purposes.  The current parking lot will be redveloped with a mixed-use building with one floor of sub-grade parking. Gasoline was detected in soil at a level above residential/urban residential RBCs near to the southwest corner of the property.  

In February 2018, additional assessment was performed at the the site related to a property transaction. Eleven borings were advanced to a depth of 32 feet bgs at the site. Groundwater was not encountered.  Soil samples collected from the site were generally consistent with or below conditions as known at the time of closure of the 1989 release.  One boring (DP-7 at 19-20 feet bgs) advanced in the eastern portion of the former service station building detected lead at 1,880 ppm.  TCLP testing of this sample and four others with detected lead > 100 ppm only revealed one exceedance. Due to the depth of the sample, it is not likely to be disturbed or encountered by site workers.  Also, historical testing of shallow perched groundwater did not reveal high levels of lead. 

Due to historical detections of gasoline and VOCs exceeding urban residential RBCs for the vapor intrusion pathway, GeoDesign collected five soil gas samples from the site.  No VOCs were detected above residential RBCs.  Due to the planned future use (i.e, residential apartments above commercial/retail space), the ventilation that will accompany future below-ground parking, and the soil gas testing results, future employees and residents are not at risk from vapor intrusion. The 2018 investigation did not reveal evidence for additonal releases.  As documented in a letter dated April 9, 2018, the NFA determination remains in force. (JKS 4-13-18).",67989.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2018-04-13 07:57:07.647
