1495,34-90-0450,34,90,0450,3487.0,1990-11-20,1999-03-18 13:49:10,DAMEROW FORD SERVICE CENTER,12375 SW MILLIKAN WAY,BEAVERTON,97005,(503) 644-1131,False,1.0,MATRIX,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"A 1,000-gallon waste oil UST was removed from the SE corner of the Service Center building at this site in November 1990, along with some contaminated soil.  The site apparently wasn't closed due to inadequate confirmation sampling.  Additional sampling was conducted in March 2001, but no report was completed.  A third round of confirmation sampling was conducted in June 2006, finding up to 18,400 ppm heavy oil in the soil and 20,770 ppb heavy oil in the groundwater.  Although highly concentrated, the contamination was limited in extent and depleted in volatiles.  After calculating site-specific RBCs, the contractor concluded that the heavy oil was not a risk, but that benzene in the groundwater (302 ppb) posed a vapor intrusion risk.  Additional sampling to delineate the extent of the contamination was recommended but apparently not conducted.  (6/29/09 KPD)",,,20342.0,0.0,KDANA,2009-06-29 11:57:22.290
