1653,36-90-4263,36,90,4263,10577.0,1990-11-02,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Old Pepsi Building,925 NE 3rd St,MCMINNVILLE,97128,(503) 472-5114,False,7.0,,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Site re-opened on : 8/8/2008 By Virginia Deck.  Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 9/12/1991.
Closed date shown as 9/12/1991 but there is no NFA in the file.  Jim Glass ""reopened"" this site and will be the Proj. Mgr. to review the site file for closure... 8/8/08.",,"The property is known locally as the “Golden Valley Brewery” (GVB), and was previously referred to as the Old Pepsi Building.  The property had been used as a gas station or other commercial fueling operation since the 1920s.  Petroleum products stored at this facility included gasoline and heating oil. Petroleum contamination was discovered during the decommissioning of underground storage tanks located north of the existing building.  One 500-gallon gasoline tank and one 500-gallon heating oil tank were removed along with 20 cubic yards of petroleum contaminated soils, which was treated and resued on-site.  To help resolve concerns associated with older analytical methods and inconclusive observations made during cleanup of the site, additional assessment was required.  Analytical results from that assessment support a Soil Matrx no further action (i.e. no groundwater impacts) determination for this portion of the site.  As such, our file review indicates that given the current and reasonably likely future land use, the cleanup of this site is adequately protective of human health, safety, welfare, and the environment and that no further action will be required at this time.",16639.0,0.0,JGLASS,2009-07-02 17:10:09.483
