1735,24-90-4322,24,90,4322,10714.0,1990-12-21,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Western Baptist College,5000 DEER PARK DR SE,SALEM,97301,(503) 581-8600,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : Initial GW 20/45 day bcs ***

Initial report indicates groundwater was impacted. Additional investigation did not encounter groundwater to 18 feet. Location on hillside seems unlike to have significant groundwater. 1/10/91 report indicates sheen on water. Unsure if this may mean sheen testing soil or if there was groundwater at that time. Site has municipal supply that is not expected to change.",,"The site was originally developed in 1870 as the Oregon Institute for Deaf-Mutes and then became the Oregon State Tuberculosis Hospital. Later it became the Western Baptist College before becoming the current site of Corban University. Contamination is the result of a 500 gallon underground gasoline storage tank that had a top mounted dispenser. Soil and soil gas in an approximately 20-foot by 35-foot area around the former tank remain at concentrations less than applicable screening levels. While concentrations of gasoline somewhat exceed the residential vapor intrusion screening level, a soil gas sample shows that future residential use of the area is acceptable. Groundwater was not encountered in any soil borings down to 18 feet. The tank was decommissioned by removal and no soil is known to have been excavated. The site is expected to continue to be used as a school or other campus oriented facility that is connected to municipal water.",88976.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2019-08-07 09:02:33.457
