1772,21-88-4088,21,88,4088,315.0,1988-10-07,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Franko #6,906 HWY 101 S,LINCOLN CITY,97367,(503) 994-8842,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,4.0,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : SEE ALSO: 21-93-4029 *** Pjt Mgr = JLG,Lincoln City Pride LUST #21-93-4029,"In October 1988 petroleum contamination was discovered in test borings placed near the underground storage tank nest.   Further assessment in 1990 near the area of the petroleum distribution pump-island confirmed more widespread impacts.  Four groundwater monitoring wells were installed at that time.  All the underground storage tanks were removed in February 1993.  Gasoline, diesel and heavier oil contamination was confirmed.  In 2001 petroleum contaminated water and free-phased gasoline was found to be leaking out of drums stored behind the former station building. After attempts to have the drums removed by the property owner failed, DEQ authorized a State or Oregon contractor to remove the leaky drums in late 2001 early 2002.  Polychlorinated biphenyl (PCB) contamination was identified in shallow heavy-oil contaminated soil in the area of the former tank nest.  Based on the small volume of contaminated soil, no further remediation in the area is needed unless the area is disturbed or exposed through excavation or construction on the property. A Prospective Purchaser Agreement was received by DEQ in July 2013.  The former Frabko #6 property and 6 adjacent tax lots were acquired by Goodwill Industries of the Columbia Willamette, redeveloped, and the retail store is now open.  A Certificate of Completion has been issued for satisfactorily completing all requirments required during redevelpment of the site and associated with the Order on Concent - DEQ No. 13-12. A No Further Action determination was provided on 3-31-15.",18154.0,0.0,JGLASS,2015-03-31 15:55:00.257
