1837,34-91-0011,34,91,0011,10637.0,1991-01-08,1999-03-18 13:49:10,LAURELWOOD ACADEMY,RT 2 BOX 196,GASTON,97119,(503) 652-2225,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,"ECSI #1839, LUST #34-12-0909, and LUST #34-12-0922","Six USTs were decommissioned at this site in January 1991.  Two 3,000-gallon gasoline USTs and one 3,000-gallon diesel UST in a common tank pit were removed from the site.  A 750-gallon gasoline UST in a separate location was also removed, and a 1,000-gallon heating oil tank was decommissioned in-place.

Significant contamination was encountered around the sixth UST, a 3,000-gallon tank holding xylene that was beneath a furniture factory.  About 30 cubic yards of visibly-contaminated soil was removed from around the accessible north end of the tank and aerated on-site.  Up to 19,150 ppb xylenes were detected in shallow groundwater, along with 9,500 ppb ethylbenzene.  Monitoring was conducted through mid-1996, when concentrations had dropped to 650 ppb xylenes and 44 ppb ethylbenzene.",40383.0,0.0,KDANA,2014-08-13 16:30:41.577
