Petroleum Contaminated Soil on-site from ground water collection trench.  Approximately 750 yd3 of tph-G-D-Heavy Oils PCS.  Permit Addendum dat",Assigned to BCS,"5-5,000 gal tanks decommissioned and removed; 2 diesel, 3 gasoline in 2013. Twelve soil samples and 2 water samples collected and analyzed. Gas and diesel detections were found in samples.
According to the Risk-Based Evaluation Report submitted in 2002, Two USTs were beneath the ""Gas House"" maintenance building; 1-10,000 gal and 1-2,000 gal. The 2,000 gal UST was removed, and the 10,000 gal tank was decommissioned in place. Gasoline-impacted soil was encountered; approx. 50cyd PCS was excavated and disposed at Newberg Landfill. Ten monitoring wells were installed to assess groundwater flow and contaminant plume over time. In 1992 a groundwater extraction and treatment system was initiated; system was designed to intercept the hydrocarbon plume and prevent off-site migration. Additional 550 cyd PCS from excavation for treatment system installation was treated on-site and transported for use at another site. In 1998 a bioremediation injection treatment was implemented and BTEX generally decreased in the source area. Estimated PCS remaining at site was ~350cyd left in place.
In late '85 or early '85 a gas spill of approx. 500 gal occurred while filling the 10,000 gal UST. Gas was washed into a pit located to the East of the fairgrounds property and reportedly not recovered.",23873.0,0.0,JCLAUSS,2020-08-04 11:48:04.747
