2144,34-89-0055,34,89,0055,8631.0,1989-04-06,1999-03-18 13:49:10,BASELINE EXXON,971 SE BASELINE ST,HILLSBORO,97123,(503) 640-4211,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,,,"Five gasoline USTs and one waste oil UST were removed from the site in April 1989 along with 350 cubic yards of PCS.  Three groundwater monitoring wells and three soil vapor extraction wells were installed at the site in June 1989.  The vapor extraction system operated from January 1990 until September 1990 and removed a reported 240 gallons of gasoline hydrocarbons.  An additional 400 cubic yards of PCS were removed in October 1990.  Groundwater contamination remained high in one of the monitoring wells when work stopped on the project in the summer of 1991.

Portions of the site were subsequently taken by expansions of 10th Avenue and Baseline Street, and the site itself was purchased by the City of Hillsboro in August 2008.  Confirmation sampling on and near the site found low levels of residual soil and groundwater contamination.  The City placed restrictions on the site prohibiting residential redevelopment or groundwater use, and DEQ determined that the residual contamination did not pose an unacceptable threat to the proposed redevelopment of the site for a Walgreens store.",23851.0,0.0,LKENT,2010-04-07 12:48:23.410
