2152,20-90-4035,20,90,4035,10322.0,1990-12-07,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Monaco Coach Corp,325 E 1ST ST,JUNCTION CITY,97448,(503) 998-1068,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"(11/26/07 MPC)  Discovered the wrong name on this site ""Crow Valley RFPD"" changed to Monaco Coach Corp.",,"The site was originally developed in 1972 into a recreational vehicle manufacturing facility and is currently used an RV and boat storage facility. Contamination was caused by leaks from two underground storage tanks, one gasoline and one diesel, located beneath a paved portion of the site. Both soil and groundwater were contaminated from the leaking tanks. Approximately 75 cubic yards of soil was excavated and disposed at Short Mountain Landfill.  Approximately 8,200 gallons of petroleum impacted groundwater was pumped from the UST pits and managed at Fuel Processors in Portland, Oregon. Contaminated soils remaining onsite appear to be limited in extent and do not exceed risk based concentrations for occupational use.  Groundwater contamination also appears to be limited in extent but does exceed risk based concentration limits for groundwater ingestion by workers. The total area of impacts to soil and groundwater is believed to be less than 100 feet by 100 feet. The property is currently connected to municipal water and is an occupational site zoned for light industry.  The commercial/industrial use of the property is allowed by current zoning and is not expected to change in the foreseeable future. The No Further Action determination presumes that groundwater at this site will not be used for any beneficial purposes and that this property will not be used residentially.",305.0,0.0,GDECK,2017-07-19 16:20:18.453
