2182,20-91-4007,20,91,4007,,1991-02-01,1999-03-18 13:49:10,JEWELL'S AUTO SERVICE-ZELLNER PROPERTY,198 HWY 99,EUGENE,97402,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,See LUST 20-91-4074,"See Also ECSI #6181 - 

20-91-4074 ZELLNER PROPERTY","The site was undeveloped agriculture land until the early 1950s.  In 1951, the site was developed into a service station on the northeast corner of the site.  The service station had been through at least two different configurations before the underground storage tanks (USTs) were removed in 1991 and 1993.  During UST removal activities, two releases were identified, and DEQ created two LUST files for the Site.  LUST #20 91 4007 is for the releases confirmed at the gasoline UST tank nest located in the NE corner of the property.  A leak at a waste oil UST that was removed in June 1993 resulted in LUST #20-91-4074 between the 4 Corners Barber Shop and Ivy Market buildings.
Staton Construction decommissioned three 8,000-gallon gasoline USTs, piping and dispensers in January 1991.  TMC Environmental, Inc. (TMC) completed an investigation in January 1991 that confirmed the presence of contamination, creating LUST 20-91-4007.  TMC collected four sidewall samples (East, West, North, & South Sidewall) as well as one groundwater sample from the bottom of the tank pit (TMC, 1991). Soil removed during decommissioning activities were placed on visqueen to be aerated by the property owner.  The DEQ was notified and the tank pit was backfilled.  Based on soil and groundwater analytical results, TMC recognized the need for further delineation of soil and groundwater contamination.  In February 1991, TMC oversaw the installation of three monitoring wells (MW-1 through MW-3) and nine soil borings (B-1 through B-9) to further delineate the petroleum contamination beneath the site.  During well installation and soil boring advancement,  
In 2016, EGR & Associates collected additional soil samples near the former waste oil tank (LUST 20-91-4074), and installed an addition well.
In late 2018, DEQ reviewed the file and current risk at the site.  In January 2019, DEQ issued a conditional No Further Action letter restricting land and groundwater use, as well provide a vapor mitigation system beneath any new structure completed on the Tax Lots 4300 and northern 1500.  An Easement and Equitable Servitudes was recorded with Lane County on January 7, 2019.",25154.0,0.0,CJACOBS,2019-01-16 15:58:33.310
