2267,23-90-0018,23,90,0018,,1990-08-01,1999-03-18 13:49:10,SCHOOL DISTRICT BUS BARN,716 NW 6TH ST,ONTARIO,97030,889-5374,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,8/90 2 USTs decom.  Contam in soil & gw. Original decom form also listed a WOT. 8/91 4 MWs installed. Quarterly GW starts. 12/91 @165 cu yds PCS removed. 2/92 5th MW installed. Quarterly monitoring thru 93. Benzene in wells. 4/01 DEQ requests info.,10/17/2002- file transfered to Bend office,"Two petroleum underground storage tanks were decommissioned in 1990. Soil and groundwater sampling identified petroleum contaminated soil and groundwater. Residual petroleum contaminated soil was left in place due to its proximity to structures. Five monitoring wells were installed. Groundwater sampling was conducted in 1991, 1992, 1993 and 2002. Gasoline constituents were detected in the monitoring wells sporadically. Groundwater monitoring results for the sampling event in 2002 showed no gasoline constituents in four of the monitoring wells.  However, hand written notes in our file indicate that free product was measured in the fifth monitoring well. DEQ sampled four monitoring wells (MW-5, MW-6, MW-7, and MW-8), a free product recovery well (6-inch well), and two irrigation wells in May 2007 using grant funds from the EPA .All constituents analyzed for were non-detect in the monitoring wells MW-5, MW-6, and MW-7, as well as the residential irrigation well. Several hydrocarbons were detected in the 6-inch well.Based on recent groundwater sampling data, soil data collected in 1991, and an evaluation of applicable pathways for the Ontario School Bus Barn site, it is recommended that either a soil-gas survey be performed or indoor air samples in the building adjacent to the former UST be collected for benzene.  A NFA determination for this site can not be granted at this time based on historic benzene concentrations in soil adjacent to the building.
