Also, 20-91-4007 JEWELL'S AUTO SERVICE-ZELLNER PROPERTY (apparent double-entry in the LUST database - close with ECSI and LUST NFA when the time comes)... gdeck 7/2/2018","The site was undeveloped agriculture land until the early 1950s.  In 1951, the site was developed into a service station on the northeast corner of the site.  The service station had been through at least two different configurations before the underground storage tanks (USTs) were removed in 1991 and 1993.  During UST removal activities, two releases were identified, and DEQ created two LUST files for the Site.  LUST #20 91 4007 is for the releases confirmed at the gasoline UST tank nest located in the NE corner of the property.  A leak at a waste oil UST that was removed in June 1993 resulted in LUST #20-91-4074 between the 4 Corners Barber Shop and Ivy Market buildings.
In 2016, EGR & Associates collected additional soil samples near the former waste oil tank, and installed an addition well.
In late 2018, DEQ reviewed the file and current risk at the site.  In January 2019, DEQ issued a conditional No Further Action letter restricting land and groundwater use, as well provide a vapor mitigation system beneath any new structure completed on the Tax Lots 4300 and northern 1500.  An Easement & Equitable Servitudes was recorded at Lane County on January 7, 2019.",25154.0,0.0,CJACOBS,2019-01-16 16:00:17.343
