SITE RE-OPENED on : 10/7/2016 By Virginia Deck. Chris Richardson is investigating violation of EES.  Previous Final Invoice Request Date and NFA Date: 7/7/2010.  

*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : On Hwy 99W (State right of way) 3ft deep, product from 1.5ft absorbant pads in hole, blocked off man cover with plywoood.  Texaco station on corner.  City putting trees in, doing excavation, dug hole, oil (possibly gas). *** QUARTERLY GW MONITORING OCCURRING ON-SITE.  OFF-SITE INVESTIGATION REQUESTED 2-8-2000.",see also: 36-97-4133,"The property, previously known as the Morris Texaco, and currently in business as the Newberg Shell Service Center, has been used as a retail gas station since the 1920s.  The property has been in private ownership for over 100 years and is currently owned by Archie Morris.    

Petroleum contamination was discovered in 1991 when soil and groundwater contamination was observed during the installation of a tree in the public right-of-way (sidewalk) of East 1st Street.  A second petroleum release was discovered in 1997 during upgrade work being performed on the three active gasoline underground storage tank systems.  Since the 1991 report of contamination, Mr. Morris has conducted multiple investigations to determine the extent of contamination. Between June and August 2005, he had contaminated soil removed from the area with the highest concentrations.

