2407,18-91-0022,18,91,0022,1149.0,1991-03-20,1999-03-18 13:49:10,"OREGON STATE HIGHWAY, 4-11 CHEMULT",NORTHEAST CHEMULT HWY 97,CHEMULT,97731,(503)365-2275,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,7/92 six USTs decom. 200 cu yds pcs removed. High diesel concen. GEM remove 1260 cu yds PCS. Collect smpls. Elevated gas and diesel. Sampled on-site well. No BTEX.  Need additional cleanup.  Letter sent 10/1/02.,ODOT EA# 4035-204-092,"The Chemult Maintenance Site is an active Oregon Department of Transportation (ODOT) facilityu.  Contamination was discovered originating from on-site fuel underground storage tanks (USTs) that ODOT decommissioned on July 16, 1992. 

To delineate the vertical and lateral extent of the plume, ODOT advanced 11 on-site soil borings and constructed monitoring wells in eight of these borings between May 12, 2005 and October 14, 2009

On-site fuel released impacted soil and groundwater in a perched aquifer zone at a depth of approximately 40-42 feet below ground surface.  

Contaminated soil was removed and the vertical and lateral extents of the groundwater plume indicate some travel off site east-northeast from the site to at least the ODOT/Union Pacific Railroad right-of-way boundary, although concentrations are continuing to decline.

Based on remaining risk level identified,  current uses, ownership status, limited access, and remote location, developments in this area, including water well construction, are not likely in the foreseeable future and the site is currently protective of human health and the environment.",18698.0,0.0,DANDERS,2016-09-22 16:12:20.080
