2418,26-90-0516,26,90,0516,,1991-03-21,1999-03-18 13:49:10,AMERICAN PROPERTY MANAGEMENT,1730 SW SKYLINE BLVD,PORTLAND,97221,,False,,,,,True,False,,,False,,,,,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : CLOSED *** ,,,121790.0,,LLO,2016-03-25 13:41:14.430
2419,20-91-4093,20,91,4093,10695.0,1991-03-19,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Wagon Works,388 W 13TH AVE,EUGENE,97401,(503) 345-6414,False,2.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,G/D release to Soil/GW (off-site impact claimed from Gasoline release) last work 7-11-91 Needs 340-122-240 investigation...RS 5-28-93,,"The property was used as a gasoline service station until 1972. The site then operated as an auto repair business. Three 6,000-gallon gasoline USTs were removed from the property on March 1, 1991. Soil samples were collected from the excavation sidewalls that identified petroleum contamination. A water sample was also obtained from the excavation pit, identifying petroleum impacts to this media.  

A soil sample collected from the east sidewall detected gasoline at 472 ppm, benzene at 0.35 ppm, toluene at 0.890 ppm, ethylbenzene at 2.7 ppm, and xylenes at 8.2 ppm. The pit water sample contained gasoline at 9,700 ppb, benzene at 330 ppb, toluene at 1,000 ppb, ethylbenzene at 220 ppb, and xylenes at 1,500 ppb. The three remaining confirmation soil samples were non-detect for petroleum contaminants (gas and BTEX).

A report documenting site assessment conducted by BB&A Environmental on May 14, 2010 was submitted to DEQ on June 28, 2010. Three borings were installed for the collection of soil and groundwater samples. Only lead was detected in groundwater samples, and minimal gasoline (8.14 ppm) was present in soil from one borehole.",16545.0,0.0,CRODDA,2010-08-18 10:24:26.223
