2465,03-91-0135,03,91,0135,7138.0,1991-03-27,1999-03-18 13:49:10,"LAKE OSWEGO, CITY OF",5705 SW JEAN RD,LAKE OSWEGO,97034,(503) 636-3601,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,True,False,False,"The AS/VSE system has been shut down.  First round of compliance quarterly GW sampling has been completed for possible site closure.  TPH and constituent concentrations are below applicable RBCs.  Report documenting results of first quarter 2009 monitoring event was received on April 14, 2009.  Three of four consecutive quaterly events have been completed after system shutdown.  No report for 2nd quarter 2009 monitoring event received.  Called Erik Chapman of Bergeson-Boese on 12-14-09.  Report for last (4th) quarterly monitorign event follwoing system shutdown was submitted to City of Lake Oswego in early July 2009 for their review..  Report included recommendation for deed restriction and soil management plan.  Missing groundwater monitoring report not received by DEQ until May 2010, along with argument for clsoure of release.  Comments on this report and closure request provided by DEQ in letter dated 6-30-10.  Additional clarifying information requested for Conceptual Site Model already completed.  Groundwater monitoring and remediation suspended. On 10-13-11, BB&A submitted report responding to remaining comments/issues raised in DEQ letter of 6-30-10.  Based on addtional evaluation, BB&A concluded groundwater in area of site (including impacted property to east) is not likely to be used.  Colander well 300 feet south of site is not used as a drinking water source.  Comment solicitation letter sent to nearby properties on 12-5-11.  Comment period ends 1-9-12 (JKS 12-15-11).  

On December 27, 2011, comments were received from the consultant for the adoining property owner (17607 Pilkington Road).  The consultant inquired concerning use restrictions that would be requried for the impacted property.  In an email communication dated 12-28-11, DEQ responded that none were necessary.  The consultant for the property owner was further informed that a liability/indemnity agreement could be requested from the City of Lake Oswego but DEQ would not be a party to those discussions and such an agreement was not a condition of closure.  On January 5, 2012, DEQ was contacted by the owner of residential property south of Jean Road (Calonder Property).  Mr. Calonder inquired about protocols for testing his well, although he repeatedly indicated there was no evidence of petroluem contamination (odor or sheen).  No other comments were received during the comment period (JKS 1-17-12).",,,3877.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2012-06-14 13:47:51.220
