2475,26-91-0151,26,91,0151,5020.0,1991-04-09,1999-03-18 13:49:10,DON RASMUSSEN COMPANY,1737 SW MORRISON AVE,PORTLAND,97205,(503) 288-8351,False,1.0,MATRIX,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"A 2,000-gallon waste oil UST, located beneath the floor in the basement of the building, was decommissioned in March 1991.  Up to 21,000 ppm TPH, 560 ppm TPH-G, and 2.4 ppm PCE were present in the soil but not removed.  Three borings were advanced in May 1994 to determine the extent of contamination.  One boring encountered 61,500 ppm TPH, 850 ppm TPH-G, 5.0 ppm PCE and 0.74 ppm TCE.  Very little contamination was detected otherwise.  Investigation and cleanup is very difficult due to limited clearance in the basement and large debris (bricks, concrete, wooden beams, etc) in the soil.

A second UST (300-gallon gasoline) was discovered beneath the sidewalk on Morrison Street in front of the building during light rail construction in the area.  The UST was removed in February 1996 along with 15 tons of PCS.  Additional PCS could not be removed due to utility lines, the adjacent building, etc.  Gasoline (up to 2,300 ppm) remains in the soil.  DEQ issued an NFA letter (with a pocket-in-place closure) for the gasoline UST in November 1996.

The site was added to ECSI (#1684) due to the PCE and TCE detections, but remains unassigned.  The current owner (Harsch Investment Properties) has indicated that they plan to redevelop the site at some point and will deal with the problems then.  Realistically, little can be done while the building is in place.  (7/13/09 KPD)",LUST #26-94-0061; ECSI #1684 & #1799,,1178.0,0.0,KDANA,2009-07-13 16:41:03.660
