2515,04-91-0170,04,91,0170,276.0,1991-04-25,1999-03-18 13:49:10,BOB'S TEXACO,2615 MARINE DR,ASTORIA,97103,(503) 325-0770,False,,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Gasoline vapors were reported in the basement of Astoria Realty in April 1991 and traced back to Bob's Texaco (about a block away).  A soil sample found 13,000 ppm gasoline at Bob's at 16 ft bgs.  The four USTs at Bob's were emptied but not decommissioned.  Robert & Mary Kankkonen were determined in March 1992 to have an inability to pay.  No investigation or cleanup has been conducted.  Roger Gilbert purchased the site in Nov 1996 but has not responded to any Backlog letters.  As of April 2007 there were $7,293 in unpaid invoices on this project.  (6/3/09 KPD).  In March 2011, DEQ met with City of Astoria, Columbia Memorial Hospital, and Karen Homolac of Business Oregon.  The hospital is interested in acquiring the Bob's Texaco property for parking.  The hospital was going to work with Business Oregon to apply for Brownfield Assessment funds.  In August 2011, DEQ was contacted by Kevin Schleh of GEOCON Northwest.  The hospital was awarded $50,000 to do Phase I and II ESAs of the property.  The current property owner (Mr. Gilbert) and Columbia Memorial Hospital entered into a purchase agreement that ends June 30, 2013.  In part using funds from Business Oregon, the USTs were decommissioned in May 2012.  Two rounds of follow-up investigation were performed in May and June 2012.  Extent of groundwater contamination roughly defined.  Soil-gas samples contained consituents at very high levels, raising concerns about risks to residents of nearby dwellings. Columbia Memorial Hospital reportedly preparing an application for a PPA. (JKS 1-31-13)",,,18136.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2013-01-31 15:28:30.770
