2517,26-91-0166,26,91,0166,,1991-04-24,1999-03-18 13:49:10,DON RASMUSSEN CO.,2001 SW JEFFERSON,PORTLAND,97201,(503) 224-8313,False,,,3.0,ADMCLO,False,True,,,False,,,,,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : Tank is in public right-of-way adjacent to Don Rasmussen BMW (below Vista Bridge). Tank contained mixture of PS300 (deisel/bunker fuel).  Static WL:15'; top of tank: 15'.  24-APR-91: pumped 1275 gal. water and 470 gal. oil. 26-APR-91 ~1000 gal. of fuel and water in tank; tank ~2000 gal. - out of commission for a number of years. *** see also 26-91-009; duplicate file for 26-91-0176.  Please see 26-91-0176 for most current updates on file.,,,2537.0,,BALBERT,2003-07-23 14:30:03.000
2518,24-91-4113,24,91,4113,5583.0,1991-04-12,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Valley Motor Company,2405 COMMERCIAL STREET SE,SALEM,97302,(503) 585-1231,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Project De-Assignment letter sent 7/16/2015.,,"Petroleum contamination found beneath the site during investigations in 1991.  Contamination was from two gas stations that previosly occupied the site between 1960 and 1983 - Phillips 66 on the north and Douglas Oil on the central part of the property.  Contamination at the Phillips 66 site was limited to soil and groundwater in the tank pit.  Cleanup action applied to the groundwater of tank pit greatly reduced contaminant levels.  Contamination at Douglas Oil was limited to soil only inside the former tank pit. Contamination in the soil was at low levels and did not require cleanup. Remaining contamination at both sites is now below applicable risk levels and closure was propsed in DEQ's Project Manager's staff report dated October 14, 2019. An No Further Action for the site was issued on ___",157278.0,0.0,GDECK,2019-12-31 15:46:35.403
