2529,15-91-0019,15,91,0019,1274.0,1991-03-20,1999-03-18 13:49:10,"CHEVRON U.S.A., INC. - 91509",7600 CRATER LAKE HWY,WHITE CITY,97503,(503)826-4291,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"Benzene present in MW-3 and vault 3 near MW-3 at 3,400 and 2900 ppb respectively.  Needs further investigation, new MW-3A reported 15,000ppb benzene in Mar-04, project currently unassigned, benzene concentrations remain consistently high at new well (MW-3A), currently on annual monitoring schedule due to property ownership situation (Esc, 5-oct-09)",15-10-0970 LIL' PANTRY LLC - WHITE CITY,"An environmental assessment was completed at the facility in March and April 1991 to determine if 2,600 gallons of unaccounted for gasoline was released from the UST system.  Petroleum contaminated soil and groundwater were identified through the assessment, with samples obtained from trenches and pits excavated around the site building, storm drain, pump islands, and product lines.  During assessment work it was also discovered that a floor drain in the service building connected to a storm sewer drain, but contractors removed line and installed a connection to the sanitary sewer.

Free-phase petroleum was noted floating on water in the trenches, and appeared to enter the excavations from beneath the storm drain at the northern end of the east pump island.  A soil vapor extraction (SVE) system was installed prior to backfilling the UST excavations.  The SVE system operated from June 1993 to October 1997.  The remedial system restarted in June 1998 after a spike in groundwater concentrations at a sump located on the northwest corner of the UST basin.  Groundwater monitoring has been conducted intermittently since wells were installed in 1991.",2221.0,0.0,CRODDA,2011-09-26 09:49:14.840
