2552,20-91-4127,20,91,4127,2752.0,1991-05-02,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Eugene Sand & Gravel II,3000 DELTA HWY NORTH,EUGENE,97401,(503)683-6400,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,"See Also LUST 20-91-4363, 20-91-4064, and ECS I# 1210","June 29, 2019: Please see the DEQ Staff Memo recommending NFA,included in webdocs, and the ECSI File #1210. 

There were 7 total USTs associated with the Eugene Sand and gravel property.
•Tank 1.  Island #1 Gas (10,000-gallon unleaded);
•Tank 2.  Island #1 Diesel (10,000-gallon);
•Tank 3.  Island #2 Gas (20,000-gallon regular);
•Tank 4.  Island #2 Diesel (20,000-gallon);
•Tank 5.  Island #2 Diesel (10,000-gallon);
•Tank 6.  Concrete Batch Plant (2,000-gallon fuel oil); and
•Tank 7. Waste Oil (3,500-gallon). 

Tank 6 had an overfill release on February 6, 1991 and was assigned LUST#20-91-4064.  The tank was decommissioned by removal shortly after the release along with removal of impacted soil.  A No Further Action (NFA) was given on April 26, 1991.

Tanks 1 through 5  were removed on December 6, 1991 along with some soil, but this area was found to have significant soil and groundwater contamination from tank leaks.  DEQ assigned LUST# 20-91-4363 to these tanks.  The excavated soil was stockpiled on site from these tanks and Tank 7.
Tank 7 was removed in May 1991 along with impacted soil.  There was also residual soil and groundwater contamination noted around this waste oil tank that required further investigation and treatment.  DEQ assigned the LUST# 20-91-4127 and ECSI #1210 for the tank.

After numerous investigations and treatment of stockpile, the soil and groundwater are below relevant RBCs so the site is being given a No Further Action for each of the ECSI and LUST files.",13125.0,0.0,GDECK,2020-08-28 14:52:03.493
