2556,26-91-0165,26,91,0165,9353.0,1991-02-19,1999-03-18 13:49:10,HANNA 914,5124 SE 17TH AVE,PORTLAND,97202,(503) 236-7055,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"A service station and car wash were built at the site in 1974.  A release of gasoline to the soil was discovered in February 1991.  Five groundwater monitoring wells were installed in June 1992, and quarterly sampling began in 1994.  In April 1995, two 20,000-gallon gasoline USTs and one 10,000-gallon gasoline UST were removed and replaced.  An SVE system began operating in August 1996, and a total of eight monitoring wells had been installed by June 1998.

The SVE system was shut down in June 2000, and quarterly groundwater monitoring apparently ended in September 2001, after sampling showed that gasoline and BTEX had been almost totally removed from the air and water.  DEQ recommended that confirmation soil samples be collected, and preliminary results from March 2002 showed up to 67.7 ppm gasoline.  However, a final report was never received, and the site was backlogged in 2005.

Delta Consultants collected samples in July 2007 from six borings at the site (now Shell Station #124726).  Gasoline (1,820 ppm) was found in one soil sample, and heavy oil (121 ppb) was found in one groundwater sample.  There has been no further correspondence with Delta or Shell since.  (7/9/09 KPD)",,,17641.0,0.0,RHOOD,2011-01-18 14:34:54.980
