2572,26-91-0176,26,91,0176,,1991-04-30,1999-03-18 13:49:10,ROTH BMW (RASMUSSEN),2001 SW JEFFERSON,PORTLAND,97201,,False,1.0,MATRIX,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"In January 2009, AMEC submitted monitoring reports for events conducted in September 2004, December 2004, and March 2005.  Significant drop in TPH-G from 1,030 to 387 ppb in MW-3. Risk-based closure requested by AMEC.  Reference in file to unresolved HOT cleanup from 1991 but this does not appear to have been addressed in 2003-2005 work.  DEQ letter of June 24, 2009 requested an additional monitoring event.  Rasmussen agreed to perform additional groundwater monitoring event before end of October 2009.  This will be used to determine if additional investigation still warranted.  Information provided to DEQ by Rasmussen suggests the 1991 HOT release is actually a concrete vault for an old cable car system.  Data pertaining to selected items (well search, inforrmation on cable car vault, and darcy velocity calculation) requested in DEQ letter of June 24, 2010 were received via email in September 2009.  AMEC reportedly completed a groundwater monitoring event in Fall 2009. Last communication was phone call on September 29, 2009 concerning the formatting of reporting for the Fall 2009 monitoring event. No report received to date by DEQ. On July 13, 2010, returned call to Chris Foy concerning status of project. *Left message* (JKS 7-13-10).  Spoke with Chris Foy on July 14, 2010.  He will look into status of report for Fall 2009 monitoring event and asked to be cc'd on all future correspondence (JKS 07-14-10).  Report for September 2009 event received 10-14-10.  Groundwater concentrations in range of data from 2004-2005 - plume appears to be stable.  Flow direction consistent with historic data. Responses to intems in letter of 6-24-10 included.  Spoke with Heidi Nelson of AMEC on 10-20-10.  Vapor system not currently in operation.  Discussed collection of ""worst-case"" sample from port on system to screen against residential soil-gas RBC standards.  AMEC will consult with their client and will contact DEQ to discuss work plan.   Sampling performed December 2010 but write-up not received until early March 2010.  Gasoline constituents not detected at concentrations exceeding residential soil-gas RBC standards. Comment Solicitation Letter sent March 21, 2011. Comment letter from City of Portland requested notification of RP of their responsbility for future contamination in ROW. Draft NFA approved by hydrogeologist and Manager. Expedited invoicing requested. (JKS 5-23-11).",,,2537.0,0.0,LKENT,2011-05-31 11:12:08.140
