2631,36-91-4155,36,91,4155,10861.0,1991-03-12,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Fredricks Property,306 NE JOHNSON ST,MCMINNVILLE,97128,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"Property Background:
The site is located in McMinnville, Oregon, on the northeast corner of the intersection of 3rd and Johnson Streets.  The Yamhill County Tax Assessor location of the property is identified as the Township 4S, Range 4W Section 21, in the SE 1/4 section of the NW 1/4 section C, tax map number T04SR04W4421BD and is located on tax lot numbers 03700 & 03800.  The property elevation above mean sea level was estimated to be 155 feet.   According to the report from Kizer Excavating Company (Kizer) entitled “UST Decommissioning Report” dated May 6, 1991, the site was a service station from 1936 to 1952, when the gas station was replaced by a “tire shop”, which operated until sometime in the 60’s.  

UST Decommissioning:  According to the DEQ file records, the UST systems were decommissioned by removal and consisted of the following:
    Number     Permit Number     Size    Product    Status
    1    None    750-gallon    Gasoline    Removed -3-12-1990
    2    None    750-gallon    Gasoline    Removed -3-12-1990.
Although no UST facility number was assigned to this site, a UST permit application and fees were provided at the time of decommissioning.  A small amount of petroleum-contaminated soil (10 cubic yards – yd3) was removed during the UST systems decommissioning and spread on-site for remediation.   Additional gasoline contamination was discovered in soil adjacent to the former pump-island during the investigation of a petroleum release across Johnson Street in 2007.  Further investigation of this area, discovery of additional UST systems, and UST decommissioning was completed by January 2012.  Additional quarterly groundwater monitoring combined with groundwater monitoring from an adjacent property demonstrated that the remaining contamination plume was stable and did not pose a threat under the current and reasonably likely use of the site.",25265.0,0.0,JGLASS,2014-02-12 13:51:19.857
