2645,15-91-0028,15,91,0028,1393.0,1991-05-30,1999-03-18 13:49:10,TEXACO STATION,428 BARNETT RD,MEDFORD,97501,(503)773-5766,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Free product last noted in 5/97, reduced monitoring to annual events, CSM submittal expected in mid 2007, will need to begin 1/4ly monitoring events",,"The site is an operating retail service station utilizing five USTs consisting of three gasoline tanks and one diesel tank.  The USTs were installed in 1991 after the decommissioning by removal of the previous tank system, which included seven USTs and associated product lines and dispensers.  As part of decommissioning activities, PCS was excavated from the UST cavity to depths of 14 feet bgs, leaving soil contamination due to facility structures near the pit.  A vapor extraction system was installed in 1993 to address remaining contamination.  A waste oil tank installed in 1991 was decommissioned by removal in 1998.

Five monitoring wells (MW-1 through MW-5) were installed in October 1992, with MW-6 installed at the northeast corner of the site in 2004.  Gasoline and related petroleum constituents have detected at the highest levels in MW-2 and MW-3.  The maximum concentration of gasoline-range hydrocarbons was measured at 173,000 ppb in MW-2 during the August 1997 sampling event.  Benzene was detected at 9,910 ppb in MW-3 in July 1994.  

In June 2006, GeoEngineers installed six probes (DP-1 and DP-3 through DP-7) to depths of 10.5 to 20 feet bgs.  Twelve soil samples were collected at depths of 2.5 feet to 19 feet bgs.  The maximum gasoline in soil was at DP-4 at 80.6 ppm and lead at 6.65 ppm in soil from 5 feet bgs at DP-6.  None of the soil samples contained BTEX above detection levels.  The only RBDM VOCs  present in soil were at boring DP-4, with n-propylbenzene, 1,2,4-tmb and 1,3,5-tmb measured at 166 ppm, 882 ppm and 314 ppm, respectively.  Groundwater was collected only from DP-6 and identified no contaminants.

In July 2007, Delta installed six borings (DSB-1 through DSB-6).  Soil from DSB-5 had gasoline at 607 ppm, ethylbenzene at 1.2 ppm, xylenes at 6.2 ppm, and 1,2,4-trimethylbenzene at 4.2 ppm.  The remaining soil samples did not contain gasoline, diesel, or RBDM VOCs.  Water samples obtained from temporary wells identified impacts, most notably at DSB-2 adjacent to Barnett Road.  Gasoline was detected at 3,120 ppb, diesel at 910 ppb, ethylbenzene at 80 ppb, xylenes at 99 ppb, 1,2,4-trimethylbenzene at 180 ppb, 1,3,5-trimethylbenzene at 62 ppb, and naphthalene at 38 ppb in water from DSB-2.  The most recent GW sampling event occurred on November 4, 2008.  Gasoline was measured at 1,300 ppb in water from MW-2, at 2,100 ppb at MW-3, and <DL in the remaining wells.  VOCs were at relatively low concentrations in MW-2 and MW-3.",11174.0,0.0,GDECK,2013-09-26 13:15:40.767
