Four USTs were removed from the site in 1991, along with over 250 cubic yards of PCS.  Seven monitoring wells were installed by the end of 1992.  Two of the wells (VA-1 and VA-4) have been monitored quarterly from 1996 through at least 2005.  The other five wells are monitored semiannually.  As of August 2005 only VA-4 appeared to be contaminated above RBCs.  More recent sampling data and a Conceptual Site Model is needed before an NFA can be issued.  (3/2/10 TMB)",,,21407.0,0.0,RHOOD,2017-12-20 10:34:14.583
