2811,02-91-4220,02,91,4220,7834.0,1991-08-01,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Truax Shell #19,29TH & GRANT,CORVALLIS,97330,(503) 758-1500,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"August 5, 1991, Discussed site with John Truax.  Truax leased site for 10 yrs, station has been at site for 20 years.  Truax has been out of the lease for more than a year.  Truax tested tanks in 1987.  Tanks are owned by the Trust...",,"(MOTT 10/31/16) The site operated as a service station from 1957 to 1989.  In November 1990, the fire department notified DEQ about a sheen observed on water in a phone vault near the intersection of NW 29th Street and NW Grant Avenue. In 1992, the USTs were removed.  In May 1994, DEQ advanced three soil borings (PC-1, PC-2, and PC-3) near the southeastern property boundary (between former USTs and phone vault). A total of four soil samples were submitted for laboratory analysis of HCID. Soil samples collected from PC-2 and PC-3 were none detect and the soil sample from PC-1 indicated a TPH-G concentration of 160ppm. Water was not encountered in PC-1 or PC-2 but was encountered in PC-3 at four feet. A groundwater sample was collected from PC-3 and analyzed for BTEX. The results were B-76ppb, T-19ppb, E-328ppb, X-633ppb. In 2000, Aspen Environmental advanced six soil borings at the site. One soil and one groundwater sample were collected from each boring. All six soil samples indicated concentration below the occupational RBCs. The highest concentrations of BTEX were observed in SP3 at 8.5’ (B-0.21ppm, T-0.41ppm, E-3.79ppm, X-10.20ppm). Concentrations of naphthalene in groundwater at all six locations exceeded the Groundwater in Excavation RBC of 500ppb. The highest naphthalene concentration was reported in sample location SP5 along the northeastern property boundary. Offsite delineation was deemed necessary. In 2016 Cascade Earth Sciences collected seven soil samples and four groundwater samples. None of the soil samples exceeded occupational RBCs. One groundwater sample (SST-GW-03) exceeded the excavation worker RBCs for naphthalene and 1,2,4-trimethylbenzene. SST-GW-03 is located offsite to the east in the northbound lane of NW 29th Street.",23294.0,0.0,MOTT,2016-10-31 14:28:36.197
