2839,02-91-4209,02,91,4209,,1991-07-26,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Family Car Wash/BP,1334 NW 9TH STREET,CORVALLIS,97330,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : GW encountered. Get one sample ND.Adjust to LUST site GW ltr. *** 30 yd3 PCS remain from release in 1992.  Tanks removed 11-21-94 as part of rebuild of new station.  PCS taken to Riverbend Landfill.  Level 2 site.  Confirmation samples at soil/H20 interface (10') show only north wall (86ppm) exceeds cleanup,Pjt Mgr=JLG,"In July 1991 petroleum contamination was found in soil and groundwater during assessment of contamination in the City of Corvallis storm-drain system.  The petroleum storage tanks were emptied in 1991 and subsequently removed in 1994 along with an estimated 30 yards of contaminated soil. All soil and groundwater investigations, cleanup, monitoring, and a risk assessment were completed by the fall of 2009.  Some contamination associated with leaks from the underground storage tank system remains. The responsible party has proposed that no further cleanup or monitoring is needed at this site.  DEQ has evaluated efforts to contain, clean up, and assess the contamination and now believes that this leak is not a threat to human health or the environment.",19016.0,0.0,GDECK,2014-09-16 16:56:19.210
