2899,36-91-4243,36,91,4243,10812.0,1991-08-19,1999-03-18 13:49:10,McDonough Property,1910 S HWY 99W,MCMINNVILLE,97128,(503)472-7397,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : 10/4/91 GW LETTER.  NFA ISSUED 9/23/92.  DISPOSAL: 950 GAL. GASOLINE, 20 WASTE OIL/HEATING OIL. SITE REOPENED 5/1/04 BY JLG. 2ND NFA ISSUED 5-17-06. SEE ALSO 36-96-4042. *** Former ARCO Property.  NFA issued 9-23-92.  Site reopened 5-19-04 by JLG.  Second NFA issued 5-17-06 with EES recorded with Yamhill Co.",36-96-4042 Shoulder of Road,"The property is former 1940s gasoline service station that was removed between 1975 and 1977.  The site was used recently for the “Golden Pacific Home” Sales.  Soil contamination was initially reported to DEQ in 1991, when petroleum contamination was discovered during removal of six underground storage tanks (USTs).  Two additional USTs were removed during subsequent excavation of approximately 1030 cubic yards of petroleum contaminated soil.  In February 2004, groundwater contamination was discovered during an assessment for a property transaction.  The owners recently completed an investigation and four groundwater monitoring events to fully assess the remaining contamination and evaluate the associated exposure concerns.  Based on soil and groundwater sampling results, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land use, the remaining contamination from the leaky UST systems has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment.  The closure plan proposes to allow the remaining contamination in soil and groundwater to naturally attenuate in place.",16454.0,0.0,JGLASS,2007-12-05 09:45:54.147
