Site address changed from original 3940 W 13th St, Eugene 97405 to 3940 W 13th Ave, Eugene 97402... g deck 3/26/09","Rollins Leasing II, USTC #20-96-7023 - located at 3960 W. 13th St.","1.    The DEQ records for UST facility #3764 (Rollins Leasing) include three USTs.  The tanks were permitted as one 12,000-gallon diesel and two 10,000-gallon diesel USTs.  The 12,000-gallon diesel UST was removed in 1996 and a release was reported under USTC #20-96-7023 at 3960 West 13th Avenue.  This cleanup site was issued a letter of No Further Action on October 7, 1999.
At the time that the original petroleum release was reported to the DEQ in September 1991, the USTs had been utilized by Rollins Leasing.  This trucking company used the two 10,000-gallon diesel USTs (DEQ permit numbers CGEJ and CGFA) at 3940 West 13th Avenue in Eugene for its operations.  Hult & Associates was regarded as the responsible party because they were the property owners when the release was reported.  Brooks Excavating and Hauling removed the two 10,000-gallon diesel USTs on September 4 and 5, 1991.  The City of Eugene fire department inspected the USTs on the September 3, 1991, and noted in a site sketch the location of the two 10,000-gallon tanks between the buildings at 3930 and 3940 West 13th Avenue.  
The initial decommissioning report submitted by Brooks dated December 4, 1991, contained lab results for sampling at a different property. 
Multiple excavations occurred to remove petroleum-contaminated soil.  A receipt from Lane County indicates 200 cubic yards of diesel-contaminated soil was disposed of at Short Mountain Landfill on October 9, 1991.",25371.0,0.0,GDECK,2011-04-18 11:17:44.413
