2/23/17 Initial address deleted from County records; current address is 3245 Fisher Rd. NE - Jen Claussen",,"The site was originally farmland and appears to have been developed sometime between 1944 and 1959 according to topographic maps.  Currently there are two warehouses on the property which were built in 1967. Contamination resulted from piping leaks in a 1000 gallon diesel tank and a 500 gallon gasoline tank. Both soil and groundwater on the site were contaminated from the releases. Approximately 500 cubic yards of contaminated soil was excavated, aerated onsite to below detectable levels, and was disposed of at an unknown location. About 8,000 gallons of un-impacted groundwater was pumped from the excavation and used to moisten the aeration pile. Contaminated soil remains under the south west corner of the northern warehouse. From approximately three feet below ground surface to a depth of about 16 feet. A groundwater sample showed low level constituents which attenuated within two years based on monitoring well data. During a site investigation for the adjacent property to the north, a monitoring well was installed just north of the northern warehouse building and within feet of the property line. No contamination was detected. The property is currently and expected to remain a commercial facility that is connected to municipal water. Public notice was given to the properties north of the site as potential downgradient receptors even though contamination does not extent offsite. No Comments were received. The investigation was limited to the location of the former tanks and extending north to the property boundary.",17372.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2017-10-25 15:52:14.390
