06-16-0741 Coos Bay Pac. Pride II","(8/17/21 - DEH) In 1991 a diesel leak from underground piping associated with an AST was reported. A partial soil cleanup was completed, leaving significant amounts of contaminated soil in place. Limited groundwater testing for petroleum constitutents BTEX and PAHs confirmed groundwater impacts. In 2002 it was estimated using site data and basic modeling that about 1,680 cubic yards of contaminated soil remained between the release area and a storm water ditch that borders the site on the east. In 2003 DEQ issued a NFA for the site based on human health screening levels. In 2015 a sheen was observed on the ditch adjacent to the residual contamination. DEQ opened a new LUST 06-15-1789 for the sheen, however the sheen is likely from the residual contamiantion from the 1991 release that was never removed. Based on this new information the 2003 NFA is no longer applicable. DEQ is requesting further groundwater monitoring at the site to assess the residual groundwater conditions related to the old diesel release, as well as a 2016 spill bucket release of gasoline (LUST 06-16-0741).",16410.0,0.0,DHANSON,2021-08-17 14:50:47.060
