3365,15-89-0060,15,89,0060,8260.0,1989-11-13,1999-03-18 13:49:10,"COLVIN OIL CO., MEDFORD #2",1325 COURT ST,MEDFORD,97501,(503)479-5343,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Off-site impacts to south at 1313 Court Street noted by DEQ in 1989.  Possible off-site impacts to north at former Medco (Alba Village development) based on 2007-2009 site assessments.,"Information on nearby sites in Alba Village and Medco (aka, Medite) ECSI and LUST files.

Site score updated May 2018 - no more FP at site. New score 1000.","(MOTT 04/09/18) Two fuel line leaks occurred at the site, one in 1979 and one in 1982. An Environmental Site Assessment conducted on the adjacent property to the south (1313 Court Street) in 1989 identified detectable concentrations of petroleum range hydrocarbons in soil and groundwater. The petroleum contamination discovered on the 1313 Court Street property was believed to originate from the Colvin Oil Co. Medford #2 site. In March 1990, three USTs were removed from the site and replaced with three new USTs (two 12,000-gallon gasoline and one 8,000-gallon diesel UST). Visible soil and groundwater impacts were observed during the decommissioning activities. In 1998, new product lines and pump islands were installed at the site and a total of 100 tons of petroleum impacted soil was removed. However, no information regarding these activities are available. Numerous soil and groundwater samples were collected at the site and the adjacent property to the north (Alba Village, ECSI #5251) between 1990 and 2017. Based on the most recent groundwater data collected at the site in 2017, groundwater concentrations onsite and along the north, south, east, and west property boundaries, are below the applicable RBCs for the site. (MOTT 8/26/18) The site was issued a NFA on August 21, 2018.",23584.0,0.0,MOTT,2018-08-26 11:06:01.720
