3463,26-92-0020,26,92,0020,,1992-01-30,1999-03-18 13:49:10,ODOT SE WATER AVE,TAYLOR STREET,PORTLAND,97214,(503) 238-8220,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"The history of this site is not at all clear.  A May 1993 report from ODOT discusses the decommissioning of 10 USTs in February 1993 from a three-block area between Water Ave and Interstate 5 on the east bank of the Willamette.  A second report in the file, from March 1999, discusses the removal of two USTs from the block immediately north of the three block area.  The final report from Jim Orr at ODOT (dated January 2005) again focuses on the three block area.  At this point, Bijan Pour focused on the southern block (Parcel 3B), saying that only a Closure Report was needed before the parcel received an NFA.  A report was planned for July 2007 but apparently was never submitted.

This project may be ready for an NFA once the site boundaries are defined.  The project should be worked on in conjunction with LUST #26-99-0182, which is within the three block area.  (10/28/10 KPD)",,,25520.0,0.0,KDANA,2010-10-28 13:28:11.657
3464,03-92-0012,03,92,0012,4281.0,1992-01-16,1999-03-18 13:49:10,LEATHERS OIL CO.,604 W WADE,ESTACADA,97023,(503) 661-1244,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : RECIEVED DATE: WAS REPORTED TO VIRGINIA EARLIER...FOUND A LEAK IN DIESEL FILL STEM...SOIL CONTAMINATION CONFIRMED 1/9/92....TANK TEST 12/13/91...REPAIRED 09-JAN-92...TANK IS SET VERY CLOSE TO CREEK... GOAL DATE FOR REPORT SUBMITTED IS 2/21/ 92 ***   Will continue active sparaging, 10-17-2002, rhr.
Remediation completed, submitted Level 1 scoping for ecological risks. Paul Siedel reviewed and found not adequate, indicated potential for risk.  I requested updated sampling.  I received raw data that shows significant decrease.  They need to redo eco-risks, but may also show decrease if they continued monitoring. They failed to consider Cutthroat trout designated habitat, and mill pond is actually a park and library across the street. Additional monitoring or scoping required.  LLC 7/22.2010

Consultant has permanently abandoned one water well on the adjacent property to the east (600 NW 6th Avenue) and welded a watertight cap over the remainign well.  Both wells are up-gradient of the site and Leathers has no plans to use in future. Comment period on proposed closure ended 7-9-12 with no comments received.  Ecological risks to Wade Creek shown to not be signficant.  Contamination in  soil and groundwater does not exceed RBCs for relevant pathway under the occupational worker scenario. Contamination limited to site and southwest cormer of adjacent proeprty to north (also owned by Leathers).  No beneficial use of groundwater in area of impact. Based on zoning, site likely to remain commercial.  Site qualifes for NFA determination with no conditions necessary (JKS 7-9-12).",,,20875.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2012-10-30 08:30:50.813
