3470,26-92-0018,26,92,0018,,1992-01-27,1999-03-18 13:49:10,ACROPOLIS,8325 SE MCLOUGHLIN BLVD,PORTLAND,97202,,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Release reported in January 1992 when ODOT encountered up to 4,400 ppm TPH 418.1 and 2,710 ppm TPH-G along McLoughlin Blvd. adjacent to site.  Three 550-gallon USTs, one 2,000-gallon UST and one 3,000-gallon UST removed from site on Oct. 30, 2000 but contaminated soil placed back into excavations per RP's instruction.  One soil sample collected beneath each UST.  Gasoline detected in all samples (up to 3,060 ppm gasoline, 3.71 ppm benzene, and 59.9 ppm ethylbenzene).  DEQ issued NON in October 2002 because only a 20-day Report with lab data was received.

A Site Investigation in August 2003 found up to 6,700 ppm gasoline in the soil.  Three groundwater monitoring wells were installed in July 2006 as part of an Additional Subsurface Investigation.  Quarterly monitoring was conducted in March, June, and September 2008, finding up to 4,900 ppb gasoline, 2,400 ppb diesel, 45 ppb benzene, and 150 ppb naphthalene.

An Ecological Risk Assessment is needed for Johnson Creek, which borders the site on the west.  The extent of the contamination has also not been fully delineated.  (7/11/13 KPD) Site re-opened on : 6/15/2021 By Gerald Gamolo. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 3/24/2021.",,,25521.0,0.0,GGAMOLO,2021-06-15 13:15:48.430
