ECSI # 3762 ARCO AM-PM - Salem","The Arco AM-PM Salem site is located at 3820 Portland Rd NE, Salem, Oregon, 97301, Marion County Tax Map #073W12CA03800.  The 0.36 acre property is situated on the northeast corner of the intersection of Portland Road and Wayside Terrace. Petroleum products (i.e. gasoline) have been dispensed at the facility since 1969. The original tank systems were replaced in 1988. A subsurface petroleum release was reported in February 1992. liquid phase petroleum (free product) has been observed in four on-site monitoring wells (MW-1, -2, -3, and -4).  A Soil Vapor Extraction (SVE) system pilot test was completed on April 8, 2010, a corrective action plan was approved on September 13, 2010 followed by installtion of a SVE system by January 2011. Since the implementation of the CAP, approximately 81,478 pounds of VOCs or an equivalent mass of 13,000 gallons of gasoline have been removed from this site.  During the most recent treatment the system was cycled to optimize mass removal, with an additional ~129 pounds of VOCs removed since February 2016. Free-Product has been eliminated in all on-site monitoring wells except for MW-2.  During 2018 assessment for soil vapors, all constituents of potential concern were below DEQ RBCs.  The closure plan for this site includes cycled operation of the SVE treatmetn system for up to 3 years (i.e. into 2022) or until measurable free-product in MW-2 is no longer detected. ",19220.0,0.0,JGLASS,2019-03-07 13:48:03.743
