3503,15-88-0016,15,88,0016,,1988-10-17,1999-03-18 13:49:10,UNOCAL BULK PLANT,103 W MCANDREWS,MEDFORD,97501,,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : Found contamination while repairing a water line. *** referred to CU Program - ECD #734.  Back to Tanks program March 2006.,ECSI #734,"A petroleum release was identified in 1988 during utility construction adjacent to the former Unocal Bulk Plant facility. Oversight of the Environmental Cleanup site (ECSI #734) was transferred to DEQ's Tanks Program. Investigation was initiated in 1988, thought bulk plant operations ended in 1991 with full demolition of buildings and removal of underground tanks. Contaminated soil and groundwater from surface and underground spills were evident in assessments completed through 2008. In 2012, test pits were used to evaluate soil near MW-9A for the presence of residual contamination. Contaminated soil (67.5 tons) was excavated from the test pits and disposed at a landfill. Confirmation soil samples showed low levels of petroleum remaining, but below risk-based concentrations for site workers. Groundwater monitoring was completed through 2012, and only MW-9A contained petroleum above risk levels for workers (through direct contact). The City of Medford was provided information on remaining petroleum in groundwater possibly in ROW for Oak Street. A contaminated media management plan and health and safety plan is available for excavations and workers in the future. The site is located in an industrial and commercial area of Medford and is unlikely to be used for any residential use in the future.",2421.0,0.0,CRODDA,2017-01-17 08:54:11.353
