3/29/13:  Antea to do injections.  B Robertston was about to approve the  pilot but retired.  doing remediation not so much for risk but to stop mtbe plume from migrating.  however, more updated bwud and csm need to be completed.  also waiting on 1st 1/4 qm results to extra check peroxide pilot test.  9/2013- injections on schedule. (RAH)


A release of gasoline to the soil and groundwater was discovered in February 1992 during installation of Stage II vapor recovery equipment.  About 300 cubic yards of PCS were removed, and four monitoring wells were installed on-site.  An additional 974 tons of PCS were removed in May-June 2004 when the USTs, dispensers, and piping runs were replaced.

There are currently 14 off-site monitoring wells in addition to the four on-site wells.  The wells were sampled quarterly from 1993 to 2006 and are now sampled semi-annually.  Only two wells are still impacted with gasoline (up to 4,190 ppb), with another four wells impacted by MTBE (up to 141 ppb).  A water supply well is 200 ft SE of the site but is unimpacted.  There appears to be no treatment system; just monitoring.  (7/16/09 KPD)

This issue at the site is MTBE, need an updated beneficial water use survey and TBA analysis requested as well as a review of possible ecological receptors.  LLC 07/19/2010",,,45354.0,0.0,RHOOD,2020-09-11 10:39:04.700
