A gasoline release (spill) occurred at this site in February 1992, and the site finally received an NFA in January 2005.  In June 2006, groundwater samples collected from an observation well in the UST nest found up to 96,100 ppb gasoline.  In February 2007, heavy oil was encountered in soil (5,400 ppm) and groundwater (10,740 ppb) during decommissioning of a 1,000-gallon used oil UST.  The file was reopened in March 2007.  In March 2009, the consultant conducted ""enhanced fluid recovery"" on the contaminated observation well using a vacuum truck, but sampling still found 42,000 ppb gasoline and 3,400 ppb benzene.  As of September 2009, at least two more attempts at EFR were planned.  (10/22/09 KPD)",,,17231.0,0.0,RHOOD,2013-01-08 10:10:01.267
