3598,29-92-0086,29,92,0086,487.0,1992-03-24,1999-03-18 13:49:10,SUNSET SERVICE,403 PACIFIC AVE,TILLAMOOK,97141,(503) 842-4721,False,7.0,MATRIX,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Neil Shaw advanced 10 borings at the service station in March 1992, finding gasoline (up to 1,800 ppm) at the north end of the tank pit.  The PCS was apparently excavated to 13 ft bgs in July 1992 and shipped to the Averill Farm (1805 Warner Rd) one mile north of Tillamook for aeration treatment.  The farm had an SWLA permit for soils from the Erskine Oil Bulk Plant (29-92-0087) but not from Sunset Service.  The estimated 100 cubic yards of PCS was piled 4-5 ft deep with vent tubes and covered with sheet rock (gypsum) as a ""conditioner"".  Treated PCS was to have been buried at Averill Farm but Tillamook County rejected the Land Use Compatibility in April 1994, finding that the farm was within the 100 year floodplain.  Six post-treatment samples collected by Neil Shaw in July 1994 showed no gasoline and only up to 100 ppm diesel.  A total of 340 cubic yards of PCS (from Sunset and Erskine) were shipped to the St. Johns Landfill in September 1994.

In January 1996 Neil Shaw collected two soil samples from a ""new island excavation"" on the west side of the Sunset Service site and two samples from a soil pile on the east side of the site.  All four samples were analyzed for TPH-G; all were ND.

The excavation of PCS at the site in 1992 did not include 710 ppm TPH adjacent to the north dispenser island and 2,000 ppm TPH at a hydraulic lift inside the service station.  Confirmation sampling is needed to determine the current extent of contamination at the site.  (12/31/12 KPD)",CONCURRENT ERSKINE OIL/NEIL SHAW UST CLEANUP AT 4TH & ELM - SEE 29-92-0087,,115763.0,0.0,KDANA,2012-12-31 08:38:25.383
