Pjt Mgr = JLG",,"On March 24, 1992, DEQ received notification of petroleum contamination when obvious petroleum impacts were observed in soil after assessments adjacent to abovegound and underground storage tanks systems at this facility.  Since 1992 several phases of site cleanup work have been completed, which included removal of two underground storage tanks and six aboveground storage tanks, treatment and disposal of an estimated 300 cubic yards of contaminated soil, and operation for two years of a groundwater remediation system.   To evaluate the effectiveness of the remediation system and to assess the risk associated with groundwater beneath the site, a total of 15 monitoring wells were installed.  Although some of these wells were destroyed, abandoned, or replaced in 2003, a group of wells have been identified or installed for compliance monitoring.  Based on the results of cleanup, site investigation, monitoring and assessment, DEQ has determined that given the current and reasonably likely future land use, the remaining contamination has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment.  The closure plan, which includes restrictions on the use of groundwater for any propose and a safety plan for any excavation at depths greater than 3 feet, will allow the remaining contamination to naturally degrade in place.  Please see the site diagrams, photos and other documents below for more information.",16313.0,0.0,JGLASS,2011-03-15 10:41:55.910
