ECSI #1211","The site has operated as a fuel service station since at least the early 1970s.  Four petroleum releases have been documented at the site from two different UST  systems at the facility.  Recovery well OW-1 was installed in March 1992, at which time a product line was severed resulting in the spill of 200 gallons of gasoline and creation of USTC #20-92-4049.  Approximately 90 cubic yards of PCS surrounding the piping was excavated, 70 gallons of product was captured in the recovery well, and over 3,800 gallons of a groundwater and product mix was pumped from the site.",2031.0,0.0,CRODDA,2010-08-12 17:01:13.567
