Pjt Mgr = JLG Site re-opened on : 2/13/2013 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 2/13/2013.",,"The site is located on the north side of the Salmon River Highway (also known as Hwy 18) about 250 feet west of the intersection with N Old Scenic Highway and in Lincoln County, Oregon. The property has been in use since the 1920's as an automotive refueling facility and/or an automotive repair facility.  A petroleum release was reported to DEQ on March 3, 1992, after decommissioning of three UST systems.  Four additional UST systems were discovered during the site investigation and cleanup.  Approximately 900 tons of petroleum contaminated soil (PCS) was removed and the site assessed for human and ecological risks.  Areas of PCS still remain on the site predominantly under the building.  Based on the current a reasonably likely future uses of the site, DEQ, has determined that with property use restrictions and a plan to handle contaminated media in the future, the contamination will no longer pose an unacceptable, or unmanageable risk to human health safety welfare or the environment.",24046.0,0.0,JGLASS,2013-02-14 11:45:46.207
