In May and June 2017 product lines were upgraded at the site.  Compliance sampling in the product trench revealed motor oil range TPH at levels as high as 131 ppm.  The contamination is in an area  known to have been contaminated by a 1992 release (26-92-0126).  The site reportedly never dispensed diesel.  The motor oil range TPH detected is likely due to degradation of the original gasolien release.  The consultant notified DEQ at the time the detections were discovered by telephone. Documentation submitted by Todd Vanek of Antea Group supports the notion that the detctions found ""old"" contamination. No furthr actions are recommended for these low-level detections (JKS 7-3-17).",26-91-0491,,3492.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2017-07-03 16:56:25.593
