3742,03-92-0114,03,92,0114,3868.0,1992-04-27,1999-03-18 13:49:10,SANDY RFPD #72,17460 BRUNS AVENUE,SANDY,97055,(503) 668-8093,False,7.0,MATRIX,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Soil matrix closure, 1992 with outstanding soil treatment issue on Trubel Road property.  30 cubic yards of soil transferred for treatment to 42923 Trubel Road in Sandy.  Treatment via solid waste permit. Non-compliance with treatment conditions. Final sampling June 2007, NDs.",,"A 200-gallon waste oil UST, a 500-gallon diesel UST, and a 1,000-gallon gasoline UST were decommissioned by removal at this location.  Thirty yards of petroleum contaminated soil (PCS) was taken to an undeveloped parcel of land owned by the Sandy Fire Department for offsite aeration.  DEQ issued a solid waste treatment permit to treat the PCS at this property located at 42923 Trubel Road in Sandy, Oregon. On June 17, 1992, DEQ issued a letter to the Sandy Fire Department stating that other than soil aeration requirements, the cleanup appeared to have met applicable DEQ requirements.   In 2007 twelve soil confirmation samples were taken from the treatment area, and no petroleum hydrocarbons were detected.",20601.0,0.0,LKENT,2011-02-11 13:53:56.040
