3825,03-90-0242,03,90,0242,688.0,1990-07-11,1999-03-18 13:49:10,BP SERVICE STATION #11007,14801 SE WEBSTER RD,MILWAUKIE,97267,(503) 654-8888,False,1.0,MATRIX,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Site re-opened on : 12/31/2008 By Kevin Dana. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 11/20/1995.Results of 1993 and 1994 due diligence investigations were note reported to DEQ.  TPH-G detected at boring HB-4 at 5 feet bgs = 1600 mg/kg.  This appears to represent new information and was not known at the time the February 1996 NFA was issued.  Letter dated 2-11-09 requested further delineationof contamination in area of boring HB-4 (March 1994).  Letter dated October 12, 2009 indicated that Delta Consultants was assuming liability for site  remediation from CP (JKS 11-3-09).  Further delineation of shallow contamination completed in June 2010 and it does not appear further delineation is necessary.  Consultant informed that because 1994 detection of gasoline hydrocarbons in soil exceeds matrix levels, conceptual site model including a discussion of applicable exposure pathways  is needed.  Requested materials supporting risk-based closure received in October 2010.  Comment solicitation letter sent on 11-9-10.  Comments received from Clackamas County in letter dated 12-16-10.  In email communication dated 12-21-10,language objectionable to the County was explained to be a typographic error or did not apply in this circumstance.  Draft NFA submitted to Hyrogeologist for review on 1-25-11 (JKS 1-25-11).",,,18419.0,0.0,LKENT,2011-06-14 08:25:11.890
