3831,03-89-0298,03,89,0298,10021.0,1989-12-04,1999-03-18 13:49:10,KIMMY'S MARKET,3141 SE HARRISON ST,MILWAUKIE,97222,(503) 254-3080,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"Four USTs were removed from this site in 1989: two 6,000-gallon gasoline USTs, an 8,000-gallon gasoline UST, and a 300-gallon waste oil UST.  Contaminated soil was excavated, stockpiled on-site, and aerated for a year before being placed back into the excavation.  Contaminated groundwater in the open excavation also volatilized for a year.  Additional confirmation sampling around the waste oil tank was requested by DEQ in 1990 but not conducted.

Limited investigations at the site resumed in 2006.  Sampling in 2006 and 2007 found low levels of oil in the soil and diesel and oil in the shallow groundwater adjacent to the former USTs.  Additional groundwater sampling around the site in February 2009 indicated that the contamination had not spread.  The City of Milwaukie subsequently expressed concerns that residual contamination at the site threatened City Well #4.  However, DEQ concluded that the low levels of residual contamination plus the lack of migration meant that there was no reasonably likely risk.",17099.0,0.0,KDANA,2010-10-26 14:45:41.133
