3835,35-89-0002,35,89,0002,1591.0,1992-03-01,1999-03-18 13:49:10,LONE ELK MARKET,800 WILLOW ST,SPRAY,97874,(503) 468-2443,False,,,,ADMCLO,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : FILE CLOSED DUE TO TRANSFER TO CLEANUP ECSI#1995 SAME SITE AS HUMPHREY MARKET 35-90-0013 *** (9/28/05 KJR) Site was administratively closed on 6/28/05 and reffered to Cleanup (ECSI# 1995) Site re-opened on : 2/19/2009 By Elizabeth Clark. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 6/27/2005.,ECSI # 1995,"(Nov. 2009) This site is an operating gas station site with historic petroleum releases that have caused widespread soil and groundwater contamination including impacts to the City water supply.  Both GW extraction and SVE have been utilized to control and remediate the plume.  In total, the remedial systems have removed the equivalent of about 14,000 gallons of petroleum hydrocarbons (as gasoline) from Site soil and groundwater.

In 2008 and 2009, concentrations of MTBE were observed in downgradient wells at concentrations higher than observed in recent years and it was determined that the treatment systems would need to be modified and re-started to prevent the spread of contamination.  It is anticipated that additional operation of the the systems for a limited period of time will allow the site to be cleaned up to risk based levels.

This work and subsequent implementation is being funded by the American Recovery and Reinvestment Act of 2009 through DEQ’s LUST Corrective Action Cooperative Agreement with U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA). 

The CAP and other site documents are located in the site document section of this database.",40506.0,0.0,KROBERT,2009-11-17 09:50:36.377
