3851,24-92-4096,24,92,4096,9199.0,1992-06-03,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Aumsville Shell,810 MAIN STREET,AUMSVILLE,97325,(503)769-2339,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,50 yd3 of contaminated soil on site 5-1-92 no gw tph4200 72600 ppm (RS) 3-19-93 jlg,,"On June 3, 1992, DEQ received notice that gasoline had leaked from underground storage tanks (USTs).  The contamination extended beyond the property lines, onto the neighboring properties, and across Main Street.  Based on the following information from the investigation, cleanup and risk evaluation completed for the Site, the remaining soil and groundwater contamination does not pose a threat to human health or the environment: 

•    The primary sources of contamination including three (3) UST systems and approximately 315 tons of PCS have been removed from the Site.  There are no operating USTs remaining.  Residual contamination is expected to attenuate over time.
•    Water supply to the Site and adjacent properties is serviced by the City of Aumsville.  There are no private or domestic wells located within the LOF or on properties adjacent to the Site.  In addition, utility setback requires preclude installation of water wells on-site and on the adjacent, down-gradient, impacted properties, 
•    The Site is zoned for Commercial use.  This use is expected to remain the same for the foreseeable future. 
•    Properties within the LOF that are zoned or currently used for residential purposes do not have remaining contamination in excess of DEQ Generic Risk-Based Concentrations (GRBCs) for Residential use. 
•    The extent of soil and groundwater contamination on and where applicable beyond the Site has been defined.  Remaining contamination exists beneath the Site and under the Main Street and 8th Street right-of-ways. Contamination remaining in soil and groundwater is below the applicable DEQ GRBCs for the current and reasonably likely future uses of the properties.

As such, the Site meets the general requirements for a conditional risk-based closure.",17769.0,0.0,JGLASS,2016-03-25 13:32:17.090
