3871,18-92-0037,18,92,0037,345.0,1992-06-10,1999-03-18 13:49:10,YONNA VALLEY COUNTRY STORE,24985 HIGHWAY 140 E,BONANZA,97623,,False,,,3.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : Discovered date of purchase.  Former owner never registered USTs; illegally decommissioned (~1991 fall); never cleaned up; well abandoned due to contamination. Will recommend enforcement; Mr. Neuroth is seeking legal advice. ***
11/28/06: This site is being administratively closed because a suspected release was reported to DEQ but it was never confirmed. There is no documentation of a release - just a phone call from a Mr. Tom Neuroth who claimed that the former owners of this site never registered the underground storage tanks (USTs), illegally decommissioned the USTs in 1991, never cleaned up the release, and abandoned a well due to contamination.
The former owner, Joseph Sergi, Jr., has documented in writing that a release did not occur. He stated that:
•    The tanks were removed in 1986 by himself and his father.
•    There was no sign of discolored soil, odor, or contamination of any kind.
•    Mr. Neuroth contracted to purchase the property in 1991, but only made a few payments before filing for bankruptcy.
There is no record in Oregon Water Resource Department's database of a well abandonment or new well drilled at this location.  There is an onsite well registered with the Health Division - so the claim that it was contaminated and abandoned appears unfounded.
I have spoken with Mrs. Sergi and their story appears credible, therefore I recommended this site be administratively closed. Marcy Kirk",,,18181.0,0.0,GDECK,2014-02-03 15:02:09.677
