3895,32-92-0230,32,92,0230,3459.0,1992-06-19,1999-03-18 13:49:10,STEVE'S AUTO REPAIR & SERVICE,207 S RIVER STREET,ENTERPRISE,97828,(541)426-4417,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,True,False,False,False,,ECSI 2345,"[June 2010] An estimated 5,400 gallons of unleaded gasoline was released through a broken pressurized line into the shallow soils and groundwater in May 1992 according to the records in the DEQ file. Initial response activities included the installation of two recovery wells. Approximately 400 gallons were recovered from the wells. 

Records indicate that three underground storage tanks (USTs) were removed from the site in May 1995. Post-removal sampling found only a small amount of petroleum contaminated soil (PCS) within the UST cavity.

A site investigation was performed in December 2009. The investigation consisted of the installation of six gw monitoring wells, 3 on-site and 3 off-site. A second gw monitoring event was also performed in March 2010.  Based on the results of this investigation the site has been recommended for a NFA determination following a 30 day public comment period that ends on May 31, 2010.

No comments were recieved and the NFA determination was issued on June 8, 2010.

Select site documents and reports are included in the site document section of this database.",20302.0,0.0,ECLARK,2010-07-16 08:27:35.377
