No report g&d release, needs CAP, last heard from 7-13-92..RS",ECSI # 1960,"This site is a former bulk pertroleum facility that operated from ~1926 to 2006, occupying approxmately 1.37 acres on the corner of McDaniel Lane and Lafayette Avenue in McMinnville, OR. The facility included 7 ASTs, a card-lock dispenser island, a storage building, loading racks, and railway remote fills. On July 13, 1992, DEQ received a report of gasoline, diesel and lubricating oil contamination in soil and groundwater.  The contamination extended beyond the property lines onto adjacent properties and into the McDaniel Lane and beyound Lafayette Avenue right-of-ways.  The card-lock dispeners were decommissioned in 2006, along with removal of the Bulk Plant's loading rack and buildings.  In 2014 DEQ approved a Corrective Action Plan for this site. Treatment continues with improvements to process and operating schedules that increase effectiveness and reduce remedial expenses. Investigations to detetermine the magnitude and extent of contamination east (across Laffayette Avenue) of the Barker site have recently been completed.  Redevelopment of the property south (across McDaniel Lane) is currently being considered, which may include a change to the receptor designation (i.e. from Commercial to Urban-Residential).  Although on-site reuse has been discussed, no specifc plan has been proposed.",29572.0,0.0,JGLASS,2019-05-15 10:55:15.523
