gasoline & diesel release",See Also: 24-92-4109 and ECSI 6132,"(MOTT 01/19/18) In 1992, three USTs (one 500-gallon gasoline, one 1,000-gallon gasoline, and one 5,000-gallon diesel) were removed from the site.  Impacted soil was removed and confirmation soil sampling was conducted. Confirmation soil samples indicated concentrations below the applicable RBCs for the site.  Groundwater samples were collected near the former UST areas in 2016/2017 and were ND for TPH, VOCs, and PAHs. A Phase I ESA completed in June 2016, indicated evidence of an additional UST near the southeast corner of the property and a UST vent located along the southern property boundary. A GPR survey confirmed a UST was present in the southeast portion of property. The UST was determined to be a 675-gallon HOT and was decommissioned in place by filling with concrete slurry in August 2016. Soil samples were collected at the east and west end from 6 feet bgs and analyzed for NWTPHDx. The results were ND for both samples. The UST vent pipe observed along the southern portion of the property was determined to be a remnant from an old UST. A GPR survey confirmed the UST was no longer present and must have been previously removed (there is no record of this tank in UST database). Soil samples were collected from the north and south ends at 8 feet bgs and were ND for TPH-G, D, and O. (MOTT 03/20/18) LUST #24-92-4130 was issued a NFA on March 20, 2018. See ECSI 6132 for non-UST related issues at the site.",18015.0,0.0,MOTT,2018-03-20 09:37:41.740
