3972,18-92-0045,18,92,0045,8261.0,1992-08-14,1999-03-18 13:49:10,"COLVIN OIL CO., KLAMATH FALLS #1",3434 S 6TH ST,KLAMATH FALLS,97601,(503)883-8026,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,ECSI 4872 Metler Bros. TL 900 (Colvin Oil),"The former Metlar Brothers mill site was a remanufacturing facility from 1923 to the early 1960s that bought lumber from local saw mills in order to produce doors, window frames and other wood component parts.  The remanufacturing process included wood-treating. The former mill property was been divided into two tax lots.  The western half, tax lot 900 (ECSI 4872), is currently owned by the Colvin Oil Company and has had a petroleum service station, in various configurations, on the property since 1970.  The eastern half, tax lot 800 (ECSI 4457), is currently owned by the Pacific Crest Credit Union with a drive through automated teller machine (ATM).  A release of pentachlorophenol (PCP) has been documented at the tax lot 800 site. 

Multiple site investigations has been performed at the Colvin Oil site related to the site's history as a lumber mill and gas station. The primary contaminants found were petroleum related.  A No Further Action determination was issued on 12/1/09.  DEQ's NFA Decision Document dated 10/15/09 and the NFA dated 12/1/09 are located in the site document section of this database.",23585.0,0.0,KROBERT,2009-12-01 13:48:50.400
