4548,16-91-0101,16,91,0101,4262.0,1991-12-17,1999-03-18 13:49:10,LEATHERS OIL CO.,158 5TH ST,MADRAS,97741,(503) 661-1244,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : LEATHERS REPORTED TO VIRGINIA ESMOND ON 12-13-91  MET REPORTING REQUIREMENT. FAILED PRODUCT LINE TIGHTNESS TEST AT 1 GAL/HR.  (PRESSURIZED SYSTEM); INVENTORY RECORD SUPPORT LOSS.  WILL HELIUM TEST WEEK OF  12-17-91  CLEANUP WILL START AFTER HELIUM TEST HELIUM TEST WILL BE USED TO GUIDE EXCAVATION/REPAIR EFFORT.  REVERSED DECISION TO ALLOW OPERATIONS TO CONTINUE (I.E. WILL ASK LEATHERS TO DISCONTINUE USE OF U.L. UST/LINE *** high btex in groundwater. groundwater sparging and vapor extraction systems active. 800 tons contaminated soil to crook county landfill in 1999.,,"Leather oil Company Station No.34 reported a release of gasoline in 1991. Thirteen monitoring wells were installed onsite and offsite, with groundwater monitoring occurring from 1994 through 2011. A remediation system consisting of groundwater sparging and soil vapor extraction was operated until 2004. Approximately 806 tons of gasoline petroleum contaminated soil was excavated and disposed at a landfill.

