4594,26-93-0014,26,93,0014,3901.0,1993-01-22,1999-03-18 13:49:10,BARBUR TEXACO,8604 SW BARBUR,PORTLAND,97219,(503) 245-5567,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"On soil gas quarterly monitoring, 3 events completed to date (9/2008), results look better since 1st qm.  Next event Late Oct. 2008.  

Vapor mitigation in operation next to adjacent apartment buildings (set about 1 foot bgs or less), so does not affect results on s-g samples on that property-based on discussion with previous project manager that the mitigation system is very questionable.

David Coles of Coles Environmental submitted a summary report for historic soil vapor sampling at the site.  Soil-gas detections were compared to OSWER screening levels and RBC values for indoor air using attentuation factors of 0.01 and 0.005.  All were below applicable RBC standards.  OK'd suspension of vapor sampling in August 2009.  Coles will use PID to screen vapor from sampling points on semiannual basis (JKS 08-21-09).  Review of historic groundwater analytical data received from Coles Environmental.  In the context of the conceptual site model already submitted, contaminants in groundwater exceeded RBC standards for vapor intrusion and contact by workers in excavation.  However, soil-gas  sampling completed previously has demonstrated that risks of vapor intrusion are not unacceptable.  Groundwater ingestion exposure pathway already shown to be incomplete.  Coles proposed suspension of GW monitoring (already suspended), and one additional year of PID monitoring of vapor sampling points.  Also proposed was deed restriction on site and property to south to address risks to excavation workers (Contaminated Media Management Plan).  Terms of RAO from August 2001 met except for CAP submittal.  Letter responding to August 2010 DEQ letter received from Coles on 4-14-11.  Remaining issues addressed sufficiently.  Comment solicitation letter sent to adjacent stakeholders 4-13-11 (JKS 4-20-11).  On May 19, 2010, DEQ received request for 8-week extension of comment period from City of Portland BES so they can do a detailed evaluation of utility lines, storm water, soil, groundwater, and surface water in the area of the site (JKS 5-18-11).  Two week extension granted for purposes of discussing future City plans in ROW (JKS 5-23-11).  June 2011 investigation results reported in September 2011.  BES investigation confirmed the northern and eastern portion of undeveloped property west of SW Barbur Court has groundwater impacted by gasolinea and constituents above direct contact RBC in excavations.  Barbur Station LLC, Plaza 5 LLC and Mr. Don Peters have signed and executed E&ES agreements.  Impacted properites have executed liability/indemnity agreements. .Draft NFA in preparation  Site ready for closure (JKS 2-27-12).",,,20639.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2012-02-28 07:34:36.430
