5022,26-93-0129,26,93,0129,,1993-07-26,1999-03-18 13:49:10,GABRIEL COMMERCIAL PROPERTY,203 NE GRAND AVE,PORTLAND,97232,,False,1.0,MATRIX,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,UST Facility ID #12628 (adjacent property).,"The original commercial building at the site was constructed in 1929, and the Gabriel family purchased the site in 1943.  An environmental investigation in 1993 discovered a 500-gallon heating oil tank with contaminated soils near the building, and gasoline-contaminated soils in the southeast corner of the block.  UST Environmental Services reported removing about 120 tons of  petroleum-contaminated soils, and DEQ issued a No Further Action letter in December 1993.  The NFA determination was rescinded in June 1994 after Bob Cyphers, the owner of UST Environmental, was determined to have falsified sampling and disposal data on his projects.

A new investigation in December 2017 found gasoline-contaminated soils in the southeast corner of the block.  In July-August 2019, 200 tons of gasoline-contaminated soils were removed from the southeast corner of the block, and 19 tons of oil-impacted soils were removed from beneath a hydraulic hoist inside the building.  Additional gasoline-contaminated soils extended beneath Grand Avenue and Davis Street and could not be removed.  In 2020, construction began on the Grand Avenue Apartments, a 9-story apartment building with ground-floor commercial and retail spaces and one level of sub-grade parking.  The residual contamination does not pose an unacceptable risk to either the residents or occupants of the apartments, or to excavation workers in the streets.",29410.0,0.0,KDANA,2021-03-31 09:33:22.033
