5138,15-93-0067,15,93,0067,1854.0,1993-08-09,1999-03-18 13:49:10,GOLD HILL CITY SHOP,CORNER OF 5TH ST & 5TH AVE,GOLD HILL,97525,(503)855-1525,False,,,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,19214.0,0.0,GDECK,2011-04-22 13:55:46.687
5139,10-93-0068,10,93,0068,11182.0,1993-08-10,1999-03-18 13:49:10,MYRTLE DAIRY,336 NW OAK ST,MYRTLE CREEK,97457,(503)440-4300,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"The current buildings onsite were built in the 1950s and a 1,000 gallon gasoline underground storage tank was believed to have been installed at that time. The tank was out of service by the mid-1980s. The exact cause of the contamination is unknown. At the time of decommissioning, during the UST removal, about 45 cubic yards of soil was excavated and aerated onsite however the final disposition of this soil is unknown. A soil vapor extraction system was operated from March 1994 until December 1996 and a groundwater extraction system was operated from March 1994 until June 2008. Soil, groundwater, and soil gas are impacted with gasoline both onsite and offsite to the southeast and south. Remaining soil contamination appears to be present from about 9 to 12 feet below the ground surface. Groundwater impacts appear to be in a limited zone at about 13 feet below ground. Current land use of an impacted property is residential. Other properties in the area, including the site are used commercially and it is assumed that the property will remain in commercial use. A beneficial water use determination found no use of groundwater within 500 feet of the site. The site and all surrounding properties are expected to remain connected to municipal water. An opportunity to comment on the proposed closure was given to all neighboring properties and the City of Myrtle Creek. No comments were received.",16161.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2018-12-05 08:17:05.483
