5272,24-93-4196,24,93,4196,11311.0,1993-11-07,1999-03-18 13:49:10,A B & I Property,6989 3RD ST SE,TURNER,97392,(503) 632-3467,False,1.0,,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,Original NFA issued 11/6/1995 by Virginia Esmond.  Site reopened 12/6/2007 by Jim Glass based on new information. Site re-opened on : 12/6/2007 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 11/6/1995.,,"American Brass and Iron operated a recycling business at the location from about 1976 to 1991.  Action Wood Products, which remanufactures wood products, currently operates at the site.      

The property owner removed a 1000-gallon underground storage tank in 1993, and reported petroleum contamination to DEQ.   Contamination was found in the former tank pit soil.   The property owner removed an estimated 400 tons of petroleum-contaminated soil.  The contaminated soil was treated on site with oversight from DEQ, and reused at the property when it met safe levels. 

A 2007 environmental site assessment conducted in preparation for sale of the property documented petroleum contamination in shallow groundwater beneath the site.  The property owner conducted an investigation to determine the extent of the groundwater contamination in 2008.   

    As a condition of the no further action determination, DEQ is requiring that restrictions be placed on future groundwater use and use of the property for residential purposes.  The current and reasonably likely future land use for this site is manufacturing, warehousing, and processing.  With conditional approval, the zoning permits a manufactured dwelling for the property owner or a caretaker.  There are also properties within one quarter mile of the site that are zoned for both residential and commercial. 

Based on the results of cleanup, site investigation, and assessment, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land use, the remaining contamination has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment.",10499.0,0.0,JGLASS,2009-06-26 11:46:49.120
