5294,10-93-0099,10,93,0099,9392.0,1993-10-12,1999-03-18 13:49:10,SUTHERLIN AIRPORT,AIRPORT,SUTHERLIN,97479,(541) 459-2856,False,7.0,MATRIX,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : M293   MATERIAL RELEASED: AIRCRAFT FUEL.  10/12/93 DECOM IN DEC 1990.   WATER IN PIT WAS TESTED AND CITY OF SUTHERLIN DID NOT DO ANY CLEANUP.  PURCHASED BY DOUGLAS COUNTY WHO IS NOW SAMPLING AND WILL CLEANUP.  JMB *** Tanks decommissioned by City of Sutherlin in 1990.  Douglas County purchased site and conducted investigation.  No benzene detected in four GW samples at former pit.,,,39979.0,0.0,GDECK,2011-05-12 14:50:09.403
5295,26-93-0187,26,93,0187,966.0,1993-10-27,1999-03-18 13:49:10,CHEVRON PRODUCTS #9-6587,8517 SW TERWILLIGER BLVD,PORTLAND,97219,(503) 245-4274,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : DISCOVERED DURING OVERSPILL PROTECTION INSTALLATION.  SOME STAINED SOIL NEAR PUMP ISLAND TO BE REMOVED ALSO. *** SIte assessment report shows need for further delineation and remediation. 

Installed ten groundwater monitoring wells. Initially offsite impacts exceeded vapor intrusion pathway for residential receptors, in residential neighborhood.  Conducted pilot test for dual phase, but did not meet goals so system not installed. However, it appears the concentrations are lowering and may be candiate for closure if owner agrees to deed restriction or conditional NFA. LLC 7/20/2010

Work plan for soil-gas investigation consisting of four soil-gas points submitted to DEQ. Work plan approved.  Notified by consultant on 11-17-11 that the owner did not want soil-gas ponits installed on sidewalk adjacent to building.  Consultant proposed alternate location adjacent to sidwalk but closer to the dispensers.  Feige & Associates report dated 7-18-11 documenting confirmation soil sampling in area of dispensers.  Sample near southeast dispenser exhibited gasoline and ethylbenzene above occupational worker RBCs for soil vapor intrusion pathway.  Laboratory notes indicate data is likely biased low. 

To address potential risks from soil contamination as revealed in historical investigations, soil gas samples were collected from the site in March 2012 (SVP-1, SVP-3 and SVP-4) and October 2012 (SVP-2).  No detections exceeding residential soil-gas RBCs so pathway appears to not pose significant risk. SAIC proposed to complete a CMMP to address risks from benzene and naphthalene detected in groundwater in the vicinity of MW-9 at concentrations above construction/exavation worker RBCs for the groundwater in excavation pathway.

In May 2013, SAIC submitted a CMMP which included figures showing the extent  of soil and groundwater contamination.  In October 2013, DEQ provided comments on the CMMP.  In December 2013, DEQ mailed notifications concerning a proposed closure of  this release to the City of Portland and nearby property owners.  Beyond the City of Portland BES, comments were not received during the comment period.  DEQ received a revised CMMP in March 2014.  The CMMP was provided as a courtesy to the City of Portland BES. 

Investigations showed that contamination is largely restricted to the northwestern portion of the site and adjacent rights-of-way.  Low levels of gasoline and VOCs in groundwater may be present in the extreme NE corner of the residential property at 706 SW Taylors Road, but not a levels posing unacceptable health risks under residential use scenario.  Groundwater contamination in nearby rights-of-way does not exdeed construction/excavation worker RBCs.  Site qualifies for closure under RBDM regulations (JKS 3-5-14).",,"To address potential risks from soil contamination as revealed in historical investigations, soil gas samples were collected from the site in March 2012 (SVP-1, SVP-3 and SVP-4) and October 2012 (SVP-2).  No detections exceeding residential soil-gas RBCs so pathway appears to not pose significant risk. SAIC proposed to complete a CMMP to address risks from benzene and naphthalene detected in groundwater in the vicinity of MW-9 at concentrations above construction/exavation worker RBCs for the groundwater in excavation pathway.

In May 2013, SAIC submitted a CMMP which included figures showing the extent  of soil and groundwater contamination.  In October 2013, DEQ provided comments on the CMMP.  In December 2013, DEQ mailed notifications concerning a proposed closure of  this release to the City of Portland and nearby property owners.  Beyond the City of Portland BES, comments were not received during the comment period.  DEQ received a revised CMMP in March 2014.  The CMMP was provided as a courtesy to the City of Portland BES. 

Investigations showed that contamination is largely restricted to the northwestern portion of the site and adjacent rights-of-way.  Low levels of gasoline and VOCs in groundwater may be present in the extreme NE corner of the residential property at 706 SW Taylors Road, but not a levels posing unacceptable health risks under residential use scenario.  Groundwater contamination in nearby rights-of-way does not exdeed construction/excavation worker RBCs.  Site qualifies for closure under RBDM regulations (JKS 3-5-14).",2109.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2014-03-05 15:25:41.660
