Buy 2 010 Florence, LUST # 20-20-0197","Groundwater and soil contamination have been found beneath the site due to past and current operations as a bulk petroleum storage facility and later as a cardlock. The bulk petroleum facility operated from about 1950-1990 on Tax Lots 5901, 5902 and 5903.  The bulk facility was demolished after 1990.  The first petroleum release was reported during demolition activities (LUST 20-90-4228) and about 3600 tons of PCS was removed. The south side of the site (Tax Lot 5900) was developed into a cardlock facility in 1991.  A petroleum release from a leaking valve was reported from the cardlock facility in 1993 (20-93-4199).  The valve was replaced and groundwater and soil vapor remediation was conducted between February and May 1994.  Intermittent groundwater monitoring has been completed at the site from 1991 through 2018.  Data shows that concentrations of petroleum contamination in the groundwater have significantly decreased over time.  DEQ has reviewed all of the site data to date and has determined that the remaining contamination in soil and groundwater no longer poses a risk as long as the following conditions are met: 1) property remains commercial, 2) DEQ be notified of any new building construction which could require some type of vapor mitigation controls, 3) no groundwater be used on the property, and 4) a contaminated media management plan be developed. These requirements have implemented through a deed restriction that was recorded on the property with the Lane County Clerk on July 30, 2020.  DEQ has proposed and plans to issue a No Further Action for the site once all administrative closure activities are complete.",14599.0,0.0,GDECK,2020-12-02 15:39:31.663
