5558,10-94-0015,10,94,0015,9276.0,1994-02-25,1999-03-18 13:49:10,ALLEN & GIBBONS LOGGING INC.,740 STANTON PARK RD ,CANYONVILLE,97417,(503) 839-4294,False,,,4.0,NFA,True,False,,,False,,,,,,,,17697.0,,MBELSKY,1997-04-17 10:15:12.000
5559,20-94-4019,20,94,4019,1250.0,1994-03-07,1999-03-18 13:49:10,J & R Service Center,525 W HARLOW RD,SPRINGFIELD,97477,(503)726-5158,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Mr. Ronald E. Coil and/or Ms. Nicki Gustin, 159 E. 15th St., Eugene, OR i
97401, have now purchased the property and have accepted the i
responsibility of the cleanup.  They have submitted a SWLA application i
for PCS remediation and have already mov",,"The site was an auto repair and fuel service station since 1968. A petroleum release was identified through a site assessment in March 1994. Five underground storage tanks were removed in 1994. Decommissioning records indicates two 4,000-gallon, one 6,000-gallon, and one 8,000-gallon gasoline tanks were in a single nest north of the former service station building. One 550-gallon waste oil tank was situated in a separate area east of the station. A soil sample was collected from the end of each gasoline tank and analyzed for petroleum hydrocarbons. Soil samples were collected as part of a site assessment in 1994. Borings were installed at the gasoline and waste oil tanks. Groundwater was at 8 feet bgs. Soil adjacent to the pump islands and tank nest had gasoline at 1,450 ppm and diesel at 276 ppm. Constituents were measured: toluene = 49 ppm, ethylbenzene = 35 ppm, xylenes = 190 ppm. Remaining soil samples were low or non-detect. Gasoline was present in soil (1994) at 2,100 ppm. Five push probe borings (B-1 to B-5) were installed in 2006 at the former dispenser islands and tank nest. Soil samples were collected from above the soil-groundwater interface (3 to 4 feet bgs) and 7 feet bgs. Analysis found no petroleum contaminants. Groundwater was treated through air sparging after tank removal and soil excavation activities. Since 2006, MW-2 was been tested annually to determine if concentrations would decrease below risk levels for direct contact by excavation workers. In the April 2013 sampling event, water from MW-2 contained 1,2,4-trimethylbenzene at 1,820 ppb and gasoline at 27,500 ppb, both above the referenced RBC for Groundwater in an  Excavation. DEQ agreed to close the site with conditions, including a health and safety plan. A deed restriction was recorded for the property in 2006.",18780.0,0.0,GDECK,2014-11-20 11:42:42.553
