5574,34-94-0007,34,94,0007,9918.0,1994-01-13,1999-03-18 13:49:10,CORNELIUS FAST SERV INC,990 N ADAIR ST,CORNELIUS,97113,(503) 359-4212,False,1.0,RBCA,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"On-going quarterly GW monitoring.  The latest report from 4 consecutive quarters of monitoring indicates gasoline and constituents are below RBCs.  Has proposed to discontinue GW monitoring. Suspension of groundwater monitoring approved in March 2009.  Contacted by owner (Bob Barman), who expressed concerns that BP/Unocal was being up front about impacts to property.  Told him I was waiting for results of risk-based evaluation.  Conceptual Site Model report received in November 2009.  Based on review of CSM, additional information related to BWUD should be collected (i.e. adjacent sections within 0.25 mile radius should be searched).  Also, some level of restriction on use of water well WW-East for potable purposes is necessary.  Lastly, owing to zoning, some remedy must be proposed for soil contamination above residential RBC standards for vapor intrusion.  Comment letter should go out early in week of December 14, 2009.  Consultant forwarded email on February 11, 2010 asking for copy of letter requesting additional dellineation; I informed consultatnt that letter of December 11, 2009 did not ask for additional delineation, merely better documentation of CSM findings.  No reply to letter yet (JKS 4-30-10).  Spoke with Justin Dauphinais of Stantec.  They are working on a work plan to address issues in response letter of 11 December 2009.  I suggested a meeting to discuss remaining issues would be useful. (JKS 6-10-10).Meeting with consultant held in July 2010. Went over letter of 11 December 2009 and explained DEQ concerns.  On August 11, 2010, Stantec reported that owner (Bob Barman) has rejected the notion of a use restriction on the site well (JKS 8-11-10).  Spoke with consultant on 5-24-11.  Draft of letter responding to December 9, 2009 DEQ letter has been prepared and submitted to Conoc Phillips for review.  Project being tranferred to SAIC but Stantec will see the submittal of the response letter through.  Received written reply to December 2009 letter in July 2011.  DEQ comment letter of 8-8-11 identified need for soil-gas investigation work plan (JKS 9-15-11).  Following a September 2011 conversation with new consultant (SAIC), additional information has not been received.  Risks from groundwater containing constituents at levels above possible futurre residential scenario must be addressed, as well as the question about possible use of the car wash well for potable purposes.  Inquiry sent 2-27-12 (JKS 2-27-12).  Work plan to assess soil-gas conditions in area of historic soil samples containing gasoline and consituents above urban residential RBCs for vapor intrusion received 3-30-12.  DEQ commentd on SAIC workplan in letter dated 4-19-12.  No subsequent report received (JKS 1-23-13).",,,26318.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2014-01-28 15:39:46.780
