5854,03-94-0107,03,94,0107,7282.0,1994-06-03,1999-03-18 13:49:10,STAFFORD OIL - CHEVRON,204 E MAIN ST,MOLALLA,97038,(503) 829-5441,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Petroleum-contaminated soil was encountered at the site in June 1994 during a pipeline replacement.  About 120 cubic yards of PCS were excavated and shipped off-site for aeration treatment.  Four monitoring wells were installed at the site in July 1994, and free product gasoline was encountered.  Four off-site wells were added in February 1997.  Texaco (and later Chevron) assumed responsibility for the cleanup beginning in 1999.  Two additional monitoring wells were installed in February 2000, and free product was encountered beneath Engle Street on the west side of the site in November 2000.  Ten monitoring wells (MW-11 thru MW-20) and a piezometer were added to the area between May 2002 and February 2003.  DEQ approved a Corrective Action Plan (CAP) for a dual-phase extraction (DPE) system in December 2003.  Three final off-site monitoring wells (MW-21 thru MW-23) and two soil vapor monitoring wells were added in February 2004.  The DPE system was constructed in the fall of 2004 and began operating in November 2004.  The DPE operated at the site until August 2009, recovering an estimated 5,395 lbs. of gasoline via the soil vapor extraction system and 37.76 lbs. of gasoline via the groundwater extraction system.  Four quarters of compliance monitoring (Sept. 2009 thru June 2010) subsequently demonstrated that residual contaminant concentrations were below the Compliance Criteria established in the CAP.",LUST #03-88-0126,,22921.0,0.0,LKENT,2012-01-09 07:26:44.497
