Received the SWLA application",Farmer's Oil Company,"This site was used to store up to 65,000 gallons of petroleum products between January 1973 and August July 8, 1994, when the USTs were permanently decommissioned by removal. Gasoline and diesel contamination in soil was observed and DEQ file #24-94-4189 was assigned. The investigation and cleanup was then combined with the Wilco site to the south #24-87-4010. After a thorough assessment and risk evaluation of the two sites was completed a decision was made to use engineered and institutional clontrols to address remaining exposure concerns.  Based on the results of the completed cleanup actions, monitoring, on and off-site investigations, and risk-assessment of the remain areas of contaminated soil and groundwater, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land uses, the remaining contamination has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment.",122455.0,0.0,GDECK,2019-07-15 17:37:53.120
