Site re-opened on : 2/2/2021 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 3/27/2003.",,"In January 1995, a site investigation was performed and soil samples were collected during the investigation. Samples were analyzed using the HCID and TPH-G methods. Sample 1-N-6, collected six feet (ft) below ground surface (bgs), measured TPH-G at 319 milligrams per kilograms (mg/kg) and sample 2-1-8.5A, collected 8.5 ft bgs, measured TPH-G at 1398 mg/kg. In August 1997, Abiqua Engineering, Inc. (AEI) and Bill Goff Construction removed three underground storage tanks (2 – 272 gallons; 1 – 522 gallons). A pocket of contaminated soil under the building foundation was left in place. Five soil samples were collected during decommissioning. The sample nearest to the foundation, P707464-01, detected TPH-G at 143 mg/kg, five ft bgs. During the summer months of 2008, the Stone Front Store building was destroyed. In September 2008, EnviroLogic Resources performed a soil boring investigation. Three borings were placed in the northern portion of the property. TPH-G was not detected in any of the samples. In April 2021, a second soil boring investigation was conducted with five borings collected within the historic excavation area. TPH-G was not detected in any of the samples.",29158.0,0.0,ALEIDEL,2021-07-02 17:13:36.490
