6349,21-95-4010,21,95,4010,4143.0,1995-01-24,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Lincoln County Road Dept.,225 W OLIVE ST,NEWPORT,97365,(503) 265-5747,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Pjt Mgr = JLG,,"On January 24, 1995, DEQ received notice that gasoline and diesel had leaked from underground storage tanks located on this property. The contamination did extend to the property line and may have historically impacted the property to the east. During the course of this site cleanup, two underground storage tanks were removed along with approximately 73 cubic yards of petroleum contaminated soil. A map of the area is attached to this web site showing the locations of the former underground storage tanks and remaining soil and grondwater contamination.",65278.0,0.0,JGLASS,2014-09-25 13:17:52.400
6350,24-95-4011,24,95,4011,,1995-01-25,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Ed Parks Residence,1314 MARILYN STREET SE,SALEM,97302,(503) 378-1825,False,7.0,MATRIX,4.0,NFA,False,True,,,False,,,,,240-GAL HOT DECOM BY FILLING IN-PLACE WITH PEA GRAVEL.  NO PCS MANAGED.  NO GW ENCOUNTERED. 190-GAL OILY WATER & 8-GAL SLUDGE TAKE TO ASPEN ENVIRONMENTAL.  2 CONFIRMATORY SOIL SAMPLES TESTED 28 & 74 PPM NWTHH-DX AS TESTED BY WY'EAST.,,,26703.0,,GDECK,2000-05-24 14:15:45.000
6351,21-95-4012,21,95,4012,11481.0,1995-01-26,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Otis 76 Service Center,1264 SALMON RIVER HWY 18 PO BOX 95,OTIS,97368,(541) 996-4844,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Complaint investigation revealed heavy sheen and gasoline odor in upgradient septict tank excavation 8/99,21-21-0338 OTIS MARKET LLC,"The site is located on the south side of the Salmon River Highway (also known as Hwy 18) about 250 feet west of the intersection with N. Old Scenic Highway in Lincoln County, Oregon. The property has been in use since the 1940's as an automotive refueling facility and/or an automotive repair facility. On January 26, 1995, DEQ received notice that gasoline petroleum had leaked from underground storage tanks and more recently polychlorinated biphenyl (PCB) contamination was discovered.  Two additional UST systems were discovered/decommissioned during the site investigation and cleanup.  A total of approximately 212 cubic yards of petroleum and low-level PCB contaminated soil (PCS) was removed and the site assessed for human and ecological risks.  Areas of PCS still remain on the site and groundwater has been impacted.   Based on the current a reasonably likely future uses of the site, DEQ, has determined that with the property use restrictions and a plan to handle contaminated media in the future, the contamination will no longer pose an unacceptable, or unmanageable risk to human health safety welfare or the environment.",24315.0,0.0,GDECK,2021-04-22 16:33:29.640
6352,21-95-4013,21,95,4013,5709.0,1995-01-27,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Lincoln Cnty Road Dept 3,827 NE YAQUINA HEIGHTS DR (3RD STREET),NEWPORT,97365,(503) 265-5747,False,7.0,MATRIX,4.0,NFA,True,False,,,False,,,,,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : SOIL MATRIX CLOSURE *** Prj Mgr=KWF,,,2363.0,,GDECK,2003-10-23 10:18:48.000
6353,21-95-4014,21,95,4014,3923.0,1995-01-27,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Lincoln Cnty Road Dept II,980 NE MILL ST,WALDPORT,97394,(503) 265-5747,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Prj Mgr=JLG,,"On January 27, 1995, DEQ received notice that gasoline and diesel had leaked from underground storage tanks located on this property. The contamination did extend beyond the property lines into the East Ruble Street and N. Mill Street right-of-ways.  Investigation and cleanup activities began upon the removal of the first UST system. The site formerly operated as a Lincoln County vehicle fueling facility that dispensed petroleum products (i.e. gasoline) since 1954 from one 2000-gallon UST system located on the southeastern portion of the property.  During the course of this site cleanup, two underground storage tanks were removed along with approximately 73 cubic yards of petroleum contaminated soil.  Several groundwater monitoring wells were installed and soil vapor assessment was completed next to the neighboring residence.  Based the results of the monitoring and specific assessments, the site appears to no longer pose a threat to human health and the environment given the current and reasonably likely future use.  The property is as of this writing vacant, the DEQ-NFA issued, and is to be marketed for sale.",20644.0,0.0,GDECK,2013-08-21 13:09:33.893
