Referred back to LUST program for NFA closure of 12,000-gal Bunker fuel tank cleanup 7/30/2012.",referred to cert program 6/22/00.,"In late March and early April 1995, one 12,000-gallon bunker fuel Underground Storage Tank was decommissioned by removal at this site. Approximately 1,220 tons (or 812 yd3) of petroleum contaminated soil were excavated and transported to an authorized disposal facility in McMinnville, Oregon.  In areas accessible to remedial excavation, the final concentrations of total petroleum hydrocarbons in the soil were within DEQ’s Level II Soil Matrix Cleanup Standards.  Groundwater was encountered in the excavation (1995) and in two of the five assessment probes in 2012.  The water sample collected in 1995 did not report detectable concentrations of volatile or semi-volatile petroleum constituents.  This analytical result is further supported by the 2012 soil sample results that found no detections.",125051.0,0.0,JGLASS,2013-05-09 08:58:53.537
