6486,36-95-4035,36,95,4035,6130.0,1995-03-20,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Franko #23,1023 N ADAMS,MCMINNVILLE,97128,(503)472-9883,False,4.0,GW,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"cc: Ron McPherson, Eureka Mgt. Group, 11650 SW 67th Ave, Suite 210, Portland OR 97223-8590,  (503) 635-7505.    Received the SW-LoA application & signed CR agreement 3/25/96.",Pjt Mgr = JLG,"Soil and groundwater contamination was initially reported to DEQ on March 20, 1995, when the first of several underground storage tanks were being removed.  The site was used as a service station from the 1960s until 1995.  Prior to the property’s use as a filling station, the site had been location of a single family residence.  Since the 1995 report of petroleum contamination, ICA Restated Profit Sharing of Mesa, Arizona, has completed significant soil cleanup and extensive groundwater investigation on and extending beyond the property boundary.  The closure plan proposes to allow the remaining contamination in soil and groundwater to naturally attenuate in-place. Based on soil and groundwater sampling results, DEQ has determined that, given the current a reasonably likely future land use, the remaining contamination from the underground storage tanks has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment.
",22104.0,0.0,JGLASS,2010-02-10 17:39:04.390
