6514,10-95-7006,10,95,7006,653.0,1995-01-23,1999-03-18 13:49:10,HOLLAND'S AUTO SERVICE,236 NE 1ST,OAKLAND,97462,(503)459-3712,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,This was a FA site for new tanks in 1995. The tanks were later removed in 2013.,,"The site has been used as an automotive repair and fueling station since at least the 1920s. Contamination is the result of leaks from underground fuel tanks and likely some additional contribution from the long time use of the property for automotive repair. Subsurface soil, groundwater, and sediments in Ash Creek have been affected by the petroleum contamination. About 390 cubic yards of impacted soils were excavated and treated under a Solid Waste Letter of Authorization in April 1995. Nearly 100 gallons of impacted sediments from Ash Creek were removed from around a drainage outfall in September 2012. Contaminated soil and groundwater remains on the western half of the property and extends to the north beneath the Ash Street right-of-way.  Remaining contamination in soil and groundwater is below applicable screening levels for reasonable and likely future property use within the impacted areas. Contaminated sediments remain in Ash Creek.  However, all concentrations are below ecological screening values.  Ash Creek receives storm water runoff from a large portion of town and remaining contamination may have been contributed from a variety of non-point sources. The property is expected to remain a commercial property that is connected to the municipal water system.",18386.0,0.0,GDECK,2018-05-25 09:17:57.543
