6574,29-95-0083,29,95,0083,8940.0,1995-04-06,1999-03-18 13:49:10,BAY CITY DELI MART,8335 HWY 101N,BAY CITY,97107,(503) 377-2002,False,7.0,MATRIX,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,LUST #29-18-0076,"Two USTs were decommissioned by removal from the site in April 1995: a 4,000-gallon gasoline UST and a 2,000-gallon gasoline UST.  Three additional USTs were discovered during the decommissioning: an empty 2,000-gallon UST (between the two gasoline USTs), an empty 550-gallon UST (on the northwest property line), and a 220-gallon waste oil UST (behind the service station building).  The additional USTs were decommissioned by removal.

Approximately 22 cubic yards of diesel- and oil-contaminated soils from around the two smaller tanks were excavated and treated on-site.  Approximately 350 cubic yards of gasoline-contaminated soils from the gasoline UST pit were treated at an off-site residential property owned by the station owner/operator.  About 20 tons of the on-site treated soils were subsequently disposed of at an off-site landfill in June 1996.  The off-site treated soils were remediated to below 100 ppm gasoline and remained at the residence.  DEQ issued an NFA for the cleanup in September 1997.",24069.0,0.0,KDANA,2018-11-20 09:33:13.097
