6603,20-95-7019,20,95,7019,6219.0,1995-04-17,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Astro #207,925 6TH AVE W,EUGENE,97402,(503) 243-7899,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : CONTAMINATION DISC. DURING RETROFITTING NEW PIPE AND TANK LINING *** 685 yds3 taken to PEMCO.  Free product in UST tank nest.  Bob Miller 
(consultant) attempted a short-term pump and treat of the excavation.  A VES and air sparge system was installed at site and 
operated 1995 - 2017.  High TPH and benzene concentrations were observed in some of the wells.",,"This is an active gasoline station. In April 1995 the contamination was discovered during a tank and piping upgrade. Free product was discovered in the tank area. They removed 684.56 tons of petroleum contaminated soil and it was thermally treated and disposed by PEMCO. Five onsite monitoring wells (MW) were installed 4/95 and they were being monitored until 9/15. A cut-off trench was dug and in July 1996, an air sparging pump system started in MW2, MW5, and ten points in the cut-off trench. Various attempts were also made (1997, 2001, 2009, 2011, 2012) to use bioremediation to remediate the groundwater. MW2 and MW5 are in the tank nest and MW1 is in a downslope direction. On 8/17/96 free product was observed in MW-5 and a sheen was observed between 2004 and 2008 and again in 2014. A thin gasoline sheen had been obesrved in MW2 from 10/09 until the monitoring well was abandonded on 10/21/2016 in preparation for the tank decommissionings. On 10/4/09 surface water runoff was observed entering the top of the well casing MW1 due to a poor seal which was later repaired. Current plans are to remove the tanks and as much of the petroleum contaminated soil as they safely can without endangering the street, and then re-install new tanks in the same location. This is being performed in March - June 2017.",9432.0,0.0,TDANOVI,2017-06-14 14:42:01.277
