6804,23-95-0334,23,95,0334,4225.0,1995-04-18,1999-03-18 13:49:10,VP VALLEY PRODUCTS,518 MAIN ST,NYSSA,97913,(503)889-5531,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,See ECSI 3910,ECSI 3910,"[March 2010] The site is a former petroleum service station.  The site was declared an Orphan in July 2003.  Extensive soil and groundwater contamination has been documented on- and off-site.  A dual phase extraction system operated on the site from November 2004 to May 2006. 

A Conditional No Further Action determination was issued for this site on March 23, 2010.  All of the potential exposure concerns are addressed through: 1) Elimination during development of the site-specific CSM (discussed in detail above); and 2) Institutional controls as defined in the Easement and Equitable Servitude (E&ES). 

The E&ES includes the following restrictions.
a) Groundwater shall not be extracted through wells or by other means or used at the site for consumption or other beneficial use, as long as the hazardous substance concentrations exceed the acceptable risk level for such use;
b) Prohibit residential use; 
c) Prohibit the construction or expansion of future structures on the site unless appropriate measures (i.e. passive venting, vapor barrier) are taken to mitigate the potential for vapor intrusion. Proposed measures will be required to be submitted for DEQ review and approval.

Petroleum contamination remains in the subsurface.  In the event subsurface excavation is necessary in the Locality of the Facility (LOF), the Contaminated Media Management Plan  dated December 29, 2009 should be referenced to plan for appropriate health and safety measures as well as soil and groundwater management that will need to be performed. 

Select site documents may be viewed in the site document section of this database.",59908.0,0.0,KROBERT,2010-03-23 16:17:44.893
