Discovery: site assessment.  Cause: unknown.  Date discovered: 4/18/95
RP phone #: 258-5453",,"In 1995, 4 USTs were removed from the site. In 2020, further environmental investigation showed residual gasoline and diesel contamination remained at the site, primarily located in the southwest portion of the former excavation. Contamination was also encountered within the center of the excavation, possibly suggesting that when the USTs were removed in 1995, contaminated soil may have been placed back in the excavation instead of being properly disposed. Contamination was present in soil and groundwater at levels that should be remediated.
A total of 599.57 tons of petroleum contaminated soil was excavated and 28,504 gallons of contaminated groundwater was removed from the excavation. The final excavation measures approx. 43’Lx32’Wx13’D with no remaining visual indications of contamination on the excavation sidewalls. Confirmation sampling shows highest remaining contamination is located on the southeast bottom of the excavation with gasoline at 1,700ppm and diesel at 470ppm. The highest remaining contamination on the sidewalls is located on the northwest with gasoline at 330ppm and diesel on the northeast sidewall at 130ppm.
Per the Progress Report submitted 5/12/2020, a new risk based evaluation following additional site activities is needed to determine site status. Additional work should include soil and groundwater sampling to determine the extent of contamination, soil gas sampling to determine if the vapor intrusion into buildings from soil and groundwater pathways are complete, and drinking water well sampling to determine if the ingestion and inhalation from tap water pathways are complete.
",21303.0,0.0,JCLAUSS,2020-05-18 11:33:06.550
