10.17.2012:  draft ees to peter nelson, draft nfa and ees to hydro for review.  (RAH)

Met with Fagan on 6-11-2002, rhr. Owns property downgradient to site.   He requested to withdraw from DEQ oversight.  Enforcement referral on 3/24

Wohlers Environmental worked at the site in late 90s early 2000.  Impacts in Hogan Road, attributed to Falcon site.  Not conclusive. 

Tanks installed in 1973, and according to Kevin Kelty, leaking and patched and lined.  Lots of line leaks. The lines were repaired, and trenches dug.  Monitoring wells installed, but unclear if at proper depth.

Vapor intrusion evaluated by BB&A, leak detection compound questionable. 

This site remains open because there are two tanks in temporary closure and they have not evaluted leaks and potential for impacts related to the tanks.  Because the facility is not in compliance the site should not be closed, especially if additional investigation is to be done in the area of the temporarily closed tanks.",,,19171.0,0.0,RHOOD,2020-12-30 14:03:19.743
