(assuming the below was written by Laurey Cook):
Due to re-development of the site as a retail business, several monitoring wells have been abandoned.  Six offsite wells will continue to be monitored on a quarterly basis and replacement wells will be installed around the new building after construction work is completed. Latest GW monitoring report indicates MW-7 followed by MW-14 have highest residual petroleum contamination.  The USTs have been decommissioned by removal.

A vapor barrier with passive venting was installed at the site.  Initial groundwater sampling showed benzene exceeding the vapor intrusion into indoor air pathway for occupational use.  The levels seem to be decreasing.  DEQ requested evaluation of the system, sampling was not conclusive.",26-90-0055,,4073.0,0.0,RHOOD,2012-04-02 14:02:37.917
