7324,20-96-7004,20,96,7004,6963.0,1996-01-25,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Barger Texaco,4945 BARGER DR,EUGENE,97402,(541)998-2300,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Site assessment in Jan. 1996 identified contamination; 4 USTs decom'd in April 1996 (new tanks installed); PCS removed; free product in MW-2 in 2000; off-site impacts - C. Rodda 5/26/2010,See Also: 20-80-4003,"Four underground storage tanks (UST) were decommissioned by removal in April 1996. Nine confirmation soil samples were collected from the sidewalls and bottom of the UST excavation, which extended up to 15 feet bgs. The highest concentrations of petroleum contaminants following soil removal included gasoline at 370 ppm, diesel at 2,300 ppm, and benzene at 1.5 ppm. A petroleum sheen was present on the water that entered the UST excavation, and a sample was collected that contained benzene at 100 ppb. Contractors removed 1,193.5 tons of petroleum-contaminated soil was excavated from the pump islands, product lines, and tank cavity as part of cleanup actions. The contaminated soil was disposed of at Coffin Butte Landfill. In November 1996, three monitoring wells (MW-1 to MW-3) were installed. Soil samples were collected during well construction and contained petroleum. Initial groundwater samples from the wells had high concentrations of BTEX constituents, including benzene at 9,300 ppb. Two push probes (GP9 and GP10) were installed in February 1999. Groundwater samples collected from the probes had petroleum contaminants, including benzene at 4,800 ppb, toluene at 9,500 ppb, and total xylenes at 14,000 ppb at GP9. Monitoring wells MW-4, MW-5, and MW-6 were installed in 2000. During this phase of investigation, a passive collection canister for free product was installed in MW-2. In a five-month span, only 6.5 ounces of free phase petroleum was collected from the well. Semiannual GW monitoring was initiated in 2002. Analysis for BTEX, MTBE, and naphthalene constituents on samples found contamination only in MW-2 near the northern property line (benzene at 540 ppb and naphthalene at 31.2 ppb). Off-site investigation was conducted, and some contamination migrated in groundwater to the south of Barger Drive (MW-8). No petroleum constituents were detected in MW-8 in any sample event, though total gasoline hydrocarbons were measured up to 248 ppb in 2012 testing. Final samples collected from MW-8 showed gasoline below risk levels. The USTs and associated piping & dispensers were removed in 2013. Soil gas samples were collected in 2014 that showed no risk to workers from petroleum vapors at the site or adjacent properties.",22691.0,0.0,GDECK,2016-01-05 17:40:48.110
