7524,26-96-0095,26,96,0095,1072.0,1996-02-20,1999-03-18 13:49:10,TOSCO 5664/UNOCAL STATION #5664,110 SW ARTHUR ST,PORTLAND,97201,(503) 223-9652,False,1.0,GW,1.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"
11/26/18 CNFA issued

8/17/18 

Results of Final Performance Sub-Slab Vapor Sampling Event and Request for Certification of Completion and NFA Determination

DEQ will hold a public comment in October 2018 to announce its proposal to issue a Certificate of Completion and conditional NFA letter.  A replacement EES will be recorded on the property deed. 
1/12/18

Revised Construction Completion Report submitted.  Confirmation testing to verify that active vapor collection is effective is pending. Upon receipt of acceptable monitoring data DEQ will issue a Certificate of Completion following public comment period.  


NOTE: Active PPA file in LUST drawer at NWR.

5/20/16: subject prop. EES should be recorded today, staff memo going to HDL (short with arcadis cap rb closure request), shorter PN.  EES for Miller (neighbor) will be recorded soo.  (RAH)


4/2016:  subject property conditional-partial nfa was written toward the end of 2015.  CAP/closure request in review, need to complete and record ees for 7-11 property, public notice for site closure request.  (RAH)

10/2015:  Soil Vapor data (RAH)


7/2015:  Miller accepting ees (711 property owner), LaGrand has their comfort letter, Chevron doing more soil gas mon/modeling on south portion of property, for diesel sg.  ppa draft has to be on database before 1 sept (along with publishing notice to website and oregonian, sec. of state due 15th).   (RAH)

1.30.15: see email in file re: next steps for Chevron and re: sv sampling at sv-3 for diesel/heating oil. (RAH)

1/2015:  Soil gas on south near the residence has steadily decreased over the last 3 annual events.   After further historical review, Chevron presented that the 7-11 property was a gas station through 1985.  Based on that, Chevron does not want to access that property since they wouldn't want to be held responsible for what may be on the 7-11 property.  I am reviwing that and implications based on gw extent and for Vi, which if site closed this way would also require EES on 7-11 property.


5/2013:  soil gas report received. several constituents above residential and comm. rbcs.  need to delineate soil gas, keep sg sampling, maybe even restart of expand remedial efforts.  reply due 31 May. (RAH)

5.1.12:  approved soil gas portion of work plan w/some comments (see 4/5/12 email to chris angier).  they didn't discuss the gw delineation.  after follow-up, chris indicated party to the west was going to allow access to get that info.  access agreement being worked out w/7-11. (RAH)

12.20.11:  asked for soil gas and delineation work plan by 30 Jan. (RAH)

7.25.11:  2nd quarter qm being worked on by stantec, then arcadis takes over QM.  Work plan to be submitted by Arcadis for gw delin (toward 7-11) and soil gas sampling, plan to submit week of 12 sept.-per meeting with Chevron, Arcadis, and me. (RAH)

1/2011:  letter sent requesting next steps.  resp. due 28 jan.  (RAH)-from that had meeting on 1/25/11.  System off, consultant to continue w/qm.  there will be a change in RP management from Conoco to Chevron. Should occur in April/May.  After transfer, will meet w/chevron to discuss soil gas sampling strategy.

 ozone air sparge remediation system in-place. Product has been measuredin MW-4 in Nov. 2009 (~1"") & over time.  Bailed it out.  Keep check on that (RAH).",,"9/6/18  MTPugh

DEQ will hold a public comment in October 2018 to announce its proposal to issue a Certificate of Completion and conditional NFA letter.  A replacement EES will be recorded on the property deed.

11/26/18
CNFA has been issued. EES has been recorded.  Cert. of Completion has been finalized and submitted to Dept. of Justice for entering into Multnomah Court. ",18659.0,0.0,MPUGH,2018-11-28 07:07:50.127
