7687,24-96-4046,24,96,4046,153.0,1996-03-19,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Don's Shell (Exxon),110 E WASHINGTON ST,STAYTON,97383,(503)769-2400,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Project deassignment letter sent 11/6/2012.  EES mailed to RP with request to notarize, no response received.  Project deassigned. rhr.",,"The site operated as a fuel service station beginning in 1955 when four underground storage tanks were installed. A petroleum release from the underground storage tank system was confirmed in 1999 when the tanks were assessed for leaks. Soil and groundwater were contaminated by petroleum spilled or leaked from the tank system. Petroleum-contaminated soil was excavated and the tanks were decommissioned in 1999. The site currently is used for commercial (restaurant) purposes, and will likely be used commercially in the future. Groundwater is not used at the site or adjacent properties for drinking water, as municipal water is provided. Public notice was completed in December 2011 to provide an opportunity for comments on the proposed site closure. No objections to closure were received. Petroleum contaminants remain in soil and groundwater at the site. Groundwater samples detected contamination above levels considered safe for direct contact by construction or excavation workers. A health and safety plan, incorporated in a Contaminated Media Management Plan, was included with an Easement & Equitable Servitudes document recorded on the property deed through Marion County.",18032.0,0.0,CRODDA,2015-03-30 15:13:20.757
