7757,34-96-0216,34,96,0216,,1996-04-05,1999-03-18 13:49:10,WASHINGTON COUNTY - 240TH PLACE,7485 SW 240TH PLACE,BEAVERTON,97007,,False,1.0,GW,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"The site is a 1-acre farm in rural Washington County.  The County acquired the property through foreclosure in 1992.  A 1996 investigation identified three 1,000-gallon USTs, a 250-gallon AHOT, and over a dozen drums and containers of oils, pesticides, and herbicides.  In 2000, DEQ negotiated a PPA (00-06) with prospective purchaser Darrin Mossor, limiting Mossor's investigation and cleanup costs to $20,000.  Kleinfelder completed a ""Soil and Groundwater Assessment Report"" in August 2003, finding up to 3,380 ppm diesel and 21,400 ppm heavy oil in the soil.  (7/21/09 KPD)

The Department on September 22, 2003 certified that the RP has fulfilled obligations under the PPA.  There are present and future restrictions in the use of the property.  Soil and groundwater contamination remaining at the site must be addressed before a NFA determination can be made and the site declared closed. (BNP)",,,27538.0,0.0,KDANA,2009-09-23 15:47:31.320
