Site location originally reported as 15324 Monitor-Woodburn Rd; now known as Woodburn Monitor Rd NE ...gdeck 6/13/2014",,"In 1996, when the tank was decommissioned in place due to the closeness of the store front, contamination was noted. An additional geoprobe investigation in 2006 show petroleum hydrocarbons and their constituents above risk levels for indoor air -- vapor intrusion into building for occupational receptors, and above drinking water ingestion and inhalation for occupational and residential receptors.  Due to lack of progress, additional work was conductd by DEQ in 2010 through early 2014. The data indicates that the site does not pose an imminent risk at that time. Monitoring wells were installed by the previous owner in 2014, but due to lack of funds the investigation has stopped. The magnitude and extent of the contamination still needs to be determined and any seasonal variations need to be assessed. Also the investigation needs to determine if the plume is still migrating or if it has stabilized. Additional detailed information are included in the site documents linked to this Website. ",17699.0,0.0,TDANOVI,2016-12-05 17:08:53.280
