8033,21-96-4103,21,96,4103,2155.0,1996-06-20,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Agate Beach Time,4852 N COAST HWY,NEWPORT,97365,(503)265-8755,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : TRUCK TO TANK TRANSFER SPILL.  IMPACTS DOWN TO AT LEAST 3 FT DEEP.  INVESTIGATION IS ONGOING.  CUMMINS TRANSFER MADE THE DELIVERY, OVERFILLED 3 USTS. *** Truck to tank transfer spill.  Impacts down to at least 3 ft deep.  Investigation is ongoing.  Cummins Transfer made the delivery, overfilled 3 USTs.",,"Soil contamination was initially reported in 1996, following the overfilling of underground storage tanks at the site.
Cleanup activities at the site have included the removal of petroleum-contaminated soil, free product removal from the groundwater, operation of soil-vapor extraction and groundwater treatment systems, and the decommissioning of all underground storage tanks.  The area of groundwater contamination is stable or shrinking and does not extend beyond the property boundaries.  Based on the review of this file, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land use, the remaining contamination has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment.  The corrective action plan proposes to allow the remaining contamination to degrade naturally in place and restrict the use of onsite groundwater for domestic drinking purposes.",19420.0,0.0,GDECK,2008-03-26 16:44:05.717
