8089,21-96-4114,21,96,4114,10949.0,1996-07-12,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Taft Elementary-Middle Sc,1540 SCHOONER-CREEK RD,LINCOLN CITY,97367,(541)867-7171,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Removed two 2,000 gal. & two 5,OOO gal gasoline & diesel USTS in June 1998.  160 tons of PCS excavated & taken to Riverbend Landfill.

The site address was originally reported as 1540 Schooner-Creek Rd.  We are keeping it as is in the LUST and UST database. This address is no longer recognized by Google Maps. In town, Schooner-Creek Rd is 51st St.  More accurate and current addresses for this site are 1545 SE 50th Street & 4916 SE Keel Avenue; these addresses are cited in the NFA letter and EES.... gdeck 3/6/2020.",,"[J Glass, 2019] The southern portion of the site was formerly used as an elementarty school.  The NE corner of the property was used as a bus parking and refueling station from 1969 until June 1998, when the UST systems were decommissioned by removal.The NE corner of the propoerty is as of this writing still being used to park school buses.  Contamination remains beneath portions of the site and under SE 51st Street. The contamination consists primarily of gasoline; however, diesel and heavier oil range petroleum have also been detected. Petroleum contamination is located in subsurface soil at depths from 3 feet to the depth of the shallow groundwater, Groundwater flows easterly toward the creek at depths that s vary between 3 and 6 feet below ground surface.  Although the site appears to meet Oregon’s Cleanup requirements with a pavement cap to stabilize residual soil and groundwater contamination and with restrictions on groundwater use and residential uses, additional cleanup or use restrictions may be required if the current use changes, if the residual contamination is disturbed by removal of the protective pavement cap, if increased groundwater occurs, or excavation in the area is required.  DEQ is working with the Lincoln Co.School Dstrict to evaluate futre uses and to ensure the contamination plume remains stable, that there is no current of future threat to the adjacent residennts, utility workers, future occupants of the site, or to the Siletz River (aka Schooner Creek) sensative areas. ...JGLASS.

[G Deck, 3/6/2020] The site address was originally reported as 1540 Schooner-Creek Rd.  We are keeping it as is in the LUST and UST database. This address is no longer recognized by Google Maps. In town, Schooner-Creek Rd is 51st St.  More accurate and current addresses for this site are 1545 SE 50th Street & 4916 SE Keel Avenue; these addresses are cited in the NFA letter and EES.... GDECK 3/6/2020.",16334.0,0.0,GDECK,2020-04-15 16:20:02.470
