8263,20-96-7053,20,96,7053,150.0,1996-08-23,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Row River Store,37570 ROW RIVER RD,DORENA,97434,(503)946-1567,False,2.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Pjt Mgr = C Rodda

11/2207: Unassigned project as of 11/6/2007 - no response from RP since November 2005. - C. Rodda

Water district for Dorena provides potable water at site & adjacent properties.  NFA requested by RP in 9/25/2008 letter with Final Soil Disposition/Property Owner Statement - C. Rodda, 9/30/2008

FILE MOVED TO OFFSITE STORAGE ",,"During decommissioning of the USTs in 1996, contaminated soil was encountered and excavated.  Approximately 200 cubic yards of PCS was removed and transported off-site to property owned by Bob Jones.  Yinger estimated that three cubic yards of contaminated soil remained at the southeast corner of the remedial excavation, left in place due to the proximity of the mercantile building.

An application for soil treatment was received by the DEQ in September 1996.  The Solid Waste Letter Authorization (SWLA) was issued by the DEQ in November 1996.  The PCS was removed from the subject property and placed at 76119 Booth Kelly Camp Road in Dorena for soil aeration.  The PCS was spread out 12 inches thick on plastic sheeting and tilled according to the approved SWLA.  

Groundwater monitoring was initiated in January 1997 at the request of the DEQ.  Two water samples were collected from springs located along the Row River and were analyzed for BTEX  constituents as well as EDC  and EDB .  The water samples measured no detectable concentrations of these gasoline-related compounds.

Yinger installed two monitoring wells (MW-1 and MW-2) in March 1998.  The wells were completed to a depth of 9.5 feet and 18.5 feet bgs, respectively.  Well MW-1 was located near the dispenser island at the east side of the property, and MW-2 was installed just outside of the remedial excavation west of the UST cavity.  Samples were collected in March and June 1998 and measured BTEX, EDC, and EDB below laboratory detection levels.   The direction of groundwater flow was determined to be west towards the Row River. 

Six soil samples were collected from the PCS treatment area at the time the monitoring wells were installed.  Only one soil sample (#3031) measured gasoline above detection levels at 17 ppm.
Additional groundwater monitoring was conducted in November 2004 and June 2005.  The water samples were again analyzed for gasoline-related contaminants, and only toluene was detected at 0.770 ppb in MW-1 during the November 2004 event.  The remaining samples measured no concentrations above laboratory detection levels.

As part of the risk-based evaluation, an additional boring was installed adjacent to the remedial excavation limits on February 10, 2008.  The soil sample (#8736) was obtained from 7 feet bgs at the southwest corner of the former UST cavity, and measured gasoline-range hydrocarbons and RBDM VOCs  below laboratory detection levels.",18029.0,0.0,LFINCHE,2010-10-25 14:36:09.810
