8539,06-96-0075,06,96,0075,5242.0,1996-11-15,1999-03-18 13:49:10,DORA STORE,15219 SITKUM LN,MYRTLE POINT,97458,(503)572-3652,False,1.0,,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Original NFA issued 4/13/1997.  
I would like to request we re-open the Dora Store USTC project (06-96-0075).  I believe the 1996 sampling and cleanup was inadequate and did not fully identify the extent of impacts present at that time.  I do not believe the new UST installed at that time is the source of the contamination observed now.  Same RP and everything else.... Eric Clough, 2/18/2010.

*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : CHARGE TO FUND CODE FA-5242 *** Site re-opened on : 2/24/2010 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 4/3/1997.",,"The site is located at 15219 Sitkum Lane in Dora, Oregon, which is northeast of Myrtle Point.  The site was formerly operated as a country store with a gasoline UST.  The Dora Store was subsequently closed and the building incorporated as part of the attached residence.  The site is currently an occupied residence and all above grade fueling equipment has been removed.

In 1996, petroleum hydrocarbon contamination was discovered during the decommissioning by removal of a 1,000-gallon UST.  Petroleum-impacted soil was encountered and approximately 30 tons of soil was removed and treated off site.  No petroleum hydrocarbons were detected in the confirmation soil samples submitted to the laboratory.  The site was assigned Leaking UST (LUST) number 06-96-0075.  A new 1,000-gallon UST was installed in the excavation, replacing the original UST.  The site was issued a No Further Action determination in 1997.

The site is currently an occupied residence. Fueling operations ceased in 2002 and all above-ground fueling equipment has been removed. Three soil borings were advanced by a contractor to bring the site into compliance with temporary closure regulations. The contractor verbally reported encountering PCS and impacted groundwater, but did not submit any samples
for laboratory analysis to confirm his findings. The 1,000-gallon
UST installed in 1996 remains in place.

A SI was completed in December 2009.Nine subsurface explorations were completed, three monitoring wells were installed, and soil, groundwater, and soil gas samples were
collected.   Petroleum contamination was documented and the 1997 NFA was recinded. Additional groundwater monitoring will be performed at the site. The SI report is availible for viewing in the Site Document section of this database.",21466.0,0.0,GDECK,2011-04-28 16:28:52.137
