8602,23-96-0038,23,96,0038,4059.0,1990-09-25,1999-03-18 13:49:10,"GENERAL FARM SUPPLY, INC.",312 MAIN ST,NYSSA,97913,(208) 459-4371,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,3.0,False,False,False,False,False,See ECSI #4555,ECSI 4555,"The site was a former petroleum service station since at least 1949 until General Farm Supply filed for bankruptcy in 1991.  The site is owned by Malheur County, which acquired it through tax foreclosure proceedings entered in 1994 and recorded in 1996.  

Multiple investigations and an IRAM have been completed at the site.  The investigations delineated the extent of the General Farm contamination and also documented releases at two other sites: the former Goodman Oil service station (LUST 23-09-0031) and the former Nyssa Laundromat site (ECSI 2949). The groundwater plumes from the sites (General Farm, Goodman Oil, and Nyssa Laundromat) are co-mingled. 

The General Farm site was issued a Conditional NFA determination on April 22, 2010.  Select site documents may be viewed in the Site Document section of this database.  See ECSI # 4555 for more details and additional site documents releated to this site.",91114.0,0.0,KROBERT,2010-04-22 12:51:34.547
