8643,34-96-0724,34,96,0724,,1996-12-17,1999-03-18 13:49:10,"MCMAHON, S HOT",2920 SW 119TH AVENUE,BEAVERTON,97005,(503) 646-1072,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,28075.0,0.0,EMCMORR,2008-06-19 11:32:34.657
8644,14-96-0042,14,96,0042,,1994-10-20,1999-03-18 13:49:10,O'LEARY ROAD ORCHARDS,4930 O'LEARY ROAD,DEE FLATS,97031,,False,7.0,MATRIX,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,(9/28/05 KJR) site backlog letter sent 9/28/05,,"[May 2010] Four non-regulated USTs were decommissioned by removal from three separate excavations in October 1994.  The USTs ranged in capacity from 210 gallons to 990 gallons and stored gasoline and diesel  Evidence of petroleum contamination was only observed during the removal of a 210 gallon gasoline UST (Tank #1).  A release was reported to DEQ and leaking UST (LUST) No. 14 96 0042 was assigned to the site.

Six confirmation soil samples were collected in October 1994 following the removal of the USTs and analyzed for hydrocarbon identification. Concentrations of diesel and heavy oil were not detected in any of the six confirmation soil samples. Concentrations of gasoline were only identified in the soil sample collected from the Tank #1 excavation.  This soil sample was further analyzed for gasoline and contained a detected concentration of 23,500 milligrams per kilograms (mg/kg). 

Approximately one ton of petroleum contaminated soil (PCS) was excavated and transported to Finley Buttes Landfill for disposal.  Groundwater was not encountered.

One soil confirmation sample was collected from the bottom of the excavation and analyzed for gasoline.  Gasoline was not detected.

A No Further Action determination was made for this site on May 13, 2010.  The NFA letter may be viewed in the site document section of this database.
