8649,26-96-0727,26,96,0727,6642.0,1996-12-17,1999-03-18 13:49:10,AVIS RENT A CAR SYSTEM INC,9555 NE AIRPORT WAY,PORTLAND,97220,(516) 222-3406,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"Site re-opened on : 5/29/2008 By Lynne Kent. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 12/6/2007.

Avis has operated at the site since about 1984.  A release of virgin motor oil to the soil was reported in December 1996.  Approx 80 tons of PCS were removed.  Four USTs were decommissioned and replaced in December 1997, and 10.5 tons of gasoline-contaminated soil were removed.  Another 54 tons were removed in November 2000.  Six groundwater monitoring wells were eventually installed.  Most of the wells were clean, but as of March 2007 MW-5 still showed gasoline (576 ppb), BTEX, and MTBE.  Several pockets of PCS remain at the site.  The contractor recommended an NFA after the March 2007 sampling, but final NFA approval was apparently held up (7/29/09 KPD). The site was reassigned.  According to the initial evaluaiton leaching to groundwater was exceeded for soil. But for the groundwater contamination, groundwater ingestion was found incomplete. The benzene concentrations of up to  8.2 ppm was reported, but vapor intrusion was not found to be a complete pathway because no building was current within 10 feet (this does not account for future construction).  The consultant conducted soil gas sampling and modeled groundwater.  I am proposing an NFA for the site.  LLC",,,11601.0,0.0,LKENT,2012-01-17 08:29:49.373
