8768,26-97-0062,26,97,0062,,1997-01-21,1999-03-18 13:49:10,"KIMMEL, D HOT",3202 SE 167TH AVE,PORTLAND,97236,,False,7.0,MATRIX,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"A contractor (REA Tech) identified 91 ppm TPH-418.1 adjacent to a 10,000-gallon abandoned-in-place HOT at this site address in January 1997.  No further investigation or cleanup appears to have been conducted.  In March 1997, the Powell Valley Road & Water District reported finding ""lots of diesel"" in the ground around copper distribution lines in the area, including oil-saturated soil at 167th & Tibbetts, one block north of the HOT.  The lines were encountered during road maintenance work, and again no further investigation or cleanup appears to have been conducted.

Based on available property records, it appears the Goodall Oil Company acquired an easement in 1962 for the distribution of heating oil to the Wundervoll neighborhood.  A 10,000-gallon HOT was to be placed on the NE corner of Lot 1, Block 5 (the current site address) to serve the neighborhood.  Distribution lines would be laid 2-3 ft bgs along the northern and western sides of streets in the neighborhood, within 5 ft of either side of the tax lot lines.  Sunset Fuel Company acquired the easement in September 1965 and apparently operated the system until abandoning the easement in November 1976.

Potentially, this ""site"" encompasses the entire Wundervoll neighborhood, which covers 8 ""blocks"" and 91 lots.  If the heating oil distribution system served the entire neighborhood, investigating this site would be a massive undertaking.  Historically, DEQ has looked to Sunset Fuel Company as the most viable RP.  (7/30/09 KPD)

REA was Chuck Getter company, found to be not reliable. ",,,28161.0,0.0,LCOOK,2010-11-17 13:46:44.490
