9210,20-97-7034,20,97,7034,5215.0,1997-05-14,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Del Oeste Vet Hospital,90238 PRAIRIE RD,EUGENE,97402,(503) 689-2581,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"PrjMgr=DRB - completed environmental site assessment.  One tank located on VEt i
Hospital property and other located on property line.

Vet hospital address is 20238 Prairie Rd., offsite migration into Prairie Road, free product since at least Jan. 2004, Crodda 9/18/07",,"The site is now the Del Oeste Vet Clinic but was previously a fuel service station and part of Weyerhaeuser (NW Hardwoods) operations. DEQ records indicate that five underground storage tanks have been used at the property since the 1960’s. In 1988, two tanks of unknown capacities were removed that had stored gasoline and diesel. At the same time, a third tank (unknown capacity and product) was filled in place. Two 1,000-gallon gasoline tanks that had been used at the service station were decommissioned in 2001. An environmental site assessment was performed for Diamond Hardwoods in August 1995 that identified a petroleum release from an underground tank system. Additional site assessment activities were conducted on behalf of Lane County in April 2002 prior to a utility install and road expansion project as contamination was previously encountered in this area. Five probes were installed within Prairie Road. Soil samples found petroleum contamination to 11 feet bgs in P3. Groundwater samples from the borings identified BTEX, including benzene at 520 ppb. Adjacent to the site, 1,625 cubic yards of contaminated soil was removed for the Lane County project in 2002. Soil was treated successfully off-site. In 2003, free product was discovered in a site monitoring well. Additional investigation has been on-going, including groundwater monitoring and soil sampling.",132674.0,0.0,CRODDA,2014-10-03 15:52:47.863
