9314,34-97-0442,34,97,0442,,1997-04-18,1999-03-18 13:49:10,JD & L INDUSTRIAL RENTALS INC.,31830 NW COMMERCIAL ST,NORTH PLAINS,97133,,False,4.0,GW,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"The site was a service station prior to 1965.  Jack Oakes acquired the site in 1969.  A release was reported in April 1997, apparently on an adjacent property and traced to this site.  An 8,000-gallon gasoline UST (with 120 gallons of gasoline still in it) was removed in September 1997, and a 2,000-gallon gasoline UST was removed in September 1999, both from the northwest corner of the site.  DEQ eventually issued a NON in November 2003 and an NOV in January 2004 due to a lack of investigation into the extent of contamination.

The attorney for Jack Oakes, Thomas Benke, argued both that Oakes was an innocent purchaser (he couldn't reasonably have known about the contamination in 1969) and that the adjacent property is contaminating this site and not the other way around.  DEQ drafted a Remedial Action Order (RAO) in November 2005 to compel further investigation and cleanup, but dropped the matter in April 2007 after deciding that the site wasn't a high priority.  [Note: off-site migration, if occurring, does make this site a high priority, barely].  The site was subsequently backlogged.  (8/4/09 KPD)

There is a lien for $40,776.48, on this project, $22,766.78 is interest. This project is also on the backlog list and has submitted a CRA. (04/07/21 XC)",34-93-0210.  Oregon Canadian Forest.,,29390.0,0.0,XCRUZCU,2021-04-07 10:44:02.130
