9612,36-97-4133,36,97,4133,9867.0,1997-08-19,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Morris Texaco II,101 E 1ST ST,NEWBERG,97132,(503)538-0512,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"Site re-opened on : 10/7/2016 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 7/7/2010.  Reopened to investigate EES violation.

Site closed in database again.  Review of EES violation complete. It wasn’t that big of a deal. They just needed to pave over an area in the parking lot. Original NFA stands.  5/31/2017  gdeck
",see also: 36-91-4079 (Morris Texaco) for all of the site documents,"The property, previously known as the Morris Texaco, and currently in business as the Newberg Shell Service Center, has been used as a retail gas station since the 1920s.  The property has been in private ownership for over 100 years and is currently owned by Archie Morris.    

Petroleum contamination was discovered in 1991 when soil and groundwater contamination was observed during the installation of a tree in the public right-of-way (sidewalk) of East 1st Street.  A second petroleum release was discovered in 1997 during upgrade work being performed on the three active gasoline underground storage tank systems.  Since the 1991 report of contamination, Mr. Morris has conducted multiple investigations to determine the extent of contamination. Between June and August 2005, he had contaminated soil removed from the area with the highest concentrations.

On October 26, 2005, DEQ received a report summarizing environmental work performed to date and an evaluation of the risk associated with remaining contamination.  The closure plan includes some restrictions on the future use of the property and proposes to allow the remaining contamination to naturally degrade in place.

No Further Action determination letter issued 7/7/2010.",17214.0,0.0,GDECK,2019-08-14 11:55:51.377
