Site re-opened on : 5/1/2019 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 4/10/2017.",,"The parent company of U-Haul (Amerco Real Estate) has owned and operated this property since 1977.  DEQ UST registration records indicate an installation date of May 1978 for the permitted tanks that were decommissioned at the site in October 1997.  The focus of investigation at this site has been a petroleum release discovered at the time of the decommissioning by removal of both of the registered tanks.  Contaminated groundwater was presentexcavations and free phase gasoline and contaminated groundwater was pumped from the gasoline tank excavation.  1998 site investigation included two off-site monitoring wells on the adjacent St. Vincent De Paul property with gasoline impacted groundwater. In December 2015, a vapor intrusion investigation was completed in order to assess potential risk to indoor air at the St. Vincent De Paul building.  There does not appear to be unacceptable human health risk for current occupational exposures or potential future urban residential exposures in the area of remaining groundwater contamination.  NFA letter issued 5/8/2017.   ---------- Site re-opened 3/17/2019 due to complaint regarding vapors on adjacent property.",20980.0,0.0,GDECK,2019-05-01 11:54:07.433
