10160,15-98-0002,15,98,0002,4261.0,1998-01-08,1999-03-18 13:49:10,LEATHERS OIL CO,5020 TABLE ROCK RD,CENTRAL POINT,97502,(503) 661-1244,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : RELEASE FROM GAS & DIESEL TANKS.  VERBAL LAB REPORT ONLY.  GW IS NEARBY BUT NOT ENCOUNTERED YET (12-15' DEEP).  1/29/98:  NEW LAB RESULTS INDICATE GW IMPACTED BY GASOLINE 220 PPB BENZENE ***,,"Prior to 1974, land use is unknown but likely agricultural or undeveloped. The site has been a fuel service station since the early 1970’s. Leathers Oil Company purchased the station in 1974 from another oil company and added a 4,000-gallon UST to the four USTs in place at the time. In 1998, six USTs (including one additional UST encountered during site work), dispensers, and associated piping were decommissioned by removal. The tanks included gasoline, diesel, and waste oil products. A petroleum release was discovered and reported to DEQ, creating Leaking Underground Storage Tank (LUST) #15-98-0002. Gasoline, diesel, BTEX, and naphthalene were Contaminants of Interest (COI) for the site. Soil and groundwater was contaminated by the release from the petroleum UST system. Soil-vapor samples were collected inside the station building. Results indicated no risk from vapor intrusion into indoor air. 
Closure was approved by DEQ in 2016 pending the abandonment of the on-site potable well (no longer in use).  During the public comment period for site closure, the adjacent property owners, Looney Commercial, LLC, objected to the closure citing that their property had been impacted.  An Off-Site Contamination Migration Policy letter was issued to Looney Commerical LLC. in 2018.",20853.0,0.0,GDECK,2019-04-17 14:20:27.663
