10376,34-98-0166,34,98,0166,5684.0,1998-03-11,1999-03-18 13:49:10,SETNIKER AUTO SERVICE CENTER,13320 SW PACIFIC HWY,TIGARD,97223,(503)639-3588,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"1/7/03:  site work completed.  GW monitoring reports for work done in 03 submitted in 7/05.  In December 2005,  a CAP was submitted for the site.  The CAP proposed a Dual Phase Extraction system.  Groundwater extraction from MW-5 and MW-8 proposed, along with SVE system at MW-1, MW-2, and MW-3.  CAP approved January 2006.  In April 2006, RP proposed GW monitoring in lieu of CAP implementation.  RP informed that further delays would result in site being referred to enforcement.  Application for Prospective Purchaser Agreement received from new owner (Paul Pettijohn) in March 2007.  On April 11, 2007, Order on Consent was issued, directing Mr. Pettijohn to implement the CAP of December 2005.  Letter sent 09 January 2009 requesting CAP implementation date.  Consultant proposed doing one additional monitoring event to determine if groundwater concentrations had dropped before impementing CAP.  Following sampling event in January 2010, Consultant has proposed a three-year program of annual monitoring, citing apparent constituent reductions in at least one well.  MSBA informed that a soil-gas investigation of adjacent residence must be performed, due to extremely high levels of benzene in MW-2.  Work plan for soil-gas investigation receive in November 2010.  Comments on work plan and conditional approval given on 11-19-10.  Soil-gas investigation performed 3-9-11 and await report of findings (4-20-11). Still await soil-gas report. Email inquiry sent 6-8-11. Reply from MSBA indicates RP has not paid consultant, but expects to be able to pay in next 60 days. Informed MSBA that DEQ is not able to evaluate whether to vacate Order without reviewing the soil-gas investigation report (JKS 6-14-11).  As of 8-17-11, MSBA indicated RP was still slowly paying down amount owed (JKS 9-13-11).  DEQ still without report documenting 2011 annual monitoring and the February 2011 soil-gas investigation.  MSBA proposed to combine the annual monitoring data from 2011 and 2012 with soil-gas investigation data into one report, to be submitted in mid-March 2012. **Follow up** (JKS 2-27-12).",,,21774.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2012-02-27 15:15:09.020
