10447,34-98-0212,34,98,0212,2372.0,1998-03-26,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Pacific Car Care,11900 SW PACIFIC HWY,TIGARD,97223,(503) 639-1121,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"Green sheet in file has project named, Pacific Car Care.  (RAH)

-9/20/2018:  From August indoor air sampling, diesel results were acceptable.  Redoing the Gx air samples.  (RAH)

-11/22/2017: Figuring RP.  Next steps:  additional indoor air sampling.  Yoo party needs to clean up their basement a bit-furnace and piping inspections and upgrade as needed, clean the AST exterior and ensure best management practices.  after that, IA sampling and determine if risk and if mitigation necessary (some sort of venting potentially. (RAH)

-In LUST file there is also a folder from Cleanup from Referral to LUST. -RAH

6/2013:  ODOT received it's parcel in the spring.  Awaiting to hear on status of soil gas/hand auger work.  (RAH)

9/26/12:  soil gas work plan approved given they add gx to analysis.  (RAH)

11/30/11: need some sg delineation closer to house. soil gas issues at SG-7 and SG-4 for future use (neighboring property).  Geodesign going was to collect some more samples in November from SG-7 and SG-8 (which were installed in October 2011).  (RAH).

4.20.11:  Approved soil gas and gw delineation work plan.  asked they inform me when field work will be completed. Barring any major issues, this site should be a good candidate for closure, given the re-use (major part of 99 and open space)(RAH)

10/28/2010:  Met with GeoDesign on 10/27 to discuss next steps.  Work plan should be submitted ~december (if they can set up budgets etc).    

9.2010:  Based on Belfor Env. report, ODOT owns property, county is managing expansion and paying CR.

7.2010:  County owns property now, tanks were removed in June 2010.  property being raized and redeveloped into a turn lane. (RAH)

If Mr. Lee (current RP):
Next QM: 9/30/2006, late QM reports due 24 Mar 2006,-if none then WL or what ever may be appropriate PCE in soil gas issue.  Most likely missed Jan07QM (should be WL or PEN).  Asked for rept by 7May07, other info. due 18 May07

Reports due 31 January 2008, if none, time for enforcement?
Washington County performed investigation in May 2008 and a round of groundwater sampling.  Should get a report this summer.  May need to do enforcement on RP, pending how things turn out.  Been trying to work things out through County, will need follow-up pending the potential transaction.  my suggestion was if no enforcement, have RP sample extra on back end to make up for missed events.

10.2017:  The City of Tigard completed a site investigation using brownfield funds received by EPA. The investigation included collecting soil, soil vapor, indoor air, and groundwater samples from the Washington County/Hoffarber and Yoo Properties. The report is available on WebDocs.

The investigation showed that indoor air concentrations in the adjacent residence to the south (downgradient) had levels of TPH-Dx at 830 ug/m3, which is above the residential RBC of 100 ug/m3. It shoudl be noted that a heating oil tank is located in the basement. DEQ and Washington Dept. of Health notified the property owner of the result and suggested that they limit time in the basement and service the HOT to determine if it was properly vented. It should also be noted that a sump is located in the basement due to the very shallow water table.

DEQ has not determined the source of the indoor air concentration, but is engaging with Washington County (property owners of the Hoffarber property) to conduct additional investigation that shoudl include: soil vapor and groundwater samples upgradient of the Yoo Property. Previous investigations did not include diesel analysis (only gasoline and constituents).",,,19582.0,0.0,RHOOD,2018-09-20 09:25:58.280
