10659,20-98-7017,20,98,7017,3094.0,1998-05-19,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Elmira Family Store,88773 TERRITORIAL RD,ELMIRA,97437,(541) 935-7537,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,1.0,False,False,False,False,False,Pjt Mgr = DRB Site re-opened on : 2/19/2009 By Elizabeth Clark. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 1/31/2004.,Environmental Cleanup Site Information (ECSI) as site number 4037,"A petroleum release was reported to DEQ in 1998 during a site investigation. DEQ assigned leaking underground storage tank (LUST) number 20-98-7017. The site is also listed in DEQ’s Environmental Cleanup Site Information (ECSI) as site number 4037. The station’s underground storage tanks were removed in 1999. Private domestic wells supply drinking water for this site and for all surrounding properties. A down gradient residential well has recently(2010) been impacted by petroleum contamination believed to be associated with the Elmira Family Store site. That well has now been abandoned and a new improved-design drinking water well installed by DEQ. The full extent and degree of impacts to soil, groundwater, and drinking water in the area have been adequately defined. Two rounds pf petroleum vapor intrusion into buildings sampling have been completed. Based on the results of air, soil-vapor, and seasonal groundwater monitoring, risk-based conclusions that require on and off-site use restrictions and engineering controls have been made.  If the engineered and institutional controls are put into place on and off-site and the current land and water use stay the same, the remaining contamination was determined to no longer pose a threat to human health, safety or the environment.",20067.0,0.0,JGLASS,2019-01-09 16:23:10.683
