9/25/18 Entered F.I.R. date - JClaussen",,"The site was historically used as an automotive repair and fueling facility from at least 1946 into the 1980s. Leaks in underground storage tanks and at the fuel dispenser appear to be the cause of contamination. Soil and groundwater were historically impacted on the western half of the property and may have extended beneath the Highway 99 right-of-way. Three fuel tanks were decommissioned in 1998 and at that time about 20 cubic yards of impacted soil was excavated and disposed of at an unknown location. Recent sampling indicates that nearly all of the contamination appears to have naturally attenuated and remaining contamination is present at low levels, well below applicable Risk Based Concentrations in a few locations. The property is being redeveloped and expected to be used commercially and connected to municipal water.",88899.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2018-12-05 09:44:19.717
