10760,05-98-0435,05,98,0435,4245.0,1998-06-12,1999-03-18 13:49:10,LEATHERS OIL CO,50654 COLUMBIA RIVER HWY,SCAPPOOSE,97056,(503) 661-1244,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"1/7/03:  response from consultant.  does not want to conduct shallow aquifer test.

There is an on-site shallow drinking water well within feet of known groundwater contamination.  I requested that they resample the monitoring wells and drinking water well.  Past well sampling has not shown impacts to drinking water. However, there appears to be a threat based on older data.  Marty indicates sampling was done in 2010 but has not presented report.  7/22/2010 LLC

In April 2011, DEQ solicited comment from nearby property owners concerning investigation and cleanup performed at this site.  In May 2011,DEQ was contaced by Robert Weber, owner of the property located at 33653 Johnson Landing Road. Mr. Weber cited concerns about residual constituent levels in MW-3 and the potential they could impact his water wel.    In response, in January 2012, MSBA advanced a boring down-gradient of MW-3 and converted it to a temporary monitoring well.  Groundwater from this boring did not exhbit detectable levels of petroleum hydrocarbons.  Also in January 2012, the Oregon Health Authority's Drinking Water Program added VOCs to the required analytical methods for annual sampling (the site water well is within 100 feet of an operating UST system) and this samplking is required for the Construction Standard Waiver.  (JKS 11-7-12).

Presented propsoed closure to Manager in February 2013.  Management indicated that a sample must be collected from the down-gradient drinking water well at Weber-Farrell property (33653 Johnson Landing Road).  The well was sampled on March 12, 2013.  VOCs were not detected in the sample.  Also in March 2013, the Hydrogeologist approved the proposed closure.  It was necesary to modify the BWUD and exposre pathway sections. (JKS 4-24-13)",,,11478.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2013-04-24 12:33:10.873
