11162,34-98-0701,34,98,0701,16.0,1998-08-27,1999-03-18 13:49:10,WEST BEAVERTON SANITARY SERVICE,5320 SW ALGER ST,BEAVERTON,97075,(503) 645-2140,False,1.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"A 6,000-gallon diesel UST and a 2,000-gallon gasoline UST were decommissioned by removal from this site in August 1998.  Five soil samples from the walls of the excavation pit were ND by HCID; however, 111 ppm diesel was detected in a stockpile soil sample.  Groundwater entered the excavation pit at 9 ft bgs and initially showed 1,100 ppb TPH and 139 ppb benzene.  A 4"" observation well was installed in the backfilled pit, and after a total of 5,000 gallons of groundwater were pumped from the well, no TPH or BTEX was detected in the groundwater in October 1998.

No soil samples were collected beneath the tanks or the dispensers, and the wall samples should have been analyzed for Dx after the diesel detection in the stockpile.  In addition, the observation well was not registered or otherwise documented, so the groundwater results are suspect.  Additional soil and groundwater sampling is needed before this site can be closed.  (6/28/10 TMB)",,,17941.0,0.0,KDANA,2010-11-03 08:24:07.923
