11331,26-98-0824,26,98,0824,6460.0,1998-09-28,1999-03-18 13:49:10,DOLLAR RENT A CAR,9105 NE AIRPORT WAY,PORTLAND,97220,(503) 249-4797,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"1 gas & 2 oil decommission by removal in 98.  Soil & GW Contamination found.  2 limited SA completed.  Significantplume under Dollarfacility with benzene up to 48, 500ppb detected.  Indoor air benzne monitoring & ventilation.  SVE and ozone sparge system installed.  monitoring shows levels of benzene and gasoline in indoor air okay.  Submitted CAP, DEQ and Port commented.  High naphthalene needs to be addressed.  BBE, consultant, did not agree with requested modeling of groundwater, and suggested CAP is only draft screening levels.  DEQ requires complete CAP with proposed cleanup levels. LLC 7/2010.  Work plan for investigation received 7-21-11 (JKS 7-25-11).  Active remediation suspended after October 2011 event. BB&A proposes additional quarterly monitoring.  

In October 2012, BB&A performed a second injection event using the BOS-200 product.  As a result of the previous remediation via ISCO, SVE and AS, as well as the injections to promote enhanced bioremediation, levels of gasoline and VOCs in MW-9 went to non-detect.  In addition, the footprint of the groundwater plume contracted significantly, with the remainder in the area between MW-6 and MW-7 north of the site building. 

Indoor air sampling performed generally prior to remedation revealed benzene at levels above occupational RBCs. Later air sampling (2011-2012) completed near the end of remediation, generally revealed benzene below the applicable RBCs for indoor air.   Two rounds of sub-slab sampling did not reveal gasoline or VOCs at levels above occupational worker RBCs. 

Site is located in the Portland Wellfield.  Groundwater Modeling performed for an adjacent LUST site (former National Car Rental 26-91-0431) resulted in the calculation of maximum allowable source area concetnrations (MASACs) for the shallowest grounwater, assumign the installatino of hypothetical production wells screened in the CRSA/TGA.  Although groundwater containing gasoline exceeding construction/excavatino worker RBC (14,000 ppb) remains in MW-6/MW-7, the detections are below the applicable MASAC.  The City of Portland BES and Water Bureau were allowed to comment on the proposed clsoure.  No comments indicating they did not concur with the risk evaluatino for groundwater in the wellfield were received by DEQ. 

BB&A prepared a CMMP to manage risks from soil/groundwater contamiantion encountered in the future.   Staff Memo approved and uploaded to LUST database. (JKS 3-12-15)",,"1 gas & 2 oil decommission by removal in 98.  Soil & GW Contamination found.  2 limited SA completed.  Significantplume under Dollarfacility with benzene up to 48, 500ppb detected.  Indoor air benzne monitoring & ventilation.  SVE and ozone sparge system installed.  monitoring shows levels of benzene and gasoline in indoor air okay.  Submitted CAP, DEQ and Port commented.  High naphthalene needs to be addressed.  BBE, consultant, did not agree with requested modeling of groundwater, and suggested CAP is only draft screening levels.  DEQ requires complete CAP with proposed cleanup levels. LLC 7/2010.  Work plan for investigation received 7-21-11 (JKS 7-25-11).  Active remediation suspended after October 2011 event. BB&A proposes additional quarterly monitoring.  

In October 2012, BB&A performed a second injection event using the BOS-200 product.  As a result of the previous remediation via ISCO, SVE and AS, as well as the injections to promote enhanced bioremediation, levels of gasoline and VOCs in MW-9 went to non-detect.  In addition, the footprint of the groundwater plume contracted significantly, with the remainder in the area between MW-6 and MW-7 north of the site building. 

Indoor air sampling performed generally prior to remedation revealed benzene at levels above occupational RBCs. Later air sampling (2011-2012) completed near the end of remediation, generally revealed benzene below the applicable RBCs for indoor air.   Two rounds of sub-slab sampling did not reveal gasoline or VOCs at levels above occupational worker RBCs. 

Site is located in the Portland Wellfield.  Groundwater Modeling performed for an adjacent LUST site (former National Car Rental 26-91-0431) resulted in the calculation of maximum allowable source area concetnrations (MASACs) for the shallowest grounwater, assumign the installatino of hypothetical production wells screened in the CRSA/TGA.  Although groundwater containing gasoline exceeding construction/excavatino worker RBC (14,000 ppb) remains in MW-6/MW-7, the detections are below the applicable MASAC.  The City of Portland BES and Water Bureau were allowed to comment on the proposed clsoure.  No comments indicating they did not concur with the risk evaluatino for groundwater in the wellfield were received by DEQ. 

BB&A prepared a CMMP to manage risks from soil/groundwater contamiantion encountered in the future.   Staff Memo approved and uploaded to LUST database. (JKS 3-12-15)",9324.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2015-03-23 08:59:31.863
