11435,29-93-0093,29,93,0093,788.0,1993-05-18,1999-03-18 13:49:10,G & G MINI MART,203 GARIBALDI AVE E,GARIBALDI,97118,(503) 322-3287,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Two 1,000-gallon gasoline USTs were removed from the site in July 1993.  Soil and shallow groundwater contamination were encountered, but the RP was unable to pay for further investigation and cleanup.  DEQ paid to have 29 tons of stockpiled PCS removed in February 1995.  Subsequent owners / operators also had an inability to pay.

A viable RP acquired the site in November 2007 and launched their own investigation and cleanup.  Four monitoring wells were installed in April 2008, and three additional USTs were removed in September 2008, along with 156 tons of PCS.  A report summarizing the removals and four quarters of groundwater monitoring was received in December 2009.  Additional documentation of the extent of residual contamination was received in June 2010 and February 2011.  Residual soil contamination is generally below the groundwater table (at 3 ft bgs) and the groundwater does not appear to be tidally influenced or migrating to any significant extent.",,,18488.0,0.0,LKENT,2011-08-02 07:07:08.837
