11503,26-95-0269,26,95,0269,11512.0,1995-10-12,1999-03-18 13:49:10,BLUE SKY FILTERS (DUPLICATE),2833 NE SANDY BLVD,PORTLAND,97232,,False,,,3.0,ADMCLO,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,ECSI #2054 and LUST #26-95-0267,Two leaking USTs at this site were reported separately to DEQ in October 1995: a heating oil tank (26-95-0267) and a solvent tank (26-95-0269).  DEQ consolidated the project under the first file number and administratively closed the second file number.,9581.0,0.0,KDANA,2018-05-16 09:58:01.650
11504,26-95-0267,26,95,0267,11512.0,1995-10-12,1999-03-18 13:49:10,"BLUE SKY FILTERS, INC.",2833 NE SANDY BLVD,PORTLAND,97232,,False,,MATRIX,3.0,,True,False,False,,False,True,False,False,False,,ECSI #2054 and LUST #26-95-0269,"A 750-gallon fuel oil UST and a 275-gallon Stoddard solvent UST were decommissioned by removal from this site in October 1995.  The solvent tank was located beneath the floor of a former dry cleaning building, and hand-excavations of contaminated soils proceeded gradually from October 1995 to March 1996 to prevent undermining the building.  The excavation ultimately extended out the back of the building and encompassed the fuel oil tank pit.  A total of 16 tons of contaminated soils were removed.  Because PCE, a dry cleaning solvent, was detected in the soil, the LUST file was administratively closed and the site referred to the Cleanup program in June 1997 for further action.  See ECSI #2054 for more information on this site.",9581.0,0.0,KDANA,2018-05-16 09:34:58.100
