ConococPhillips also RP for second release reported in 2007 after site assessment - C. Rodda, 6/4/2010",ConocoPhillips LUST#20-07-1918 (Phillips 66 agreed to cover drinking water issues for cleanup project - CJB 5/10/2018),"Four USTs  were removed in November 1998, and consisted of two 10,000-gallon gasoline, one 10,000-gallon diesel, and one 8,000-gallon gasoline tanks. As part of cleanup activities, 460 cubic yards of petroleum contaminated was removed from beneath the dispenser islands and an additional 50 cubic yards from the tank cavity. Groundwater monitoring wells have been installed at the site, but water is not consistently available in the wells. The fuel service station temporarily ceased operating in 2008. In June 2010, contractors began additional remedial actions of excavating petroleum-contaminated soil that was not accessible during station operations. Excavation was completed up to 19.5 feet bgs, and over 1300 tons of contaminated soil was removed from the site. Groundwater monitoring, private drinking water well sampling, and other assessment activities occurred at and near the site from 2011-2018. Phillips 66 agreed to annual testing through 2021 of adjacent property drinking water wells as a precaution.",31072.0,0.0,CJBROWN,2018-05-10 09:13:51.440
