11802,22-98-4187,22,98,4187,9196.0,1998-11-16,1999-03-18 13:49:10,USA Mini Mart #1,1306 MAIN ST,SWEET HOME,97386,(541) 367-3916,False,,,,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : SUSPECTED RELEASE - WILL CONDUCT TTT ON SYSTEM. RELEASE NOW CONFIRMED.  12/8/1998 *** vapors in sanitary sewer.  Crack in a shear valve found.  Repairs made and vapor problem appears under control.  Delineation of soil contamination needed. EPA grant letter sent 4/13/2006... TMD,,"The contamination was discovered due to a complaint from the Sweet Home Public Works Department. On 11/16/98 first responders were called including the Sweet Home Fire Dept. A neighbor smelled gas coming from their shower (location not specified). A nearby sewer manhole showed a 10% LEL reading and the next sewer manhole approximately 3 blocks away and behind the A&W restaurant showed a 23 % LEL reading. There were gas odors in neighboring businesses (locations not specified). A crack in a shear valve dispenser was found. Repairs were made at that time; however, the initial owner did not have money for the investigation. A subsequent owner pulled out all of the tanks and found two unknown ones in 2007.  Some of the tanks had holes in them. However, due to the cost of this work, this owner also did not perform an investigation, and while the DEQ was in the process of placing a lien on the site, it was sold. The new current owner hired a consultant and monitoring wells have been installed.  However as of the fall of 2012, the full extent of the contaminationi is still being assessed.",17766.0,0.0,TDANOVI,2012-10-22 16:35:48.847
11803,21-98-4193,21,98,4193,568.0,1998-12-01,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Burnt Woods Store,25 HARLAN BURNTWOODS RD,BLODGETT,97326,(541) 453-4641,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"was assigned to JLP; deassigned 4/5/04.
Domestic well was sampled according to 2002 report. Score may need to be adjusted by Project Manager.
Update-AF- Resampled drinking water well in Dec.2018.  All good. same as 2002, but with lower detection levels.  Site ready for closure.",,"In November 1998 the Burnt Woods Store owners took three underground storage tanks, containing gasoline and diesel, out of service. They also removed the dispenser island and associated piping and replaced the whole system with two aboveground storage tanks. During removal of the tanks, the contractor also removed approximately 40 tons of soil, but some petroleum-contaminated soil remained at the site. 
In December of 1998, the onsite water well was sampled.  Then again in January of 2002, the onsite well and a nearby neighbor’s well was sampled.  Finally in 2018, the onsite well was sampled again.  There were no detections in either of the wells above cleanup levels. Given these results, we have no indication of any movement of contamination into the water or off the property. DEQ believes that after 20 years the volume of remaining soil  contamination is negligible.  Please see the NFA Staff Memo, Oct 24, 2018, for more detail.",153608.0,0.0,GDECK,2019-04-17 13:56:46.063
