11893,15-98-0087,15,98,0087,6796.0,1998-12-21,1999-03-18 13:49:10,GEORGE GROOM TRUCKING INC,6898 CRATER LAKE HIGHWAY,WHITE CITY,97503,(541) 664-3925,False,8.0,POCKET,4.0,NFA,True,False,,,False,,,,,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : 1900 PPM TPH-G, DIESEL TANK RELEASE, PLAN TO DO SOME REMEDIAL EXCAVATION NEXT YEAR (1999) *** GW not impacted beyond pit, PCS treatment in-progress.  Cleanup of PCS completed. Soil placed onsite",,,22576.0,,MBELSKY,2000-12-21 14:13:53.000
11894,15-98-0088,15,98,0088,4083.0,1998-12-22,1999-03-18 13:49:10,WESTERN OIL&BURNER MEDFORD/ RETER FRUIT,5 S STAGE RD,MEDFORD,97501,(541)779-1389,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : 3 TANKS FILLED WITH SAND IN 1987.  GW IMPACTED WITH BTEX DISCOVERED IN SITE ASSESSMENT. *** 3 tanks filled w/ sand in 1986.  GW impacted w/ BTEX discovered in site assessment.,,"The site is located in Medford at 5 South Stage Road and operated as a Western Oil and Burner service station from the 1950s until 1986 when the property was purchased by Reter Fruit Company. The facility is now used as office space for a commercial operation. Observations during borehole installation in 2007 identified silt and sands with some clay and gravel to 17.5 feet below ground surface. Groundwater was encountered at 9 to 13 feet bgs, and has been recorded in site monitoring wells at 3 to 11 feet bgs. Groundwater flow direction has generally been recorded to the northeast. As part of decommissioning activities in 2001, WSE excavated 1,500 cubic yards of petroleum-contaminated soil. Eight confirmation soil samples were collected at the excavation limits and analyzed for gasoline- and diesel-range hydrocarbons. Gasoline was detected in soil at 3,700 parts per million, and diesel was 1,600 ppm.  Four monitoring wells (MW-1 through MW-4) were installed to 15 feet bgs in October 1998. Soil samples were not collected during well construction. The initial groundwater sampling event detected benzene at 1,310 parts per billion, toluene at 2,750 ppb, ethylbenzene at 900 ppb, and xylenes at 4,750 ppb in MW-3.  Concentrations of gasoline constituents increased in wells at the next sampling event in March 2001. Well MW-4 was abandoned in 2001. EMS installed two additional monitoring wells (MW-5 and MW-6) in October 2001. Soil samples did not contain gasoline, BTEX, or naphthalene above detection levels. Quarterly monitoring was initiated in May 2003. Five borings (B1 through B5) were advanced in May 2007 to collect soil samples for a risk-based site evaluation, analyzed for petroleum-related VOCs and lead. Relatively low concentrations of several VOCs were detected in soil, and gasoline was 470 ppm in soil from B3.",20740.0,0.0,CRODDA,2013-01-07 10:17:29.363
