11907,34-98-1109,34,98,1109,,1998-12-28,1999-03-18 13:49:10,COLE PROPERTY,16186 SW 1ST ST,SHERWOOD,97140,,False,4.0,GW,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** New address is 16186 SW 1st St. (was 375 NW 1st St.)  (8/2015-RAH)


5.3.2015: no comments from the City.  Short staff memo uploaded to database and in file.  Working on nfa. (RAH)

3/24/16: notice letter to City sherwood, due 4/24.  staff memo is mostly represented by Marty Burck.  need to draft final nfa. (RAH)

6/16/2015:  no work done since Bijan retired.  See my message to Marty Burck dated 2/24/2015, that highlights next steps.  needs follow-up (RAH)


A service station operated at this site until 1956.  In December 1998, two 1,000-gallon gasoline USTs were removed, along with 675.86 tons of PCS.  Groundwater was encountered 9-20 ft bgs.  Contamination remained in all four excavation sidewalls, but further removal was limited by First Street to the north and Main Street to the west.  Eight borings were advanced around the excavation in September 1999 to determine the extent.  Residual contamination (up to 14,800 ppm gasoline) was found to be concentrated beneath the former service island.

Five groundwater monitoring wells were installed in April 2000.  At about the same time, 242 tons of PCS were removed from around the former service island.  The monitoring wells were sampled quarterly in 2001 and 2002.  In June 2003, the contractor proposed collecting soil vapor samples prior to completing a Conceptual Site Model.  DEQ felt the sampling would be insufficient.  A revised Corrective Action Plan was finally received in September 2006, basically proposing two soil vapor sampling locations instead of one.  The CAP was approved in January 2007.

No reports have been received since this time.  The site was backlogged at the end of 2007 when Bijan Pour retired.  (8/18/10 KPD)",,8/19/2015:  Note address was changed from 275 NW 1st St. to 16186 SW 1st St.,33113.0,0.0,RHOOD,2016-05-03 10:30:42.953
