12130,21-99-4009,21,99,4009,8648.0,1999-01-28,1999-03-18 13:49:10,B & B Market & Gas,315 S GAITHER ST,SILETZ,97380,(541)444-1010,False,7.0,MATRIX,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,FA GRANT PROJECT.  FOUR TANKS DECOMMISSIONED BY REMOVAL.  9 TONS OF PCS TO RIVERBEND LANDFILL.  SEVEN CONFIRMATORY SOIL SAMPLES AND PIT WATER SAMPLES.  SOIL MATRIX CLOSURE,,,88880.0,0.0,GDECK,2016-08-31 11:34:13.390
12131,22-99-4010,22,99,4010,3616.0,1999-01-29,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Albany Cardlock,236 E 1ST AVE,ALBANY,97321,(503) 682-3865,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,Cleanup measures undertaken between 2005 and 2010 to address petroleum hydrocarbons in soil and groundwater.  Possible future exposure to soil contamination that exceeds DEQ's Risk-Based Concentrations for indoor air exposure will be addressed by an institutional control.  DEQ will require that any future site development must include vapor barrier installation to mitigate possible petroleum vapor intrusion.  Future site excavation work will also need to incorporate appropriate contaminated soil handling measures.,20418.0,0.0,GAITKEN,2014-01-28 08:37:55.110
12132,24-99-4013,24,99,4013,11927.0,1999-02-02,1999-03-18 13:49:10,"Berg & Son, Inc.",14554 MARQUAM ROAD,MOUNT ANGEL,97362,(503) 873-5238,False,7.0,MATRIX,4.0,NFA,True,False,,,False,,,,,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : 2 USTS... FARM TANKS; SAW ONLY CONTAMINATION UNDERNEATH THE GAS UST.  WILL BE DOING TEST PITS ON SAT 2/6/99 TO DELINEATE CONTAMINATION.  OWNER DOING THE SITE WORK. *** DECOMMISSIONED BY REMOVAL A 1000 GAL GAS AND 1000 GAL DIESEL UST WITH SCRAP TAKEN TO CHERRY CITY METALS.  425 GALS OF TANK CONTENTS TAKEN TO OIL PRODUCTS IN MT ANGEL.  306 TONS PCS TAKEN TO MARION COUNTY SOIL RECYCLING NEAR WOODBURN.  NO GROUNDWATER.,,,31779.0,,CONV,2004-01-26 09:03:26.000
12133,27-99-4014,27,99,4014,11597.0,1999-02-03,1999-03-18 13:49:10,R.B. Shell,2385 SALEM & DALLAS HWY NW,SALEM,97304,(503) 371-1758,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,NFA,True,False,,,False,,,,,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : HISTORIC RELEASE? SYSTEM UPGRADED.  THE TANKS ARE CURRENTLY IN USE.  TANKS ARE LINED AND THE RELEASE MAY HAVE OCCURRED PRIOR TO LINING. *** ORIGINAL RELEASE REPORTED 2/3/99 AS RESULT OF SA.  3 GW MONITORING WELLS INSTALLED.  4 QTRS GW DATA COLLECTED.  SITE IN COMPLINCE WITH ALL RBCs FOR ALL PATHWAYS EXCEPT FOR 1,2,4 TRIMETHYLBENZENE IN TAPWATER @ 34 PPB VERSUS RBC OF 16 PPB.",,,24395.0,,GDECK,2001-08-09 15:05:26.000
12134,24-99-4017,24,99,4017,3840.0,1999-02-11,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Ball Bros Chevron,5325 DENVER ST SE,TURNER,97392,(503) 743-2125,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : WASTE OIL IMPACTS MORE THAN LIKELY DUE TO PAST PRACTICES (INDUSTRIAL). *** some soil impacts observed in secord st. west of site during sewer line repair by city of turner...2-11-2000...jlg,,"Petroleum contamination was initially reported to DEQ in January 1999 when petroleum contamination was observed during the decommissioning by removal of two underground storage systems.  In May 1999 a third tank was decommissioned by removal west of the initial decommissioning site. During the decommissioning and subsequent cleanup the owner had an estimated 260 cubic yards of contaminated soil removed.  The petroleum contaminated soil was transported to an off-site property where it was treated to acceptable levels and reused. Contamination was observed throughout the former tank pits and was documented to have impacted both soil and groundwater. 

After review of the soil and groundwater sample results, the property owner conducted an investigation to determine the extent of the contamination on the subject property. This included installation of four groundwater monitoring wells in September 2000 and quarterly groundwater monitoring.  In 2008, the current property owner expanded the investigation by installing a series of push-probe sampling points and a fifth groundwater monitoring well. Quarterly groundwater monitoring continued through 2009.  

Based on the results of the completed cleanup actions, the on-site monitoring and off-site investigations, and risk-assessment of the remain areas of contaminated soil and groundwater, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land uses, the remaining contamination has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment. The proposed plan would allow any remaining contamination to naturally degrade in place.",20593.0,0.0,GDECK,2010-12-23 16:17:20.967
12135,24-99-4019,24,99,4019,681.0,1999-02-17,1999-03-18 13:49:10,Quick Stop Fuel,3498 PRINGLE RD SE,SALEM,97302,(503)364-5250,False,1.0,LOWIMP,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,property may have transferred to new ownership recently (10/10/02) requested Mod-app for USTs and further assessment for possible LIS closure,,"The service station building was constructed in 1952 and the current USTs were installed in 1976 and 1980 respectively. The site has operated since that time as some combination of service and/or fueling station. Soil and soil gases on the property are impacted with gasoline, diesel and related constituents.  Borings installed to a maximum depth of 31 feet did not encounter groundwater when left open several hours. Shallow groundwater is not believed to be impacted. A previous owner reportedly removed an unknown amount of petroleum contaminated soil from around the tanks and disposed of it at the Columbia Ridge Landfill. No other documentation, including confirmation sampling on this removal is available. Additional soil borings have delineated the full vertical and horizontal extent of contamination. Contaminated soil remains onsite from about five to ten feet below ground in the vicinity of the fuel dispenser, USTs, and extending to approximately the eastern property boundary. The remaining contamination is below applicable screening levels.
•    The site is expected to remain an occupational facility and service station surrounded by residences, all of which are expected to remain connected to municipal water. If the property is redeveloped into a residential or urban residential space further investigation and/or remediation will be required. The property owner and residents to the east were given an opportunity to comment on the proposed closure because contamination approaches the property line. No comments were received.",55577.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2018-04-13 11:14:41.600
