12211,26-99-0182,26,99,0182,,1999-02-26,1999-03-18 13:49:10,ODOT REGION 1 PARCEL 2C,SE SALMON ST / MAIN ST / WATER AVE / I-5,PORTLAND,97214,,True,1.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"ODOT and Hart Crowser investigated 18 parcels between SE Water Ave and the Willamette River in Portland in 1999 as part of the Eastbank Riverfront Project.  Parcel 2C was bounded by SE Salmon St, Main St, Water Ave, and Interstate 5.  ODOT previously had removed 5 USTs and 350 cubic yards of PCS from two UST pits at the site in 1993.  This LUST site focused on the discovery of two ""asphalt batch plant USTs"" in February 1999.  The USTs were removed but sampling found up to 10,800 ppm diesel and 13,300 ppm heavy oil in the soil.  No removal was apparently conducted.

In May 2001 two individual waste oil USTs were removed from the site, and an NFA was issued in April 2002.  (See LUST #26-01-0026).  In November 2001 Hart Crowser recommended additional soil and groundwater sampling around the two 1993 UST pits and the asphalt batch plant pit in preparation for a risk-based closure.  ODOT submitted a report in January 2005 that may or may not have covered all the bases.  (See LUST #26-92-0020 for a copy of the report).

This project should be completed in conjunction with 26-92-0020, both of which are open and backlogged.  (10/28/10 KPD)",LUST #26-92-0020 and #26-01-0026,,32003.0,0.0,KDANA,2010-10-28 14:18:05.830
