dba JOY TRAVEL PLAZA","10/17/2002-file transfered to Bend; assigned to J Klemz

9/9/11-file returned to The Dalles. LC
This was LUST 01-99-0011.  County was Baker then changed to Malheur which changed LUST to 23-99-0011.","Based on environmental investigations, hazardous substances present in soil and groundwater at the subject property are attributable to leaking underground storage tanks at the site location vicinity of Latitude 44°17'33.0"" North, Longitude 117°13'25.9""West.  

Contaminants include gasoline, diesel and petroleum constituent compounds.  Affected media include subsurface soil and groundwater. Horizontal and vertical extent of contamination extends beyond the excavated tank pit at Latitude 44°17'33.0"" North, Longitude 117°13'25.9""West.  

Do not place groundwater wells in the vicinity of the contaminant source area at Latitude 44°17'33.0"" North, Longitude 117°13'25.9""West (see Figure 2 in the NFA letter).  Providing clean & safe drinking water to on-site workers and the traveling public is the responsibility of the site owner.

Contaminated groundwater should not be utilized for any beneficial purpose in the general area of the leaking underground storage tanks at Latitude 44°17'33.0"" North, Longitude 117°13'25.9""West.

Dissolved contamination remaining in groundwater indicates groundwater in the vicinity of the contaminant source area at Latitude 44°17'33.0"" North, Longitude 117°13'25.9""West should not be used for beneficial purposes or groundwater should be further characterized to prove it does not represent a threat to human health. Additional cleanup and/or disposal requirements will be needed in the event that unanticipated changes to land or groundwater use occur in the vicinity of the leaking underground storage tanks or if the remaining contamination is disturbed or removed from the ground.

Under Oregon's Risk Based Decision Making process that evaluates exposure pathways for site contaminant concentrations in environmental media, site conditions are currently protective of public health, safety and the environment under Oregon Cleanup Rules for Leaking UST Systems.",11295.0,0.0,CKENNED,2019-12-05 07:27:32.810
