12393,26-98-1133,26,98,1133,7317.0,1998-10-26,1999-04-14 09:20:01,"K.F. JACOBSEN & CO., INC.",1208 N RIVER ST,PORTLAND,97227,(503) 239-5532,False,1.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Four soil samples and a groundwater sample were collected around a 10,000-gallon gasoline UST at this site in September 1998 prior to filling the tank in place.  (The tank could not be removed because it was partially underneath a 10,000-gallon diesel AST).  Diesel and heavy oil were detected in all four soil samples, at concentrations up to 4,970 ppm diesel and 8,750 ppm heavy oil.  TPH (5,340 ppb) was detected in the shallow groundwater.  The gasoline UST was decommissioned in place in February 1999.  The RP attributed the detections to contaminated fill rather than a tank release, and decided not to proceed with an investigation due to ""current economic conditions"".  DEQ agreed in March 2003 that the site was a low priority.  (8/17/10 KPD)",,,4969.0,0.0,KDANA,2010-08-17 09:05:54.710
