12457,22-99-4053,22,99,4053,1970.0,1999-04-15,1999-04-23 13:21:29,Plaza Gas CC #17,2812 SANTIAM HWY SE,ALBANY,97321,(541) 926-1817,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : 12 SAMPLES 1310, 112 HEAVY OIL, ALL OTHER SAMPLES HAD TPH-G DETECTIONS.  HARDING-LAWSON ASS.351 ROLLING OAKS DR, SUITE 100, THOUSAND OAKS, CA 91361. *** BENZENE CONTAMINATION IN GW TO 482 PPB.  ADDITIONAL DOWNGRADIENT DEFINITION REQUESTED 5-1-00. Site re-opened on : 12/19/2013 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 6/27/2013.",,"(MOTT 07/11/17) A retail service station utilizing one 2,000-gallon gasoline, one 4,000-gallon gasoline, and one 12,000-gallon gasoline UST operated at the site from 1966 to 2002. Operations ceased at the site in 2002 and all three USTs were removed. During the UST removal approximately 794 tons of petroleum impacted soil and 2,000-gallons of pit water were removed from the site. Numerous assessments have been conducted at the site between 1998 and 2015, including evaluation of offsite impacts. Soil, groundwater, and soil gas data was collected during these assessments. In 2015, a water-based slurry mixture of petrophyllic bacteria and BOS 200® was injected at 62 points along the south side of the Santiam Highway. Groundwater contaminant concentration trends indicate that natural attenuation is occurring, future off-site contaminant migration is unlikely, and contaminant concentrations should continue to decline.  However, impacts reamain in the ODOT right-of-way and future excavation work will likely require worker protection in the form dermal protection, ventilation, and possibly respiratory protection.  The responsible party (Truax) signed ODOT's License and Agreement for contamination remaining in the right-of-way. A CMMP (dated 8/29/11) and EES (dated 4/1/13) serve as requirements for the conditional closure determination for this site. The site was issued a Conditional NFA on 8/28/17.",19299.0,0.0,GDECK,2017-09-13 09:23:07.643
