12554,06-99-0026,06,99,0026,1378.0,1999-05-11,1999-05-11 14:49:44,CRAIG & CRAIG INC DBA TNT MARKET,899 D St,COOS BAY,97420,(541) 267-2409,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"PCS hauled off-site, GW sampled beneath pit bottom w/low hit of benzene, need further assessment.
Project Deassignment letter sent 11-6-2012.",,"The site has reportedly operated as a market since the 1950s. The first underground storage tanks were installed at the site in 1971 and the USTs were upgraded in 1999. The cause of the release reported in 1999 was overfills, due to contaminated soil being found above the tanks during decommissioning. Soil, groundwater, and soil gases are impacted with gasoline and related components beneath the south end of the site and the southern half of the vacant lot to the west. At the time of UST decommissioning, 150 cubic yards of contaminated soil were excavated and disposed of at the Roseburg Landfill. New upgraded tanks were then installed in the old UST pit in 1999. Contaminated soil remains in the southern half of the site and the west adjacent vacant lot from about 12 feet below ground extending down to about 30 feet (see attached figure). The limited groundwater available in the area flows in thin seams beginning at 12 to 13 feet below ground. Groundwater contamination does not extend beyond the known extent of soil contamination. The store and nearby properties are connected to city water and the area is expected to continue to use municipal water.  The land use in the vicinity of the site is expected to remain primarily residential. An opportunity to comment on the proposed closure was given to the neighboring property owners and the City of Coos Bay. No Comments were received. Final NFA letter was issued April 30, 2021.",18873.0,0.0,JCLAWSO,2021-05-13 11:31:59.733
