12631,01-99-0016,01,99,0016,6447.0,1999-05-13,1999-05-25 14:53:13,STRATTON'S STORE,107 MAIN ST,UNITY,97884,(541) 446-3421,False,4.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : PETRO SERVICES DOING SAMPLING 6-3-99 J. KRUCK - KES - ASSITSTING WITH OVEREXCAVATION DISCOVERED GW IMPACT. ***,10/17/2002-file transfered to Bend office,"Past site use is retail fueling station with underground storage tanks (USTs).
Cause of contamination is petroleum fuels leaking from USTs.
In October of 2017, subsurface explorations were completed at 22 locations via direct push soil borings and temporary well installations for the collection of subsurface soil and groundwater samples. Groundwater samples were collected from a subset of 12 boring locations.
Contaminated media include subsurface soil, soil gas and groundwater.
Contamination left in place include petroleum and petroleum chemical compounds.
Land use assumptions include continued site operations as a retail fueling station (occupational use). The site is zoned Residential Commercial, which allows for residential and commercial land use. 
Groundwater is contaminated.  Water use assumptions include city water supplied to the site.
The no further action (NFA) determination is conditional on the following: if site use changes to residential use, additional investigation and risk assessment shall be conducted regarding contaminant concentrations in subsurface soil, soil gas and groundwater.  The site is currently un-remediated.  
Additional site investigation shall either demonstrate an absence of unacceptable health-based risks associated with residential exposure pathways or the contamination should be abated by contaminant mass removal or installation of engineered mitigation and control systems.  A deed notice has been placed on this property to memorialize these conditions.
DEQ notes that shallow groundwater at the Site is contaminated and should not be utilized for beneficial purposes.  Soil and groundwater samples impacted by petroleum hydrocarbons have been encountered at the site, primarily in the immediate vicinity of the former USTs.",39962.0,0.0,KROBERT,2018-05-08 09:03:22.257
