13504,03-99-1185,03,99,1185,300.0,1999-10-19,1999-10-20 13:47:43,BUCKEROO FORD INC,213 W MAIN ST,MOLALLA,97038,(503) 829-2391,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"6/30/03:  Council of Gov't has property.  Plan is to establish the car dealership, then come talk to DEQ about additional work.
Contamination discovered in right-of-way adjacent to site in 1999.  Contamination traced to site property.  Approximately 1,000 cubic yards of contaminated soil was removed from an excavation in the southwest corner of the site property.  Soil and groundwater contamination found to extend under the building and adjacent to the building.  Soil-gas sampling performed in 2002 in shop area of building revealed extremely elevated levels of VOCs.
In June 2004, DEQ performed additional investigation of the site including installation of four monitoring wells. Highly contaminated groundwater documented in area of MW-4.  In 2008, an SVE system consisting of horizontal trenches was installed and operated for approximately one year.  Following deactivation in May 2009, a second round of soil-gas samples  were collected.  The system remained largely deactivated for the next 2-3 years. No detections above residential, urban residential or occupational worker RBCs were detected in the May 2009 samples.  System was reactivated and operated during business hours between June and August 2012.  An SVE exhaust sample contained benzene at a level  above the residential RBC for the soil gas vapor intrusion pathway.  Future commercial use likely, although residential use is conditionally allowed.  Due to groundwater containing benzene and gasoline at levels above construction/excavation worker RBCs for direct contact in excavations, a CMMP must be prepared prior to future intrusive work or development.  The NFA will have a condition that assumes future commercial use. (JKS 5-23-13).",ECSI #3991,,79129.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2013-05-23 11:04:29.057
