13580,36-99-4153,36,99,4153,8181.0,1999-11-01,1999-11-02 18:14:43,Morrison Oil,179 Hwy 99W    (1 MILE E OF DUNDEE),DUNDEE,97115,(503) 286-1673,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : PROPERTY IS (TAX LOT #3325BD-500), ON HIGHWAY 99W, 1 MILE EAST OF DUNDEE. *** Work plan requested to delineate GW impacts (B-3), submittal deadline 1-31-2006, rhr.
CRA submitted shows facility address as 179 Hwy 99W. - 5/15/2014 gdeck.

November 2014- Test pit investigation completed as per October 2014 work plan.  Test pits generally east of former fueling system did not exhibit evidence of soil contamination.  Groundwater samples from TP-3 revealed gasoline at 1,100 ppb and benzene at 0.2 ppb. Contaminated soil in area of test pit TP-2 was removed in November 2014.  137 tons were removed and transported to Riverbend Landfill in McMinnville. 

September 2015 - Soil gas monitoring points SGP-1 through SGP-3 installed.  SGP-2 detected gasoline TPH at 720,000 ug/m3.  The area around SGP-2 was flagged for a possible soil removal action. 

October 2015 - montoring wells MW-1 and MW-3 installed at the site to evaluate groundwater conditions.   During drilling of MW-2, boulders and cobbles were encountered and the well could not be installed. MW-4 was installed in an alternate location.  The initial sampling of the wells in November 2015 did not reveal detectable levels of gasoline or RBDM VOCs.  Quarterly groundwater monitoring was initiated in November 2015.

March 2016 - Wohlers submitted a workplan for the removal of additional soil from the area of SGP-2 and subsequent installation of SGP-4 to confirm removal of PCS. 

May 2016-  Wohlers supervised the removal of soil from the area east of the November 2014 remedial excavation.  Soil was removed to a maximum depth of 12 feet bgs. Confirmation sampling  did not reveal gasoline in soil at levels above 71 ppm and non-detect levels of VOCs. In addition, soil gas monitorng pont SGP-4 was installed near the remedial excavation. Gasoline and VOCs were detected in soil gas but at concentations below residential RBCs. 

Monitoring wells MW-1, MW-3 anmd MW-4 were sampled November 2015, March 2016, June 2016 and August 2016.  Monitoring wells MW-1 and MW-3 typically purged dry and would not recover following purging. As a result, samples from MW-1 and MW-3 were collected pre-purge. Gasoline and VOCs were not detected at levels above detection limits. 

WRD database searched revealed six wells within a 0.25 mile radius of the site.  Completion depths for the wells ranged from 190 to 644 feet bgs. Shallow, likely perched, groundwater is unlikely to impact deeper aquifers.  The city of Dundee confirmed connection to city water for properties in the vicintiy of the site. 

Approximtately 538 tons of contaminated soil was removed from the site between 1999 and 2016.  Based on the removal of significant source material and based on analysis of soil gas samples collected prior to and after the last removal event (May 2016), residual contamination does not pose unacceptable risks to likely future site occupants from vapor intrusion.  Apparent groundwater flow directions are variable and inconsistent with site topography.  This suggests that the wells may not reflect equilibrium water table conditions (i.e., perched conditions) (JKS 2-14-17)


Site is currently vacant.",,"

