13684,22-99-4171,22,99,4171,5267.0,1999-12-02,1999-12-03 15:52:40,Jack's Truck Stop,4196 SANTIAM SE,ALBANY,97321,(541)926-1989,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"During the 1999 UST #5 decommissioning approximately 33.49 tons (22.3 cubic yards) of petroleum-contaminated soil was removed and transported for treatment and disposal at the former United Soil Recycling facility in Woodburn, Oregon. Two gasoline and three diesel USTs remain in use at this facility.  Multiple site investigations were completed between 2007 and 2017 including installation of seven permanent groundwater monitoring wells. After a small spill in 2017, the Oil-Water Seperator and the storm water conveyance systeme were upgraded. 

Groundwater monitoring was completed on the site from 2007 through 2019. In October 2019, the owner's consultant, submitted a final groundwater monitoring report update and a request for site closure.  DEQ reviewed the report and determined that the site no longer posed an unacceptable risk with the following restrictions: 1) no groundwater from beneath the site could be used, 2) a CMMP and HASP would need to be prepared for any subsurface work in the area of contamination, 3) no residential use or development would be allowed on the property, and 4) DEQ-approved vapor mitigation plans would be required before any re-development or new building expansion or construction on the site.

A CMMP/HASP was prepared and an Easement and Equitable Servitudes implementing the above restrictions was recorded on the property on June 11, 2020.  DEQ plans to issue a conditional NFA in June or July 2020 once all final documents are received and final closure completed.",21469.0,0.0,NSAWKA,2020-06-15 11:58:05.670
