13764,26-99-1374,26,99,1374,,1999-12-15,1999-12-15 16:08:52,KING FOOD MART,3510 NE MARTIN LUTHER KING JR. BLVD,PORTLAND,97212,,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,NFA,False,False,True,,True,,,,,,,,33200.0,,BALBERT,2002-11-01 15:43:54.000
13765,26-99-1377,26,99,1377,9584.0,1999-12-16,1999-12-16 11:36:52,ANDY'S AUTO SUPPLY,2150 SE POWELL BLVD,PORTLAND,97202,(503) 232-9587,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"A 1,000-gallon waste oil UST was removed from the site in December 1999.  Sampling found up to 44,100 ppm waste oil extending from the UST to a nearby dry well.  A total of 390.74 tons of PCS were excavated, and the cleanup reportedly met Soil Matrix requirements.

A 4,000-gallon gasoline UST and two 3,000-gallon gasoline USTs extending beneath the sidewalk into Powell Blvd were decommissioned in-place in June 2000 due to nearby utility lines.  Sampling found up to 16,700 ppm gasoline in the soil and 12,000 ppb gasoline in the shallow groundwater.  Three monitoring wells were installed in May 2002 and sampled for four quarters.  ODOT objected to leaving contamination in the right-of-way, however, and the project apparently stalled.

In May 2006, Laurey Cook pointed out that benzene concentrations in the soil (up to 4.37 ppm) exceeded vapor intrusion RBCs, and recommended additional sampling to delineate the extent of benzene contamination.  The project was backlogged in February 2008 when no work was completed.  (8/26/10 KPD)

Reached out for the LUST backlog project, owner was under the impression that the site had been closed and no longer wanted to be contacted by DEQ (4/26/21 XCC)",,,17453.0,0.0,XCRUZCU,2021-04-28 16:12:51.550
