EPA grant letter sent 1/16/2007. TMD",Note that there was a former bulk facility and abandoned gasoline station directly west of this site that was never investigated.,"The site was formerly a rural market, residence, and gasoline station that dispensed petroleum products and performed car repairs. The initial investigation was conducted in November  1999, and three tanks were decommissioned and removed in March 2000.  The excavation was enlarged in September 2001 and two additional formerly-unknown tanks were discovered and removed; the petroleum contaminated soils were sent to Riverbend Landfill. Due to lack of funds, additional work was conducted under an EPA grant in 2007 and 2009-2010. The onsite utility locator consultant indicated there may be another unknown tank onsite to the west of the house and beneath the blackberry shrubs, but this was not investigated. The remaining petroleum contaminated soils are limited in extent and groundwater impacts are limited to the northern part of the site (see map attached to the ""no further action"" letter). The onsite residential well has seen some concentrations of petroleum and solvent contaminants, but they are not above acceptable standards; moreover, during some sampling events no petroleum or solvent contaminants were detected. The onsite water supply well should be tested periodically for petroleum constituents whenever it is used again. The monitoring wells that DEQ installed for the investigation were properly abandoned by overdrilling in November 2016.",18100.0,0.0,TDANOVI,2017-08-29 11:00:12.053
