Site re-opened on : 12/4/2017 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 9/24/2001.  Site assessment for redevelopment shows higher concentrations and access to USTs that were closed in place.  Site reopened 12/4/2017 due to redevelopment making PCS and groundwater accessible.  ...gdeck / crichardson",,"In September 1999, site assessment sampling was conducted at the property and a petroleum release was reported and assigned LUST project number 10-99-0083.  In September 2000, two USTs were decommissioned in-situ and four USTs were decommissioned by removal (see Figure 3).  In 2017, the property was redeveloped as a Dollar General store.  During redevelopment work the two USTs decommissioned in-situ in 1999 were exposed and permanently decommissioned by removal.  Site assessment sampling at the time of the Dollar General redevelopment resulted in a report of petroleum contaminated groundwater in excess of what was previously documented to be present at the site.  The 1999 petroleum release project that received a No Further Action determination in 2001 was re-opened.  The Dollar General site development work included contaminated media management and removal of the two tanks previously decommissioned in-situ.  Soil and groundwater contaminant concentrations do not exceed any of the applicable screening levels and do not pose an unacceptable risk of exposure.  ",16504.0,0.0,ECLOUGH,2018-10-04 08:02:20.163
