14121,23-00-0005,23,00,0005,,2000-02-16,2000-02-23 11:50:22,CAIRO MARKET,3850 HWY 201,ONTARIO,97914,,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"[March 2010] The site was a country store that dispensed petroleum from 1929 to 1970.  The site is currently used for storage.  

In August 1999, DEQ was notified of a potential petroleum release at the site.  Petroleum contamination was encountered during excavation activities associated with the installation of a septic tank.  The release was formally reported to DEQ in February 2000 and assigned LUST # 23-00-0005.

Soil and groundwater have been impacted at the site.  The sources of contamination at the site are historic releases of petroleum products from the former UST systems and AST system.  Remaining soil contamination is located greater than 4 feet bgs.  Shallow groundwater fluctuates between 3 feet bgs and 8 feet bgs.  The general groundwater gradient is towards the north and to the east.  Both groundwater levels and migration direction are likely influenced by agricultural related irrigation in the area.

The site site was proposed for a Conditional NFA determination following a public comment period and the recordation of an E&ES.  The E&ES was recorded on 3/19/2010 and includes the following:  1) no residential use will be allowed on the property; 2) require a minimum 30 foot well seal for any new well installed on the site property; 3) required a carbon well head treatment system be installed and regularly maintained on any new well installed on the site property; and 4) require proper handling, characterization, and disposal of any contaminated media (soil, groundwater) encountered during any subsurface excavation.

No public comments were recieved during the 30 day public comment period.  The Conditional NFA determination was issued on 3/25/2010.

Select site documents may be viewed from the site documents section of this database.",34900.0,0.0,KROBERT,2010-03-25 07:25:20.920
