15400,30-00-0019,30,00,0019,83.0,2000-07-31,2000-08-07 11:43:00,PILOT ROCK CHEVRON,234 SW BIRCH,PILOT ROCK,97868,(541) 443-2290,False,7.0,MATRIX,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : SOIL CONTAMINATED BY OVERFILL MIXED WITH OTHER CLEAN SOIL FROM TOP OF TANKS....NO WAY NOW TO DETERMINE VOLUME OF PCS..ENTIRE PILE WILL BE SAMPLED.. 30 YDS. ***,10/21/02-File transferred to The Dalles office,"This site is a former gas station site.

Four petroleum underground storage tanks were decommissioned in 2000 and petroleum contaminated soil was excavated from the tank excavations and treated offsite under a Solid Waste Letter of Authorization.  A heating oil tank may also have be present at the Site. 

Based on a file review completed by DEQ in 2006, it was determined that additional work was required at the site including:

1.    A final treatment report for the petroleum contaminated soils treated under the Solid Waste Letter of Authorization.
2.    Determine the extent of residual petroleum contamination in soil and groundwater.
3.    Determine if residual contamination exceeds risk based concentrations for site specific exposure pathways and receptors.
4.    If unacceptable risk is present, initiate cleanup of remaining contamination.
