May 2019, Reviewed file and contacted RP.  Additional work was completed in 2017 and 2018.  See public summary and staff memoradum recommeding an NFA. May 2019 the NFA was finalized.",,"Petroleum leaked from one 3,000-gallon gasoline underground storage tank (UST) and one 10,000-gallon diesel UST.  These tanks were removed in October 2000 along with approx. 85-100 cy of soil.  Two more excavation occurred in 2017 to remove as much as possible with out compromising the bldg.  The drinking water well onsite was sampled in 2017 and 2018 and results were clean for all contaminants of interest. No Further Action was recommended in Dec 2018 and public comment requested by the neighbors.  After 30 days, none was received so moved forward with NFA.  May 2019 NFA was finalized.",18914.0,0.0,GDECK,2020-04-20 09:56:54.713
