18054,21-01-4018,21,01,4018,,2001-07-05,2001-07-13 12:48:34,Nashville Store,11663 NASHVILLE RD,BLODGETT,97326,503 456-2009,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,3.0,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : 2 USTS (500 & 1000 GAL) GAS & ?, TAKEN OUT OF SERVICE PRE-1974; PROPERTY NOW OWNED BY A TEXAS BANK *** 2 USTs (500 & 1000 gal) gasoline & ? taken out of service pre-1974.  Property previously owned by a Texas bank, obtained through PPA by Coastal Food Bank Non-Profit.",,"The property formerly known as the Nashville Store was previously used as a retail gas station, country store, and US-Post Office from the 1930s until closure in the 1970s.  Ownership passed through several hands until Coastal Range Food Bank acquired the property in 2003 from a lien holder in Irving Texas through a perspective purchaser agreement.    

Petroleum contamination was discovered in 2001 during a site assessment performed by a prospective purchaser.  Since the 2001, report of contamination, three underground storage tanks have been decommissioned by removal, contaminated soil removed, an array of monitoring wells installed, quarterly monitoring performed, and risk assessment completed. 

Based on the results of cleanup, site investigation, monitoring and assessment, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land use, the remaining contamination has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment.  ",81564.0,0.0,JGLASS,2008-01-15 14:26:23.093
