18352,17-01-0012,17,01,0012,,2001-07-30,2001-08-09 11:07:14,FORMER CHEVRON BULK TERMINAL #20-9248,"505 NE ""F"" ST",GRANTS PASS,97526,,False,4.0,GW,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Esc reviewing quarterly GW reports only - 2005

Note: Dames and Moore did a Site Assessment for this site in 1988; not sure why the release was only entered into our system in 2001 when we apparently received this info by Chevron staff Brett Hunter","adjacent site ""The Oil House"" 17-97-0067; plume of free product from The Oil House possibly moving onto this site","This is a former bulk terminal that started fuel distribution before 1900. The former Chevron above ground storage tank farm was purchased by the adjacent property owner to the east in 1987 and is currently owned and operated by The Oil House. The site is now used as a lumber yard. It currently consists of two service garages, an office building, and a warehouse. The site was initially investigated in 1988 and 6 monitoring wells (one on the adjacent site near the tank farm) have been installed and were monitoring from 2002 until 2008. In 2008 an additional two monitring wells were installed on teh south edge of the property and all of the monitoring wells were sampled until June 2012. Numerous soil sampled have been collected from various depths over time. No soil has been removed from the site, nor has any treatment occurred. The investigation is continuing and a conceptual site model was formulated in 2012; however, there are some data gaps that are being addressed.",39384.0,0.0,TDANOVI,2017-07-12 17:27:45.867
