18479,21-01-4020,21,01,4020,,2001-08-20,2001-08-24 15:33:58,Tom Litfin Motors,4821 SW HWY 101,LINCOLN CITY,97367,541-994-4940,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,3.0,True,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : CONDITIONAL RISK-BASED CLOSURE; RESTRICTION ON GW USE & HEALTH & SAFETY PLAN FOR ANY TRENCHWORKERS. *** Pjt Mgr = JLG.  Conditional NFA: restriction on GW use & Health & Safety Plan for any trenchworkers.,,"Soil contamination was initially reported to DEQ in August 2001, when petroleum contamination was detected during an assessment along the west side of Highway 101 by Oregon Department of Transportation.  An auto repair shop had operated at the site under different names between 1950 and 2001.  As part of the historic Taft area revitalization, the Lincoln City Glass Foundry has moved into the building The redevelopment includes a glass museum, a glass blowing studio, and classroom.  Since the 2001 report of petroleum contamination, the Lincoln City Urban Renewal Agency has removed a portion of the building to allow for construction of the new intersection between 48th Street and Highway 101.  Multiple areas of contamination were removed during cleanup of the site and a groundwater investigation, including risk evaluation, has now been completed.  Based on the sampling results, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land use, the remaining contamination has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment.  The remaining contamination in soil and groundwater is stable or shrinking in size and will naturally degrade in place.",39559.0,0.0,JGLASS,2011-08-30 17:51:39.113
