19125,34-01-0060,34,01,0060,,2001-11-09,2001-11-14 14:49:25,LAURELWOOD ACADEMY,39645 SW LAURELWOOD RD,GASTON,97119,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"The workplan for further site investigation has been approved but there is no record that it has been implemented.  Site investigation report received on July 17, 2009 (JKS 7-17-09).  Report reviewed and comment letter sent on 8-07-09.  Off-site borings B16 and B17 indicated that impacted groundwater was adjacent to HIll Creek; Additional investigation to west along north side of Hill Creek is warranted including installation of monitoring well; Additional information about Hill Creek and possible seeps requested; Screening against SLVs for Ecological Risk Assessments suggested; In April 2010, in accordance with approved work plan, EVREN advanced two additional borings along the north side of HIll Creek and installed MW-5 between May 2009 borings B16 and B17.  Impacted groundwater detected in MW-5.  RP and Laurelwood informed in August 2010 that a Level I (Scoping ERA) should be completed.  EVREN proposes to complete this evaluation following the fourth quarter of compliance monitoring following installation of MW-5. (JKS 11-17-10).  Fourth monitoring event conducted following installatino of MW-5 revealed levels of gasoline, BTEX, and trimethylbenzenes above the most stringent of RBC standards.  Per EVREN, ecological risk assessment (level 1- scoping) is in preparation (JKS 1-31-11).  BWUD received May 2011.  Door to door survey, water use search, and well search revealed possible receptors in LOF.  Subsequent information showed groundwater in area has no likely beneficial use.  Level I ERA submitted in July 2011.  Review by Toxicologist showed the groundwter to creek pathway was complete but remedial action probably not necessary.  DEQ requested additional monitoring and possible statistical analysis of data from MW-5.  Events performed in November 2011 and February 2012.  Await data from May and August 2012 and report documenting all events after the fourth event.

Based on review of data from the final compliance monitoring event (August 2012), Paul Seidel agreed there were no unacceptable ecological risks. Comment Solicitiation Letter sent to nearby property owners on 1-15-13.  Comment period ends 2-18-13. No comment received.  Zoning potentially allows for future residential use. NFA with conditions assuming future commercial use and requiring preparation of CMMP. (JKS 4-10-13)",HOT #34-01-8213,,43416.0,0.0,KDANA,2014-10-23 12:52:24.733
