19392,10-01-0018,10,01,0018,,2001-12-19,2001-12-27 15:00:35,WADDLE FAMILY TRUST,2770 YOKUM RD,RIDDLE,97469,,False,7.0,MATRIX,4.0,NFA,False,False,True,,False,,,,,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : HISTORICAL TANKS LAST USED IN 1960'S *** ,,,43789.0,,MBELSKY,2002-03-27 13:43:21.000
19393,03-01-0068,03,01,0068,1753.0,2001-12-17,2001-12-27 17:00:43,GRIMMS FUEL CO. II,1631 S SHORE BLVD,LAKE OSWEGO,97034,(503)636-8441,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"A sheen was observed on water down-gradient at the base of the retaining wall along the north edge of the property. A temporary pump and treat was set up to pull water from a northern observation well. The system was discontinued in 2004 and several monitoring wells were installed.  During the facility upgrade in 2006, several unknown tanks were discovered and decommissioned in place due to the site limitations. No work performed at site in 2008.  In 2009, Roger N. Smith will complete additional groundwater monitoring and a risk-based evaluation.  Report entitled Site Closure Under the Generic Remedy for a Simple Risk-Based Cleanup received in late June 2009.  Review of report noted some data gaps for constituents, and undelineated groundwater beyond monitoring well MW-2.  Also based on constituents in soil and groundwater above vapor intrusion RBC standards, additionl cleanup or investigation may be necessary.  Comments provided in letter dated 7-20-09.  Delineation borings on north side of property found some impacts to groundwater.  Seep samples much less impacted than in 2003-2004 (JKS 2-26-10).  Work plan for installtion of monitoring well (MW-6) received July 13, 2010 and approved (JKS 07-13-10).  In August 2010, monitoing well MW-6 installed and initial sampling complete.  RNSA wishes to not proceed with further delineation. DEQ decided in letter dated 1-12-11 to postpone decision on need for additional investigation based on data from MW-6.  In July 2011, based on apparent decreasing levels of gasoline hydrocarbons in MW-6, RNSA proposed a quarterly monitoring schedule.  Quarterly monitoring initiated in August 2011.  Gasoine and consituent levels have been ND for two consecutive quarterly events.  If levels remain low, addtional investigation north of MW-6 may not be necessary.  Residence west of site not within 100 lateral feet.  Continue to monitor plume stability.  Consider use restriction to preclude residential exposures to contaminants in groundwater.  (JKS 12-15-11).  As of February 2012, levels in MW-6 remain non-detect.  One additional event planned for May 2012. In May 2012, DEQ reviewed and commented on scope of work for remaining monitoring event. DEQ discussed project status with RNSA on 1-28-13.  Discussed idea of soil-gas investigation data. If representative samples do not show detections above urban residential RBCs, use restriction may not be needed.  RNSA discussing with RP (JKS 1-31-13).",03-89-0215; 03-98-0078; ECSI #2283; UST Facility ID #9650,,1996.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2013-01-31 14:48:56.333
