19489,26-02-0003,26,02,0003,,2002-01-17,2002-01-22 09:05:51,RENTAL CAR QUICK TURNAROUND AREA,7102 NE AIRPORT WAY,PORTLAND,97218,,False,1.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Site is operated by five rental car companies.  Each company operates a dedicated UST and associated dispenser.  All USTs are linked to a common fill port west of the building.  In May 2001, MTBE was detected in a Port monitoring well west of the building.  In October 2001, the Port advanced borings in the area of the remote fill pad and found soil and groundwater contamination. The first wells were installed in October 2002. In early 2003, it was discovered that selected dispensers lacked under-dispenser containment and a limited amount of petroleum contaminated soil was removed. An additional source of conatamination was found to be from defective spill buckets at the remote fill.  
Free product was first encountered in April 2004.  Free product historicallly detected  in MFG-1A, MFG-5, MFG-13 and SS-6.  Product removed using active and passive methods.  Product not detected at the site as of early 2012.

In May 2007, Tetra Tech submitted a CAP proposing free product recovery, SVE remediation near the remote fill pad and foundation wall, and enhanced bioremediation through injection of air and nutrient. .  The SVE pilot system operated from October 2008 to January 2009.  The full-scale system operated from January 2009 to December 2012.  The enchanced bioremediation pilot system operated from May 2008 to April 2010.  The full-scale system, consisting of 44 air injection wells, operated from June 2010 to May 2013.

A March 2013 confirmation investigation found minimal contamination remained in the area of the remote fill pad.   During post-remedial monitoring, one detection of gasoline in grounwater from MFG-1A during one event exceeded the RBC for direct contact in excavations (14,000 ppb).  A 90% UCL of the arithmetic mean was calculated using data from MFG-1A and was found to be well below the RBC. 
Site is not located in the wellfield.  Shallow groundwater has no beneficial use.  Commented initiated on 12-19-14.  Site ready for closure (JKS 2-12-15)",,"Site is operated by five rental car companies.  Each company operates a dedicated UST and associated dispenser.  All USTs are linked to a common fill port west of the building.  In May 2001, MTBE was detected in a Port monitoring well west of the building.  In October 2001, the Port advanced borings in the area of the remote fill pad and found soil and groundwater contamination. The first wells were installed in October 2002. In early 2003, it was discovered that selected dispensers lacked under-dispenser containment and a limited amount of petroleum contaminated soil was removed. An additional source of conatamination was found to be from defective spill buckets at the remote fill.  
Free product was first encountered in April 2004.  Free product historicallly detected  in MFG-1A, MFG-5, MFG-13 and SS-6.  Product removed using active and passive methods.  Product not detected at the site as of early 2012.

In May 2007, Tetra Tech submitted a CAP proposing free product recovery, SVE remediation near the remote fill pad and foundation wall, and enhanced bioremediation through injection of air and nutrient. .  The SVE pilot system operated from October 2008 to January 2009.  The full-scale system operated from January 2009 to December 2012.  The enchanced bioremediation pilot system operated from May 2008 to April 2010.  The full-scale system, consisting of 44 air injection wells, operated from June 2010 to May 2013.

A March 2013 confirmation investigation found minimal contamination remained in the area of the remote fill pad.   During post-remedial monitoring, one detection of gasoline in grounwater from MFG-1A during one event exceeded the RBC for direct contact in excavations (14,000 ppb).  A 90% UCL of the arithmetic mean was calculated using data from MFG-1A and was found to be well below the RBC. 
Site is not located in the wellfield.  Shallow groundwater has no beneficial use.  Commented initiated on 12-19-14.  Site ready for closure (JKS 2-12-15).",9686.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2015-02-12 08:09:58.237
