20337,13-02-0005,13,02,0005,2220.0,2002-05-10,2002-05-13 15:11:09,TIM'S TIME SAVOR-TIME OIL COMPANY,306 HWY 20 NORTH,HINES,97738,(503)573-2609,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"Cost Recovery Sent to JK on 6/14/07 from Liz Clark.
Warning Letter - failure to perform GW monitoring - sent 12/14/07.  JKlemz",,"Time Oil Co. (currently TOC) operated a retail gasoline station at the Property from 1957 until 2002 and operated the convenience store until 2005. Two 10,000-gallon underground storage tanks (USTs) that reportedly contained stove oil and diesel fuel were installed beneath the western portion of the Property in 1958 (Figure 2). In 1984, one 10,000-gallon gasoline UST and one 12,000-gallon gasoline UST were installed to the south of the convenience store. In 1990, the two 1958-vintage USTs were removed from the Property and one additional 10,000-gallon gasoline UST was installed next to the two 1984-vintage USTs. The two 1984-vintage USTs and the 1990-vintage UST were removed in June 2007, along with the fuel-dispensing pump islands, canopy, and associated piping. Evidence of a petroleum release attributable to these USTs was not observed during the removal activities; however, evidence of a prior release from the 1958-vintage UST system that had been removed in 1990 was confirmed.
Following UST removal activities in 2007, TOC sold the Property to a restaurateur who renovated the former convenience store building into a restaurant (Country Seasons Café).  The business folded and the restaurant building vacated shortly after TOC initiated a dual phase extraction (DPE) remediation at the Property in June 2012. The building and Property have been vacant since 2012 except for monthly visits by TOC’s contract staff responsible for maintaining the remediation system and conducting quarterly groundwater monitoring.

Following treatment of contaminated groundwater and based on sample results for soil, groundwater and soil gas, acceptable risk levels are not exceeded, and a No Further Action determination is recommended for this site. The No Further Action determination will be recorded in DEQ’s underground storage tank database (Facility No. 2220 and LUST No. 13-02-0005).",122278.0,0.0,TENGLAN,2016-07-18 14:02:27.907
