20499,10-02-0011,10,02,0011,,2002-05-28,2002-05-30 13:36:37,UNION PACIFIC RAILROAD BLDG,1858 AIRPORT RD,ROSEBURG,97470,,False,2.0,GENREM,4.0,NFA,False,False,True,,False,,,,,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : U.P. IS CLEANING UP THEIR OWN CONTAM. THERE IS A HOT ON THE OTHER SIDE OF BLDG.  WILL REPORT TO NWR. *** Gasoline and HOT tanks decommissioned.  Benzene detected in GW in HOT pit. Investigation outside tanks pit did not detect any BTEX compounds. PAh's below RBCs,,,20388.0,,MBELSKY,2003-04-24 10:54:35.000
20500,22-02-4010,22,02,4010,7158.0,2002-05-31,2002-05-31 10:12:10,M & M #15 Fasttrack Gas,1545 E PACIFIC BLVD,ALBANY,97321,(503)222-4201,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : 3 USTS REMOVED 5-31-02. *** 3 USTs removed 5/31/02.  Pjt Mgr = JLG.,,"Petroleum contamination was discovered on or around May 31, 2002, during the decommissioning of underground storage tanks at this facility and USTC file number 22-02-4010 was assigned.  In October 2002 remedial excavation work was performed while simultaneously conducting further investigation of the extent of the petroleum release(s).  Approximately 500 tons of petroleum-contaminated soil were removed.  After the remedial excavation work was completed 24 temporary sampling probes and 4 permanent groundwater monitoring wells were installed.  Free product or LPH (liquid petroleum hydrocarbons) measuring 0.54 feet was observed.  In July of 2003, five dual-phase extraction (DPE) wells were installed to remediate the LPH in the vicinity of KMW-3.  Treatment system operation continued and additional monitoring wells were added in 2003 & 2004.   Groundwater flow calculations estimated flow to the north-northwest.  During the recent semi-annual monitoring the foot print LPH has continued to be reduced and no observations of LPH were made the 2009-2010 year of compliance monitoring. Some contaminated soil and groundwater remains. Based on a summary of the historical and current soil sampling results DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land use, the remaining contamination has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment. The closure plan proposes to allow the remaining contamination in soil and groundwater to biodegrade naturally in place.",22848.0,0.0,JGLASS,2013-06-11 14:37:27.390
