20734,26-02-0241,26,02,0241,,2002-06-26,2002-06-27 11:09:19,US BANK/FORMER SERVICE STATION,300 E POWELL BLVD,GRESHAM,97080,,False,1.0,MATRIX,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"The City of Gresham encountered three USTs (two 500-gallon USTs and one 250-gallon UST) beneath Powell Blvd adjacent to a US Bank parking lot entrance while digging a trench for a 12"" water line in June 2002.  The three USTs were removed, and a total of 33.02 tons of PCS were excavated.  Confirmation sampling found up to 4,380 ppm gasoline and 566 ppm diesel remaining in the soil.

ODOT is the current site owner (having acquired the strip of right-of-way in March 1972 while widening Powell Blvd), but may be exempt from liability if the property was condemned.  The adjacent property owners (the Fourier and Larson families) acquired the property after the split with ODOT, and so never owned the contaminated parcel.  The previous owners are deceased.  Unless someone volunteers to investigate, the site is effectively an Orphan.  (5/11/10 TMB)",,,45654.0,0.0,KDANA,2010-06-28 15:28:42.080
