21334,26-02-0841,26,02,0841,,2002-08-26,2002-09-11 12:16:26,EL INDIO/FORMER SERVICE STATION,920 E POWELL BLVD,GRESHAM,97080,,False,7.0,MATRIX,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"The City of Gresham encountered PCS beneath Powell Blvd adjacent to this site while digging a trench for a 12"" water line in August 2002.  Sampling found up to 174 ppm gasoline and 26 ppm diesel.  A service station at the site was operated by Humble Oil Company from 1957-1971 and by Hudson Oil Company from 1978-1986.  Humble subsequently merged with ExxonMobil.  The site is currently occupied by a Plaid Pantry (930 E Powell) and El Indio II, a satellite of the El Indio Mexican Restaurant on NE Halsey.

ODOT is the current site owner (having acquired a strip of right-of-way in January 1973 while widening Powell Blvd), but may be exempt from liability if the property was condemned.  The adjacent property owner acquired the property after the split with ODOT, and so never owned the contaminated parcel.  Humble Oil Company and the previous property owners could not be located.  Unless the contamination can be linked to ExxonMobil, this site is effectively an Orphan.  (5/6/10 TMB)",,,46677.0,0.0,KDANA,2010-06-29 15:29:11.080
