21513,24-02-1019,24,02,1019,5258.0,2002-10-08,2002-10-08 17:17:33,Oak Park Automotive,4335 SILVERTON RD NE,SALEM,97305,(503)585-6445,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : TANKS REMOVED IN 1988 BY ODOT; FORMER TEXACO STATION. *** Tanks removed in 1988 by ODOT; former Texaco station.
Pjt mgr = JLG.",,"Underground storage tanks used for storing gasoline and used oil at this property were removed in 1988. During an October 2002 environmental assessment of this property, contamination was discovered in the soil next to the former underground storage tanks south of the existing auto repair shop and in the vicinity of a used-oil aboveground storage tank and oil/water separator north of the shop, indicating that the tanks had previously leaked.  DEQ recently reviewed the tank cleanup file for this site. The file contains multiple reports describing the history of the site, the decommissioning by removal of the UST systems, remedial excavation of petroleum-impacted soils, and an assessment of the potential risks associated with the remaining soil and groundwater contamination. An estimate of the volume of petroleum-contaminated soil proposed to be left in place was also provided. Based on the review of this file, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land use, the remaining contamination has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment. The closure plan proposes to allow the remaining contamination to degrade naturally in place and restrict the use of onsite groundwater for domestic drinking purposes.",5371.0,0.0,JGLASS,2013-07-12 16:27:54.633
