22071,20-02-1576,20,02,1576,,2002-12-31,2003-01-02 09:47:36,FORMER DEXTER GAS STATION,38851 DEXTER ROAD,DEXTER,97431,,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"The earliest known use of the site began in in 1978 when the site was developed as a fueling and automotive repair station. Reportedly, the underground storage tanks were removed in 1989 and fueling operations ended. The exact cause of contamination is unknown but believed to be from leaks in the underground storage tanks. A drinking water well installed in the former tank pit is believed to have created a preferential pathway for shallow groundwater contamination to migrate down into the aquifer used for drinking water. Soil in the southeast corner of the site and drinking water within about 300 feet of the site were impacted with gasoline and related constituents. Approximately 55 cubic yards of contaminated soil was excavated from around the southeast corner of the onsite building. The onsite well was also decommissioned in March 2003. Contaminated soil remains beneath the southeast corner of the onsite building. There are no apparent remaining impacts to groundwater. The property is zoned rural commercial and the current property owners have indicated they plan to continue commercial use of the property. Soil contamination remaining onsite may pose unacceptable risk in a residential scenario. Further investigation or remediation is required prior to residential use of the property. Currently the site receives drinking water from a well on the neighboring property to the north and this is expected to continue. Any future well installed on the property should be installed with caution, as far away from the former tank pit as possible, and with a deeper than normal well seal to limit a potential connection between shallow and deep groundwater. An opportunity to comment was given to all property owners within the estimated historical extent of contamination. No comments were received.",47920.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2019-10-22 14:53:38.320
