23816,20-03-1750,20,03,1750,9886.0,2003-08-22,2003-08-22 13:09:57,CHEVRON #9-1321,3375 GATEWAY STREET,SPRINGFIELD,97477,(503) 741-0293,False,2.0,GENREM,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Site Assessment identified low BTEX and Gx in one boring north of tank pit.  Below all commercial, trench, and construction worker RBCs.",,,1893.0,0.0,GDECK,2006-11-22 11:53:21.240
23817,03-03-1751,03,03,1751,1215.0,2003-08-22,2003-08-22 15:43:36,MOUNTAIN PARK CHEVRON,2 MONROE PARKWAY,LAKE OSWEGO,97035,(503) 636-0945,False,4.0,GW,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,LUST #03-93-0158,"Four groundwater monitoring wells were installed at the site in August 2003 as part of a site assessment and were sampled quarterly through September 2006, finding low concentrations of petroleum products and constituents including MTBE.  Two 1,000-gallon USTs, holding heating oil and waste oil, were decommissioned by removal from the site in December 2003.  PCS was encountered but not removed.  Soil and groundwater samples collected from nine borings across the site in June 2004 identified gasoline, diesel and heavy oils in soil and groundwater, but minimal levels of PAHs and VOCs.  The contamination was concentrated beneath the south end of the service station building, where hydraulic hoists were located.  As the contamination could not be removed, DEQ issued a Conditional NFA letter in January 2008.

In November 2016 the service station building was torn down during a site renovation, and about 265 tons of PCS were removed from beneath the building.  Three 10,000-gallon gasoline USTs and one 10,000-gallon diesel UST were decommissioned by removal from the site in April 2017 along with the fuel dispensers and product pipelines, and an additional 73 tons of PCS were removed.  Residual concentrations of gasoline, diesel and heavy oils in soil and groundwater at the site do not exceed RBCs for applicable exposure pathways.  No further investigation or cleanup is required.",142469.0,0.0,KDANA,2018-06-06 07:29:01.883
