24273,26-03-2208,26,03,2208,6621.0,2003-10-17,2003-10-17 16:28:45,SANDY BLVD CARDLOCK,11426 NE SANDY BLVD,PORTLAND,97220,(503) 682-3865,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Diesel- impacted soil was discovered during UST decommissioning in October 03.  Quarterly GW monitoring and reporting were conducted.  The last 4 onsecutive monitoring events indicate constituent concentrations below the generic RBCs and have been requested to be discontinued.  A risk-based evaluation report has been submitted with a request for a NFA determination.  Comments solicited from affected or nearby parties.  Draft EE&S sent to owner (Moran LLC attn: James Carr Moran, Sr.) on or about 8-17-09. Moran LLC (owner) will agree to terms of draft EE&S, but will not sign a License and Agreement Concerning Contamination with ODOT.  Truax Harris Energy has leased to Petrocard and is effectively ceasing to exist as corporation.  DEQ can't compel RP to sign agreement because residual contamination does not exceed Construction Worker and Excavation Worker RBCs.  Final EE&S sent to RP on 10-21-09.  Site should close when recorded EE&S is returned (JKS 10-30-09).  Call to Mr. Moran for update on 12-30-09.  Some medical issues have arisen that have prevented him from getting to Multnomah County to record EES. He will call me when he is feeling better and ready to proceed (JKS 12-30-09).",,,22455.0,0.0,KDANA,2010-10-04 09:55:43.840
