24484,26-03-2419,26,03,2419,1471.0,2003-11-18,2003-11-18 14:14:32,JRJ PROPERTIES LLC,9425 N BURRAGE AVE,PORTLAND,97217,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Four gasoline USTs were located in an alleyway between the Portland Provision Company (PPC) and Kenton Packing Company (KPC) buildings.  PPC decommissioned two of the USTs in 1991 and removed 70 cubic yards of PCS.  (26-91-0033).  The two remaining tanks were decommissioned in July 2001 and 660 cubic yards of PCS were removed.  (26-01-0037).  The KPC site, owned by JRJ Properties, was added to the LUST database to investigate the extent of residual contamination on that site.  The site contractor, however, argued that the contamination was already well characterized, and disagreed that additional sampling was needed.  The site was referred to ECSI (4139) in 2004 when TCE was identified in the groundwater; however, Site Assessment has yet to evaluate the site.  (7/13/10 KPD)
DEQ reviewed data collected during investigation of UST Cleanup File No. 26-01-0037 in 2000-2002.  Data collected from JRJ property largely showed minimal to ND levels of contamination north of the JRJ building, including in the area of a suspect concrete oil tank.  The suspect oil tank was the cause for the opening of this release incident.  Based on DEQ's review, soil and groundwater conditions at the JRJ property are in compliance with RBCs in effect at the time the NFA was issued for the adjacent property to south (9348 North Peninsular Avene) - UST Cleanup file No. 26-01-0037.  In June 2013, DEQ issued a notification letter to the owner of the former PPC property concerning the proposal to issue an NFA Addendum to the February 2004 NFA for 26-01-0037.  No coments received.  (JKS 9-18-13).",ECSI #4139,,38763.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2013-09-18 14:51:13.003
