24542,36-03-2477,36,03,2477,,2003-11-12,2003-11-26 14:05:27,Former Dundee Gas Station,509 SE HWY 99W,DUNDEE,97115,,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : SITE LOCATED ON SW CORNER OF INTERSECTION OF 5TH & 99W.  ABANDONED GAS STATION.  5000-GAL UST STILL ON SITE.  PROPERTY IN TRUST.  PREVIOUS WORK BY AGI, FOUND BENZENE IN GW (900 PPM TPH-D), NO RELEASE REPORTED.  OTHER TANKS PULLED ~1988-89.G *** Site located on SW corner of intersection of 5th & 99W.  Abandoned gas station.  5000-gal UST still on site.  Property in trust.  Previous work by AGI, found benzene in GW (900 ppm TPH-D), no release reported.  Other tanks pulled ~1988-89... jlg",,"The property was historically used as a lumberyard in the1940s & 1950s, to dispense gasoline from the 1960s to the 1970s, and as a used car lot in the 1980s.    

Petroleum contamination was first reported to DEQ by a consultant performing a site assessment in 2003.  The underground storage tanks from this site were reportedly removed in 1980’s, however, no record of the decommissioning was provided.  In 2005 a site investigation was performed to determine if any UST systems remained at the facility,   establish the extent of the remaining contamination, and evaluated the potential exposure concerns.  Groundwater monitoring wells were subsequently installed and sampled quarterly between November 2005 and May 2006.

Based on a summary of the historical and current soil and groundwater sampling results, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land use, the remaining contamination from the leaky underground storage tank systems has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment.  The closure plan proposes to allow the remaining contamination in soil and groundwater to biodegrade naturally in place.",80474.0,0.0,JGLASS,2008-09-11 18:45:59.357
