24558,20-03-2493,20,03,2493,11881.0,2003-12-02,2003-12-02 08:36:08,Lane Transit District / LTD,3500 E 17TH AVENUE,EUGENE,97401,(541) 741-6100,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,NFA,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Robert Despain with Staton reported heavy oil sheen on groundwater in vicinity of waste oil tank during site assessment work.  Will need to re-open project and complete groundwater investigation (Esc 1-feb-10)
Previous NFA issued 4/20/2004.
Site re-opened on : 2/19/2010 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 4/20/2004.",,"The site is used by Lane Transit District and includes facilities for vehicle maintenance. A tank for storing waste oil is located adjacent to a service garage. In 2003, a remote fill line was cut during facility improvements. The tank was then overfilled with waste oil that spilled into the excavation surrounding the line and a petroleum spill was reported to DEQ. Contaminated soil was removed to the extent practicable, and groundwater was pumped from the excavation. Further assessment outside of the excavation confirmed a limited lateral extent of contamination. The site was issued a letter of “No Further Action” in April 2004. 
In January 2010, workers encountered petroleum contaminated soil during additional facility upgrades. DEQ was notified of the contamination and opened the LTD project closed in 2004. Assessment was conducted in 2010 and 2011 to determine the extent of soil and groundwater contamination. Some solvents were detected in groundwater samples collected near the waste oil tank. DEQ asked for further delineation, and groundwater collected from the property limits identified a solvent (carbon tetrachloride) at the laboratory detection level.",2441.0,0.0,GDECK,2011-11-09 13:38:47.703
