24988,34-04-0302,34,04,0302,,2004-03-04,2004-03-04 11:56:53,"BEARCE, JACQUELINE",6690 NW 271ST AVENUE,HILLSBORO,97124,1-760-321-9285,False,1.0,MATRIX,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"A residential HOT and a farm-use gasoline UST were decommissioned at this rural residence in the spring of 2004.  Almost 22 tons of PCS were removed from around the UST and shipped to the Hillsboro Landfill.  (Only 62 ppm diesel was found at the HOT).  Confirmation sampling at 13 ft bgs found 1,120 ppm gasoline, along with 5.95 ppm benzene, 11.9 ppm ethylbenzene, 44.3 ppm toluene, and 75.8 ppm xylenes.  The consultant used UCLs and mass balancing and a site-specific Dilution Attenuation Factor to argue that there were no significant risks.

The on-site domestic well was reported to be 60 ft from the gas tank, and a neighbor's well had a static water level of 14 ft bgs.  (No groundwater was encountered at the Bearce site to 17 ft).  No Cost Recovery Agreement was received, and when DEQ followed up in late 2005 the property had new owners (Bobby & Amanda Chin).  In April 2007 the new owners expressed little concern with the outstanding issues.

This site scores high due to the domestic well.  (7/11/13 KPD)",,,84307.0,2783.0,KDANA,2013-07-11 16:38:30.223
