25678,24-04-0993,24,04,0993,,2004-05-28,2004-05-28 16:13:49,Home Fire Stove,1695 MARKET ST NE,SALEM,97301,503-364-6339,False,1.0,,,,False,False,True,,True,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : KARL VANZANDT (CAPITOL ENVIRONMENTAL) WENT TO DECOM A HOT.  FOUND TWO 240-GAL USTS END TO END.  ONE WAS A HOT, THE OTHER A SURPRISE WITH STODDARD SOLVENT.  CONSIDERING IT A NON-REGULATED SITE AT THIS POINT. *** Karl VanZandt (Capitol Environmental) went to decom a HOT.  Found two 240-gal USTs end to end.  One was a HOT, the other a surprise with Stoddard solvent.  Considering it a non-regulated site at this point.",Release report references two tanks; one a HOT and the other a solvent tank. I don't find a HOT listed in LUST for this location.,"(ARL 02/03/2021) On May 25 and 26, 2004, Capitol Environmental Consulting, Inc. decommissioned two 240 gallon steel underground storage tanks (USTs). One tank was a heating oil tank and the other was thought to contain Stoddard Solvent. The release was reported to DEQ on May 28, 2004. Soil sampling performed during tank decommissioning discovered total petroleum hydrocarbons in the gasoline range.  <br/><br/>

Point Source Solutions completed a Risk-Based Corrective Action Determination on November 7, 2019. In March 2020, a geophysical survey was performed near the tank nest to order to inspect the building's plumbing in relation to the former USTs. In July 2020, Point Source Solutions submitted a Subsurface Environmental Investigation.  <br/><br/>",85008.0,0.0,ALEIDEL,2021-03-04 09:40:53.940
