25754,10-04-1069,10,04,1069,,2004-05-01,2004-06-10 12:57:12,"ODOT-DRAIN, FORMER GAS STATION",NW CORNER 1ST & B STREETS,DRAIN,97435,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : SOIL & GW CONTAMINATION DISCOVERED AT HISTORIC GAS STATION PROPERTY DURING SITE ASSESSMENT. *** ODOT now owns this  property that formerly was a gas station, ODOT has completed a large remedial excavation (~1,200 yards) but took no confirmation samples, also purged, treated, and disposed of unknown quantity of water under NPDES permit

NFA mailed 16/aug/2016",,"[Jan. 2010] In August 2003, ODOT performed an investigation within the West B Avenue right of way in preparation for future road work.  The investigation included push probes from the site to the south side of West B Avenue (adjacent to the Cowboy Shell site LUST No. 10-89-000).  This investigation documented the presence of petroleum contamination within B Avenue and also on the former service station property (primarily gasoline up to 2,440 mg/kg in soil; no groundwater samples were collected).  Due to the presence of contamination, the DEQ assigned LUST No. 10 04 1069 to the site.  It is unclear whether the contamination was related to historic releases at the site, the former service station located to the south or both.

In November 2009, ODOT performed remedial excavation of contaminated soil beneath the site property and adjacent Highway 38.  Approximately 1,200 cubic yards of material was removed and disposed of at an approved landfill.

In December 2009, GeoPotential conducted a geophysical survey of the site to identify any USTs, UST pits (i.e., backfilled excavations of removed USTs), buried piping, and any other features of environmental interest. No tanks or pits were identified.  Due to traffic, the survey was limited to the property, the sidewalk easement and small portion of roadway in the southeast corner that could be safely accessed.  

Three probes were advanced in December 2009 to collect soil and groundwater samples for laboratory analysis. Based on previous investigations the SI results, the nature, extent, and magnitude of the contamination has been delineated on the site.  Petroleum hydrocarbon concentrations are limited to a maximum TPH-Gx of 2,440 mg/kg at less than 9 feet bgs within the southeast corner of the site. 

A copy of the Site Investigation report documenting the 2009 sampling event is availible in the Site Document section of this database.",85083.0,0.0,ECLOUGH,2016-08-16 15:38:56.517
