26022,10-04-1337,10,04,1337,5679.0,2004-07-06,2004-07-09 15:11:11,SCHOLFIELD'S MARKET,1625 HIGHWAY 101 S,REEDSPORT,97467,(503) 271-5423,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,Contamination discovered while Verizon was setting pole on site near building.,"10-96-0001, ONE STOP MARKET","In 2004, Verizon was setting a pole located in the paved parking area between the building on-site and North 16th St. A water line ruptured revealing oily water. Obvious soil and groundwater contamination was also observed during utility work. The release was reported to DEQ on July 6, 2004. <br/><br/>

On September 14, 2012, Scholfield's Market was inpsected by DEQ's Underground Storage Tank (UST) program and failed the triennial facility inspection. The operating certificate was revoked on November 19, 2013 and the station was placed on temporary closure. <br/><br/>

In February 2020, Tyree Oil, Inc. requested DEQ review and oversite for the project. After initial review, additional sampling of soil and groundwater along the sout and east boundaries of the porperty was requested. The investigation includes soil and groundwater samples collected from nine geoprobe locations dispersed around the site. In addition, one groundwater sample was taken from the monitoring well directly west of the building on-site. The nine geoprobe locations were drilled to approximately 10 feet (ft) below ground surface (bgs). Groundwater samples were taken at the soil-groundwater interface and soil samples were collected within 0.5 to 3 ft bgs and 5 to 8 ft bgs. Samples were analyzed for total petroleum hydrocarbons in the gasoline, diesel, and heavy-oil range; BTEX+N; volatile organic compounds (VOCs); polyaromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs), and dissolved lead. <br/><br/>

Contamination remaining in soil and groundwater beneath the site consists mainly of gasoline-range hydrocarbons and heavy-oil range hydrocarbons. The contamination appears to extend beneath Hwy 101, south of the site. Concentrations of the remaining contamination on-site and off-site are below all applicable Risk Based Concentrations (RBCs).",21768.0,0.0,ALEIDEL,2021-03-25 17:53:20.690
