26621,22-04-1936,22,04,1936,,2004-09-21,2004-09-24 16:23:22,Nofziger Farm,36882 KGAL DR,LEBANON,97355,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : TWO 1500-GAL USTS POPPED UP FROM GROUND 20+ YEARS AGO AND HAVE BEEN USED AS ASTS EVER SINCE.  STILL IN USE.  RELEASE IS FROM FORMER UST LOCATION. *** Pjt Mgr = C. Rodda.  Two 1500-gal USTs popped up from ground 20+ years ago and have been used as ASTs ever since.  Still in use.  Release is from former UST location.

De-assignment letter sent 11/4/2011.

Site was re-assigned in 2014 to C. Rodda. New well installed without DEQ review, sampled two times in 2014 with low concentrations of petroleum (below MRLs) in May and September samples. DEQ closing site with recommendations for in NFA. RP is making monthly payments on invoice, NFA to be issued when paid in full (CJR 12/12/2014)",,"The site is utilized as a grass seed farm in rural Linn County. Two 1500-gallon underground storage tanks were removed from the property in 1983. The tanks were located on the eastern half of the property and held gasoline and diesel products. A shop building was constructed over the former tank location in 1995. An assessment was completed in 2004 that identified a release of petroleum from the former tanks to soil and groundwater. DEQ requested additional investigation, including the on-site water supply well. Domestic wells near the site are 1/3-mile away. Approximately 20 yards of petroleum contaminated soil was excavated from the former tank location adjacent to the shop building. Soil samples were collected from the sidewalls and bottom  and analyzed for gasoline and diesel. DEQ requested follow-up samples with analysis for VOCs and PAHs based on the concentrations of gasoline and diesel in the confirmation samples. A new water supply well was installed in 2013 and was tested in May and September 2014. Some petroleum contaminants were detected in each sample but at concentrations below drinking water standards. DEQ recommended a carbon treatment system for the residence at the site.",96292.0,0.0,CRODDA,2014-12-12 16:14:22.083
