27213,34-05-0011,34,05,0011,12223.0,2004-12-23,2005-01-03 10:22:15,KOUKLANI PROPERTY,60405 NW SUNSET HIGHWAY,TIMBER,97144,,False,4.0,GW,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Two tanks (a 6,500-gallon gasoline UST and a 6,000-gallon UST with gasoline and diesel compartments) were removed from the site in January 2005, along with 37 tons of contaminated soils and 1,327 gallons of contaminated groundwater.  Confirmation sampling found gasoline and diesel remaining in the soil and shallow groundwater.  Three monitoring wells were installed in March 2007, but no cleanup was conducted.

In September 2016, additional soil and groundwater samples were collected on behalf of a new property owner, and only low levels of contamination were identified.  No contaminants were detected in the monitoring wells in March and June 2017.  A restriction was recorded with the property deed in June 2018 prohibiting consumption or other beneficial use of shallow groundwater at the site.

A draft CNFA letter was prepared in July 2018.  Final invoices have not been paid, and the property appears to have been abandoned.",,,87995.0,4498.0,KDANA,2021-08-02 15:11:58.330
