4/20/05 Admin closure because contamination appears to be related to contaminated fill and not a release from an UST",ECSI #4481,"A 2004 environmental site assessment determined that a service station (at 3014 SE Powell) had previously operated at the site from about 1935-1950, and that Robben & Sons Heating, a commercial heating oil delivery company, had operated at 3024 SE Powell from about 1940-1970.  Two 10,000-gallon heating oil USTs at Robben & Sons appeared to have been replaced by a 3,000-gallon heating oil tank circa 1960, but the fate of the other tanks was unknown.  Soil samples collected from the site in January 2005 found up to 391 ppm diesel and 2,590 ppm heavy oils, and a release was reported to DEQ.  However, no leaking tanks were identified, and DEQ subsequently determined that the contamination was likely from imported fill materials rather than leaking tanks.  The LUST file was administratively closed in April 2005, and the contamination was referred to DEQ's Environmental Cleanup program.  See ECSI file #4481 for more information.",89255.0,0.0,KDANA,2021-04-08 13:48:18.490
