27402,03-05-0198,03,05,0198,953.0,2005-02-08,2005-02-08 16:42:24,CONOCOPHILLIPS #3705 II,453 SE FIRST,CANBY,97013,(503)263-6876,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"9/26/05 letter sent requesting reports/info by 10/17/05. 10/20/05 report received.

02/25/09 letter sent requesting work plan for additional well along north side of property.  DEQ was informed by Stantec that site had been transferred to Delta.  Contacted Delta and they had not received letter in transition.  Letter emailed to Delta on 4-10-09.  Await work plan.  DEQ received letter dated 10-12-09 indicating that Delta Consultants had assumed liability from CP (JKS 11-3-09).  In May 2010, Delta submitted a work plan for the installation of monitoring well MW-1.  Work plan was approved via emial on May 18, 2010.  Well was reportedly installed at teh site on or around June 22, 2010.  Report documenting the installation of MW-1 north of UST pit received in September 2010. Gasoline, diesel, or oil-range hydrocarbons not detcted in soil samples collected at depths of 30 and 38 feet.  Oil-range hydrocarbons detected in groundwater from MW-1 at 420 ppb. Initial groundwater monitoring event in September 2010 did not reveal detectable levels of gasoline, diesel, oil, or RBDM VOCs (JKS 10-28-10).  Monitoring underway (JKS 12-9-10).  November 2010 data had no detections of petroleum hydrocarbons or BTEX (JKS 2-8-11).  In April 2011, consultant reported there were no detections in site monitoring wells.  June 2010 detection of TPH-O was not repeated.  Antea Group will start on a risk-based evaluation in support of request for NFA status (JKS 5-24-11). Antea Group submitted a risk-based closure report in April 2012. The document was mostly complete, although a figure showing the locations of water wells identified in the vicinity of the site was not provided.  Ante Group provided the missing figure in May 2012.  Per Antea Group, CP is fine with a conditional NFA prohibiting residential use of site.  Public comment period opened  May 7, 2012 and closed June 8, 2012 with no comments received.  Site ready for NFA (JKS 6-18-12).",LUST #03-05-0198,,18596.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2012-09-05 08:37:11.690
