27963,03-05-0759,03,05,0759,,2005-04-18,2005-04-19 11:28:12,WOOD PROPERTY,12401 S CASTO RD,OREGON CITY,97045,,False,7.0,,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"A release of gasoline (86 ppm) was reported at this rural farm site in April 2005.  Wesley Wood claimed he sold the property at a discount to Richard & Sheri Hallwyler in June 2005 and so was no longer liable.  DEQ soon lost contact with Wood and was unable to establish contact with the Hallwylers (no phone numbers were available, and the parties didn't respond to letters).

In October 2014 Universal Applicators decommissioned by removal a 500-gallon HOT at the site.  Soil sampling found only 200 ppm diesel at one end of the tank, below the Soil Matrix Level III cleanup standard of 1,000 ppm determined to be applicable for the site.  A report was submitted to the HOT program for certification.  In November 2014, UA mentioned in an e-mail to DEQ that the gasoline tank had also been decommissioned and that no contamination had been encountered.  UA planned to amend their Soil Matrix Cleanup report to include information on the gas tank decommissioning.  (12/4/14 KPD)",,,94979.0,5105.0,KDANA,2014-12-04 10:30:28.270
