28089,22-05-0885,22,05,0885,7065.0,2005-04-29,2005-05-04 17:13:20,Timeout Food Stop,1810 MAIN ST,SWEET HOME,97386,(503) 367-4264,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : DISCOVERED CONTAMINATION DURING SITE ASSESSMENT ASSOCIATED WITH POTENTIAL SALE. *** Discovered contamination during site assessment associated with potential sale.

1/14/2010: unassigned C. Rodda as project manager as part of ""Assigned Project List"" evaluation required by manager; site has not been active since reported in 2005 and is now on Tanks Backlog (C. Rodda)

6-27-2013, based on latest UST SOC compliance inspection, Truax Corporation, Corvallis, OR currently operating retail portion, PetroCard operating cardlock portion.  Truax accepting UST compliance responsibilities.  Field citation issued for overfill alarms and cathodic protection monitoring violation. rhr 6-27-2013 ",,,22781.0,0.0,HROSE,2013-06-27 10:41:52.323
28090,15-05-0886,15,05,0886,6520.0,2005-04-25,2005-05-05 15:10:18,COLVIN OIL 76,7640 CRATER LAKE HWY,WHITE CITY,97503,541-479-5343,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,NW Pump & Equipment is the RP & Invoicee since they caused the leak while making a repair to the system.  GW extraction system installed but no longer operating as of October 2006,"15-92-0044 and 15-96-0042: NFA with pocket closure in May 1998 (see WebDocs page for 15-96-0042) - C. Rodda, 2/11/2011","In April 2005, an unleaded gasoline release was reported after free-phase petroleum was found in observation wells within the tank nest. Based on inventory records, an estimated 1,800 gallons of fuel was lost from the tank system. Half of the fuel was recovered through cleanup efforts, with over 14,000 gallons of water and 900 gallons of free product pumped from observation wells. The fuel and water mix was aerated in a treatment tank and discharged to the municipal storm sewer under permit. Four monitoring wells were installed in June 2006. During well construction, soil samples were collected from the borings and no contaminants were present above laboratory reporting limits. Quarterly monitoring confirmed contamination in groundwater, including gasoline, benzene, and MTBE. Groundwater flow has been measured to the southwest. Two additional monitoring wells were installed in February 2010 immediately south within Antelope Road and adjacent to another tank cleanup site. Groundwater contained only toluene at 1.0 ppb during the initial sampling event, with remaining results below detection levels at these two wells throughout 2010 monitoring. Well MW-6 contained the highest concentrations of petroleum in monitoring since 2006, and concentrations seemed to be decreasing or remained stable. Only MTBE was detected in the last sampling event of November 2010 at MW-5 and MW-7. Soil samples were collected during well installation in 2006, and no petroleum contamination was detected. However, each boring was located far outside of the known or potential source areas for a tank system. Petroleum contamination was left in place from the previous release (closed in 1998) at the facility.",15441.0,0.0,CRODDA,2012-05-22 16:11:16.403
