GeoScience installed 3 borings for site assessment on 9/7/2005, additional assessment by Wohlers Environmental in November 2005 - C. Rodda",,"The site currently operates as a retail service station with three USTs  and one dispenser island.  A 2005 site assessment identified petroleum contamination in groundwater by fuel released from the UST system.  A site assessment in September 2005 included three push-probe borings installed to a depth of 20 feet.  Petroleum contamination was not present in soil samples collected from the boreholes.  Impacts to groundwater were identified on-site in two of the temporary wells, and included detections of benzene (234 ppb), toluene (184 ppb), ethylbenzene (79 ppb), and xylenes (98 ppb).   Groundwater monitoring was performed quarterly until March 2009.  Concentrations of gasoline and RBDM VOCs were present throughout the monitoring.  Wells MW-1, MW-3, and MW-4 measured relatively low concentrations of petroleum contaminants throughout their sampling history.",17052.0,0.0,CRODDA,2009-12-23 09:30:48.860
