29957,34-06-0149,34,06,0149,1373.0,2006-01-25,2006-01-26 07:51:18.000,SHELL STATION #121438,6055 SW HALL BLVD,BEAVERTON,97008,,False,4.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"QM;  next event: 8/2016 , site will need CMMP eventually

3/15/17See my 8/31/16 email to Cliff at URS. (RAH)

From Dec. 2015 meeeting:
-City plans to develop it's property to west of the Shell property.  will need engineering controls, see the unocal 5664 EES with 1st and Arthur-would be similar and Gerding edlen was involved with that project also. 
-need more delineation, not having them run dx for sg given the extremely high gx anyway, cumulative failure of tph.
    - Cliff to provide most recent data tables, me reply to 10/2015 rept and 12/2015 qm rept (see if it did this I think I was waiting for Cliff to provide data tables, but have further sampling up to 2nd quarter 2016 now)), City and Shell to begin discussions of cost reimbursements.  
    -Shell prop will need ees for occ also and more vi and ?indoor sampling as sg conc. > vi for occ. (RAH)


8/2015: GP samples indicated even more contamination (from 2013).  AECOM to install one add. MW (114) and two add. SG points on City Beaverton Prop. approved work plan in June.  Note re: soil gas on subject prop., sg-1 acceptable results for current use.  if no add. sg points are installed closer to sg-02, then would need to prohibit any buildings west of sg-01. For soil gas, should technically analyze for Dx also, but given the gas hits, i have not requested it given the gas release is the larger of the plumes (will need to cleanup up or protect for diesel also in the end though).  with the Gas as high as it is, it's a given with the diesel, the cumalative risk is unacceptable, also.  (RAH)

1/2015:  video of stormsewer showed no major structural issues.  Appears to be no new source contributing to this release.  Soil delineation is pretty good now.. GW not delineated in the vicinity of GP-1 and MW-111.  GP-1 h20 fails exc. worker.  Soil gas fails occupational on subject property and city property, needs delineation.  (RAH)

1/2014;  approved video plan of stormwater system. (RAH)

10.2013:  Inv. on beaverton property, no new source found.  contamination may be following utility.  URS to do more soil gas sampling and video of utililty. 

4.11.2013:  reviewed sg/mw-111 install report.  delineation not complete.  one more round of sg sampling and from MW-111-gw.  URS developing work plan for completing delineation and possibly looking for potential other sources out here (based on verbal from gas station owner that some sort of surface release occurred on the City Property some time in the past during construction work). (RAH)


6.19.12:  installed one additional MW toward west for delineation.  will complete a couple extra quarters and determine conditions. (RAH)

After 11/2011 event, should have updated csm.  But should get some delineation west of mw106/7 area.  ~6 Jan 2012.

12/5/2011:  replied to oct. 2011 report.  response from URS due 1/6/12. (RAH)


From KD
Two releases were reported at this site in 2006.  In January, 8.72 tons of PCS were removed from beneath a missing spill bucket.  In April, a hoist in the service bay was removed, and contamination was detected in the soil down to 10 feet bgs.  Neither release has been further addressed.

Seven borings were advanced around the site in August 2007 as part of a site assessment, finding gasoline and diesel in the soil and groundwater, primarily on the west side of the site.  Five groundwater monitoring wells were installed in a circle around the edges of the site in May 2008, and have been sampled quarterly since.  The two wells on the west side of the site are moderately contaminated.  Groundwater flow is to the northwest.  Downgradient, off-site monitoring wells are needed to determine the extent of the contamination.  (2/10/11 KPD)",LUST #34-94-0030,,18857.0,7003.0,RHOOD,2017-03-15 12:12:45.553
