30293,24-06-0482,24,06,0482,,2006-03-20,2006-03-24 16:26:27.000,Turner Dairy,4481 HENNIES RD SE,TURNER,97392,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : DISCOVERED WHEN EXCAVATING FOR AST RELEASE. *** Pjt Mgr = JLG.  Discovered when excavating for AST release.,,"On March 20, 2006, DEQ received notice that gasoline had leaked from both an above-ground storage tank (AST) and an underground storage tank (UST) on this property.  The Site has been farming property from early 1900s and is, as of this writing, an organic dairy.  UST systems were used for gasoline storage between ~1940 and 1981.  AST systems were used for gasoline storage between 1981 until removal in 2006.  Site contamination was determined to be due to leakage from both AST and UST systems. Approximately 450 tons of petroleum-contaminated soil removed from the site was transported for disposal to Riverbend Landfill in McMinnville, Oregon. Petroleum contamination remains in soil and groundwater north, northeast, and east of the former fuel storage area. This remaining area of petroleum contamination extents approximately 100 feet downhill toward the water supply well.  Water supply to the residence and dairy cattle operations is provided by the on-site well. After extensive assessment of the sub-surface lithology and three separate water bearing zones, DEQ has determined that the confined-aquifer used for human and dairy cattle drinking water appears to be isolated from the area of remaining contamination. Procedures for working in the area of the remaining contamination are clearly defined in a “Contaminated Media Management Plan”.  As such DEQ has determined that with limitations on future contaminated media management, the remaining contamination is stable, should naturally attenuate over time, and should not pose a threat to human health and the environment given the current and reasonably likely future use.",12330.0,0.0,JGLASS,2017-01-31 11:11:03.743
