30342,26-06-0530,26,06,0530,3968.0,2006-03-30,2006-03-30 16:08:56.000,KEVIN'S AUTO SERVICE,536 SE TACOMA ST,PORTLAND,97202,,False,7.0,,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"An environmental investigation was conducted in March 2006 on three adjacent properties, including Kevin's Auto Service.  Soil samples were collected from 22 borings across the three properties and analyzed for petroleum products.  Gasoline (up to 1,020 ppm), diesel (2,260 ppm), and heavy oil (10,700 ppm) were all detected, with most of the contamination and most of the borings at Kevin's Auto.  No groundwater was encountered to 50 ft bgs.

The buildings at the site were razed in 2012, and the site is currently being used for construction equipment staging for the Sellwood Bridge Replacement Project.  Two gasoline USTs (2,000- and 3,000-gallon capacity) were removed in September 2013, along with 170 tons of PCS.  Full investigation and cleanup of the site will not be conducted until completion of the Sellwood Bridge project.  (11/21/13 KPD)",ECSI #5684,,20676.0,0.0,KDANA,2013-11-21 11:03:54.360
