30428,06-06-0615,06,06,0615,,2006-04-01,2006-04-11 13:50:54.000,FORMER TOSCO/UNOCAL BULK PLANT 0531,1893 ROSEBURG RD,MYRTLE POINT,97458,(503)572-2926,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : ACTIVE BULK PLANT- RELEASE IS CUMULATIVE FROM HISTORIC PRACTICES...CPJ 4/1/06 TRANSFERRED FROM VCP TO TANKS PROGRAM 4/1/06..CPJ. SEE ALSO LUST# 06-90-0017 AND ECSI# 2532. *** Transferred from VCP to Tanks Program 4/1/06.  Active bulk plant; release is cumulative from historic practices...cpj 4/1/06.

LUST # 06-90-0017 release and UST facility #620 has the same address as the 06-06-0615 release, but the UST system is actually south and across the street from the bulk facility. 

There are no USTs at this CU site LUST # 06-06-0615 and ECSI # 2532. All of the leaks were from the AST or piping that went to and from there to their loading docks or incidential spills over the years. (8/18/2017 TMD)","ECSI# 2532 and LUST #06-90-0017 (the latter release is not from this site, but from the facility to the south). LUST # 06-90-0017 release and UST facility #620 has the same address as the 06-06-0615 release, but the UST system is actually south and across the street from the bulk facility. There are no USTs at LUST # 06-06-0615 and ECSI # 2532. All of the leaks were from the AST or piping that went to and from there to their loading docks or incidential spills over the years.","This facility was constructed in the late 1960's and the sources of the contamination have been historical spills over time. There were two initial spills, of about 100 gallons of oil each, in April and May, 1998, which went into secondary containment, but then due to malfunctions in the oil/water separator system, were discharged through the local storm drain and into a drainage ditch to a field across the highway from the plant. In late 2001-early 2002, a line leak occurred and free product was observed near the surface and along the north ditch. These releases were cleaned up at the time and additional soil borings and monitoring wells were installed and sampled and analyzed over time to investigate the site. The public comment period extended through March 3, 2017. An Easement & Equitable Servitude had been placed on this site. A conditional ""no further action"" determination was issued for this site on November 27, 2017.

Leaking Underground Storage Tank database # 06-90-0017 release and Underground Storage Tank facility #620 has the same address as the 06-06-0615 release, but the underground storage tanks are actually south and across the street from the bulk facility. There are no underground storage tanks at the 06-06-0615 site. All of the leaks were from the aboveground storage tanks or piping that went to and from these tanks to their loading docks or incidential spills over the years.",11553.0,0.0,GDECK,2017-11-27 15:50:42.007
30429,26-06-0616,26,06,0616,,2006-04-11,2006-04-11 16:05:38.000,PIEREN'S AUTOMOTIVE,2105 N KILLINGSWORTH ST,PORTLAND,97217,,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"An environmental assessment of the site in March 2006 identified a 675-gallon gasoline UST and a 275-gallon waste oil UST outside the building, and an in-ground hydraulic hoist and floor drain inside the building.  Soil sampling found contamination near the hoist and waste oil UST.  The two tanks and the hoist were removed in June 2006 along with 30 cubic yards of PCS.  Contaminated soils to the north of the hoist could not be removed.  An initial sample of this area had found 17,000 ppm diesel, 34,000 ppm heavy oil, 1.8 ppm PCBs, and 0.4 ppm TCE.

The TCE concentration exceeded residential vapor intrusion standards, so DEQ required an EES be placed on the site prohibiting residential redevelopment.  The EES was recorded in February 2008, and a conditional NFA letter was issued.

In September 2008, an additional 34.54 tons of PCS were excavated from the site, and 630 lbs. of RegenOx were added to the excavation pit.  An additional 100 lbs. of RegenOx were injected into the backfilled excavation through three borings in October 2008.

Information on the additional remediation was submitted to DEQ in March 2012, and the project was re-opened for further evaluation in May 2012.  DEQ concluded in June 2012 that additional confirmation sampling was necessary before the EES could be removed.  Until such sampling is conducted, the February 2008 EES and conditional NFA remain in place.",92622.0,7468.0,KDANA,2013-04-01 09:56:02.263
