30660,20-06-0847,20,06,0847,5230.0,2006-05-12,2006-05-12 09:42:09.000,Hwy 99 Cardlock,50 HIGHWAY 99 N,EUGENE,97402,(541)683-4433,False,1.0,RBCA,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Pjt Mgr=CRodda,"20-91-4335  Pacific Petroleum
20-17-0611  Highway 99 Cardlock","The Highway 99 Cardlock facility is an active fuel station with numerous underground tanks used to store petroleum products. Gasoline and diesel products are distributed at two separate cardlock stations, and this letter specifically addresses the gasoline facility for which a petroleum release was reported in 2006. The facility utilizes one 12,000-gallon and one 4,000-gallon capacity tanks for gasoline storage.

An environmental assessment was performed at the gasoline tank system in 2006, and included investigations of the adjacent diesel cardlock and truck shop at 2455 West 5th Avenue. Nine borings were advanced surrounding the gasoline cardlock dispensers and tanks. Gasoline contamination was present in soil samples obtained from the boreholes. Groundwater samples collected from the push-probe borings at the gasoline cardlock detected VOC constituents, as well as some PAH compounds above DEQ standards. Low levels of petroleum were detected at the diesel tank system and truck shop.

In March 2007, three monitoring wells were installed near the 4,000-gallon gasoline tank. Soil samples were collected from the borings advanced for well construction, but did not contain petroleum contamination. Monitoring performed from April 2007 through July 2009 provided information on the petroleum contaminant levels in site groundwater. Gasoline-range hydrocarbons were detected at concentrations ranging from 1,290 ppb (July 2009) to 5,660 ppb (January 2008) in MW-11. Wells MW-9 and MW-10 measured relatively minor levels of contamination, and were not included in 2009 groundwater monitoring.",21459.0,0.0,GDECK,2017-05-30 17:41:02.047
