30760,24-06-0947,24,06,0947,8963.0,2006-05-10,2006-05-23 14:46:45.000,Del Web Cardlock,1190 INDUSTRIAL DR,SALEM,97303,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : DURING A BASELINE ENVIRONMENTAL ASSESSMENT (BEA) FOR THE PURPOSE OF A PROPERTY TRANSFER, DIESEL CONTAMINATION WAS DETECTED IN THE SOIL AND GROUNDWATER...KLEINFELDER *** aka Truax Harris Energy, LLC - Site 294.",LUST#24-18-0525 Del Web/Industrial Drive,"The site currently operates as a cardlock fuel facility utilizing four USTs  and one pump island. Observations during boring installations at the site identified gravel and cobbles with sand and silt to depths of up to 20 feet bgs .  The depth to groundwater in site monitoring wells was recorded at approximately 6 to 13 feet bgs.  Groundwater flow direction has generally been recorded to the southwest, but has also been measured to the southeast.
A baseline environmental assessment was performed in April 2006 and included the installation of four borings (KGP01 through KGP04) for the collection of soil and groundwater samples.  The borings were advanced to depths up to 16 feet bgs adjacent to the UST nest and dispenser island.  Soil and water samples were collected from each boring, with groundwater encountered at 6 to 12 feet bgs.  Analysis identified diesel- and lube oil-range hydrocarbons at maximum concentrations of 21.5 ppm  and 223 ppm respectively.  Soil also contained concentrations of PAHs  above laboratory detection levels.  Groundwater samples also contained petroleum contaminants, measuring diesel up to 2,070 ppb , lube oil at 1,630 ppb, and several PAHs at KGP01. Additional site characterization activities were completed in February 2007.  Six borings (KGP05 through KGP10) were advanced up to 20 feet bgs.  Soil samples were obtained from 5 to 15 feet bgs.  Groundwater was encountered at 8 to 17 feet bgs and samples were collected from each borehole.  The highest concentrations of diesel (205 ppm) and lube oil (493 ppm) were detected in the soil obtained from boring KGP08.  No further analysis for constituents was completed on soil samples during this phase of assessment.  Groundwater samples also contained diesel and lube oil, with the highest concentrations measuring 1,420 ppm and 2,690 ppm, respectively, at KGP10.  The only additional analysis completed was for BTEX  constituents, which all measured below laboratory detection levels.  Groundwater monitoring was initiated in June 2007 following installation of four monitoring wells.  Results identified the maximum concentrations of diesel at 2,750 ppb and lube oil-range hydrocarbons at 2,210 ppb in KMW03 during the initial sampling event in June 2007.  During the final sampling event in March 2008, diesel was detected at 1,290 ppb in KMW03 and lube oil was measured at 1,370 ppb in KMW02.  Several PAHs and BTEX constituents were detected during each monitoring event at relatively low levels.",24087.0,7694.0,JCLAUSS,2018-05-11 14:28:25.277
