30814,24-06-1001,24,06,1001,7160.0,2006-05-10,2006-05-31 14:52:22.000,Truax Harris Energy #302,4180 PORTLAND RD NE,SALEM,97303,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : DURING A BASELINE ENVIRONMENTAL ASSESSMENT (BEA) FOR THE PURPOSE OF A PROPERTY TRANSFER, DIESEL CONTAMINATION WAS DETECTED IN THE SOIL AND GROUNDWATER.  THIS SITE HAS PREVIOUSLY BEEN ISSUED A NO FURTHER ACTION STATUS FOR SOIL ONLY. SEE ALSO 24-92-4217 NORTH SALEM ARCO *** Duringa baseline environmental assessment (BEA) for the purpose of a property transfer, diesel contamination was detected in the soil & GW.  This site has been previously issued a NFA for soil only (24-92-4217).",24-92-4217 NORTH SALEM ARCO,"Observations during boring installations at the site identified silt and fine sand up to 45 feet bgs.  Groundwater was encountered in boreholes during 2006 assessment activities at approximately 3 to 12 feet bgs, and has been recorded in site monitoring wells at depths of 42 to 45 feet bgs.  Groundwater flow direction has generally been recorded to the east, but has also been measured to the south and southeast.  An environmental assessment was performed in April 2006 and included the installation of KGP01 through KGP06 for soil and groundwater samples.  The borings were advanced to depths of up to 40 feet bgs adjacent to the UST nest and dispenser islands.  Soil samples were collected from each boring at depths of 5 to 40 feet bgs.  Water was encountered in four borings at 3 to 12 feet bgs, and samples were collected of the shallow groundwater encountered in the borings.  The soil sample obtained from KGP06 contained concentrations of petroleum compounds.  The remaining borings did not measure concentrations of the analyzed compounds above laboratory detection limits.  Gasoline-range hydrocarbons and RBDM VOCs were below laboratory detection levels in each water sample.  Compliance groundwater monitoring was initiated in February 2007 utilizing wells still present from the previous investigation in 1993.  Water samples were collected on a quarterly basis from the monitoring wells KMW01, KMW02, and KMW03.  The last sampling event for all the wells occurred on November 2, 2007.  Water samples obtained from the wells contained several PAHs, and in KMW01 diesel was measured at 1,360 ppb and lube oil was 2,520 ppb.  Gasoline- and diesel-range hydrocarbons as well as BTEX constituents were measured below laboratory detection levels in the final monitoring event for KMW02 and KMW03.",115811.0,7696.0,DBA,2016-06-17 12:12:21.763
30815,24-06-1002,24,06,1002,,2006-05-12,2006-05-31 15:43:25.000,Lee Prantl,9344 MT ANGEL GERVAIS RD NE,GERVAIS,97026,Vacant,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,True,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : 550-GAL GASOLINE FARM UST, LAST USED ABOUT 10 YEARS AGO, CONTAINED 290 GAL OF WATER WHEN ASPEN DECOMMISSIONED IT.  IT'S HALF UNDER DETACHED EQUIPMENT GARAGE, WHICH WILL BE DEMOLISHED TO REMOVE THE IMPACTED SOIL TO PROTECT THE ONSITE WELL. *** 550-gal gasoline farm UST, last used about 10 years ago, contained 290 gal of water when Aspen decommissioned it.  It is half under a detached equipment garage, which will be demolished to remove the impacted soil so as to protect the onsite well.",,,99378.0,7720.0,GDECK,2007-08-27 15:57:42.653
