30821,24-06-1008,24,06,1008,12275.0,2006-05-17,2006-06-01 12:44:06.000,Wright Property,2121 FAIRGROUNDS RD NE,SALEM,97301,503-743-2291,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : HOT RELEASE REPORTED IN APRIL 2006 (24-06-0683); APPEARS AT THIS POINT TO ONLY HAVE REGULATED TANKS ON SITE. PERMITTING TO BE DETERMINED. ***.  HOT release reported by another consultant in April 2006 (24-06-0683); CJE says it appears at this point that there are only regulated tanks on site.,24-06-0683  DAVE WRIGHT ESTATE (HOT site)... this file administratively closed since there were no heating oil tanks; only gasoline.,"Petroleum contamination was initially reported to DEQ in early 2006 when the property owner had an environmental assessment performed.  Following the discovery of contamination, the property owner removed five underground storage tanks ranging from 1000-gallons to 2000-gallons in size.  Contamination was only observed in the NE corner of the former tank pit and was documented to have impacted both soil and groundwater. 

The property owners conducted an investigation to determine the extent of the contamination and installed three groundwater monitoring wells in 2007.   The area of contamination was determined to be centered beneath the former pump-islands.  In November 2008, the property owners removed twenty five tons of the most heavily contaminated soil, installed a series of push-probe sampling points and evaluated the results for any risk to human health or the environment. 

Based on the results of the site investigation, the follow up assessment and the completed cleanup actions, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land use, the remaining contamination has been reduced to levels protective of human health and the environment.  The proposed plan would allow any remaining contamination to naturally degrade in place.",97069.0,7846.0,GDECK,2010-02-05 16:55:25.883
