31188,02-06-1374,02,06,1374,,2006-07-28,2006-07-31 07:55:30.000,"GARMON, SUE",744 NW 12TH ST,CORVALLIS,97330,541/757-1781,False,1.0,RBCA,1.0,CRT,False,True,,,False,,,,,,,,99707.0,8216.0,CONV,2006-07-31 07:55:30.000
31189,34-06-1375,34,06,1375,5112.0,2006-07-31,2006-07-31 11:51:04.000,CORNELIUS ESTBY II,1021 E BASELINE STREET,CORNELIUS,97113,,False,4.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Items requested in September 25 2008 DEQ letter largely provided.  Comment letter sent on January 6, 2009 - investigation to delineate impacted groundwater downgradient again requested; Requested update on investigation on west adjacent property; work plan requested by February 10, 2009 - no work plan received.  Notified by K&S that Estby suspended work at site due to lack of funds.  Received report for monitorign performed in 3Q2009 (first event after monitoring resumed).  Levels of TPH-G in MW-1 jumped from 3.55 to 84.8 mg/L.  Benzene jumped from 114 to 19,600 ug/L.  Since this is only 3rd nonconscutive event since well installation, it is hard to know if this represents new release or not. Supposedly, the station was out of operation since early 2009 and tanks are empty. (JKS 10-20-09).  Attorney for Ms. Meyers reports his client has no funds and K&S is sitting on the report for the off-site investigation.  Warning letter sent to M&G Collections on August 19, 2010 requesting written notice of intent to comply within 30 days and completion of monitoing event within 60 days (JKS 09-13-10).  Called Ward Greene on September 23, 2010. Situation unchanged - still no money to pay K&S or do additional work until property is sold. Informed that furhter inaction may lead to enforcement (JKS 9-23-10).  RP requested ATP in letter dated 9-23-10.  ATP evaluation concluded in November 2010 no undue hardship.  Follow-up letter sent 12-14-10 - No reponse.  2nd Warning Letter sent 2-8-11.  Letter from M&G dated 3-22-11 claimed no funds to proceed.  PEN sent 4-14-11 (JKS 4-20-11). Letter received from RP dated May 9, 2011 - no compliance demonstrated. Referral made to OCE in July 2011.  Penalty and Order issued 10-25-11.  Order became final January 2012.  In October/November 2012, M&G contacted DEQ and reported there is a prospective buyer.  M&G requested what needed to be done to bring site into compliance with Order.  Discussed performing a snapshot monitoring event to assess site conditions.  Approved proposal for monitoring in December 2012.  Await results of monitoring.  Despite request, no contact from interested buyer (JKS 1-22-13).

Work plan to perform groundwater monitoring, soil gas sampling and delineation investigation submitted to DEQ in November 2018. Work Plan approved. Waiting for investigation results. (JKS 4-22-19).",,"July 2006 investigation in area of USTs revealed gasoline contamination.  Follow up investigations performed in 2007 and 2008.  Infrequent groundwater monitoring peformed until August 2009, which coincided with a significant increase in gasoline and benzene.  Owner at the time suspended all work. DEQ took owner to Enforcement in 2010 for failure to perform groundwater monitoring and delineate the extent of contamination.  
Additional groundwater monitoring perfomed in December 2012, February 2016, August 2016, December 2016 and December 2018.  Work plan for soil gas investigation and borings to delineate extent of contamination submitted in November 2018. Work plan approved.  Await investigation per approved work plan 

USTs are in temporary closure status.  Permit modificaiton application needed for new owner as of 2015.  (JKS 4-22-19).",21384.0,8219.0,JSCHATZ,2019-04-22 11:36:58.610
