31352,26-06-1538,26,06,1538,,2006-08-24,2006-08-25 06:58:44.000,"SPALDING, SALLY",6030 SE 20TH AVE,PORTLAND,97202,(503) 235-2926,False,1.0,RBCA,1.0,CRT,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"*** SEQUENT LUST COMMENTS : 25KPPM AND ND ***

8/27/2010 from Dana Thompson Tanks and Soil: 
At the request of DEQ Staff, DTT&S staff went to the site to determine the
current vertical extent of petroleum impact, but the rocky soil conditions halted the advance of sampling equipment. On August 17,2010 DTT&S staff cut and removed a section of the concrete driveway. A mini excavator was used to excavate soil at the west end of the tank. Impacted soil was noted to have spread 12"" north and 18"" south of the center line of the west tank end, and halted vertically on the surface of a large boulder. There was no evidence that
petroleum had spread to the edge of the boulder to penetrate beyond 76"" bgs.
Soil along the north and south side walls of the tank was excavated and there
was no visual or olfactory evidence that the release at the had spread laterally
beyond the tank side walls. It is estimated that there may be three to five cubic feet of petroleum impacted soil remaining beneath the west tank end.",,,98837.0,8371.0,RWELLS,2010-08-27 14:23:45.113
