31657,20-06-1843,20,06,1843,5069.0,2006-10-13,2006-10-16 14:19:37.000,MURPHY PLYWOOD,1900 IRVING RD,EUGENE,97402,(541) 461-4545,False,2.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Two separate tank systems were decommissioned from facility in 2006. Low detections of diesel and lube oil detected in soil, no groundwater encountered (CJR 10/13/2014)","20-89-4006 Georgia Pacific
ECSI # 1082","The site is located within a large plywood facility owned by Murphy Company. A petroleum release was reported in October 2006 when three underground storage tanks were removed from the property. DEQ assigned LUST #20-06-1843 to the release at one of two decomissioned tank systems. Contractors coordinated the tank decommisioning activities and sampling. Two different tank systems were decommissioned in September 2006. Tank Area #1 consisted of one 10,000-gallon diesel tank and one 2,000-gallon gasoline tank, and was the source of the reported petroleum release creating this LUST site. Tank Area #2 included only one 10,000-gallon diesel tank. Both locations utilized a dispenser separated from the tank nest by piping. No petroleum release was reported for Tank Area #2, located south of the warehouse building. Six soil samples were collected from the excavations at each tank end, most from 10 to 11.5 feet below ground surface. One shallow soil sample was collected from each dispenser location. Per DEQ decommissioning requirements, the contractor analyzed each soil sample for the presence of hydrocarbons using the NWTPH-HCID method. Lube oil was detected in sample D from the dispenser of Tank Area #1 located north of a lubricant shed. Further analysis for TPH-diesel measured diesel at 50.5 parts per million and oil-range hydrocarbons at 71.6 ppm. Based on the detections of petroleum in the 2006 sampling, DEQ requested additional assessment to confirm minimal contamination was present at the site. The requested work was not completed, and the site was put on a list of backlog projects. Following a cursory review of file records, DEQ evaluated whether the site was eligible for closure without further investgation. Murphy Plywood representatives agreed to DEQ oversight related to No Further Action determination in August 2014.",1200.0,0.0,CRODDA,2014-10-13 12:46:38.600
