31770,26-06-1956,26,06,1956,,2006-10-31,2006-11-06 09:40:46.333,Sacred Temple,7315 N FESSENDEN ST,PORTLAND,97203,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Release reported in November 2006 following investigation by Western Geologic, on behalf of Wells Fargo.  No 20-day or 45-day reports have been submitted to DEQ to date. Benzene reportedly detected in four samples, presumably soil.  RP contacted in April 2009 and copy of Western Geologic report requested.  RP claims he never received it, although the file contains a paper copy of an email communication from WG to the RP which included the report in electronic form.  Second email sent 6-3-09, requesting update of inquiry by 6-17-09.  Report provided to DEQ on 6-5-09.  DEQ comment letter requesting a work plan for delineation of impacts in the area of boring DP-4 was sent on 6-30-09.  Letter did not incolude a deadline.  No response as of 10-23-09.  Second letter requesting work plan with deadline was sent on 10-28-09.  Western Geologic report scanned and emailed to RP on 11-24-09.  RP requested ATP analysis via email on 1-22-10.  ATP letter sent out 1-13-10.  DEQ informed that ATP documents not received by RP and a secon packet was sent out.  On August 19, 2010, Financial Analyst provided his preliminary ATP analysis. Analysis concluded that RP could dispose of a property that is producing negative income - not undue hardship (JKS 09-15-10).  

Contacted by consultant (Tetratech) that is brother in law of Mr. Champ on 11-12-10.  He has reviewed DEQ correspondence and believes DEQ's request for a soil-gas investigation is reasonable.  He will look into procedures and costs associated with doing investigation so that site could be backlogged (JKS 12-9-10).

In September 2014, Alpha submitted a report documentuing a soil-gas investigation at the site.  Gasoline and related VOCs were not detected at concentrations above RBCs for even residential property use.  Based on depth of contaminatino at boring DP-4 (17 feet bgs), residents, occupational workers and construction/excavation workers are unlikely to contact contamination at DP-4 (JKS 1-26-15).",,"Release reported in November 2006 following investigation by Western Geologic, on behalf of Wells Fargo.  No 20-day or 45-day reports have been submitted to DEQ to date. Benzene reportedly detected in four samples, presumably soil.  RP contacted in April 2009 and copy of Western Geologic report requested.  RP claims he never received it, although the file contains a paper copy of an email communication from WG to the RP which included the report in electronic form.  Second email sent 6-3-09, requesting update of inquiry by 6-17-09.  Report provided to DEQ on 6-5-09.  DEQ comment letter requesting a work plan for delineation of impacts in the area of boring DP-4 was sent on 6-30-09.  Letter did not incolude a deadline.  No response as of 10-23-09.  Second letter requesting work plan with deadline was sent on 10-28-09.  Western Geologic report scanned and emailed to RP on 11-24-09.  RP requested ATP analysis via email on 1-22-10.  ATP letter sent out 1-13-10.  DEQ informed that ATP documents not received by RP and a secon packet was sent out.  On August 19, 2010, Financial Analyst provided his preliminary ATP analysis. Analysis concluded that RP could dispose of a property that is producing negative income - not undue hardship (JKS 09-15-10).  

Contacted by consultant (Tetratech) that is brother in law of Mr. Champ on 11-12-10.  He has reviewed DEQ correspondence and believes DEQ's request for a soil-gas investigation is reasonable.  He will look into procedures and costs associated with doing investigation so that site could be backlogged (JKS 12-9-10).

In September 2014, Alpha submitted a report documentuing a soil-gas investigation at the site.  Gasoline and related VOCs were not detected at concentrations above RBCs for even residential property use.  Based on depth of contaminatino at boring DP-4 (17 feet bgs), residents, occupational workers and construction/excavation workers are unlikely to contact contamination at DP-4 (JKS 1-26-15).",100017.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2015-01-26 14:03:19.817
