31776,29-06-1962,29,06,1962,,2006-10-04,2006-11-07 16:25:24.290,Highway 101 Right-of-Way,NE Corner of 7th St & Hwy 101,NEHALEM,97131,,True,4.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Small abondoned tanks with gasoline found in roadway during ODOT construction project.  Investigation is being performed under Stimulus money. LLC,,"The Site consists of the right-of-way (ROW) at the northeast corner of 7th Street and Highway 101, also known as H Street, in the City of Nehalem. 

The Site is defined as the location of three abandoned USTs found by ODOT during a 2006 highway reconstruction project and the area immediately surrounding the tanks. The USTs were removed in 2006 by ODOT, who reported petroleum contamination in the soils and groundwater surrounding the tanks. The Site is currently covered by a sidewalk. 

The USTs at the Site were associated with the former service station located at 36005 7th Street in Nehalem, Oregon, directly to the east of the Site. The former service station property associated with the Site is currently operating as a retail establishment.  

On 11/18/2009, 11 soil borings were completed to assess the soil and gw at and near the Site. Three of the borings were completed as monitoring wells.

Concentrations detected in soil did not exceed the relevant screening levels at applicable points of compliance, with the exception of the benzo(a)pyrene and naphthalene detected in boring B-6. It is recommended that a copy of this report be maintained by the property owner (City of Nehalem) so that this exceedance is known in the event that a construction project or land use change is conducted in the vicinity of boring B-6. The remaining concentrations of constituents in soil do not pose an unacceptable risk.

Concentrations in gw did not exceed the relevant screening levels at applicablepoints of compliance. The Site was flooded immediately preceding the sampling of MW-3, so it is recommended that the additional groundwater data be collected during the summer dry season.  A sampling event is scheduled for Aug. 2010. 

This site is being investigated with ARRA funding.  The SI Work Plan and the SI Report are included in the Site Document Section of this database.",112745.0,0.0,LKENT,2010-12-15 15:33:06.073
