31992,20-06-2177,20,06,2177,,2006-12-22,2006-12-22 11:13:07.207,"Kochan, Phil",1673 Wilson Ct,EUGENE,97402,,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,True,False,False,False,False,,,,100535.0,9014.0,UPACHMA,2007-01-25 14:47:26.363
31993,36-06-2178,36,06,2178,,2006-11-30,2006-12-22 16:35:26.140,Dave Redford,13530 SE KIMSEY RD,DAYTON,97114,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Two farm tanks next to each other, 1 diesel and 1 gas... John Harding (Xavier).",,"The site has been a rural residence since at least 1947 and may have been developed as early as 1924. Contamination is the result of multiple corrosion holes in a 675-gallon gasoline tank that formerly held diesel fuel. Soil and groundwater within about 35 feet of the former tank pit were impacted by gasoline and to a lesser degree diesel fuel. Two fuel tanks (675-gallon gasoline and 500-gallon diesel) were decommissioned by removal in April 2007. About 40 tons of soil was excavated to a depth of 19.5 feet below ground, which removed a majority of the contamination. Additional sampling conducted on the property has shown that there are no longer detectable concentrations of contaminants in the soil. However, groundwater covering an area about 25 feet by 35 feet beneath the former tank pit and extending south remains impacted with gasoline and related constituents. The onsite drinking water well is located about 125 feet away from the former tank pit. It was sampled and is unimpacted by the remaining contamination. The property is assumed to remain a rural residence that uses an onsite drinking water well. Any future well installed on the property should be installed with caution, as far away from and up gradient (north) of the former tank pit as possible in order to limit potential impacts from any remaining contamination. The investigation was limited to an area shown on the attached figure. If other fuel tanks exist or existed on the property they have not been addressed at this time.",100537.0,8919.0,CRICHAR,2019-06-18 15:03:28.540
31994,17-06-2179,17,06,2179,,2006-12-07,2006-12-28 09:36:26.883,Nesika S.W. Inc.,202-212A Redwood Highway,CAVE JUNCTION,97523,541-592-6707,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,101532.0,8961.0,GDECK,2007-03-20 18:25:48.340
31995,26-06-2180,26,06,2180,9344.0,2006-12-28,2006-12-28 16:00:59.307,FALCON INC II,1725 E POWELL BLVD,GRESHAM,97030,(503) 643-8046,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"File recalled from archives and cost recovery account reopened due to a request from an impacted property owner (Galen Fancher) north of the site to be released from the requirements of the E&ES dated September 22, 2009.  At the request of DEQ, the monitoring well on the adjacent property was sampled in August 2012 and January 2013.  Levels of gasoline and related contaminants were shown to be less than the levels known at the time of closure of this release in 2009.  DEQ prepared a Full Release of Easement and Equitable Servitudes which was reorded with Multnomah County on April 4, 2013 (JKS 4-22-13).",,,17652.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2013-04-22 11:32:50.083
