32236,34-07-0219,34,07,0219,,2007-02-21,2007-02-22 09:11:14.917,Elmo Studd's Building Supplies,16255 SW Upper Boones Ferry Rd,TIGARD,97224,(503) 684-0300,False,7.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"In February 2007, three small unregulated USTs discovered in utility trench from adjacent Fanno Creek Place property which crossed Elmo Studd's.  20-day report with analytical data submitted but no site plan provided. DEQ contacted RP on 5/5/09.  Bill Fagan confirmed that Hart Crowser did some additional work on behalf of developer (OPUS) but he did not receive a report. Rich Ernst of Hart Crowser indicated that a proposal for follow-up Phase II was not approved by their client.  He believes work may proceed when economy turns around.  On May 14, 2009, Hart Crowser sent partial documentation including photographs,site sketch, and brief narrative.  Letter sent to RP on May 18, 2009 requesting work plan be submitted by July 20, 2009.  RP called on May 22, 2009, and indicated the letter of May 18 had been given to Hart Crowser for review;  Hart Crowser retained on July 10, 2009; Call from Rick Ernst on July 22, 2009, requesting 2-week extension to work plan request (granted-new due date August 5, 2009) (JKS 7-22-09).  Report for additional investigation received.  5 borings advanced at locations on and off-site.  Soil sample taken in area of impacted west sidewall sample of 2007 excavation - no detections in soil.  Groundwater samples from all borings did not exhibit detectable concentrations of TPH-G and volatile organic compounds.  Likelihood of impacts to Fanno Creek low.  NFA requested.  Letter requesting better documentation of CSM being sent - should close if information recieved (JKS 2-10-10). Response to February 2010 letter received in May 2010.  Requested documentation concerning beneficial uses of groundwater, zoning, and locality of the facility provided by Hart Crowser.  Comment Solicitation letter sent on June 7, 2010.  City of Tigard indicated no objections to the proposed closure.  Opus Northwest did not provide any comments.  Multiple lines of evidence suggest that vapor intrusion risks are minimal and site qualifies for NFA status (JKS 7-20-10).",,,101850.0,0.0,LKENT,2010-09-30 08:26:53.953
