32523,03-07-0506,03,07,0506,,2007-04-17,2007-04-18 13:11:45.523,Knuth Estate,3203 SE Concord Rd,MILWAUKIE,97267,,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"e=105,000 4/16/07",,,101956.0,9544.0,IGAFFNE,2014-05-20 15:01:35.887
32524,26-07-0507,26,07,0507,,2007-04-17,2007-04-18 13:15:59.813,French American International School,8500 NW JOHNSON ST,PORTLAND,97229,,False,4.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,,LUST #26-06-1700,"The site, a parking lot on the east side of the school, previously housed a natural gas compressor and regulator station, which was reportedly abandoned in 1960.  In the fall of 2006, two heating oil USTs and one heating oil AST were removed from the site, along with about 16 tons of PCS.  (See LUST #26-06-1700 for more information).  Two diesel USTs were discovered and removed in the spring of 2007, along with about 125 tons of PCS.  A groundwater investigation in May 2008 found signficant concentrations of diesel in 7 of 10 downgradient borings.  Eight additional borings in March 2009 and nine borings in May 2009 also found diesel-contaminated groundwater, extending from the north end of the parking lot west towards the school.  A final round of groundwater sampling from six borings in July 2010 determined that the contamination ended at the nearest school building.  Two sub-slab vapor samples were collected from beneath the building in August 2011 to determine if there were any potential vapor impacts.  No contaminants were detected in either sample.  DEQ determined that the residual soil and groundwater contamination was too deep to pose a direct contact threat and was too depleted in volatiles to pose a vapor intrusion threat.",98978.0,9545.0,KDANA,2012-03-29 11:29:50.463
