Site addrress was reported to LUST as 494 High St. Address corrected to 494 State St... 9-16-15 JLG",ECSI 4732,"Petroleum contamination was initially reported to the Oregon Emergency Response System (OERS) as a spill on or around October 5, 2006 and Incident #2006-2512 was assigned.  The site was added to the ECSI system on November 27, 2006, and file number #4732 and file name “Charter Realty Group - PGE Vault” was assigned. After the initial investigation, it was determined that the source of the contamination was likely a buried heating oil tank.  As such on June 13, 2007, a petroleum release from a leaking UST system was report to DEQ and file number #24-07-0850 and file name “Charter Realty Group” was assigned. Strong petroleum odors were reported to be emanating from a steel screen over an underground vault area that was also being used by Portland General Electric (PCE) for power transformers.  It was determined that the UST system was located in a walled off portion of the vault under the sidewalk/street adjacent to the southeastern corner of the Charter Realty Building.  Petroleum from the UST system and asbestos containing material was removed. Although PCB #1248 was identified in a ‘oily wipe” test, no leakage was observed or reported from the transformers and PCB analytical results from soil and groundwater samples were non-detect. Based on the information from the investigation, cleanup and risk evaluation completed for the Site, the remaining soil and groundwater contamination does not appear to pose a threat to human health or the environment.",98573.0,9894.0,GDECK,2018-03-06 17:03:44.970
