1/2013:  Soil gas results look good, moving forward to notices for ODOT and CIty of Milwaukie and finish drafting nfa. (RAH)

2.28.12:  reviewed MW5-7 install report and QM.  Plan to meet w/urs to adjust QM. (RAH)

11/8/11:  approved work plan, work was completed 11/23-23. (RAH)

10.27.2011-Results continue to decline (mw-3 particularly).  URS plans to complete next qm and compare to older closed release.  Previous DEQ PM requested downgrad delin (from MW-3), but pending review, that may not be necessary. (RAH)


KD Notes below:
Soil samples were collected at the site in August 2007 for an Environmental Site Assessment, and low to moderate levels of gasoline and diesel were detected.  A single groundwater sample also showed gasoline.  Delta Consultants installed four groundwater monitoring wells at the site in July 2009, and found gasoline and diesel in all four wells.  Quarterly groundwater monitoring began in February 2010.  The tanks and dispensers were decommissioned in July 2010; no additional soil contamination was observed.

Quarterly groundwater monitoring is on-going.  Gasoline remains in all four wells, but diesel is only being detected in MW-3.  Unfortunately, the most contaminated well (MW-3) is also the downgradient well.  Additional sampling is needed to determine if the groundwater contamination extends off-site.  (12/6/10 KPD)",LUST #03-96-0303,,104767.0,10303.0,RHOOD,2013-01-14 11:19:06.420
