3/2014:  drafting nfa, some upper soil remains, but should be ok for current occ. and for neighbor given amount of trenches, water results look acceptable, and the removal.  (RAH)

6.2013:  soil gas results in sg-2 exceed occupational RBC.  2 events completed so far.  jackson foods is renovating property.  will keep sg mon, but will need to inv. on prop. west. (RAH)


7.12:  Phase II esa reviewed.  will complete an additional gw monitoring event (this month) and we can see how results look at the new MWs.  Requested to URS that we discuss after we receive results. (RAH)


Field work being completed 4/25-26. (RAH)

3/22/12:  Approved work plan, URS to complete w/in ~6 weeks.  Will collect two quarters of data from proposed wells and evaluate.   one soil sample had an ethylbenzene hit of 41 ppm (composite between 5-10 feet).  given composite, i think we can look at gw as primary driver (gw is between 5-8 feet btc).  All other soil data was acceptable for commercial.  (RAH)  ok to suspend monitoring at MW-1b and MW-2.

2.13.12:  From Laurey, some delineation necessary in waste oil area and west of HOT.  also, soil gas sampling.  Looks like they need to delineate west of TMW-3 also onto adjacent property.  (RAH)

