Evidence of a release was noted while reviewing laboratory analytical data from due diligence subsurface investigation conducted at the site. The soil samples from SB-3 and 6 show detections of NWTPH in the Diesel and Motor oil range that are below the RBCs. The groundwater sample from SB-4 has minor concentrations of naphthalene that is below the RBC for tap water (and 2-methylnaphthalene which has no RBC).",LUST #34-89-0208 & #34-91-0173,Due diligence site assessment conducted in August 2007 indicates that since the last site closure in 1997 there has been no new petroleum release.,104373.0,10421.0,LKENT,2009-02-20 12:12:30.140
33381,26-07-1364,26,07,1364,851.0,2007-09-11,2007-09-11 09:52:37.533,Shell Station #120440,10120 SW Capitol Hwy,PORTLAND,97219,,False,4.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,"LUST #26-88-0097, #26-15-1118 & #26-15-1122","Soil and groundwater samples were collected at the site in August 2007 as part of an Environmental Site Assessment.  Very low levels of soil contamination were detected, but one groundwater sample showed some gasoline and diesel.  Additional samples collected in August 2009 from five temporary monitoring wells again showed virtually no soil contamination and only one moderate hit of groundwater contamination (5,100 ppb gasoline and 1,600 ppb diesel).  DEQ determined that the contamination was limited and did not pose any current or future threats under reasonably likely exposure scenarios.",104374.0,10422.0,KDANA,2015-08-25 14:51:37.380
