33383,20-07-1366,20,07,1366,8136.0,2007-09-10,2007-09-11 14:45:09.127,Shell 120475,1080 W 7th Ave,EUGENE,97402,,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"Evidence of a release at this site was noted during review of laboratory analyticl reports from due diligence subsurface investigation. All 6 water samples from this site as well as several soil samples have detections of petroleum constituents that exceed the RBCs (Kevin McCarthy, Delta Environmental, 9/10/07).

11/22/2010: MWs installed in late 2009 have not shown similar conditions to the high concentrations found in borings during 2007 Phase 2 (along Van Buren Ave.); still likely off-site impacts (below RBCs) to the north under 7th Ave. based on GW flow direction - C. Rodda 11/22/2010",20-89-4018 SUNNY West 7th,"In August 2007, Delta Environmental Consultants conducted an environmental site assessment on behalf of Shell Oil at this active service station near downtown Eugene. Six borings were installed to collect soil and groundwater samples. Groundwater was encountered at 15 to 20 feet bgs. Petroleum contamination in soil was highest in the sample from boring TK-SB3 (gasoline at 2,330 ppm, diesel at 140 ppm, oil at 331 ppm, ethylbenzene at 46.9 ppm, and xylenes at 179 ppm). Several other VOCs  and PAHs  were detected in soil. Diesel was 388 ppm and heavy oil was 2,370 ppm in soil collected from DS-SB7. Soil samples were obtained from 5 to 15 feet bgs. Groundwater contamination was evident at DS-SB6 (gasoline at 25,900 ppb, diesel at 1,480 ppb, benzene at 11,000 ppb, and MTBE at 10 ppb). DEQ asked for further groundwater assessment in 2009, and six monitoring wells were installed. Groundwater monitoring has been conducted to evaluate petroleum concentrations over time, and soil-gas sampling was initiated in 2012 to evaluate potential vapor intrusion. Sampling through May 2016 identified a continued presence of petroleum contaminants in soil-vapor and shallow groundwater.",23504.0,10410.0,CRODDA,2016-09-20 16:15:00.400
