33387,34-07-1370,34,07,1370,1325.0,2007-09-12,2007-09-13 09:45:09.210,Shell Station #120522,11465 SW Pacific Hwy,TIGARD,97223,503-244-8006,False,4.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"8.1:  FIR (RAH)

7.23.12:  draft nfa going to manager review. (RAH)


6.6.2012:  drafted nfa and to hydro.  still need to notify gators pub owner.  (RAH)


Soil and groundwater samples were collected at this site in August 2007 as part of an environmental site assessment.  Little soil contamination was observed, but gasoline, diesel, and motor oil were detected in the groundwater.  An eighth groundwater monitoring well was added to seven pre-existing wells at the site in April 2009, and quarterly monitoring of the wells began in January 2010.  Contamination is concentrated in MW-5, the downgradient well on the west side of the site.  The consultant is attributing the contamination to surface runoff from the on-site car wash.  (7/27/10 KPD)",LUST #34-92-0092,,104396.0,10428.0,RHOOD,2012-08-01 09:40:24.333
