33391,20-07-1374,20,07,1374,8140.0,2007-09-11,2007-09-14 15:38:39.640,Shell 121618,86623 FRANKLIN BLVD,EUGENE,97405,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"Evidence of a release was noted while reviewing laboratory analytical data from due diligence subsurface investigation conducted at the site. The soil samples from SB-5 and 6 at this site 121618 have detections of petroleum constituents in soil samples that exceed the RBCs for leaching to ground water. SB-5C has NWTPH-Gx at 174 mg/kg (RBC of 260, benzene at 0.144 mg/kg (RBC of 0.0084 and trimethylbenzenes also above the RBCs.  SB-6C has NWTPG-Gx at 144 mg/kg. Several other borings also have detections of VOCs and PAHs that are below the RBCs. …Kevin McCarthy, Delta Environmental 9/11/07.",20-89-4034 Sunny LLC,"The site is located south of Eugene off Interstate 5. The property operates as a retail fuel station that has historically used underground tanks to store various petroleum products. Four gasoline, two diesel, and two kerosene tanks were decommissioned by removal in May 1989, at which time a petroleum release was recorded as Sunny LLC (DEQ Tanks File #20-89-4034) and closed in 1997. In August 2007, consultants conducted an environmental site assessment on behalf of Shell Oil. Six borings were installed up to 15 feet below ground surface for the collection of soil samples. Groundwater was not present in the borings, which were advanced to refusal at bedrock. Soil from boring DS-SB5 had gasoline at 174 parts per million, diesel at 676 ppm, oil at 331 ppm, and benzene at 0.144 ppm. Several other VOCs and PAHs were detected in soil from this boring and at DS-SB6. The remaining soil samples did not contain any of the analyzed constituents above laboratory detection levels. In Sept. 2009, consultants installed four borings (TMW-2 to TMW-5) north of the tank system. Soil samples from 5 to 25 feet bgs measured low levels of petroleum. Groundwater was present during this phase of investigation at 13 to 19 feet bgs in three borings and at 29 feet bgs in TMW-3. Water collected from TMW-5, the northern-most sample location, did not detect petroleum, but samples from TMW-2 and TMW-3 had elevated concentrations of contaminants including gasoline at 120,000 ppb. Based on the levels of contamination and uncertainty of groundwater conditions, DEQ asked for further investigation. Three monitoring wells were installed and tested for petroleum contaminants. Some gasoline, benzene, and other petroleum compounds were detected in the water samples. A private well located east of the site was tested for petroleum contamination in March 2013 at the request of the property owner. No petroleum was found in this well water sample.",23515.0,10420.0,CRODDA,2013-04-08 18:33:59.893
