33462,26-07-1444,26,07,1444,1357.0,2007-09-21,2007-09-25 11:16:16.300,Shell Station #120789,18031 SE Stark St,PORTLAND,97233,,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Evidence of a release was discovered during review of analytical data for a due diligence investigation in 2007. There are petroleum constituent concentration detections below RBC screening levels in the attached lab reports for site #120789.  There are detections of 10.7 mg/kg Diesel Range TPH(RBC is 2800 mg/kg) and 105 mg /kg Motor Oil Range in the SB-3 soil sample.  In addition, there were detections of  PAHs and NWTPH-Dx in the Motor Oil Range in the SB-2 soil sample.  Groundwater was not encountered during the investigation.",,,18842.0,10502.0,LKENT,2009-03-03 17:34:56.653
33463,26-07-1445,26,07,1445,7597.0,2007-09-21,2007-09-25 11:17:17.270,Shell Station #124731,5820 NE Glisan St,PORTLAND,97213,,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"The site was previously referred to as Panoco 34 File No. 26-90-0322 that received NFA determination in October 1990.
Laboratory data generated during due diligence subsurface investigation in 2007 showed only 1 detection of petroleum compounds above laboratory MRLs, a detection in the NWTPH-Dx Motor Oil Range of 4.25 mg/kg vs. an MRL of 3.96 mg/kg.  However, none of the soil samples contained concentrations of any constituent above the RBC screening level.  No groundwater was encountered during the investigation.",LUST #26-90-0322,Due diligence site assessment conducted in August 2007 indicates no new release.,104571.0,10504.0,LKENT,2009-03-03 16:54:57.663
33464,26-07-1446,26,07,1446,11797.0,2007-09-24,2007-09-25 11:20:22.813,Shell Station #124396,20800 NE Sandy Blvd,FAIRVIEW,97024,,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Evidence of a release was noted during review of analytical data for a due diligence investigation in 2007.  None of the soil samples contained concentrations of any constituent in excess of the RBC screening level.  Phenanthrene was detected at concentration of 15.4 ug/kg (MRL 14.4 ug/kg) in soil from boring SB-3.  This is the only detection at this site.  Although the VOCs for SBs 3-8 were lost in the laboratory, exceeded hold time and were not run, no TPH-G was detected in these soil samples. No groundwater was encountered or collected at the site.",,Due diligence site assessment conducted in August 2007 indicated no significant soil contamination.,90352.0,10509.0,LKENT,2009-02-26 18:20:53.850
33465,29-07-1447,29,07,1447,8062.0,2007-09-20,2007-09-25 11:25:12.870,Jackson & Son Oil,511 Garibaldi Street,GARIBALDI,97118,503-738-5833,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Prior release (29-97-0519) involved removal of two 2,000-gallon USTs and 320 cubic yards of PCS.  Up to 3,170 ppm gasoline and 1,010 ppm diesel remained in soil, along with minor BTEX in groundwater.  Closed as pocket-in-place in February 1999.

Second release reported September 2007.  Diesel (8,320 ppm) in pea gravel at bottom of tank pit.  Discovered during a Site Assessment.  Further investigation recommended by contractor.  (6/30/09 KPD)

Bank foreclosed on retail side, Point Source Solutions did investigation and found impacts.  LLC 8/25/2010

DEQ requested additional work.  Mark Yinger consultant for RP says report not valid.  RP sends back invoices.  UST compliance saw evidence of release and sheens on bioswale.   LLC 1/19/11

Tim O'Gara consultant did investigation work requested and found fresh diesel evidence in sandy layer downgradient of tanks.  UST compliance said tanks in compliance. Owner performed spill bucket tests.  LLC 11/15/11

Files sent to Eastern Region.  LLC",LUST #29-97-0519,see site document section for select project reports.,90352.0,10480.0,ECLARK,2012-07-24 14:35:46.050
