33476,20-07-1458,20,07,1458,6445.0,2007-09-12,2007-09-26 12:15:17.680,Shell 168254 - Main St,4124 Main Street,SPRINGFIELD,97478,,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"Release was discovered through review of analytical data from a due diligence investigation.  Soil samples from SBs 6,7 & 8 have gasoline, diesel, and/or oil range hydrocarobns and other petroleum VOCs above the most stringent RBCs for leaching to groundwater.  Groundwater samples from SBs 4-8 all have gasoline, diesel, and oil-range petroleum hydrocarobns and petroleum VOCs detected above the most stringent RBCs for tap water. ...Kevin McCarthy, Delta Environmental 9/12/07.",20-94-4132 Truax Texaco,"In August 2007, contractors performed an environmental site assessment on behalf of Shell Oil at this active service station. Eight borings were installed to 15-18 feet bgs. Groundwater was encountered at 10 to 15 feet bgs. To further characterize contamination, contractors installed eight monitoring wells and one soil boring in December 2009. Wells were set at 20 feet bgs. Groundwater flow was calculated to be to the south. The highest concentrations in soil were found in MW-8 at the northern portion of the property. Gasoline was at 680 ppm and benzene was 9.4 ppm in soil from 9.5 feet bgs. Water from MW-8 contained gasoline at 28,000 ppb, benzene at 4,300 ppb, and MTBE at 3,400 ppb. Groundwater at wells MW-3, MW-4, and MW-5 also contained relatively high concentrations of gasoline and related VOCs. A groundwater monitoring event occurred on January 20, 2010. Water at MW-8 had gasoline at 44,000 ppb, benzene at 16,000 ppb, and MTBE at 15,000 ppb. Diesel was detected at elevated levels, including 99,000 ppb at MW-5. Groundwater monitoring continues and further investigation is proposed. Remediation (soil-vapor extraction) was initiated in 2012, but due to limited affect was discontinued late 2014.",10470.0,10429.0,CRODDA,2015-02-18 16:01:46.443
