33593,20-07-1575,20,07,1575,1386.0,2007-09-27,2007-10-15 16:49:53.653,Shell 120676 - Glenwood,3640 Glenwood Dr,EUGENE,97403,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"There are petroleum constituent detections in 5 of the 6 samples from the 4 completed borings in the attached report.  The sample concentrations from DS-6 exceed the RBCs for Benzene and NWTPH-Gx in soil, and the concentrations from TK-3 exceed the RBC for NWTPH-Gx in soil.... Kevin McCarthy, Delta Environmental 9/27/07.",20-86-4006 DAVIS TEXACO STATION,"The property is an active fuel service station that currently utilizes four underground tanks to store gasoline and diesel products. The station has operated since at least the 1980s. The facility also included vehicle service. In 1986, gasoline and waste oil tanks were removed from the site.  350 cubic yards of petroleum-contaminated soil was excavated and five new tanks were installed, including a waste oil tank and the current system consisting of three gasoline and one diesel tank. Contractors removed hydraulic hoists from the service station in 1994, and the waste oil tank was decommissioned in 1998. Delta completed a Phase 2 site assessment in September 2007. Groundwater was not encountered in the borings installed up to 35 feet bgs. Soil contamination was present at relatively low concentrations. A new petroleum release was reported to DEQ and was recorded as file number 20-07-1575. Additional investigation was conducted in 2009 with five borings advanced to 31 feet bgs. Hard silty sand was encountered in the boreholes, with sandstone present at 25 to 31 feet bgs. Soil from each borehole was screened for laboratory analysis of gasoline- and diesel-range hydrocabons, petroleum-related VOCs, PAHs, and lead. Few petroleum contaminants were detected in soil at relatively low concentrations. At boring TMW-2, gasoline was detected at 20 ppm, benzene at 0.011 ppm, xylenes at 0.082 ppm and 1,2,4-trimethylbenzene at 1.3 ppm. This soil sample was obtained from 15 feet bgs. Lead was measured in each soil sample, with a maximum concentration of 4.79 ppm. Water was present in only one of the five borings. A temporary well was installed at TMW-1 and a groundwater sample was collected after well development. Gasoline was detected at 980 ppb and MTBE was measured at 12 ppb in this water sample. A land and water use survey was completed by project consultants, and identified no current beneficial use of groundwater at the commercial property.",1921.0,10531.0,GDECK,2011-03-09 14:06:50.837
