33615,04-07-1597,04,07,1597,319.0,2007-10-17,2007-10-18 13:47:29.450,Gary's Cannon Beach Service Center II,280 N Hemlock St,CANNON BEACH,97110,,False,4.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,LUST #04-99-1403,"The Site is located at an elevation of approximately 17 feet above mean sea level (amsl) in Cannon Beach, Clatsop County, Oregon. The town of Cannon Beach is situated between the Pacific Ocean to the west and the Oregon Coast Range to the east. The overall topography of the area slopes gently to the west, toward Ecola Creek and the Pacific Ocean, located approximately 300 feet and 900 feet to the west, respectively.

Gary’s Property is bounded to the west by Webb’s Motel; to the north by the Cannon Beach Christian Conference Center (Conference Center); to the east by North Hemlock Street; and to the south by retail shops. Ecola Creek and the beach are located off-site to the west, beyond Webb’s Motel and the Conference Center.

The Site includes portions of Gary’s Property, Webb’s Motel, and the Conference Center. The Site includes areas zoned as both Limited Commercial (C1) (Gary’s Property) and Residential Motel (RM) (Webb’s Motel and the Conference Center). Gary’s Property operates Gary’s Cannon Beach Service Center (an auto repair and towing company) which occupies a single-story slab-on-grade 3,077-square-foot building. Operations on Gary’s Property historically included retail gasoline sales from the mid-1950s until 2007, when the USTs were decommissioned. Gary’s Property includes concrete retaining walls on the north and west sides.

A 10-foot easement owned by Gary’s Property is located to the west of the retaining wall, between Gary’s Property and Webb’s Motel.",18175.0,10636.0,CKENNED,2018-05-21 10:33:07.963
