33658,20-07-1640,20,07,1640,12270.0,2007-10-24,2007-10-25 10:22:15.137,Peace Health Riverbend,3333 GAME FARM RD,SPRINGFIELD,97477,541-686-6865,False,2.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"Diesel #2 product - spill occurred after pump left on overnight, creating pressure in (west) UST that broke through vent line.  Approximately 600 gallons diesel released to surface.  OERS #2007-2421.  (10/24/07 CJR)

11/13/2007: site does have a potable well, to be used as an emergency water supply for the hospital facility.  The well is not currently being used, but is located within 300 feet of the spill location -- crodda",OERS #2007-2421,"A report submitted by BB&A presented information on the site characterization initiated in October 2007 following the release of approximately 700 to 1,000 gallons of diesel fuel from the UST system undergoing testing at the time of spill.  Emergency response actions to the spill included recovering product at the surface, excavating petroleum-contaminated soil and backfill materials, and collecting confirmation soil samples.

Results of soil analysis indicated that no diesel or heavy oil-range hydrocarbons, VOCs , or PAHs  were present above laboratory detection levels in the nine confirmation samples obtained from the bottom and sidewalls of the excavation.

During the week following the spill, BB&A installed eight push probes and three manually advanced borings around the UST cavity to collect soil and groundwater samples.  Of the soil remaining following the remedial excavation, one soil sample (TC01-Middle-End-W.Tank-16’) contained detected concentration of diesel at 16.8 ppm .  The remaining soil sample measured diesel, heavy oil, VOCs, and PAHs below laboratory detection levels.  

Five monitoring wells were installed at the site in December 2007 to 30 feet bgs.  Groundwater was encountered at 20 feet bgs during well construction activities.  The initial groundwater samples were collected on January 2, 2008.  Because the laboratory detection limit was above the most stringent RBC, an estimate of the level of diesel and heavy oil was made for two of the water samples collected.  Heavy oil-range hydrocarbons were estimated at 28.6 µg/L in MW1 and 42.2 µg/L in MW3.  Xylenes were detected at 2.1 µg/L in the water sample obtained from MW3.  The most stringent RBC for xylenes in groundwater is 210 µg/L.

BB&A also completed a survey of groundwater use at and near the site.  The survey identified an emergency water supply well for the Riverbend facility located 400 feet from the spill location.  In addition, a municipal water supply well for the Springfield Utility Board (SUB) was identified within the five to ten year Time of Travel Zone.  The Sportsway Well is located approximately 1.5 miles northwest of the spill site.

The final sampling event in Oct. 2008 identified petroleum contaminants below detection levels in each monitoring well and the backup emergency supply well.",92448.0,0.0,CRODDA,2009-05-08 17:05:13.430
