33671,36-07-1653,36,07,1653,4964.0,2007-10-09,2007-10-26 13:32:54.420,Shell McMinnville 124657,2005 SW Highway 99W,MCMINNVILLE,97128,,False,2.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Soil detections consisted of PAHs in SB-6.  The groundwater results showed 4 of the 6 samples have NWTPH-Dx Diesel greater than the RBCs (170-649 ug/l) and there were toluene and MTBE hits less than RBCs. It should be noted that there laboratory QA/QC issues concerning holding time and matrix spikes... Kevin McCarthy, Delta Environmental, 10/9/07.",36-93-4094 Peavey Oil South,"The site is an active retail gasoline station located at 2005 SW Highway 99W in McMinnville. The underground storage tanks currently in use are in the southwestern portion of the property. The facility previously had a petroleum release in 1993 when Peavey Oil Company owned and operated the service station. The site has operated with retail fuel sales and a convenience store since the 1950’s, including Texaco and Shell branded stations. At least two tank systems have been permitted at the site. DEQ received a petroleum release notification in November 2007, submitted on behalf of Shell Oil. The report stated that gasoline and diesel contamination were found in soil and groundwater through a Phase II ESA. None of the soil samples collected for analysis contained petroleum contaminants but lead was detected in each sample. Groundwater samples from three borings at the southwest portion of the facility detected diesel, with a high concentration of 998 ppb.In December 2014, URS collected a groundwater sample from MW-5 and measured the groundwater elevation in this monitoring well west of the tank cavity. No petroleum-related contaminants (gasoline, diesel, VOCs, or PAHs) were detected in water from MW-5.",21281.0,10572.0,CRODDA,2015-03-24 17:43:22.217
