27-21-0324 Joseph Franko Inc","The site is currently a retail petroleum service station, and has been operated as a petroleum service station since 1968. Prior to 1968, the property was used as a petroleum distribution facility. In 1968, five underground storage tanks (USTs) and one dispenser island were removed and replaced with two 12,000-gallon fuel USTs, a 550-gallon waste oil UST, and three product dispenser islands.  A release was reported to DEQ on September 12, 2007 during a due diligence site assessment of the property. A previous UST release for this property was reported to DEQ in 1989 (LUST # 27-89-4192) and granted a no further action determination in 2005. In 2007, five borings were completed. Soil and grouondwater samples were collected and anlyzed for constituents of interest.Contaminant concentrations in soil and groundwater detected during the 2007 investigation do not exceed applicable risk-based concentrations. A proposed no further action notice was issued on March 2, 2012. No comments were received.",18610.0,0.0,JCLAWSO,2021-04-16 15:58:24.527
