33717,26-07-1699,26,07,1699,,2007-10-29,2007-11-06 12:32:58.043,GREYHOUND TANKS,NW IRVING ST BTWN 5TH & 6TH AVE,PORTLAND,97209,,True,4.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"Two tanks of unreported capacity were discovered beneath the sidewalk on the south side of Irving Street between 5th and 6th Avenues in September 2007 during reconstruction of the Transit Mall.  Both tanks were largely filled in-place, although 275 gallons of oily wastewater were pumped from the eastern tank.  Sampling by a TriMet contractor found gasoline and kerosene in soil around the tanks.

A contractor retained by Greyhound, the adjacent property owner, collected soil samples from 18 borings at the site in 2009, finding primarily gasoline and gasoline constituents, most of which were concentrated 13-14 feet bgs.  Groundwater was about 20-25 feet bgs, and samples from six monitoring wells (two pre-existing and four converted borings) also found gasoline contamination.  Eight additional borings to the north in June 2010 did not find off-site migration.

The monitoring wells were sampled quarterly in 2011, and additional soil samples were collected from two ""worst-case"" borings in April 2012.  Groundwater had no beneficial use, and the contamination was too deep to present a direct contact threat, but there were risks of vapor intrusion into indoor air and volatilization to outdoor air.  However, five soil gas samples collected in April 2013 found vapor concentrations below levels of concern.",105536.0,0.0,KDANA,2014-08-25 11:47:51.783
