33793,21-07-1775,21,07,1775,,2007-11-09,2007-11-26 14:02:22.530,Coast Arrow Vacant Lot,170 SW Arrow St,WALDPORT,97394,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"LIT updated per site map...gad 12/18/07.  

Site address also known as 170 Hwy. 101, Waldport.

3 USTs discovered while ODOT was conducting work along HWY 101; USTs were exempt from permitting (age;contents).  The site is currently a vacant lot and its history is unknown at this time... Mark Norbury (Xavier) 11/9/07.",,"The site was used as a fuel station from 1920 until the early 1940s when there was a petroleum shortage during World War II. In the 1950s the Waldport Motel operated at the property with the office building being located over the underground storage (UST) tanks. Behind the office in separate buildings at the back of the lot were motel rooms. According to the City of Waldport, the motel was demolished in 2001.
The USTs were discovered within the public right-of-way beneath Highway 101 during the installation of underground utilities for an Oregon Department of Transportation (ODOT) project. Xavier Environmental, Inc. (Xavier) inspected the site, which included sampling and decommissioning the site’s three USTs. The three USTs were all single wall steel tanks in sizes of 240-gallon, 480-gallon, and 550-gallons. The USTs were configured in a nest approximately 15’ x 18’ located in the SE corner of the property. Xavier noted no ancillary piping was found and that these three USTs were regulated but registration permits, prior to January 1974, were not required, thus the USTs did not have registration information. Xavier decommissioned, the three USTs, sampled the tank pit, disposed of petroleum-contaminated soil (PCS), and contaminated groundwater in November 2007.
DEQ and Coast Arrow, LLC enetered into a Cost Recovery Agreement in June 2018.  Upon file review and available information, the DEQ determined that a conditional No Further Action was warranted for the property.  This site closure only pertains to the three USTs discovered in the ODOT right-of-way in 2007.  Site restrictions include the prohibition of residential use at the site and vapor mitigation measures to be implemented per the Easement & Equitable Servitudes filed with Lincoln County on February 11, 2019.
C. Jacobsen - 3/22/2019",105366.0,10769.0,GDECK,2019-06-05 10:57:23.890
