33939,26-08-0009,26,08,0009,,2008-01-03,2008-01-04 11:52:02.613,Henningsen Cold Storage,19343 NE Halsey St,PORTLAND,97230,503-667-0500,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"The site was formerly a farm and is being redeveloped.  The presence of the tank was unknown prior to the encounter with an excavator.  Heating oil leaked out of the tank but was immediately contained by the contrator onsite.  BELFOR (formerly RMCAT) pumped 650 gallons of diesel from the tank.  The tank and impacted soil were excavated and and encapulated in visqueen.  Soil samples were collected and disposal of soil will be arranged in the near future. The tank, soil, and liquied will be properly disposed.",,,157739.0,10945.0,CSALNAV,2019-12-03 11:55:48.393
33940,26-08-0010,26,08,0010,800.0,2008-01-04,2008-01-07 08:21:04.770,CONOCOPHILLIPS #2705455,18222 SE DIVISION ST,GRESHAM,97030,(281) 293-5101,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Site re-opened on : 12/16/2008 By Kevin Dana. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 12/12/2008.Email correspondence in file referenced a December 2008 incident wherein a fiberglass line was damaged by a pneumatic jackhammer.  Soil samples reportedly collected but data not submitted to DEQ.  Letter dated 2-4-09 requested information related to this cleanup work.  No response received to date.  Letter dated 10-12-09 indicated that Delta Consultants was acquiring liability for site from CP (JKS 11-3-09).  Delta Consultants forwarded analytical data collected by Soil Solutions on 12-2-09.  Data indicated gasoline impacted soils (4,810 mg/kg) beneath product lines.  Sample taken from overburden also analyzed (TPH-G = 350 mg/kg).  Chromatograms for both samples analyzed by Wy' East.  Both found to consist of old, weathered, gasoline (JKS 12-11-09). Discussed project with Todd Vanek on 12-17-09.  We agreed that additional delineation of likley historic gasoline impacts identified near December 2008 line hit is warranted (JKS 12-17-09).  Call from Delta Consultants in June 2010 - CP could not provide as-builts showing product line locations so they are moving borings a little bit. They feel they will still be able to get useful data.  Informed on June 17, 2010 that work was completed and they await results. It is their plan to address the points in the letter of February 2009 in the report (JKS 6-17-10).  Await report for June 2010 investigation from Delta (JKS 9-21-10).  Borings SB-1 and SB-2 advanced in area of dispenser island 6, as close as practicable.  Gas-range TPH and constituents not detected above MRLs.  Pocket of contamination is limited in extent and shallow.  Groundwater impacts not likely due to depth of contamination.  GW has no current or likely future beneficial use.  Zoning does allow mixed use developement. Public comment period ended 1-31-11 with no comment received. Proceed with drafting NFA letter (JKS 3-24-11).",,,18496.0,0.0,LKENT,2011-06-14 08:24:11.957
