34511,26-08-0572,26,08,0572,,2008-05-19,2008-05-20 07:48:07.357,"Crouch, Martin",2236 NE 44th Ave,PORTLAND,97213,,False,2.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,107398.0,11511.0,EMCMORR,2008-09-05 11:32:18.843
34512,20-08-0573,20,08,0573,,2008-05-19,2008-05-20 07:49:26.137,"Blanchard, Bob",1105 W Hilliard Ln,EUGENE,97404,541-461-2798,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"The owner called our company on May 9, we made the visit and made a bid on decommissioning the tank.  At that time, there was a new oil stain on the foundation of the garage, next to the fill spout.  The owner had the tank pumped and also dug out about 1/2 cubic yard of contaminated soil from the top of the tank prior to our arrival on May 19. It appears that water infiltrated the tank at a broken vent pipe connection, displacing a little heating oil out the top of the tank and into the surrounding soil.  Soil samples from under the tank appear to be clean.",,,107400.0,11512.0,MJGILLE,2008-07-01 15:56:46.747
34513,24-08-0574,24,08,0574,,2008-05-08,2008-05-20 14:11:15.407,Valley Oil - Pringle Rd,2488 Pringle Rd SE,SALEM,97302,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,107409.0,0.0,NSAWKA,2012-04-10 13:36:04.653
34514,22-08-0575,22,08,0575,,2008-05-09,2008-05-20 16:41:24.863,7-Eleven Store # 24230,1490 S Main St,LEBANON,97355,,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Property was the site of an old gas station that was torn down around 1980 before the 7-Eleven store was built.... Amanda Magee (Secor) 5/9/08.,,"The subject property was developed as a service station prior to the development of the current convenience store building in 1982, which presents a potential recognized environmental condition (REC).  No records of former USTs have been found, although the building department records contained a permit for the demolition of a service station.  The existence of the service station implies the past presence of the USTs.

A Phase II soil and groundwater assessment was completed in May 2008 reporting concentrations of concern according to DEQ's risk-based concentrations list revised October 3, 2008.  Concentrations of petroleum hydrocarbons in the gasoline range were detected above DEQ's most stringent cleanup level of 100 micrograms per liter (ug/L) in groundwater samples collected from borings B-2 (3,000 ug/L) and B-3 (1,400 ug/L).  Concentrations of petroleum hydrocarbons in the diesel range were detected above DEQ's most stringent cleanup level of 88 ug/L in groundwater samples collected from borings B-2 (800 ug/L) and B-3 (600 ug/L).  Concentrations of total petroleum hydrocarbons in the gasoline range were detected above DEQ's most stringent cleanup level of 100 ug/L in groundwater samples collected from borings B-2 (4,200 ug/L) and B-3 (1,500 ug/L).  Concentrations of benzene were detected above DEQ's most stringent cleanup level of 0.35 ug/L in groundwater samples collected from boring B-2 (11 ug/L) and B-3 (2.4 ug/L).  Concentrations of ethylbenzene were detected above DEQ's most stringent cleanup level of 1.2 ug/L in groundwater samples collected from borings B-2 (17 ug/L) and B-3 (1.7 ug/L).
Concentrations of napthalene were detected above DEQ's most stringent cleanup level of 0.12 ug/L in groundwater samples collected from borings B-2 (3.2 ug/L).",107413.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2019-09-05 15:00:50.050
