34569,24-08-0630,24,08,0630,3623.0,2008-05-16,2008-05-29 13:33:27.290,Merritt River Road,5195 River Rd N,KEIZER,97303,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,,"24-20-0082 Merritt #1, Inc Keizer","The property is the location of an operating “76” branded gas station on the southwest corner of the intersection of River Road and Sandy Drive North.  The property is currently owned and operated by Merritt #1 Inc. of Salem, Oregon.    

Petroleum contamination was initially reported to DEQ in May 2008 when the adjacent property owners had an environmental assessment performed at or near the property line.  Subsequent assessment of the Underground Storage Tanks facility #3623 file revealed that an 8000-gallon gasoline tank had failed a tightness test in December 2007.  Petroleum contamination was observed in soil and groundwater at low concentrations, only slightly above the analytical method detection limits. 

The UST facility owners conducted and investigation to determine if one of more of the gasoline storage tanks had leaked and if so, the extent of the contamination.  In October 2008 a series of sampling points were drilled near the tank nest, near the piping system, and near the two dispenser-islands.  All soil and groundwater sample results were below the analytical method detection limits (i.e. none-detected – please see attached diagram)  

Based on the results of cleanup, site investigation, and assessment, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future land use (commercial), the remaining contamination levels are adequately protective of human health and the environment.  The proposed plan will allow the remaining contamination to naturally degrade in place.",20440.0,11500.0,GDECK,2020-01-28 16:31:29.527
34570,20-08-0631,20,08,0631,3354.0,2008-05-20,2008-05-29 14:53:08.193,Bald Knob Timber Co,33662 Park Dr,CRESWELL,97426,(503) 895-2159,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Dry pit, excavated PCS, took confirmation soil samples, still some petroleum contamination (Floor-625 ppm diesel, 623 ppm lube oil, 79 ppm gas; walls ND).  Concrete UST not used since 1950s; triple rinsed, taken to Delta Sand & Gravel.  Rinsate taken to Pacific Power Vac (Portland).  Stockpile sample measured 2870 ppm diesel, 2310 ppm lube oil, 741 ppm gas.   ….C Rodda 5/20/08.

Per Loren Harwood with Petree Construction, slight film on inside of tank with sludge on the bottom.  Tank contents used by boiler for drying fruits and nuts.  13,000 gallons of water was pumped from the 25' x 6' concrete tank......C. Rodda 5/29/2008","ECSI #5981, LUST #20-93-4090, and LUST#20-98-7055","The majority of the site was used as a veneer mill from the early 1950s to 2008. Prior to development as a veneer mill the site was used primarily for agricultural purposes. The site previously utilized four underground storage tanks (USTs). LUST #20-08-0631 is associated with one of these four USTs; a 25’ x 6’ concrete UST located on tax map 19031431, tax lot 5600 which was used to store petroleum fuel in the 1950’s. In 2008, this UST was removed from the northwest corner of the site. Approximately 13,000 gallons of liquid was pumped from the UST prior to decommissioning and 200 tons of impacted soil was excavated and transported off-site for disposal. Low concentrations of metals, VOCs, PAHs, and petroleum hydrocarbons were detected in soil beneath the former UST; however, concentrations were below the applicable RBCs for the site. Groundwater samples were not collected at the time of decommissioning. In 2015, one soil and one groundwater sample (B-01) were collected from the former UST area and analyzed for TPH, VOCs, SVOCs, and 8 RCRA metals. Compounds were not detected in either sample at concentrations above the applicable RBCs for the site. ... 6/28/2019 MOtt.",5101.0,0.0,GDECK,2020-01-14 11:00:49.893
