34634,29-08-0695,29,08,0695,3696.0,2008-06-11,2008-06-11 10:28:34.300,Tillamook Creamery,4185 Highway 101 N,TILLAMOOK,97141,,False,4.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"The tank where the release occurred is adjacent to LUST facility 29-00-0859, which has been granted NFA status.  BB&A requests that a DEQ project manager contact us to discuss the use of previous groundwater data from monitoring wells at LUST site 29-00-0859 for use to support the closure of the recent release.  [Potential release phoned-in April 22.  Formally reported June 11. kpd].  Supplemental investigation performed in August 2008.  Boring P-6 placed south of Latimer Road and did not exhibit evidence of contamination, effectively marking maximim extent of plume.  In phone conversation on March 19, 2009, I asked for clarification of thee points (source of local drinking water, confirmation of location for planned future construction, and clarification of future use of site well).  Responses submitted on 5-18-09.  On 6-10-09, a figure showing the inferred extent of contamination was requested.  Comments soliciated from Columbia County and adjacent owners to south (golf course) on 7-31-09.  Comment period closed on 9-2-09 with no comments received.  Preparation of draft NFA is next step (JKS 10-23-09).",,,4347.0,11629.0,LLO,2016-03-25 13:41:14.430
