34693,10-08-0754,10,08,0754,,2008-06-23,2008-06-23 09:05:33.823,Yoncall High School,292 5th St,YONCALLA,97499,,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Release was discovered during the installation of storm water drainage line.  The cause/source of the release has not yet been determined.,,,0.0,0.0,MJGILLE,2015-01-27 15:51:24.547
34694,04-08-0755,04,08,0755,11730.0,2008-06-20,2008-06-23 11:06:07.480,Astoria Shell,2264 Marine Dr,ASTORIA,97103,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"Site operated as gasoline/service station historically (1950s to 1970s) and again from 1997 to 2007; Station closed and involved in likely foreclosure.  UST compliance inspection revealed no evidence of problems with current USTs which are in temporary closure status; Subsurface investigation conducted at Site in 2008 revealed soil and groundwater impacts; Delineation of impacts not complete; Information regarding location of historic USTs is needed. In June 2009, K&S performed investigation at site to further delineate impacts noted in 2008 investigation.  Borings advanced in the area of the inferred former UST excavation, dispenser islands, and along the southern property boundary.  Boring at southeast corner of site detected gasoline-range TPH, suggesting contribution from a possible off-site source (former Bob's Texaco). At the same time, analytical data suggested evidence for a release from the former USTs.  In comment letter dated September 23, 2009, DEQ requested a network of at least four monitoring wells be installed.  In March 2010, DEQ received a work plan to install six temporary monitoring wells.  The RP reportedly preferred to perform some off-site assessment before installing permanent monitoring wells.  In letter dated April 8, 2010, work plan was conditionally approved, with the reminder that they were still required to install monitoring well network.  No investigation report received to date so checked in with K&S Environmental.  K&S provided report for review.  Cluster of borings advanced off-site near northwest corner of site (near current USTs) detected only minimal groundwater contamination, suggesting little off-site migration had occurred. K&S recommended installation of network of four monitoring wells and completion of BWUD.  Letter commenting on investigation and approving recommendation for well network sent 09--09-10.  No further progress on site investigation although risks appear to be low (JKS 12-15-11).

Solicitation of comment letter sent to abutting properties on April 26, 2013.  The City of Astoria responed on May 14, 2013 stating that they agreed with the closure (MPD 6-4-2013)",,,107887.0,11690.0,JSCHATZ,2013-08-13 09:42:28.217
