34715,24-08-0776,24,08,0776,,2008-06-17,2008-06-27 13:55:46.847,Hillcrest Youth Correctional Facility,2450 Strong Rd SE,SALEM,97302,503-986-0427,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"6/25/18 Asked for clarification of UST location from R.P. to determine building usage in vicinity of former tank. Map provided by R.P. indicates tank location in a different area of property than consultant identified. J.Claussen

According to owner, tank was empty and taken out of over 30 years ago. Release appears to be limited to soil only. Some cleanup through over excavation has been performed following removal of the UST. However, small UST (500-gallon) was located between two buildings preventing further excavation. Limited soil removal appears to have decreased contaminant concentrations in the tank pit. Release likely due to corrosion or minor over spillage... Randy Boese 6/17/08.",24-14-0377 (HOT)  Oregon Youth Authority,"The facility originally opened as the State Industrial School for Girls in 1914. Over the years the name of the facility changed several times before being permanently closed in 2017.The exact cause of the release is unknown but appears limited to the soil within 10 feet of the former underground storage tank.Soil between five and seven feet below ground is contaminated with gasoline and related constituents. Soil gas beneath the southwestern portion of the former gardeners shed is also impacted above residential screening levels. Groundwater is not known to be impacted by this release. In 2008, the UST was decommissioned by removal and about five tons of impacted soil was excavated and disposed of at Riverbend Landfill. Gasoline contaminated soil remains beneath the southwestern portion of the former gardeners shed and is estimated to be less than 10 cubic yards in volume. The facility is currently served by a groundwater well that is unimpacted by the release and city water is available as a backup. Only the one UST shown on the attached figure was investigated. If other USTs or sources of contamination are discovered, they must be remediated or investigated in accordance with DEQ rules.",88689.0,11660.0,CRICHAR,2020-08-31 09:00:21.197
34716,21-08-0777,21,08,0777,,2008-06-18,2008-06-27 15:59:30.707,Kessi Property (ODOT),21312 Highway 20,EDDYVILLE,97343,,False,4.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Check LIT position when we receive a site map... gad 6/18/08.

Hwy 20 expansion project.  This property is actually under the control of the OR DOT however county records indicate that Mr. Kessi is still the owner.  We were unclear as to whether Mr. Kessi or ODOT should be identified as the RP so we may have erred.  ISA Sample HCID results: N91 ND  S91 Detected - NWTPH-Gx 4010 ppm.  Groundwater encountered at approximately 79"" bgs (tank bottom)... Dana Thompson 6/18/08.",,,107955.0,11675.0,GDECK,2008-06-27 16:22:21.620
