34984,20-08-1045,20,08,1045,,2008-08-12,2008-08-18 15:19:29.500,Kerry Hutcheson,2195 Riverview Street,EUGENE,97403,,False,7.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Residential gasoline tank, 990 gallon.

Also 1,000-gallon HOT at property - DEQ combined gasoline with heating oil tank for single project; $200 HOT fee applied to USTC cost recovery - 12/1/2008, C. Rodda",,"One 1,000-gallon gasoline UST  and one 1,000-gallon heating oil UST were decommissioned on August 12 and 13, 2008.  The steel tanks were for personal use, less than 1,100-gallon capacity, and were therefore exempt from registration by the DEQ.  The gasoline UST was removed from the property, and the heating oil tank was left in place.    Approximately 2,350 gallons of a fuel and water mixture were removed from the two tanks and disposed of by Oil Re-Refining Company in Eugene.  The heating oil UST was cut open in order to collect soil samples beneath the tank.
Two soil samples (GTE1 and GTW1) were obtained from the ends of the gasoline UST at 7 feet bgs.  Analysis using NWTPH-Gx  method identified gasoline-range hydrocarbons at a maximum concentration of 13,500 ppm  in sample GTE1.  Further analysis for benzene was completed on this sample, identifying the constituent at a concentration of 2.11 ppm.  Testing for other VOCs  was not completed for either soil sample collected from the gasoline UST cavity.

Approximately ten cubic yards of petroleum-contaminated soil (PCS) were excavated from the former gasoline UST cavity.  The excavation was extended to a depth just over 9 feet bgs.  Two additional soil samples (GTW2 and GTE2) were collected after removing the PCS.  The confirmation soil samples were analyzed for gasoline-range hydrocarbons, and both samples detected this compound below laboratory detection levels.

Two soil samples (DW and DE) were collected beneath the ends of the heating oil UST.  Analysis was completed for diesel- and oil-range hydrocarbons using the NWTPH-Dx method .  Results identified diesel at a maximum concentration of petroleum in soil sample DW, with diesel at 53 ppm and heavy oil at 268 ppm.  
Groundwater did not enter the UST excavation during decommissioning and cleanup activities.  

The contaminated soil excavated from the gasoline UST cavity was transported to Coffin Butte Landfill in Benton County for disposal on October 2, 2008.",108616.0,11956.0,CRODDA,2009-02-10 07:35:33.867
