35042,26-08-1103,26,08,1103,,2008-08-26,2008-08-27 07:47:01.250,"Marshall, Katrina",201 SE 31st Ave,PORTLAND,97214,,False,2.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"East sample = 7,520ppm; West sample = N.D.",,,108740.0,12029.0,EMCMORR,2008-12-18 16:50:14.207
35043,29-08-1104,29,08,1104,5939.0,2008-08-27,2008-08-28 07:57:46.810,ROCKAWAY BEACH WASTEWATER PLANT,410 S 3RD AVE,ROCKAWAY BEACH,97136,(503) 355-2291,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Sampling in August 2008 found diesel and oil in soil and groundwater beneath a dispenser at the site.  The dispenser was removed and a sump installed.  Groundwater collected in the sump is pumped directly to the wastewater treatment plant.  Quarterly groundwater monitoring began in September 2008.  Contaminant levels rapidly decreased, and no contamination has been detected in the last two quarters (September & December 2009).  A 1,000-gallon diesel UST (associated with the original dispenser) was removed in September 2010.  No additional contamination was detected.  (11/3/10 KPD).  Letter sent to City of Rockaway Beach in March 2011 concerning need for some additional delineation.  On September 12, 2011, contacted by Timothy Sauter of Feige and Associates.  They received authorization to proceed wtih investigation to further delineate contamination in the area of the diesel dispenser.  He had previously discussed an investigation approach involving borings and grab groudnwater samples with Kevin Dana.  We discussed a scope of work consisting of borings advanced around the margins of the UST pit and/or dispenser excavation.  Work plan for delineation investigation received 9-15-11 and conditionally approved by DEQ on 9-20-11.  Site assessment performed in April 2012.  Extent of contamination shown to be limited.  Publc comment period on proposed closure initiated on 1-24-13 (JKS 1-31-13). No comments received to date.  Site qualifies for NFA status (JKS 2-22-13).",LUST #29-97-0464,,13083.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2013-05-03 07:27:05.840
