35047,26-08-1108,26,08,1108,,2008-08-27,2008-08-29 09:54:16.030,"Freedman, Toby",1124 SE Miller St,PORTLAND,97202,,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,108779.0,12033.0,EMCMORR,2008-12-17 14:40:57.337
35048,34-08-1109,34,08,1109,,2008-08-27,2008-08-29 09:55:32.640,American Landscape Supply,6460 NW Cornelius Pass Rd,HILLSBORO,97124,,False,4.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Transfered to LUST.  Old gasoline release at property closed out in 1991(03-90-0275).  Property subject of pending sale.  Two heating oil USTs removed in August 2008.  Soil impacts found and new release reported. Follow up investigation revealed groundwater impacts from heating oil release, as well as previously unknown gasoline impacts to groundwater.  NFA requested by consultant for buyer.  GW impacts not delineated.  BWUD needs to be done to assess risk to area receptors from shallow groundwater.  Two water wells at site, one within 40 feet of heating oil UST excavation.  Work plan for additional investigation submitted by K&S 11-04-08.  Work Plan implemented in November 2008.  Shallow water well was abandoned. Six soil borings advanced.  three borings were made into temporary wells and surveyed.  Groundwater flow to northeast. Water well search and BWUD revealed that water well located approximately 350 feet cross-gradient to former heating oil UST.  Groundwater impacts do not extend off-site.  Sampling of water well revealed no detectable TPH.  Assurance letter prepared and sent to Wells Fargo.",,,108780.0,12034.0,LKENT,2009-04-07 11:57:22.567
