35468,26-08-1529,26,08,1529,,2008-12-30,2009-01-05 10:24:42.967,Killingsworth Commercial Property,1505 NE Killingsworth St,PORTLAND,97211,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"A service station reportedly operated at this site from the 1940s until 1975.  Two 1,000-gallon gasoline USTs and a waste oil UST were reportedly removed in 1975.  The site is currently occupied by a mobile home that has been converted into a restaurant.  In January 2008, AMEC collected soil and soil gas samples as part of a Phase II ESA for Portland BES.  (DEQ didn't receive the ESA until December 2008).  No soil contamination was detected, but a variety of VOCs were detected in soil gas, including benzene (15 ug/m3), 1,2,4-TMB (8.3 ug/m3), and xylenes (173 ug/m3).  Given the lack of soil contamination, the source of the vapors is unknown.  However, the vapor concentrations are less than 100x residential RBCs, so it may not matter.  (3/23/10 KPD)",,,111080.0,0.0,LKENT,2010-12-14 08:37:16.690
