35755,26-09-0283,26,09,0283,,2009-04-09,2009-04-13 09:41:51.857,Ultimizers Inc.,29909 SE Orient Dr,GRESHAM,97080,,False,4.0,,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Sampling in February 2009 found up to 5,680 ppm gasoline in the soil and 24,600 ppb gasoline in the shallow groundwater along Orient Drive where an UST was reportedly decommissioned in 1992.  The current property owner (who purchased the site in 1992) disagreed that he was responsible, thought the contamination may have come from off-site, and said he would be financially unable to proceed for the next year or two.  The site did not rank as a high priority (based on the data available) and so was backlogged.  (7/12/10 KPD)",,"This site was reportedly used for residential homes, commercial space, and a gas station (1930s to 1960s). The uses of neighboring properties include commercial, residential, light industrial, and storage for Gresham-Barlow School District schools. The site is zoned commercial and is currently retail space. The site is likely to remain developed for commercial use in the future. There are two neighboring Leaking Underground Storage Tank (LUST) sites that are closed for which DEQ has issued No Further Action Letters. The Orient School District Site (LUST# 26-01-0044) located at 29805 SE Orient Drive is to the west and Orient Country Store (LUST# 26-06-1179) located at 29822 SE Orient Drive is to the south. One tank was removed by the owner in the SE corner of the site and was thought to be a heating oil tank or water tank. Other tanks believed to be in the southwest corner of the site were not located by a geophysical survey nor through soil borings. Contamination in the soil and groundwater remains in place and may be comingled with contamination from other historic releases in the area of the site. The contamination is not considered to pose unacceptable risks to human or ecological receptors. This site received a NFA determination in May 2019. [KMH 5-28-2019]",111050.0,0.0,KHACK,2019-05-28 09:49:30.697
