35861,26-09-0389,26,09,0389,1677.0,2009-05-11,2009-05-12 10:14:00.823,BRIGHT DAY,810 SE BELMONT ST,PORTLAND,97214,(503) 232-9186,False,,,3.0,,False,False,True,,False,True,False,False,False,,ECSI #4977,"A 500-gallon gasoline storage tank was removed from an underground concrete vault at this site in February 2008, along with 3.13 tons of contaminated backfill soil.  Sampling beneath the vault found no evidence of contaminant migration.  See ECSI #4977 for more information on this site.",106958.0,0.0,KDANA,2009-05-27 11:19:21.517
35862,34-09-0390,34,09,0390,2171.0,2009-05-11,2009-05-12 10:30:52.010,TIME OIL COMPANY #03-144 II,500 FRONT ST,GASTON,97119,(503) 285-2400,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"DEQ reviewed UST decommissionining and hoist removal report prepared by EMS dated June 19, 2009.  Data gaps with regard to TPH-D and TPH-O noted.  Also need for additional delineation of soil and groundwater impacts down-gradient of former hoist, as noted in letter of August 6, 2009.  Work plan for additional investigation submitted, in apparent response to potential property transaction.  Work plan approved with conditions on August 17, 2009.  During investigation conducted on August 25, groundwater encountered only in boring B-10 - delineation not achieved (JKS 8-25-09).  Site investigation report submitted November 2009. NFA requested.  DEQ letter dated December 9 requested additional attempt to collect groundwater data.  Second attempt at investigation will include temporary monitoring wells with pre-packed screens and hollow stem auger drilling technology.  Investigation scheduled for 12-14-09 (JKS 12-11-09).  Second attempt performed in November 2009.  Boring B-8, downgradient of April 2009 boring B-1, detected only minimal levels of TPH-G.  This indicates impacts do not extent significantly off-site.   Borings B-9, B-10, and B-11 did not exhibit diesel or oil-range hydrocarbons, indicating the hoist impacts were restricted to the site.  Comment solicitation letter to RP and ODOT in preparation (JKS 2-10-10). No substantive comments from ODOT Region 2A received. Site should proceed to closure (JKS 4-2-10).",LUST #34-92-0135,,19435.0,0.0,KDANA,2011-03-02 13:11:43.823
