36045,34-09-0573,34,09,0573,1908.0,2009-06-29,2009-06-29 13:35:07.893,STALEY'S JUNCTION III,50470 NW SUNSET HWY,BANKS,97106,(503) 759-5755,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Previous releases at site (34-93-0013 and 34-96-0063) discovered during decommissioning of fomer USTs and damage to vapor line.  ODOT is looking to acquire property for access management purposes related to construction of an interchange between Highways 26 and 47 near Buxton, Oregon.  ODOT performed investigation at site in early 2009.  17 borings advanced at site in area of former UST tank pits, and related areas. Boring GP-13957-7 south of former tank pit A exhibited free product and high levels of TPH-G, TPH-D and benzene in groundwater.  Dairy Creek runs close to southern side of facility.  ODOT likely to acquire property in early 2010.  They plan to drain USTs and permanently decommission.  They also tentatively plan to remediate site through excavation.  Further delineation of LNAPL and groundwater impacts south of site is warranted (JKS 11-13-09).  Additional site assessement performed 4-19-11.  No evidence that product extends appreciably south and east of ODOT boring GP-13957-7.  ODOT reported to DEQ stained/distressed vegetation area and apparent tire tracks on 4-14-11.  Strong smell of diesel in area.  Emergency response contractor reportedly removed impacted soil from area the weekof 4-15-11 and await results.  Initial sampling indicated signifant levels of diesel (26,000 mg/kg) and oil in soil.  In August ODOT directed the removal of additional soil from the area. Residual diesel detected at only 61.5 mg/kg.  Await ODOT report for removal.  USTs removed week of 8-10-11. Compliance soil samples from beneath USTs showed little to no evidence of contamination. Minimal contamination (likely historic) in area of dispensers.  On 11-22-11 BB&A submitted a CSM and risk-based evaluation arguing for closure.  DEQ accepted in letter dated 12-13-11.  Public comment period initiated 12-29-11.  Public comment period closed 2-1-12.  Site ready for NFA (JKS 1-27-12).",,,9846.0,0.0,GGAMOLO,2012-03-08 15:15:26.680
