36104,26-09-0632,26,09,0632,12366.0,2009-07-14,2009-07-14 15:51:41.470,Hiroi Property,3384 SE Division St,PORTLAND,97202,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"In July 2009, USTs associated with a historic gasoline station were decommissed by removal.  Site was not operated as fueling facility beyond circa 1956 and USTs wre abandoned.  During excavation, additional USTs were discovered, making a total of 5.  Compliance soil sampling revealed primarily gasoline-range petroleum hydrocarbons present at site.  Remedial overexcavation was performed in the area of the former USTs and dispenser islands. Residual contamination exceeds Soil Matrix Level II standards in several samples.  Soil Solutions performed risk-based evaluation and requested closure of release.  Groundwater not encountered to depth of 17 feet bgs during tank removal and investigation phase (JKS 2-17-10). Discussed comments on UST decommissioning report with Soil Solutions.  Agreed that investigation to determine if GW impacted preferable to review of geotechnical hole reports on file with WRD.  DEQ provided with contact information for attorney for Mr. Hiroi (JKS 2-22-09).  Comment solicitation letter sent to City of Portland BES on June 17, 2010.  Letter with BES comments received on 7-7-10. No objections to closure. BES will prepare a contaminated media menagement plan.  BES asked DEQ to notify RP of continuing liabiity for costs associated with characterization and disposal of impacted media in future. Draft NFA in progress (JKS 7-8-10).",,,142681.0,13124.0,iPMO#38,2016-10-14 07:03:01.313
