36390,03-09-0918,03,09,0918,9603.0,2009-09-17,2009-09-21 09:50:17.170,HOBART OIL COMPANY,126 DIXON AVE,MOLALLA,97038,(503) 829-2122,False,,,3.0,,True,False,False,,False,True,False,False,False,,ECSI #5356,"An underground pipe linking a 12,000-gallon diesel AST with a dispenser split open in July 2009 and saturated an adjacent gasoline UST nest.  Trenches were dug on three sides of the nest to contain the release.  The two USTs (2,000-gallon and 1,000-gallon capacity) were removed in December 2009.  Because the release was associated with an AST, the project was referred to DEQ's Cleanup program in May 2010 for further action.  (See ECSI #5356 for more information).  The LUST file was administratively closed in October 2010.",17446.0,0.0,KDANA,2010-10-21 14:36:58.827
36391,04-09-0919,04,09,0919,12328.0,2009-08-24,2009-09-22 08:47:37.040,CITY OF WARRENTON OLD WATER PLANT,86650 LEWIS AND CLARK ROAD,SEASIDE,97138,(503) 861-0912,False,,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"One 120-gallon UST for backup diesel generator associated with former City of Warrenton water treatment facility was decommissioned from site in August 2009.  Shallow groundwater noted in excavation at 4 to 4.5 feet.  Compliance soil samples collected from soil-water interface were ND using Method NWTPH-HCID. However, pit water sample exhibited TPH-D and  TPH-O at concentration near 42,000 ppb.  In October 2009, K&S superivsed removal of approximately 9.5 tons of soil from vicinity of former UST excavation.  Pit water sample collected and reportedly ND for TPH-D and TPH-O. No information concerning size of remedial excavation provided.  NFA status requested by K&S.  Letter to City of Warrenton officials has been drafted (JKS 02-25-10). March 26, 2010 report documenting follow-up site assessment activities at the site received.  Groundwater samples from the margins of the fomrer UST pit were not found to contain detectable levels of diesel-range hydrocarbons, oil-range hydrocarbons, or BTEX; Email sent to K&S on 04-5-10 requested clarification of zoning and likely future uses, as well as information about the City of Warrenton treatment system.  Follow-up email sent on 06-28-10 and follow-up letter sent on 09-15-10.  Response letter received from City of Warrenton on 09-20-10 addressed the remainder of DEQ's concerns.  News Release concerning proposed closure was sent on October 12, 2010.  One written comment in support of closure of release was received on October 12, 2010.  In my opinion, requirements for closure have been met and NFA should be issued. (JKS 11-18-10).",,,107139.0,0.0,LKENT,2011-03-11 08:08:51.020
