Most recent tank use was for gasoline.  May have been originally used for diesel fuel.",,"Private tank that had stored gasoline and possibly diesel in the past was decommissioned in place.  Observation of small holes in the tank prompted the reporting of this suspected release.  However, all sample results are non-detect for gasoline/diesel.  As there appears to be no release, DEQ is administratively the closing file based on decommissioning and sampling report. 1/12/2010.",113056.0,13429.0,GDECK,2010-01-12 18:30:16.493
36443,36-09-0971,36,09,0971,,2009-09-28,2009-10-02 17:23:34.557,City of Lafayette R-o-W,0 Third St (NE corner 3rd & Bridge St),LAFAYETTE,97127,,True,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"During trenching for utility upgrade, the city's contractor encountered a 1,000-gallon UST.  The presence of the tank was unknown prior to construction activities.  One soil sample was collected adjacent to the tank and contained 30 ppm Gx.  An additional sample was collected of soil that appeared to be impacted but was not in tank excavation.  The sample contained 221 ppm Gx.  Neither soil sample contained detectable RBCA compounds.  The city intends to decommission tank by removal as it is in the right of way.  Tank is located at the NE corner of Third STreet and Bridge Street.... Pam Brown, RMCAT Environmental Services 9/28/09.

Site De-assigned 7/2/2013.",,,113057.0,13440.0,GDECK,2013-07-02 11:38:44.387
