36446,05-09-0974,05,09,0974,2925.0,2009-10-02,2009-10-05 10:09:52.033,CLATSKANIE CHEVRON,25 W COLUMBIA RIVER HWY,CLATSKANIE,97016,(209) 652-3571,False,4.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"In September 2009, three USTs (6000-gallon and two 8000-gallon) decommissioned by removal.  Damaged spill bucket believed to be the source of the release.  Additional UST previously decommissioned in place was discovered and samples were collected beneath it. Due to high GW table, samples collected at soil-water interface but were ND using Method HCID.  Pit water sample had detectable levels of TPH-G and benzene.  During excavation for new UST system, 286 tons of soil was removed. Three confirmation wall samples and three bottom samples collected from floor and limits of enlarged excavation-all ND using Method NWTPH-Gx.  Size of excavation seems incongruous with number of confirmation samples collected. Report indicates that further investigation of extent of groundwater contamination beyond UST pit should be completed. ODOT performed investigation in ROW adjacent to site in March 2009.  Significant levels of diesl and oil-range hc contamination were detected in one ROW boring.  Risk-based evaluation received in September 2010.  Review of document revealed areas where additional information was needed.  Comments provided on 10-5-10.  Response letter with additional information received on 10-15-10.  Upon review, it appears an NFA determination is warranted.  Letter soliciting comments from ODOT and City of Clatskanie sent on 11-2-10.  No comments in opposition to closure received from either party.  Draft NFA prepared and being submitted to hydrogeologis for reeview  (JKS 01-05-11).",,,19965.0,0.0,LKENT,2011-09-12 08:00:45.623
