36475,24-09-1003,24,09,1003,12373.0,2009-10-04,2009-10-09 14:26:03.643,Lillian Humphreys,1520 N 1St Street,STAYTON,97383,503-769-5539,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"The site is located Stayton, Oregon at 1520 N. First Avenue, in the NW¼ of the NE¼ of Section 10 of Township 9 South, Range 1 West (Willamette Meridian) in Marion County (map tax lot 091W10AC01900).  The site is currently an animal supply store, and was an automobile service garage and filling station. Two 1,000-gallon underground storage tanks were identified in 2009 during a geophysical survey. A subsequent subsurface investigation in 2009 confirmed a release of gasoline to soil and groundwater.  A UST release was reported to DEQ on October 4, 2009.The property consists of 0.23 acres and is located in an area of commercial and residential properties, and a high school. 

In September 2009, a geophysical survey identified two USTs, associated piping, and a debris pit. Three borings were completed in September 2009. Four soil and two groundwater samples were collected and analyzed for northwest total petroleum hydrocarbons-gasoline (NWTPH-Gx) and diesel (NWTPH-Dx). Two groundwater samples were also analyzed for volatile organic compounds (VOCs) and one for RCRA metals.  In October 2009, one tank was removed and one was decommissioned in place due to its close proximity to a building. A debris pit was also excavated. Approximately 34 tons of petroleum contaminated soil was removed and disposed at a landfill. Seven soil samples were collected from the excavations and analyzed for TPH-Gx and TPH-Dx. One soil sample was also analyzed for RBDM VOCs and total lead.  One soil sample was analyzed for PAHs, PCBs, and RCRA metals.

Nine temporary borings were completed to collect soil and groundwater samples around the USTs and debris pit in February 2012. For borings around the USTs, nine soil samples were collected and analyzed for NWTPH-Gx and six for DEQ’s Risk-Based Decision Making volatile organic compounds (RBDM VOCs). Four groundwater samples were collected and analyzed for TPH-Gx, RBDM VOCs, and lead.  Soil samples around the debris pit were analyzed for TPH-Dx. One soil sample was also analyzed for VOCs and Extractable Petroleum Hydrocarbons (EPH). Two soil gas samples were collected beneath concrete floor slabs inside the animal supply store building, and analyzed for VOCs.

Soils encountered during subsurface investigations consisted of fill material to depths of 4 to 5 feet below ground surface (bgs), followe",113087.0,13462.0,GDECK,2013-01-14 13:04:36.570
