Feige & Assoc is currently investigating the logistics of on-site soil treatment.  No SWLA has been prepared at this time...12/1/09.",,"In November of 2009 a release of gasoline was discovered during the decommissioning by removal of Underground Storage Tanks at this site.  The cause of the contamination was reported as overfill.  All the USTs were removed.  An investigation to determine the extent of soil and groundwater contamination was completed without DEQ oversight. A risk-assessment of soil and groundwater in the remaining area of contamination and beyond was completed.  This assessment included sampling of neighboring water wells, the on-site water well, borings and permanent shallow groundwater monitoring wells. Based on this assessment, on-site subsurface soil-gas migration into indoor air was determined to still be above DEQ occupational Risk-Based Cleanup levels in the area of the former UST systems.  Prior to any additional development or re-development on the Property, Owner must submit professionally prepared plans for the proposed development to DEQ for review (UST/WREC1 or its successor).  Any such plans must consider the December 29, 2014, Conceptual Site Model to determine if engineering controls are required and the site-specific Contaminated Media Management Plan for proper handling of any contaminated soil or groundwater that may be encountered. Providing that these controls are implemented and maintained,and given the reasonably likely future use of the property, the site qualities for a Conditional Risk-Based Closure.",15344.0,0.0,ALEIDEL,2020-04-30 15:11:47.207
