36735,24-09-1263,24,09,1263,,2009-12-13,2009-12-14 08:00:31.227,"Riggleman, Beverly",1955 21st St NE,SALEM,97301,503-910-2449,False,1.0,,,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"240 Gallon Tank under walkway on south side of garage, buried 8 inches, with 9 inches of water. floor at 46"". Sample collected at 5.8 ft west (vent) = ND, East fill end at 5.8 feet = 10600 ppm.",Report received and waiting for certification page and payment. 4/27/2010,,113762.0,13749.0,MJGILLE,2010-04-27 13:38:57.927
36736,26-09-1264,26,09,1264,10309.0,2009-12-14,2009-12-14 09:32:01.613,Northside Ford Truck Sales,6221 NE Columbia Blvd,PORTLAND,97218,503-720-7475,False,7.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"On November 25, 2009, a subsurface soil sample investigation was conducted at the Northside Ford Truck facility in the vicinity of a former 1,000-gallon waste oil UST.  One soil boring was installed at each end of the former UST and soil samples were submitted for laboratory analysis.  Diesel was detected at a concentration of 66.5 mg/kg and heavy oil was detected at 431 mg/kg in one of the samples collected from 8 feet below land surface.  Groundwater was not encountered within the upper 30 feet of land surface.",,,641.0,13750.0,LLO,2016-03-25 13:41:14.430
36737,26-09-1265,26,09,1265,12369.0,2009-12-14,2009-12-14 16:08:00.130,OREGON PAPER FIBER,12820 NE MARX ST,PORTLAND,97230,503-257-1331,False,7.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"5.16.2013:  EEM, LLC completed add. inv. w/3 borings.  some low PCE in GW, but <ing/inh. from tapwater.  drafted nfa. (RAH).


A 500-gallon waste oil UST was removed from the site in December 2009.  Sampling beneath the tank found no contamination by HCID.  However, sampling along the product line found 454 ppm heavy oil.  A total of 4.64 tons of PCS was removed, and confirmation sampling by NWTPH-Dx found no residual contamination.  However, the waste oil contamination should have been sampled for other contaminants (such as solvents, metals, PCBs), and the potential for groundwater impacts was not addressed.  The RP decided not to conduct additional sampling, and the site was backlogged.  (4/2/12 KPD)",,,112409.0,13752.0,RHOOD,2013-05-16 14:30:13.257
