36886,26-10-0100,26,10,0100,,2010-02-16,2010-02-17 08:26:02.683,Allbee Klaus LLC,8002 N Lombard St,PORTLAND,97203,,False,0.0,,0.0,,False,True,False,0.0,False,False,False,False,False,62 ppm diesel,,,114371.0,13894.0,MJGILLE,2010-02-17 08:26:02.683
36887,30-10-0101,30,10,0101,8867.0,2010-02-17,2010-02-17 08:40:16.177,UMATILLA COUNTY ROAD DEPT,3920 WESTGATE RD,PENDLETON,97801,(541) 278-5424,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"On February 8 and 9, 2010, two 12,000 gallon underground storage tanks (USTs) containing gasoline and diesel, piping and dispensers were decommissioned by removal. Twenty-four soil samples were analyzed for total petroleum hydrocarbons-gasoline (NWTPH-Gx) and eighteen soil samples were analyzed for total petroleum hydrocarbons – diesel (NWTPH-Dx). Gasoline and diesel were detected in soil beneath the dispenser islands up to 926 mg/kg NWTPH-Gx and 11,900 mg/kg NWTPH-Dx.
A release of petroleum from an underground storage tank at the Umatilla County Road Department was reported to DEQ on February 17, 2010.
On February 23, 2012 excavation of petroleum contaminated soil beneath the dispenser islands and confirmation soil sampling occurred. Two soil samples were collected and analyzed for NWTPH-Gx and NWTPH-Dx. TPH-Dx was detected at  1860 mg/kg in one soil sample so further excavation was conducted and confirmation samples were collected on March 1 and March 5. Approximately 23 tons of petroleum contaminated soil was excavated and disposed of at Finley Buttes landfill in Boardman, Oregon. The tanks were recycled at Byrnes Oil Company in Walla Walla, Washington. Groundwater was not encountered to a maximum depth of 14 feet below ground surface.
Based on site specific conditions, Soil Matrix Level 2 cleanup criteria for this site are 80 mg/kg or less for total petroleum hydrocarbons as gasoline and 500 mg/kg or less for total petroleum hydrocarbons as diesel. Final soil confirmation sample results were 215 mg/kg and non-detect at less than 50 mg/kg TPH-Dx. The site therefore meets the cleanup requirements for a Level 2 Soil Matrix cleanup.",41020.0,0.0,MKIRK,2013-02-11 16:32:33.907
