37083,24-10-0296,24,10,0296,,2010-04-06,2010-04-09 13:42:52.517,City of Woodburn ROW,NE corner of Young and Doud St R-O-W,WOODBURN,97071,503-980-2408,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"City of Woodburn Right-of-Way located at NE corner of Young Street and Doud Street.  
Withers Lumber Inc., Trent Wither was interviewed, he is owner of adjacent property.
His father who is 75's years old did not know there was a tank in the street (Bob Withers).
There was a sawmill in the area in the 1920's this gas tank maybe 70 to 90 years old. Odd size 9.5 ft long by 3.5 feet wide. Also interview 80+ year old Mr Wolfers from Wolfer heating and cooling across the street, he never knew of the tank in the street and has been here all his life. Woodburn Lumber (now Withers) did have UST which were taken out in 1990 DEQ File # 24-90-4283. Wolfer's across the street has open file on release 24-91-4006.
We could find no more evidence of tanks in the vicinity of the abandoned gas tank in the street.  Karl Van Zandt, 4/6/2010.",,"A 450 gallon underground storage tank was discovered in the City right of way beneath the roadway and sidewalk on the south side of the Withers Lumber Company located at 257 Young Street during a curb replacement. The UST was removed in April 2010. Approximately 12 tons of petroleum contaminated soil was removed from the UST excavation and disposed at the Riverbend Landfill. Residual gasoline-contaminated soil was left in place due to physical obstructions. Soil, groundwater, and soil gas samples were analyzed for contaminants of concern. A request for public comment was issued on March 6, 2012 for a proposed no further action. No comments were received. A no further action determination was issued on June 13, 2012.",114955.0,14087.0,MKIRK,2012-06-21 08:40:53.080
