37184,03-10-0397,03,10,0397,3469.0,2010-04-30,2010-05-04 07:58:57.980,CARSON OIL - CLACKAMAS,9911 SE ELON ST,CLACKAMAS,97015,(503) 224-8500,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"In April 2010, corrosion in a metal piping connector caused a release of diesel to soil beneath a dispenser.  The contractor later reported (via e-mail) that 56 tons of ""contaminated rock"" had been removed and shipped to a landfill, and that a confirmation soil sample found 10,200 ppm diesel beneath a satelite dispenser.  No report was submitted, however.  (4/3/12 KPD)",,,6426.0,0.0,KDANA,2012-04-03 13:31:05.780
37185,26-10-0398,26,10,0398,6040.0,2010-03-18,2010-05-04 10:08:08.910,POWELL DISTRIBUTING - KWIK GAS,9125 NE MARTIN LUTHER KING JR BLVD,PORTLAND,97211,(503) 285-6013,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Diesel impacts found when upgrading piping.  Further investigation shows gasoline, oil, and diesel impacts at the site.  Impacts detected from ground down 25 feet to groundwater.  Tanks installed in 1939. Two adjacent ECSI sites were part of an early truck repair facility. 

File sent to Eastern Region. LLC 11/15/11",,"[Aug. 2017] The Kwik Gas Station site (Multnomah County Map 1N1E10AA, Tax Lot 3600) is located at 9125 NE MLK Jr. Blvd. in Portland. The site is 0.33 acre and has been an active gas station since at least the 1930s. Currently there is a single story building, pump islands and three 10,000-gallon underground storage tanks (USTs)  present on the property. 

During routine maintenance in March 2010, fuel dripping from the two southern fuel dispensers was observed. The leaks were repaired.  Shallow groundwater is present at or greater than 17 feet below ground surface.

Petroleum contamination in soil is primarily present in the vicinity of the pump island and is generally greater than 15 feet deep.  Shallow groundwater contamination is primarily limited to the site property and adjacent right-of-ways. A contaminated media management plan was prepared to address possible future risks to construction and excavation workers and inform decisions about managing contaminated media.

A NFA was issued on 8/28/2017.

See site document section to view select site documents.",22016.0,0.0,KROBERT,2017-08-28 14:10:03.643
