37212,26-10-0425,26,10,0425,12430.0,2010-05-05,2010-05-10 09:07:33.217,Broadway Furniture,228 NE Broadway St,PORTLAND,97232,503-281-5555,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"A 370-gallon gasoline UST was discovered off the NW corner of Broadway Furniture (at 2nd & Broadway) in February 2010.  The UST was filled in-place in April 2010 and almost 9 tons of PCS was removed in May 2010.  DEQ issued an NFA letter in November 2010.

Three additional USTs were removed from the site in December 2012: a 675-gallon HOT, a 2,000-gallon gasoline UST (both on the south side of the facility), and a 340-gallon HOT on the east side of the facility.  Soil sampling found no releases from the USTs.

Additional sampling at the NW corner of the facility in 2012 found up to 5,100 ppm gasoline in the soil at 16 feet bgs, and up to 9,800 ug/m3 gasoline in sub-slab vapors.  The residual contaminant concentrations did not exceed RBCs for current or reasonably likely future exposure pathways.",116247.0,0.0,KDANA,2014-08-21 13:32:33.387
37213,26-10-0426,26,10,0426,1881.0,2010-05-06,2010-05-10 13:53:55.287,NORTHWEST RETREADERS II,19004 NE SAN RAFAEL ST,GRESHAM,97230,(503) 665-6144,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Sampling in May 2010 around a dispenser connected to a 1,000-gallon diesel UST found up to 40,800 ppm diesel in the soil.  Reportedly, 23.80 tons of PCS were removed on May 20 and shipped to the Hillsboro Landfill for disposal.  Confirmation sampling still found up to 31,400 ppm diesel at 6 ft bgs.  Additional sampling to delineate the extent of contamination found up to 1,200 ppm diesel at 14.5 ft bgs.  The consultant calculated that 108 cubic yards of PCS remained at the site.  DEQ received a report in December 2010 recommending no further action based on a risk analysis, but no Cost Recovery Agreement was submitted.  (4/3/12 KPD)",ECSI #1268 and LUST #26-01-0009,,7986.0,0.0,KDANA,2018-05-15 07:14:45.190
