37297,26-10-0510,26,10,0510,,2010-06-02,2010-06-02 14:59:42.603,"Glueck, Keith",5907 SE 23rd Ave,PORTLAND,97202,,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,WTE ND and ETE 2810.,,,115923.0,14303.0,EMCMORR,2010-11-17 08:53:01.033
37298,26-10-0511,26,10,0511,12386.0,2010-06-01,2010-06-02 15:15:09.733,Lim's Refrigeration,930 SE Lincoln St,PORTLAND,97214,503-235-6912,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"On June 1, 2010, DEQ received a report of an unauthorized tank pull at this site.  One unregistered 3,000-gallon diesel tank was lying on the surface, while its twin was still in the ground.  DEQ demanded that a contractor be hired to properly complete the decommissioning and cleanup.  Both tanks were removed from the site along with 216.37 tons of PCS.  Confirmation sampling still found up to 3,470 ppm diesel in the ground, at depths up to 16 ft bgs.  The extent of the residual contamination still needs to be determined.  (1/27/11 KPD).  Dana Thompson notified DEQ that site characterization work was scheduled for 4-18-11.  Await results (JKS 4-20-11). Report documenting follow-up investigation recieved in July 2011.  Delineation appears to be adequate.  However, a CSM was not submitted in support of request for risk-based closure.  Letter requesting CSM and minor revisions sent 7-29-11.   Revised figures and table, as well as some information comprising a CSM was submitted to DEQ in September and October 2011.  DEQ worked with Dana Thompson to flesh out the exposure pathway evaluation.  Comment solicitation letter sent 10-19-11. Comment period ends on 11-21-11 (JKS 11-16-11).",,,115925.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2012-02-14 14:03:27.673
