37387,26-10-0600,26,10,0600,,2010-06-23,2010-06-23 09:45:51.837,"Mclaughlin,James",4909 SW 19th Dr,PORTLAND,97239,,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Soil Gas Site,,,116297.0,14394.0,EMCMORR,2010-10-08 14:59:27.750
37388,26-10-0601,26,10,0601,7912.0,2010-06-24,2010-06-24 11:25:56.773,TRIMET CENTER STREET GARAGE V,4400 SE 17TH AVE,PORTLAND,97202,503-962-2472,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Release discsovered during 06-24-10 during decommissioning of waste oil UST; Contamination (gasoline and oil-range) detected in excavation floor and sidwall samples in the northwest UST excavation  Trimet is removing all the old waste oil USTs and replacing, one at a time. Two USTs removed to date and they are in the process of doing another. Confirmation sampling revealed TPH-O at levels as high as 40,000 mg/kg in the southern portion of the northwest UST excavation.  TPH-O as high as 11,000 mg/kg also discovered in the area of a product line at Bay 29.  UST work revealed a historic series of product lines in addition to most recent lines.  Lines were probed to the extent possible and evacuated of residual product to extent possible before being capped and pumped full of grout.  Further delineation of lateral and vertical extent of contamination is needed.  Work plan for additional investigation submitted by AMEC and comments provided.  Supplemental investigation performed in November 2010.  Borings advanced along perimeter of NW UST excavation and at selected locations in area of South UST excavation largely delineated extent of soil contamination.  Groundwater samples collected cross-gradient to down-gradient of June 2010 compliance sample SW exhibited minimal to none impacts. Investigation findigns are largely consistent with results of risk evaluations performed for prior releases.  Public Notice posted to DEQ website on 4-15-11.  Public comment period closes on 5-20-11 (JKS 4-18-11). Public comment period closed with no comments received.  Draft NFA preapared and submitted to Hydrogeologist (JKS 6-22-11).","LUST #26-92-0320, #26-94-0153, #26-99-0018, and #26-04-2509",,333.0,0.0,LKENT,2011-10-12 15:50:17.677
