37475,20-10-0688,20,10,0688,,2010-07-07,2010-07-12 11:45:56.310,Monroe Alley Tank,2461 Friendly St,EUGENE,97405,,False,7.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"An underground storage tank (UST) having dimensions of 39"" diameter X 48"" length (approximately 250 gallons) was discovered on 7/2/2010 during property redevelopment for construction of a new single family residence.  Approximately 175 gallons of product was pumped from the tank prior to removal.  Approximately 1 to 5 gallons of residual fluid drained from a corrosion hole located on the bottom of the UST when the tank was permanently decommissioned by removal on 7/7/2010...Daniel Mumford, Bergeson-Boese & Assoc. 7/7/2010.",,"Contractors encountered a 250-gallon underground storage tank while excavating on your property adjacent to the Monroe Street alley. The tank was decommissioned by removal on July 7, 2010.

The tank was used to store gasoline and diesel fuel products, and had not been used for many years. Approximately 175 gallons of gasoline remained in the tank upon discovery.

Eight cubic yards of petroleum-contaminated soil were excavated from the tank location. Prior to disposal, a sample collected from the contaminated soil measured gasoline at 1,250 ppm and diesel at 243 ppm. The soil was transported to Coffin Butte Landfill in Benton County, Oregon. 

Excavation was completed up to 5.5 feet bgs. Groundwater was not encountered during tank decommissioning or soil removal activities.

BB&A Environmental completed assessment activities, including the collection of four soil samples from the bottom and sidewalls of the excavation. A soil sample collected from the south end of the excavation (WIC01-S-5.5’) measured gasoline at 26.1 ppm. Diesel was present in the east sidewall at 22.7 ppm.",116562.0,14467.0,CRODDA,2010-11-09 09:25:39.673
