37615,34-10-0828,34,10,0828,5491.0,2010-08-16,2010-08-17 14:39:59.420,SHELDON OIL - BANKS,182 N MAIN ST,BANKS,97106,(503) 842-2172,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Release reported 8-16-10. Contamination (gasoline-diesel) observed in area of dispenser island.  Soil excavated to depth of approximately 6 feet bgs. West and east sidewall samples from depth of 4 feet bgs detected TPH-G at 518 and 871 mg/kg, respectively.  Lesser concentrations of TPH-D (49.2 to 241 mg/kg) detected in samples.  20-day report indicates follow-up analyses for BTEX and PAHs performed, but data has not been received yet. Await 45-day report.  HIstoric release at site (34-96-0687).  Borings revealed groundwater contaminated with low levels of gas constituents on the south side of UST excavation and west of southern pump island.  Groundwater historically found at 12-13 feet bgs.  Letters sent on 10-19-10 and 2-3-11 requesting 45-day report.  Information submitted via emial in February 2011 but was lost through misfiling.  Information packet received 8-31-11.  Information was found to include some elements of a 45-day report.  Letter sent to RP on 12-8-11 stating that further requests for 45-day report will not be made.  Furthermore, 12-8-11 letter requested work plan for additional delineation investigation.  Follow up  investigation completed in March 2012.  In borings advanced around the dispenser islands, diesel detected in groundwater at maximum concentration of 4,600 ppb.  Very degraded contamination, consistent with levels discovered in area of dispensers in 1996 (closed file 34-96-0687).  Beneficial water use determination did not identify water wells in area of site. Likely future commercial property use.  Comment solicitation letter sent out 4-16-13. No comments received. Appropriate to close file (JKS 7-15-13).",LUST 34-96-0687 & 34-20-0368,,105905.0,0.0,KDANA,2021-02-04 10:42:12.410
