37638,22-08-1533,22,08,1533,12124.0,2008-05-15,2010-08-25 13:13:38.027,PetroCard (I-5 & Hwy34 Cardlock),33380 Hwy 34 SE,ALBANY,97322,(253) 867-3281,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"Reported to DEQ in May 2008.  ECSI 5044 initiated.  DEQ review in April 2010 determined most petroleum contamination related to Younger Oil Co site immediately adjacent to cardlock facility.  Some diesel released from PetroCard AST/UST system, but soil was excavated & water pumped from product trench in 2008.  Further investigation in 2009.  Release finally entered into database August 2010... c rodda, 8/10/2010.","22-88-4028 YOUNGER OIL COMPANY
22-06-0975 TRUAX HARRIS ENERGY # 205
ECSI #5044","Petrocard operates a cardlock fuel facility at 33380 Highway 34 in Albany. Prior to Petrocard, Truax Harris Energy operated the cardlock station. The cardlock facility consists of a northern unit (6 pump islands) and a southern unit (5 pump islands now operated by Virk, LLC). Petrocard took over operation of the cardlock station in 2006, at which time Truax conducted a site assessment. Petroleum contamination at the cardlock portion of the facility (DEQ UST Facility #12124, with above-ground tanks also utilized for diesel storage) was reported by Truax in 2006. A leaking underground storage tank cleanup project was assigned to Truax Harris Energy (Truax #205, DEQ Tanks File #22-06-0975). In 2008, Petrocard conducted work on a product line at the northern portion of the cardlock facility. Following assessment conducted by contractors on behalf of Petrocard, a separate cleanup project (ECSI #5044) was created for what was believed to be a release from the AST system based on petroleum detected at the diesel product line. Diesel for the cardlock operations was stored in above-ground tanks located at the southwestern end of the facility. Based on reported petroleum contamination by three separate station operators, DEQ assigned three project numbers/petroleum releases to the facility. In 2009, Truax requested further DEQ review of the reported releases to make a determination of liability for the identified petroleum contamination. DEQ determined that the contamination identified in 2006 during Kleinfelder’s assessment for Truax was related to the previous gasoline release by Younger Oil retail station operations (LUST #22-88-4028). Further, DEQ determined that gasoline contamination at the northern portion of the Petrocard cardlock facility was also related to the Younger Oil petroleum release. DEQ decided after further assessment that despite the presence of an on-site drinking water well, petroleum releases have been documented since 1988 and the well has not been adversely impacted. Further, Virk contracted with a well driller to deepen the well in 2012. The deepening of the well from 140 feet bgs to 168 feet bgs was approved by OWRD. Because the drinking water well currently is not at risk from the diesel release at the facility, no further action is needed for this site. DEQ requires that within the identified LOF, these conditions apply: no new water wells, notice of zoning changes, use of CMMP and HASP for future excavation.",91143.0,0.0,CRODDA,2013-10-17 15:56:33.283
37639,26-10-0851,26,10,0851,10668.0,2010-08-26,2010-08-26 14:17:11.947,LOVE'S TRAVEL STOP #449,400 NW FRONTAGE RD,TROUTDALE,97060,(503) 665-7741,False,,,3.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"5/18/12:  Site being combined with 26-07-0286. same site (RAH)


LLC:
Love's curently owns this facility which was recently purchased from Pilot Travel Centers LLC, who maintains environmental liability. Love's performed investigation activities at the site to establish baseline conditions as previous releases have been documented at this location. The investigation indicates the presence of hydrocarbons in soil and groundwater.  It is assumed that the reported hydrocarbons are associated with residual contamination from previously documented releases.  Pilot received notification of the investigation results on August 25, 2010.",26-07-0286 Flying J Travel Plaza III,This file administratively closed since file number 26-07-0286 was already an established UST cleanup project.,53793.0,14660.0,RHOOD,2012-08-31 10:34:17.683
