37745,26-10-0957,26,10,0957,8835.0,2010-09-02,2010-09-23 08:08:18.147,FRIENDLY FOOD MART,6010 NE KILLINGSWORTH ST,PORTLAND,97218,503-860-7152,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"A DEQ site inspection in January 2010 observed multiple broken spill buckets at the site.  Nine cubic yards of contaminated soil were removed from beneath the premium gasoline spill bucket in February.  In September 2010 the facility's leak detection system showed leaks in the premium gasoline product line and beneath a dispenser.  About 40 tons of PCS were excavated from beneath the product line in October.  The potential leak beneath the dispenser still needs to be investigated.  (12/21/10 KPD).  DEQ letter send to owner in March 2011 indicating need for additional data in area of dispenser.  In June 2011, DEQ received analytical report for soil sample allegedly collected from area.  No figures provided nor narrative about sample collection.  Data on COC did not match report.  Data completely unacceptable in current form.  Letters sent to owner on 6-20-11 and 9-27-11 requesting clarification.  Clarifying information received from Jeff Pike of Petroluem Compliance Services LLC in October 2011.  Documentation submittd by PCS clarified the nature of the investigation performed in the area of the dispensers north of the site building.  This area was investgated in January 2011 in response to a slighly elevated helium reading taken PRIOR to discovery of the significant product line release. Visual observations and laboraty analysis of a sample from the eastern dispenser north of the building confirmed there was no evidence of a leak at the dispensers.  All soil data collected from this area, area of the spill buckets and the remedial excavation meet Soil Matrix Level II standards.  Groundwater not encountered at any time during the investigations.  Checked with Greg Toran to ensure there were no remaining compliance concerns for the site.  Site qualifies for closure under Matrix Rules (JKS 10-27-11).",LUST #26-91-0054 & #26-13-0231,,24003.0,0.0,KDANA,2014-04-14 08:26:51.673
