37762,26-10-0974,26,10,0974,12390.0,2010-09-22,2010-09-27 15:40:33.793,SE 36th & Hawthorne,3557 SE Hawthorne Blvd,PORTLAND,97214,(503) 227-8600 x13,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Two UST removed from site on September 22, 2010.  Gray stained soil with petroleum odor observed in excavation in southeast corner of the property.  Groundwater not observed in excavation and did not enter excavation.  20-Day Report indicates at least 170 cubic yards of contaminated soil removed from excavation.  Analytical data for sample used to profile waste: 182 mg/kg gasoline using Method NWTPH-Gx, and very low levels of ethybenzene and total xylenes.  45-day report documenting UST removal and over-excavation of impacted soil reviewed by DEQ.  Comments provided via email in early December 2010.  In a meeting with consultant in December 2010, discussed need for additional delineation along south side of property and  soil-gas investigation to assess vapor intrusion risks.   Soil-gas investigation performed in May 2011 revealed significant detections in SE Hawthorne south of the site.  In August 2011, follow-up soil-gas investigation performed in SE Hawthorne and selected areas of the site per DEQ-approved work plan.  Shallow and deep soil gas data from Hawthorne ROW indicates minimal risk to buildings to south.  Gasoline and constituetns detected in SG-8 at levels exceeding occupational soil-gas RBC, indicating unacceptable future risk.  E&ES requiring vapor mitigation measure needed for closure.  Letter requesting comments on closure strategy sent 12-2-11.  City of Portland submitted comment that the property owner would be responsible for reimbursing expenses related to characterization and handling of impacted media encountered in future right-of-way work. Kalberer Properties LLC was informed of City of Portland comment on 12-13-11.  Signed, notarized and recorded E&ES document received on 3-12-12.  OK to proceed with closure (JKS 3-20-12).",,,117516.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2012-06-25 08:13:33.867
