FIR 12.12.12

10.30.12:  drafted nfa, need to complete notice with Bosserman's and finish w/ODOT.  simpler risk assessment.  (RAH)

5.21.12:  Site was delayed by bank of the Owner (JP Morgan Chase).  JP Morgan now involved, sent them a bunch of information and they will be getting bids to complete work shortly. (RAH)


8.26.11: work plan and add. info. due 9.30 (RAH)

abandon tank discovered during demo of building. Only one end of the tank showed contamination in soil: Gasoline @ 480 ppm, Diesel @ 220 ppm. RBDM,VOC's,PAH's below RBC's. Diesel in water at 9200 ppb. Gas in water 800 ppb.",,,118205.0,14988.0,RHOOD,2012-12-12 14:37:26.293
37976,34-10-1188,34,10,1188,6903.0,2010-12-02,2010-12-02 14:47:53.767,TRI-MET MERLO GARAGE,16130 SW MERLO RD,BEAVERTON,97006,(503) 642-0760,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"An initial report (from PBS Environmental) is expected by the end of February.  (1/5/11 KPD).  Pulled ECSI File 1348.  Staff report for this file references cleanup and investigation in wetlands south of site due to release in 1994.  Pulled historic file 34-89-0240 which was closed by NFA in July 1996.  Contamination detected in footprint of former fueling building is consistent with residual contamination from releases in 1990, 1993, and 1994.  Low levels of groundwater contamination detected in borings south and east of 2010 UST excavation. Attempting to locate historic analytical data for former monitoring wells to determine if contamination previously documented in this area. (JKS 3-29-11).  PBS submitted additional information related to water use at nearby properties to west.  Additional information requested by DEQ in email dated 5-27-11.  Based on conferral with Hydrogeologist, contamination in area of  southern UST pit is consistent with historic contamination from early to mid 1990s (JKS 5-27-11).  NFA preparation underway (JKS 9-12-11).  Zoning of north part of site (parking lot) for Station Community-Mixed Use allows attached and detached dwellngs.  Southern 2/3 of site is zoned Station Community- Employment Zone 3 which prohbits these uses.  Spoke with Kristin Preston about including a condition in NFA prohibiting residential development (JKS 9-19-11).","LUST #34-89-0240, 34-94-0078, 34-98-1075, 34-14-0791, and ECSI #1348",,225.0,0.0,KDANA,2014-06-23 08:31:05.023
