38093,26-11-0036,26,11,0036,2119.0,2011-01-13,2011-01-18 13:31:53.933,Cochran Electric (Former),626 SE Main St,PORTLAND,97214,,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Former dispenser inside building leaked, resulting in contamination along the north wall of building and extending under adjacent sidwalk.  Between March and May 2011, EEM performed site assesment and remedial excavation.  Confirmation samples collected along the north interior wall near the former pump island exhibited extremely high levels of gasoline constituents.  In November-December 2011, Robert Miller Consulting removed impacted soil from beneath the north foundation wall and adjacent sidewalk, to an approximate depth of 10 feet bgs.  Confirmation sampling revealed that most of the contamination was successfully removed.  However, a handfull of soil samples still contained constituents at levels exceeding occupational worker vapor intruison RBCs.  RMC installed a geomembrane liner in the excavation as it was being backfilled, as well as passive vapor collection piping beneath the liner. A sub-slab sampling port was installed in the concrete slab. Analysis of a sub-slab sample collected in February 2012 did not reveal any detections in soil-gas exceeding RBCs.  604 tons of impacted soil was removed from the site between March and December 2011. Closure of release is appropriate (JKS 4-18-12).",,,19383.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2012-04-18 09:06:37.203
