38218,10-11-0161,10,11,0161,4371.0,2011-02-17,2011-02-28 14:45:09.570,JITNEY SHOP - RFP,10650 OLD HWY 99S,DILLARD,97432,541-679-3311,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"8/28/2018: Site address originally ""Old Hwy 99S."" Changed to 10650 OLD HWY 99S... gdeck.

Release discovered at time of broken spill bucket repair... e clough, 2/17/2011.

need further site investigation, soil sample at 21"" bgs (on top of tank) had 40,000 Dx (esc 9-mar-11)",10-18-1001 JITNEY SHOP RFP II,"The site is used by Roseburg Forest Products for sawmill operations. The facility (DEQ UST Facility #4371) has six underground storage tanks at its location on Old Highway 99 South in Dillard. The tanks were installed in 1975 and are used to store various petroleum products, including diesel, transmission fluid, and gear oil. In February 2011, an inspection by DEQ staff identified a broken spill bucket for the diesel tank. When the spill bucket was repaired, the contractor found contamination outside the bucket in backfill material on top of the tank. Two soil samples were collected of the contaminated soil and analyzed for diesel-range hydrocarbons. Results showed diesel at 40,400 ppm in RFP-001 (excavation sidewall) and 34,500 ppm in RFP-002 (stockpile). Receipts show that 25 tons of contaminated soil was disposed of at the Roseburg Landfill in Sept. 2011, which included material for disposal from other areas at the facility. Only one cubic yard of contaminated soil was removed around the spill bucket. Confirmation samples were not collected following excavation of visually contaminated soil. A plan for managing contaminated media was developed by RFP in April 2015 to properly handle petroleum-contaminated soil during future UST excavation work. A health and safety plan was also developed to provide workers with protective measures for contact with contaminated media.",20935.0,0.0,GDECK,2018-08-28 14:08:42.380
