10.2018: Ready to final invoice.  After NFA issued, will still be working with Lardo on soil gas sampling as they it is expanding its restaurant.  (RAH)

12.8.2017:  Staff Memo finalized and uploaded.  next is impacted party letters and finalize EES with Sid. (RAH)

11/2017:  drafted nfa, need to record EES with Sid Cooper-owner, need to send impacted party notices to 1524 se ladd owner and city PDX, need to draft staff memo. (RAH)


4.2016;  UST decom report submitted by Alpha.  Chevron will approach Sid Cooper re: possible indemnity regarding future development. (RAH)

12.3.2015, 2 tanks decommissioned in-place by Sid.  Confirmation samples were collected.  See inspection notes in database. (RAH)

1.22.2014:  letter sent to Chevron to complete rest of inv./cleanup.  requested they contact me by 3 March. (RAH)

1.2014:  release confirmed via APEX for DEQ.  off-property impacts.  no vapor concerns.  next steps, ltr to caputo shell -verbal concern and contact Unocal re: being RP. (RAH)


11.18.2013:  Received Federal funds to do conduct investigation.  Work was completed in early November.  (RAH)


PBS was conducting site assessment work for a potential buyer of the site.  Gray stained soil with a petroleum odor was detected adjacent to a probable underground storage tank identified during a geophysical survey.  Groundwater and soil samples were collected, however the potential buyer of the site decided not to have PBS continue work on the site and analytical data has not been received. The project has been put on hold.",,See Site Document Section to view select project reports.,123293.0,15418.0,RHOOD,2018-10-19 10:48:30.740
