38926,29-11-0868,29,11,0868,7916.0,2011-08-23,2011-08-25 11:28:46.003,CITY OF TILLAMOOK  (CITY SHOPS),108-116 Birch Ave,TILLAMOOK,97141,(503) 842-2472,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"The City of Tillamook reportedly purchased this site in 1907.  In the 1920s or 1930s the site was raised with up to 15 ft of fill, mostly consisting of sand, gravel and sawdust but including pieces of wood, metal, glass, brick and concrete.  The site was developed with public works shops.  Four underground storage tanks (holding gasoline and diesel) were installed at the site beginning in 1971.  All four tanks were reportedly removed in 1989.  Sampling in the summer of 2011 found petroleum products (gasoline, diesel, motor oil) and petroleum constituents in the soil and groundwater, concentrated around the former UST pit.  A total of 132.59 tons of petroleum-contaminated soil were removed from the UST pit in late-December 2011.  Soil and groundwater contamination remains at the site, but no long-term threats to human health or the environment are anticipated.  As of February 2012, plans were to redevelop the site as a parking lot for an adjacent medical office building.",142725.0,15947.0,iPMO#38,2016-10-14 07:10:29.843
