39143,26-11-1085,26,11,1085,6815.0,2011-10-17,2011-10-18 08:33:17.120,Hayden Meadows Property,1140 HAYDEN MEADOWS DR,PORTLAND,97217,(503) 241-1111,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"In August 2011, PSI performed a Phase II ESA of the site, in part to assess conditions near a used oil UST decommissed in place in 1987.  One boring (B1) was advanced near the decommissioned UST.  Analysis of a soil sample did not reveal detectable levels of diesel or oil-range hydrocarbons or VOCs.  Analysis of the groundwater sample revealed only diesl hydrocarbons at a concentratoin of 473 ppb (the applicable RBC for groundwater ingestion under the occupational worker scenario is 430 ppb).  GRI submitted a limited conceptual site model and exposure pathway evaluation in December 2011.  Due to information concerning a pending property transaction, DEQ completed a survey of WRD records and applicable zoning regulations.  Based on minimal contamination levels, and likely limited extent of impacted groundwater, DEQ determined that closure was acceptable.  DEQ decided that public comment was not warranted.   (JKS 2-1-12)",,,22593.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2012-02-16 14:44:53.077
