39166,26-11-1108,26,11,1108,,2011-10-21,2011-10-25 07:17:58.933,"French, Marvin",1743 NE 141st Ave,PORTLAND,97230,,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"11,300 ppm DX",,,121873.0,16190.0,MJGILLE,2012-02-06 13:54:36.063
39167,34-11-1109,34,11,1109,12099.0,2011-10-25,2011-10-26 07:23:38.053,ALBERTSONS EXPRESS #591,884 NE 25TH AVE,HILLSBORO,97124,503-681-8927,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Historic investigations related to developement of the property detected low levels of gasoline and diesel-range hydrocarbons in the area of the USTs and dispensers.  However, the actual source of the low-level detections were unclear.  In September 2011, Hart Crowser completed an additional Phase II ESA at the site.  The scope of work included sampling of monitoring wells previously installed in the area of the fueling system but never regularly sampled.  Relatively low levels of gasoline and diesel hydrocarbons were detected in groundwater.  Based on the Hart Crowser findings, a release was reported. In December 2011, Stantec performed follow-up work including the installation of  additional monitoring wells.  Gasoline hydrocarbons and toluene were detected at levels exceeding groundwater ingestion RBCs for the current and likely future occupational worker scenario. At the request of DEQ, Stantec performed a BWUD consisting of a search of WRD records and limited door-to-door survey.  No wells were located and connection to city water was confirmed.  Shallow groundwater was not found to have a current or likely future beneficial use as drinking water.  Based on low risk and low levels of gasoline hydrocarbons in groundwater, further investigation is not warranted.  Public comment was not deemed necessary (JKS 3-8-12)",,,39534.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2012-03-08 10:37:35.843
