39260,26-11-1202,26,11,1202,,2011-11-21,2011-11-21 09:35:24.180,Former Clark Property,1851 NW Eleven Mile Ave,GRESHAM,97030,503-962-2472,False,,,3.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Laboratory analytical shows 6,430 diesel-range organics in a single soil sample.","This file (26-11-1202) is being administratively closed because the site was originally reported as LUST site reported by Landau Associates but confirmed by Alpha as a clean decommission per Kevin Dana. See the lab results in clean decommission File HOTD- 33475.  The Site: 1851 NW Eleven Mile Ave, Gresham, OR was tested with results of ND. ",,122155.0,16290.0,IGAFFNE,2015-02-19 14:43:56.703
39261,26-11-1203,26,11,1203,3954.0,2011-11-21,2011-11-21 14:25:07.697,ARCO 4208 II,12140 NE Halsey St,PORTLAND,97220,,False,7.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Eight dispensers were replaced at the site in November 2011.  Soil samples from beneath the dispensers showed no petroleum by HCID.  However, gasoline (296 ppm) was detected in an electrical conduit trench to the north of the dispenser islands.  Over 50 tons of PCS were excavated and shipped to Hillsboro.  No confirmation soil samples were collected.",LUST #26-91-0074,,3305.0,16291.0,KDANA,2012-06-11 08:20:57.587
39262,26-11-1204,26,11,1204,3985.0,2011-11-21,2011-11-21 14:33:51.843,ARCO 4477 II,16141 SE Division St,PORTLAND,97236,,False,7.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Ten fuel dispensers were replaced at this site in October 2011.  A single soil sample was collected from beneath each dispenser and analyzed for petroleum products.  ""Motor oil"" was detected beneath one dispenser at 2.5 ft bgs and quantified as 20.9 ppm diesel and 357 ppm motor oil.  0.5 cubic yards of PCS were excavated, and a confirmation sample from 4.5 ft bgs found 11.6 ppm diesel and 76.0 ppm motor oil.

There are two problems with the report.  First, disposal receipts show that 59.09 tons of PCS were removed.  Second, another soil sample (labelled ""18 ft"") showed 69.4 ppm diesel and 275 ppm motor oil.  No location or explanation of the sample was given.  (6/12/12 KPD)",LUST #26-89-0251,,122159.0,16292.0,KDANA,2012-06-12 08:34:21.703
39263,26-11-1205,26,11,1205,12419.0,2011-11-21,2011-11-21 16:00:30.767,Kim Property,2880 SE Division St,PORTLAND,97202,,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"GASOLINE-RANGE ORGANICS DETECTED IN SOILS AT 3,220 MG/KG.

Another cost recovery agreement signed on December 19, 2016 was recently submitted.  The recent CRA is on file.",,"Historical site use has been commercial but specific uses are unknown.  Three underground storage tanks (USTs) were removed from the northwest corner of the property below the sidewalk along Division Street. The exact cause of the contamination is unknown but is likely to have resulted from leaks in a tank(s) or connections to historical piping. Only soil is known to be contaminated.  Groundwater was not encountered during the decommissioning or in soil borings. Approximately 72 tons of petroleum contaminated soil was excavated in March of 2012 and disposed of at the Hillsboro Landfill. The three USTs were taken to Metro Metals in Portland for recycling. 467 cubic yards of petroleum contaminated soil is conservatively estimated to remain at the site. The property is expected to remain commercial use with residential properties surrounding the site. There is no consumptive use of groundwater in the area. One industrial well and one novelty irrigation well exist within a quarter mile of the site and are not expected to be impacted. The maximum extent of contamination is expected to be located within a 30 by 70 foot area, perpendicular to Division Street, and centered on the former tank pit.",122160.0,16299.0,CRICHAR,2017-04-10 09:40:30.350
39264,26-11-1206,26,11,1206,,2011-11-21,2011-11-28 07:28:27.307,"Gillaspie, Janet",2336 NE 23rd Ave,PORTLAND,97212,503-233-3980,False,2.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,0.0,16293.0,EMCMORR,2012-03-30 13:44:10.553
