39266,34-11-1208,34,11,1208,,2011-11-21,2011-11-28 07:30:45.637,"Moore, Kenneth",11785 SW Denney Rd,BEAVERTON,97008,503-646-3440,False,0.0,,0.0,,False,True,False,0.0,False,False,False,False,False,"11124-B1-S-80"" - 43,400 PPM
 11124-B2-N-80"" - 98 PPM",,,122178.0,16295.0,MJGILLE,2011-11-28 07:30:45.637
39267,26-11-1209,26,11,1209,4410.0,2011-11-21,2011-11-28 07:31:52.910,Pioneer Oil Co,9270 NE Glisan St,PORTLAND,97220,503-281-2828,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"A damaged spill bucket atop a 20,000-gallon heating oil (diesel) tank was observed during an inspection in November 2011.  A soil sample from beneath the spill bucket found 12,300 ppm diesel.  A total of 0.79 tons of PCS was removed and sent to the Hillsboro Landfill, and a confirmation sample found a total of 456 ppm diesel and heavy oil, below the Level 2 Soil Matrix Cleanup standard of 500 ppm.  (6/13/12 KPD)
See also 26-12-0883

In letter dated 11-7-12, DEQ informed Pioneer Oil Company that the figure submitted to document cleanup of contamination to soil matrix standards was not adequate for portraying site features and the extent of contaminatino.  Revised figure received on December 19, 2012.  Figure revisions are adequate to address DEQ concerns.  Site can likely close under matrix levels. (JKS 1-16-13).",LUST #26-12-0883 & LUST #26-16-0999,,122179.0,16296.0,KDANA,2016-08-08 08:26:50.577
