39328,24-11-1270,24,11,1270,617.0,2011-12-01,2011-12-14 15:23:08.537,THE ARSENAL,280 PINE ST NE,SALEM,97303,(503) 949-5074,False,4.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,24-94-4128 Kar Kleen,"In 1964, the site was developed as a fuel station with convenience store and drive through car wash. Contamination was discovered in 2011 during a Phase II investigation and is believed to be previously unidentified contamination associated with a previous release on the site (LUST #24-94-4128). Soil and groundwater beneath the northern half of the property are impacted by gasoline and related constituents. The extent of the remaining contamination is outlined on the attached figure and likely extends slightly offsite to the north-northwest by not more than about 30 feet. The likely source of the release, the previous fuel system, was replaced with a new system that meets all current regulations.  Up to 1,000 cubic yards of impacted soil was removed during the previous investigation. The site and surrounding properties are all zoned Industrial Commercial and are connected to the municipal water system. The site and surrounding properties are expected to remain commercial and connected to city water. An opportunity to comment on the proposed closure was given to surrounding property owners, utility providers, and the City of Salem. No comments were received. On March 28, 2019 an Easement and Equitable Servitudes was recorded with Marion county on the property. The EES prohibits beneficial use of groundwater, requires maintaining the pavement cap that prohibits stormwater intrusion, and requires that a Contaminated Media Management Plan be followed during any subsurface work.",154187.0,0.0,GDECK,2019-04-03 11:40:39.800
