39362,26-11-1304,26,11,1304,,2011-12-21,2011-12-27 08:44:33.733,"Watne, Donald",2826 NE 26th Ave,PORTLAND,97212,,False,2.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,0.0,16390.0,MJGILLE,2012-04-10 14:54:48.920
39363,34-11-1305,34,11,1305,11503.0,2011-12-16,2011-12-27 10:38:54.170,7-ELEVEN #35354,15900 SW TUALATIN SHERWOOD RD,SHERWOOD,97140,(214) 415-0146,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"During a due diligence investigation performed by ATC in October 2007, benzene at a concentration of 4 ppb (J flagged) was reported in groundwater sample from a boring (B-2) west of the USTs.  Following submittal of information related to zoning and beneficial use of groundwater, DEQ issued an NFA determiation in Decebmer 2008.  During a subsequent due diligence investigation in November 2011, Stantec detected benzene at a slightly higher concentration (34 ppb) in groundwater from a boring (GP-1) also west of the USTs but slightly north of the 2007 boring. In July 2012, Antea Group submitted the historic reports to DEQ, arguing that the 2011 detection did not constitute evidence of a new release.  DEQ informed Antea Group that submittal of a Cost Recovery Agreement was needed so that DEQ could complete an evaluation of whether there is evidence of a new relase.  Cost recovery agreement submitted.  DEQ reivewed the historic and current data.  Beneficial use evaluation performed to close UST Cleanup File No. 34-07-1623 showed that groundwater had no current or likely future beneficial use as drinking water.  November 2011 detections in groundwater were in similar locations to the October 2007 data collected by ATC.  Still no evidence for a significant groundwater plume or release.  NFA is warranted based on these findings.  Public comment not needed, as CAP was not required.  (JKS 9-26-12).",,,9920.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2012-09-26 10:50:35.480
