39441,15-12-0067,15,12,0067,10651.0,2012-01-20,2012-01-26 14:26:03.263,"BILL TERPENING, INC",3680 N PACIFIC HWY,MEDFORD,97501,(541) 773-7311,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"1/20/12 During excavation for valve repair, encountered impacted soils in trench. Suspected to be from drips & spills as tank and line tests at site show no leaks. Soil sample showed 5130mg Dx; 0.65T PCS removed, re-sample came back ND. No GW encountered. Cost Recovery Agreement rcv'd 2/21/18 JClaussen Site re-opened on : 8/2/2018 By Virginia Deck. Previous Final Invoice Request Date: 5/31/2018.",,"On January 20, 2012, while excavating soil to install a new sump and product piping patch, petroleum contaminated soils were observed in soils near pump dispenser #6. Soil samples were collected and sent for analysis. Analytical results indicated the presence of diesel fuel at 5,130 mg/Kg. The contaminated soil was removed and disposed of at Dry Creek Landfill in Central Point, Oregon. After contaminated soil was removed, two additional confirmation soil samples were collected from beneath the location of contaminated soil. Sampling depths ranged from four to five feet below ground surface; both sample results were non-detect (ND) for presence of diesel, gasoline, and lube oil. Confirmation sample results were below the most stringent Soil Matrix Level I levels (diesel – 100mg/kg, gas - 40 mg/kg). No groundwater was encountered. The remedial action to address environmental contamination believed to be associated with the drips/spills at pump dispenser #6 is complete, and no further action is required. This NFA only applies to the small pocket of contaminated soil discussed and does not apply toward any other areas of the property.",16580.0,0.0,GDECK,2018-08-02 14:45:30.153
