39450,34-12-0076,34,12,0076,,2012-01-26,2012-01-30 07:51:11.127,"Oldfield, Marilyn",3465 SW 87th Ave,PORTLAND,97225,,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"ETE= 32,000 ppm DX and WTE= 11,600 ppm DX",,,0.0,16483.0,MJGILLE,2012-08-22 12:14:13.087
39451,09-12-0077,09,12,0077,5332.0,2012-01-23,2012-01-30 15:17:03.847,Space Age Fuel/Sisters General Store,411 W. CASCADE Street,SISTERS,97759,(503) 212-3900,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,LUST File #09-92-0044 and #09-05-1815,"In 1989, one 5,000 gallon gasoline Underground Storage Tank (UST), one 8,000 gallon gasoline UST and one compartmentalized 5,000 gallon UST containing diesel and gasoline were decommissioned by removal.  During decommissioning a fourth 1,000 gallon UST was discovered and removed.

One 12,000 gallon and two 10,000 gallon coated steel USTS were installed 1989.  

An unspecified volume (estimated to be approximately 650 cubic yards) of petroleum contaminated soil was excavated, placed onto six-mil plastic and allowed to aerate.  Following excavation, confirmation samples indicated TPH concentrations of 7,800 milligrams per kilogram (mg/kg) and 4,200 mg/kg remaining in soil.  

An additional five test pits were completed to varying depths to further characterize the site.  The February 1990 report indicated non-detection for petroleum hydrocarbons in nine soil samples collected from the five test pits. 

It is unclear whether a portion or all of the estimated 650 cubic yards of excavated petroleum contaminated soil was used as backfill at the site or removed from the site for disposal.  A “No Further Action” (NFA) determination was issued in October 1990.

