39953,10-12-0579,10,12,0579,8634.0,2012-05-29,2012-05-30 17:32:16.117,BARNES FUEL OIL II,281 S STATE ST,SUTHERLIN,97479,(541) 459-2255,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,,"10-98-0039, 10-93-0021","The Barnes Fuel Oil site is retail service station located at 281 South State Street in Sutherlin, Oregon.  In April 2012 DEQ staff identified a damaged spill containment sump associated with a gasoline underground storage tank (UST).  Lab results of a groundwater sample collected from a UST observation well by Barnes confirmed the presence of gasoline and diesel range petroleum.  At the direction of DEQ, Barnes conducted an investigation of the release.  The principal objectives of the investigation were to 1) determine the magnitude and extent of soil and groundwater impact; and 2) evaluate risk to current and future receptors in the area.  Groundwater flow beneath the site is west to northwest.  Soil and groundwater results confirm concentrations of all gasoline and diesel-related compounds are below the generic risk-based concentrtaions for all complete or potentially complete exposure scenarios.  Impact appears characteristic of a small-volume release affecting a limited area of extent.  Remaining impact does not represent a risk to current or likely future potential receptors.  Based on this assessment, DEQ finds that no further action is required regarding additional investigation and/or remediation of the release.

Note: The site was previously investigated under USTC file numbers 10-93-0021 and 10-98-0039 in response a confirmed belowground petroleum release.  This release was remediated and investigated in accordance with UST Cleanup Rules applicable at the time of the investigation.  On March 18, 2002, DEQ determined that no further action was needed regarding further investigation of the site.",23855.0,0.0,GDECK,2013-11-07 13:17:58.613
