39978,34-12-0604,34,12,0604,,2012-05-23,2012-06-05 16:09:14.037,Roger Ritchey,43820 SW Hiatt Road,FOREST GROVE,97116,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Sampling beneath gasoline UST revealed high levels of gasoline and BTEX beneath the north end.  TPH-G detected at 9,050 mg/kg.  In May 2012, K&S decommissioned the UST and over-excavated 25 tons of soil.  Confirmatino samples collected from the limits of the excavation revealed a maximum TPH-G concentration of 226 mg/kg.  However, samples from the west and east sidewalls exhibited TPH-G, benzene and ethylbenzene at levels above RBCs for vapor intrusion under residential and/or occupational worker scenarios.  Analysis of a pit water sample revealed TPH-G and constituetns in groundwater.  In June 2012, K&S advanced four borings (T1-T4) around the excavation.  Analysis of soil and groundwater samples form the borings did not reveal any detections, indicating contamination does not extend significantly beyond the limits of the UST excavation.  In July 2012, K&S collected a soil-gas sample from the area of the former UST.  No detections in soil-gas exceeded RBCs under the residential use scenario (JKS 7-31-12).",,,124090.0,16949.0,JSCHATZ,2012-07-31 09:40:13.063
