40321,34-12-0947,34,12,0947,,2012-08-14,2012-08-15 13:56:15.910,Bierly & Thoman,18900 SW Scholls Ferry Rd,BEAVERTON,97007,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Three USTs on property - one heating oil tank and two unregulated gasoline tanks.  Initial discovery confirmed by lab report on August 8, DEQ notification occurred by e-mail on August 9th.  Per instructions, site is being reported with comment on two contaminants.
80 tons of petroleum contaminated soil excavated and disposed at Hillsboro Landfill.  Tanks recycled at Schnitzer Steel.
Three USTs were removed from the site in August 2012.  Minimal contamination found near HOT (met Soil Matrixl Level II).  Samples from beneath one gasolien UST revealed contamination.  Following the removal of 56 tons of contaminated soil, the highest remaining gasoline detection in soil was 224 ppm.  At the request of DEQ, Alphha collected two soil gas samples from the site.  There were no detections exceeding residential soil-gas RBCs. 
The site is a rural residential property and a well is located approximately 65 feet west of the former gasoline UST.  Water well at the site was sampled in February 2014, December 2014 and June 2015.  No contamination detected in groundwater samples.  Soil contamination extends to only 15 feet bgs.  Based on shallow depth of contamination and lack of impacts in water well, low levels of residual soil contamination is unlikely to impact the beneficial use of site groundwater. Site is ready for closure recommendation.  Comment period initiated on September 10, 2015.  Site qualifies for closure (JKS 9-24-15).",,"Three USTs on property - one heating oil tank and two unregulated gasoline tanks.  Initial discovery confirmed by lab report on August 8, DEQ notification occurred by e-mail on August 9th.  Per instructions, site is being reported with comment on two contaminants.
80 tons of petroleum contaminated soil excavated and disposed at Hillsboro Landfill.  Tanks recycled at Schnitzer Steel.
Three USTs were removed from the site in August 2012.  Minimal contamination found near HOT (met Soil Matrixl Level II).  Samples from beneath one gasolien UST revealed contamination.  Following the removal of 56 tons of contaminated soil, the highest remaining gasoline detection in soil was 224 ppm.  At the request of DEQ, Alphha collected two soil gas samples from the site.  There were no detections exceeding residential soil-gas RBCs. 
The site is a rural residential property and a well is located approximately 65 feet west of the former gasoline UST.  Water well at the site was sampled in February 2014, December 2014 and June 2015.  No contamination detected in groundwater samples.  Soil contamination extends to only 15 feet bgs.  Based on shallow depth of contamination and lack of impacts in water well, low levels of residual soil contamination is unlikely to impact the beneficial use of site groundwater. Site is ready for closure recommendation.  Comment period initiated on September 10, 2015.  Site qualifies for closure (JKS 9-24-15).",124834.0,17365.0,JSCHATZ,2015-09-24 12:10:53.650
