40576,20-12-1202,20,12,1202,10445.0,2012-09-20,2012-10-02 13:08:30.703,COTTAGE GROVE CHEVRON,1250 GATEWAY BLVD,COTTAGE GROVE,97424,(503) 942-0105,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"No excavation map was provided.  Equipement that was removed looked to be in good shape leaving only surficial spills and overfilling to be the cause of contamination.

Given the site is a large UST site with multiple tanks and two seperate fueling areas there are likely other currently unknown issues that exist.  

Richardson disagrees with the exact soil matric score however his ranking does not change the cleanup standard from 500 ppm diesel.",UST Facility: 10445,"In August of 2012 upgrades were made to the diesel dispenser island to include new dispenser sumps, canopy footings and product piping.  During these upogrades diesel impacted soil was encountered and excavated.  Approximately 17.5 tons of impacted soil was disposed of at the Coffin-Butte Landfill.  The cause of contamination was determined to be from surficial spills that seeped through joints and/or cracks in the concrete apron surrounding the fuel dispensers.  

In November of 2015 five soil samples were collected from around and beneith the dispenser canopy.  Diesel was detected at a maximum concentration of 378 miligrams per kilogram (mg/Kg) which is below the appicable soil matrix cleanup standard of 500 mg/Kg.  Groundwater was collected from one boring and resulted in no detectable quanitities of diesel fuel.",16764.0,0.0,GDECK,2016-12-20 13:20:17.880
