40706,26-12-1332,26,12,1332,2491.0,2012-10-26,2012-10-29 10:54:37.877,Baha Auto Body (Former),4505-4535 SE 17th Ave,PORTLAND,97202,503-962-2149,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"This site consists of two properties: Star Oilco at 4505 SE 17th (Facility ID 2491) and Baha Auto Body at 4535 SE 17th.  A 1,000-gallon HOT was removed from the north end of the Baha Auto property in October 2010, followed by two 8,000-gallon USTs and three 1,000-gallon USTs from a former service station at the south end of the property.  A total of 25.56 tons of PCS were removed from around the HOT in November 2012.  A total of 161.77 tons of PCS were excavated from around the five USTs and associated pump island at the same time.  Confirmation sampling found only 88 ppm diesel.

Six USTs were removed from the Star Oilco facility in January 2013: two 4,000-gallon gasoline USTs, two 4,000-gallon biodiesel USTs, a 6,000-gallon biodiesel UST, and a 550-gallon waste oil UST.  A total of 56.27 tons of PCS were excavated from around the USTs, along with 338.91 tons of PCS from the associated pump island.  Finally, 143.65 tons of PCS were removed from beneath the former convenience store at Star Oilco, and 48.06 tons of PCS were removed from the area between the store and the Baha Auto Body HOT.

Residual contaminant concentrations do not exceed risk-based standards for future occupational use.",125715.0,17760.0,KDANA,2013-12-30 15:05:33.780
