41256,26-13-0296,26,13,0296,12446.0,2013-03-25,2013-03-25 11:44:04.340,Dexco - East Block,2316 NE Oregon St,PORTLAND,97232,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"In June and July 2013, multiple regulated USTs (A through D and H through K) werebremoved from two properties comprising the fomrer Davidon's Bakery.  Three USTs (E through G) were handled under the HOT program.  USTs decommissioned by filing in place, sawing the tank top and filling with recycled concrete or removal.  HCID testing detected diesel in compliance sample from excavation for Tank A. However, follow-up testing did not reveal detectable diesel or heavy oil using Method NWTPH-Dx.
Significant contamination was found beneath the east end of tank K at concetnrations ranging from 8,180 to 26, 300 ppm. Follow-up testing of the highest diesel detection did not reveal VOCs or above residential RBCs.  Although th detection limit for selected PAHs exceeded the most stringent RBCs, based on the depth of the sample, the contamination does not pose unreasonable risks to residents or employees.  The diesel concentrations deetecte exceed direct contact RBCs for construction workers but delineation saples collected two feet beyond the excavation did not contain detectable diesel, indicating the pocket of soil contamination is limited in lateral and vertical extent. Groundwater not encountered and expected to be at minimum depth of 45 feet. (JKS 10-21-13)",,"In June and July 2013, multiple regulated USTs (A through D and H through K) werebremoved from two properties comprising the fomrer Davidon's Bakery.  Three USTs (E through G) were handled under the HOT program.  USTs decommissioned by filing in place, sawing the tank top and filling with recycled concrete or removal.  Approximately 145 tons of petroleum contaminated material found as fill in the USTs was disposed at Hillsboro Landfill.  HCID testing detected diesel in compliance sample from excavation for Tank A. However, follow-up testing did not reveal detectable diesel or heavy oil using Method NWTPH-Dx.
Significant contamination was found beneath the east end of tank K at concetnrations ranging from 8,180 to 26, 300 ppm. Follow-up testing of the highest diesel detection did not reveal VOCs or above residential RBCs.  Although th detection limit for selected PAHs exceeded the most stringent RBCs, based on the depth of the sample, the contamination does not pose unreasonable risks to residents or employees.  The diesel concentrations deetecte exceed direct contact RBCs for construction workers but delineation saples collected two feet beyond the excavation did not contain detectable diesel, indicating the pocket of soil contamination is limited in lateral and vertical extent. Groundwater not encountered and expected to be at minimum depth of 45 feet. (JKS 10-21-13)",127168.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2013-10-21 09:33:31.877
