42168,22-13-1208,22,13,1208,2057.0,2013-08-23,2013-09-11 15:45:00.173,CRAIG OIL INC,4420 HWY 20,SWEET HOME,97386,(503)367-2462,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"9/28/18 Requested final invoice.
10/9/18 Payment received & NFA issued.",,"This site is a tire repair shop that had one 12,000-diesel underground storage tank with two primary dispensers located directly above the tank and one satellite dispenser, located approximately 10 feet south of the tank.  The soil contamination was discovered during a DEQ inspection in August 2013 and determined to be from a customer overfill at the satellite dispenser.  Also a small amount of surface soil contamination was encountered beneath the tank’s spill bucket during the tank decommissioning in 2016.  Surface soil was impacted with diesel fuel to an approximate depth of two feet below ground surface. No indication of impacts to groundwater or surface water were noted or suspected. The full extent of contaminated soil was excavated during the tank decommissioning in September 2016 at both the satellite dispenser and spill bucket areas. Confirmation samples were collected at the bottom of the excavation were clean.  Therefore, there is no indication of any residual contamination remaining at the site from this tank.",19338.0,0.0,JCLAUSS,2018-10-12 11:47:39.540
