42719,03-14-0065,03,14,0065,12465.0,2014-01-22,2014-01-22 15:58:52.347,Capital Credit Market LLC,19203 SE McLoughlin Blvd,GLADSTONE,97027,,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,A 500-gallon waste oil UST was decommissioned by removal from this site in March 2014.  About 150 gallons of product was removed from the UST and about 4 tons of PCS was removed from around the UST.,130762.0,19795.0,KDANA,2014-06-16 14:19:51.973
42720,20-14-0066,20,14,0066,2900.0,2014-01-08,2014-01-24 15:51:07.507,McDonald Industries of OR (former),1041 HWY 99N,EUGENE,97402,(503) 688-7321,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"(MOTT 10/03/17) The site was developed for agricultural use as early as 1936. From the 1950’s through approximately 2009, the site was occupied by a series of heavy equipment sales and service businesses. The site formally used four USTs containing gasoline, diesel, waste oil, and heating oil. The USTs were decommissioned between 1985 and 1989. A discount retail store (Wheeler Dealer) and a permitted cannabis growing center currently operate out of the main site building. Two other buildings are located on the site and are used for storage and/or offices. Between 2007 and 2017, numerous surface and subsurface soil samples have been collected at the site. TPH-D was the only compound detected at a concentration above the applicable RBCs for the site. TPH-D was detected at concentrations above the construction worker ingestion, dermal contact, and inhalation RBC in two locations (GP-4@8’ and HA-1@0.5’). Soil sample GP-4@8’ was collected near the eastern property boundary and soil sample HA-1@0.5’ was collected from a trench drain inside the main site building. Sometime between 2013 and 2017 the trench drain inside the building was filled and covered with concrete. A contaminated media management plan has been prepared to address the remaining soil impacts at these locations. A total of 19 groundwater samples were collected at the site, none of the samples indicated concentrations above the applicable RBCs for the site. The site was issued a NFA in October 2017.",88735.0,0.0,MOTT,2017-10-03 11:27:07.323
42721,03-14-0067,03,14,0067,,2014-01-24,2014-01-27 11:40:39.500,Our Lady of the Lake Parish,840 A AVE,LAKE OSWEGO,97034,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"A 550-gallon diesel UST was decommissioned in-place at this site in January 2014, followed by a 1,000-gallon HOT in April 2014.  An estimated 67 cubic yards of PCS remains around the UST and 9.8 cubic yards remain around the HOT.  Diesel concentrations in both pockets pose a direct contact risk to construction workers, so a CMMP should be followed if work is conducted in these areas.",130773.0,19802.0,KDANA,2014-10-23 12:36:54.640
