42835,31-14-0181,31,14,0181,,2014-02-26,2014-02-26 15:32:00.357,Estate of George Rynearson Farm Tanks,61922 BLACKHAWK TRAIL LN,LA GRANDE,97850,,False,,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,131025.0,0.0,CKENNED,2017-08-03 09:30:05.197
42836,30-14-0182,30,14,0182,6154.0,2014-02-27,2014-02-27 11:59:25.760,PENDLETON GRAIN GROWERS INC,101 ORCHARD AVE,HERMISTON,97838,(541) 276-7611,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,"LUST 30-98-0025, ECSI 3978","Remediation of the site consisted of site and off-site contaminant characterization and contaminant removal through excavation and disposal of approximately 215 tons of petroleum-contaminated soils during decommissioning of underground storage tanks.  Additionally, seven events of enhanced fluids recovery (EFR) removed approximately 2,675 gallons of subsurface liquid; which included free petroleum product, emulsified petroleum product and dissolved petroleum.  Dissolved petroleum contamination exists in groundwater at the site and impacts the right-of-way and adjacent properties to the north and east.  The following tax lots are believed to be within the locality of facility and may be impacted by dissolved contaminants in groundwater: #8900, #9000, #9100, #9200, #9300, #9400, #9500, #9800, #10000, #1400A1, #12600A1. Contaminated groundwater should not be utilized for any beneficial purpose. Dissolved contamination remaining in groundwater requires groundwater not be used for beneficial purposes. Additional cleanup and/or disposal requirements would be needed in the event that unanticipated changes to land or groundwater use occur or if the remaining contamination is disturbed or removed from the ground.

Under Oregon's Risk Based Decision Making process that evaluates exposure pathways for site contaminant concentrations in environmental media, site conditions are currently protective of public health, safety and the environment under Oregon Cleanup Rules for Leaking UST Systems.",11474.0,0.0,DANDERS,2020-07-23 13:02:11.637
