43188,26-14-0533,26,14,0533,3475.0,2014-05-07,2014-05-07 10:01:57.827,CARSON OIL CO INC,1208 SE 8th Ave,PORTLAND,97214,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"The tank pit was ND except one sample showed 64.9 ppm of diesel. 

There were 9 dispensers on site (2)gasoline (7) diesel, none of them had sumps and all of the diesel dispensers leaked and one gas leaked. Diesel range TPH detected beneath dispsensers at concentrations ranging from 367 - 30600 ppm. Gas was 3050 ppm.

In May 2014, Carson Oil dug test pits in the area of the dispensers to determine teh lateral and vertical extent of contamination.  Contamination was found to extend to depths ranging from 11 to 13 feet bgs. Carson subsequently removed approximately 1200 tons of contaminated soil.   Following removal, one sample (ESW1-7') from the east sidewall very close tot he building contained gasoline and diesel at concentrations of 4110 ppm and 4060 ppm respectively.  This sample also contained ethylbenzene at a concentration exceeding occupational worker RBC for vapor intrusion.  A horizontal hand auger sample collected 10 feet east of sample ESW1-7 beneath the building contained gaosline at a concentation of only 34 ppm.  In September 2014, Carson collected a sub-slab soil gas sample as near as possible to sample ESW1-7'.  No detections in the soil-gas sample above reporting limits.  The volume of contaminated soil is limited.  Groundwater was not encountered (JKS 11-28-14).",,"The tank pit was ND except one sample showed 64.9 ppm of diesel. 

There were 9 dispensers on site (2)gasoline (7) diesel, none of them had sumps and all of the diesel dispensers leaked and one gas leaked. Diesel range TPH detected beneath dispsensers at concentrations ranging from 367 - 30600 ppm. Gas was 3050 ppm.

In May 2014, Carson Oil dug test pits in the area of the dispensers to determine teh lateral and vertical extent of contamination.  Contamination was found to extend to depths ranging from 11 to 13 feet bgs. Carson subsequently removed approximately 1200 tons of contaminated soil.   Following removal, one sample (ESW1-7') from the east sidewall very close tot he building contained gasoline and diesel at concentrations of 4110 ppm and 4060 ppm respectively.  This sample also contained ethylbenzene at a concentration exceeding occupational worker RBC for vapor intrusion.  A horizontal hand auger sample collected 10 feet east of sample ESW1-7 beneath the building contained gaosline at a concentation of only 34 ppm.  In September 2014, Carson collected a sub-slab soil gas sample as near as possible to sample ESW1-7'.  No detections in the soil-gas sample above reporting limits.  The volume of contaminated soil is limited.  Groundwater was not encountered (JKS 11-28-14).",8991.0,20276.0,JSCHATZ,2014-11-28 11:57:45.753
