43292,26-14-0637,26,14,0637,7299.0,2014-05-15,2014-05-23 14:31:35.127,Darigold,2720 SE 6th Ave,PORTLAND,97202,206-795-1384,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Petroleum contamination detected as stained soil with petroleum odor that failed a sheen test.  Contamination was observed during a site assessment associated with decommissioning of tank BCKKE, a 12,000 gallon diesel UST in May 2014.  Push-probe borings installed along product piping encountered contamination.  Note that this contamination could conceivably be a result of earlier releases issued log number 26-91-0361 or 26-92-0238, as tank BCKKE may be in the same portion of the facility.
Facility is also calling to report this release, but only one log number needs to be issued.  The former UST was co-located with equipment used for wastewater treatment.  As a result, access to the area is somewhat limited. 
Diesel and gasoline-range TPH were detected in soil collected near the east end of the UST.  In addition, significant concentrations of diesel (7,050 mg/kg and 9,970 mg/kg) were encountered in a product line trench north of the former UST.  A second unknown fiberglass product line was chased from the vcinity of the guard shack toward the fomer UST.  In comments provided by DEQ in August 2014, DEQ requested that soil contamination in the product trenches be further delineated. 
In August 2014, Darigold reported that space restrictions prevent a direct-push probe from accessing the area of the unexpected trench.  In addition, the sub-asphalt gravel is very dense and it is unlikely that a hand auger would be able to penetrate.  Darilgold subsequently attempted to collect soil samples by hand augering into the sidewalls but this was not feasible. They next plan to collect samples by advancing direct-push borings beyond the limits of the trench. 
This facility is adjacent to and hydraulically down-gradient of the former Land O'Lakes LUST facility (26-10-0801).  Recent sampling in an old monitoring well (490 feet) at the Darigold site revealed impact by gasoline TPH.  Darigold plans to decommission this well in the near future.  (JKS 9-23-14)","LUST #26-91-0361, #26-92-0011 & #26-92-0238",,14111.0,20338.0,JSCHATZ,2014-12-03 14:41:31.240
