43523,01-14-0868,01,14,0868,248.0,2014-06-25,2014-07-03 10:21:10.063,SHARON OIL OF BAKER CITY,1706 CAMPBELL ST,BAKER CITY,97814,(541) 523-9993,False,0.0,,0.0,,True,False,False,0.0,False,False,False,False,False,,,,18104.0,0.0,ECLARK,2014-07-03 10:21:10.063
43524,21-14-0869,21,14,0869,9180.0,2014-06-30,2014-07-03 16:07:17.757,NEWPORT MARINA AT SOUTH BEACH,2301 S.E. MARINE SCIENCE DR,NEWPORT,97365,541-867-6657,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"The single wall fiberglass diesel line did not pass the tightness test. The port of Newport hired 4C's Environmental to replace the underground fiberglass lines with double wall flexible pipe.  4C's installed turbine sumps and sump sensors and replaced spill buckets. the cause of the leak was installer error. The diesel line was bent and stressed against a concrete footing, the gas line was chipped, we believe the chip was from a rock in the bedding material.",,"The site consists of a fueling dock, fuel dispenser, a bulkhead, gangway, aboveground piping along the gangway, underground piping to the USTs, and the two USTs, all located on the northern portion of the South Bay Marina.
One gasoline and one diesel 20,000 gallon USTs were installed in 1988 under DEQs UST Facility ID Number 9180.  The facility is used to fuel recreational and commercial boats out of the South Bay Marina. During UST upgrades and fuel line replacement activities in 2014, petroleum contaminated soil (PCS) was discovered creating the DEQ LUST #21-14-0869.
In June 2014 4C's Environmental discovered leaking product lines near the bulkhead.  Using a Vactor truck, 4C's removed 12.95 tons of PCS from the area near the bulkhead.  Follow up sampling reported concentrations of petroleum related hydrocarbons near the bulkhead.
Following excavation of PCS in 2015, the location of the residual PCS is near the base of the bulkhead that supports the gangway and floating dock system.  The cost and effort needed to remove the bulkhead and shutting down the gangway and floating dock system to excavate the residual TPH-d contaminated soil outweighs the need to remove the existing PCS.  The risk of someone coming into direct contact with PCS at 10 feet bgs is unlikely.   However, in case of direct contact with PCS, precautions should be taken to protect workers and their health.",17792.0,20602.0,GDECK,2019-08-16 15:35:36.240
