43739,26-14-1084,26,14,1084,,2014-08-12,2014-08-12 09:50:51.130,"Turner, Maralyn",2144 NE 23rd Ave,PORTLAND,97212,,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"29,000 ppm DX",,,132954.0,20853.0,IGAFFNE,2015-02-26 13:05:05.277
43740,26-14-1085,26,14,1085,,2014-08-11,2014-08-12 15:33:50.210,1710 West Burnside,1710 W BURNSIDE ST,PORTLAND,97209,,False,,,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"In June 2014, during due diligence investigations related to the potential purchase of the property, evidence of soil contamination was found.  The due diligence was reportedly performed on behalf of the buyer by Wohlers Environmental.  As part of this work, soil samples were collected from at least four of six soil borings advanced at the site in the vicinty of a possible former UST cavity.  Gasoline was detected in samples collected from multiple borings at concentrations ranging from 67 mg/kg to a maximum of 1,600 mg/kg in boring DP-4 at a depth of 27 feet bgs.  Concentrations of associated VOCs in the DP-4 sample were relatively low.  Contamination in the area of boring DP-4 extended as deep as 43 feet bgs.  Groundwater was not encountered during the Wohlers investigation.  DEQ was informed by Steve Krueger of Point Source Solutions that his client purchased the property without giving him prior notification.  David Rankin of Kane Environmental reported the release to DEQ on behalf of the seller.  DEQ has not been provided with the full Wohlers report - only excerpts. 
In an email dated 9-17-14, DEQ commented on the implications of the due diligence work performed by Wohlers. (JKS 9-23-14)
