43821,36-14-1166,36,14,1166,,2014-08-21,2014-08-27 16:13:59.073,City of Dundee Fire Station,801 Oregon 99 W (N Hwy 99W),DUNDEE,97115,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"(MOTT 05/02/18) During grading of the new fire station building in August 2014, four empty USTs were discovered west of the new fire station building, along Highway 99. The four USTs were decommissioned and removed from the site. Petroleum impacted soil was observed beneath the USTs and was subsequently excavated. The UST excavation extended to total depth of approximately 15.5 feet bgs. The majority of impacted soil was removed in 2014 during UST removal activities; however, limited soil impacts remain along the western property boundary along Highway 99 at depths ranging from 8 to 14 feet bgs.  Based on results from the numerous soil samples collected at the site, remaining soil impacts appear to be limited in extent. Gasoline related compounds were detected in groundwater at the site near the southern portion of the UST excavation, including along Highway 99. A groundwater sample collected along the west side of Highway 99 did not indicate the presence of any gasoline related compounds suggesting groundwater impacts do not extend west across the road. Groundwater impacts appear to be defined and limited in extent. No compounds were detected above the construction or excavation worker RBCs. The City provides water to the site and surrounding properties. The closest municipal well is located approximately 2,500 feet to the west of the site and the closest private well appears to be located approximately 2,000 feet to the south-southeast of the site. The site was issued a NFA on May 2, 2018.",133122.0,0.0,MOTT,2018-05-03 10:17:10.547
