44139,04-14-1484,04,14,1484,1013.0,2014-10-22,2014-10-29 11:47:46.657,"FOLK, INC. DBA DELS' CHEVRON",1215 S HOLLADAY DR,SEASIDE,97138,503-738-3651,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Lab report indicated 2260 ppm of waste oil at the 4"" riser pipe where oil was removed form the tank.

In October 2015, 4Cs decomissioned and removed at 1,000-gallon waste oil UST on the north side of the property.  The tank was encountered at a depth of 3.5 feet bgs.  Compliance samples collected beneathe the ends of the UST were ND for gaosline, diesel and heavy oil per Method HCID.  A sample of overburden was collected from the top of the UST near the fill port and found to contain 174 ppm of diesel and 2,260 ppm of heavy oil.  Due to the fact the UST formerly contained waste oil, this sample was further analyzed for full-list VOCs, PCBs and TCLP Cadmium, Chromium and Lead.  None were detected.  Additional delieation samples were collected east and west of the former fill port at 6 feet bgs.  Diesl and heavy oil were not detected in the delineation samples. Groundwater was not encountered at any time during the decomissioning and site investigation work.  The pocket of contaminated overburden near the fill port is less than one cubic yard in volume and not considered likely to result in unacceptable risks to site occupant (JKS 10-10-16).",LUST #04-90-0091,,133998.0,21260.0,JSCHATZ,2016-10-11 09:08:12.717
