44174,24-14-1519,24,14,1519,3708.0,2014-10-21,2014-11-06 11:29:55.703,FORMER OIL PROD MT ANGEL CARDLOCK,140 PALMER ST,MOUNT ANGEL,97362,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,1.0,False,False,False,True,False,Stained soil with the odor of petroleum products observed during excavation activities to expose underground storage tanks on the subject property.  Analysis of suspected petroleum contamination is being conducted to identify the types of petroleum hydrocarbons present.  Further excavation activities may reveal the source of the contamination.... Robert Ransdell 10/21/2014.,"LUST 24-14-1733, ECSI # 6042","October 2014 DEQ partnered with Marion County to do an assessment of the facility following bankruptcy of Oil Processors business and the subsequent tax foreclosure. As part of this assessment, DEQ contracted for an assessment following the decommissioning by removal of underground storage tank systems.  During the decommissioning petroleum contamination in soil and groundwater was observed and reported to DEQ. This project includes multiple phase of work:  1. The initial assessment, which included the removal of the underground storage tanks.  2. The expanded assessment, which included installation of groundwater monitoring wells. 3. The issuance of a No Further Action determination for the former cardlock facility (northern tax lot #8700), 4. The historic spill investigation, which includes further off-site assessment (to the south-southeast)  5. Application for use of EPA Site Assessment grant funding,  6. Work plan development, 7. Close coordination with Tribal leaders and State Historical Preservation office for potential cultural discoveries. 8. Evaluation of Threatened and Endangered Species. & 9. Public involvement,  Based on the Report of findings, DEQ has determined that with restrictions to use of the site for residential purposes and no consumptive use of groundwater, petroleum contamination remaining at the site does not pose a threat to human health safety of the environment.",20494.0,21250.0,KROBERT,2016-07-06 08:18:01.097
