44289,26-14-1634,26,14,1634,,2014-12-03,2014-12-03 15:23:56.950,"Stuart, George & Donna",12347 SE Harold St,PORTLAND,97236,,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"The site was sampled 11/18/14 by another vendor and the results were 81.8 ppm oil with a note from the lab (The result for this hydrocarbon range is elevated due to the presence of individual analyte peaks in the quantitation range that are not representative of the fuel pattern reported.) The vendor may have assumed that it did not need to be reported however it is Xavier's opinion that it needs to be reported as a Soil Matrix. Xavier Environmental took soil samples and the lab reported 11/24/14 as Non Detect for diesel, however we are submitting this due to the samples from the initial vendor.",,,0.0,21450.0,MJGILLE,2016-03-21 08:45:59.327
44290,26-14-1635,26,14,1635,12481.0,2014-11-20,2014-12-04 07:23:07.610,Dan Hall's Machine Shop (Former),1831 N Killingsworth St,PORTLAND,97217,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Site historically operated as a service station fro 1925 to the late 1950s and a machine shop from the late 1950s to 1970.  After 1970, the site was operated as an automobile machine shop.

In 2014, a geophysical survey identified five unregistered USTs at the site.  Four were south of the site building near North Killingsworth and one was near the northwest corner of the building.  

In October and November 2014, EVREN advanced borings near the USTs.  Indications of contamination were4 observed near Tank T1 and T2.  Shallow soil near the fill port for T1 (sample SS01-2') contained gasoline (310 mg/kg), diesel (3,200 mg/kg) and heavy oil (21,000 mg/kg) and a release was reported to DEQ in November 2014.

In February 2015, EVREN decommissioned and removed the five USTs.  The highest levels of contamination were observed in the west sidewall of the Tank T1 exavation.  Gasoline (366 mg/kg), diesel (840 mg/kg) and heavy oil (15,000 mg/kg) were detected in sample GS01-T1-W2 at 2 feet bgs.  Lesser detections of petroleum hydrocarbons were detected in soil near Tanks T2 and T5.

Following decommissining, EVREN removed contaminated soil from the excavations to depths ranging from 6.5 to 10.5 feet bgs.  Proximity to the north property boundary and North Campbell Avenue prevened removal of soil in the area of sample GS01-T1-W2.  41 tons of contaminated soil were removed from the site and disposed at Hillsboro landfill. 

The gasoline detection at sample GS01-T1-W2 exceeded the residential/urban residential RBC for vapor intrusion. However, data from post-removal confirmation samples and delineation boring HB01 indicate the pocket of soil is de minimus and unlikely to result in unacceptable risk.  Contamination extends a limited distance beneath N. Campbell Avenue west of the site.  Groundwater not encountered to depth of 11.5 feet bgs.  USGS data indicate groundwater at depths below 100 feet.  (JKS 4-17-15).

Following remediation, approximately 4 cubic yards of contaminted soil remains west of former Tank T1.",,,134246.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2015-04-17 14:44:05.120
