44618,24-14-1733,24,14,1733,3708.0,2014-10-21,2015-02-24 18:23:40.537,MT ANGEL CARDLOCK TL8700,140 PALMER ST (Tax Lot 8700),MOUNT ANGEL,97362,(503) 588-5212,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,1.0,False,False,False,False,False,This new LUST # created 2/24/2015 for Tax Lot 8700 to separate it from LUST # 24-14-1519.,24-14-1519  FORMER OIL PROD MT ANGEL CARDLOCK,"In October 2014 DEQ partnered with Marion County to do an assessment of the Oil Processors facility following bankruptcy of the business and the subsequent tax foreclosure.  DEQ contracted for an assessment of the site following the decommissioning by removal of four underground storage tank systems (including piping and dispensers).  During the decommissioning petroleum contamination in soil was observed and reported to DEQ.  Based on the laboratory results of soil and groundwater samples collected during the site investigation, DEQ has determined that, given the current and reasonably likely future use (commercial) of the site, the low concentrations of petroleum contamination remaining at the site do not pose a threat to human health, safety, welfare or the environment as long as certain conditions are maintained.  The conditions of this no further action determination include no use of groundwater and no residential use.",20494.0,0.0,GDECK,2015-06-15 11:24:17.570
