45169,34-15-0781,34,15,0781,12485.0,2015-06-08,2015-06-09 08:57:16.793,Dental Care Today - Hillsboro,150 SE 3rd Ave,HILLSBORO,97123,,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Gasoline range - 430 ppm. Diesel range - 3100 ppm. Residual range - 9100 ppm. Appears to be a mixed product.

In June 2015, a 545-gallon regulated UST near the southeast corner of the buidling was discovered.  Assessment revealed soil impacted by gasoline (430 mg/kg), diesel (3,100 mg/kg) and heavy oil (9,100 mg/kg) in boring 3 near the south end of the UST.  Following decommissining and removal of the UST, approximately 12.6 tons of contaminated soil was removed from the excavation. Confirmation samples were ND at the limts of the excavation.  
In December 2015, a 675-gallon HOT was encountered during parking lot renovation.  Assessment revealed diesel at concentrations up to 3,400 mg/kg in soil near the ends of the UST.  Following removal, approximately 300 tons of petroleum contaminated soil was removed from the excavation.  Confirmation samples collected at the limits of the excavation did not contain detectable diesel or heavy oil. Groundwater was not encountered to a maximum exploration depth of 11.5 feet bgs.  Site qualifies for closure under the Soil Matrix rules (JKS 4-26-16).",,"Gasoline range - 430 ppm. Diesel range - 3100 ppm. Residual range - 9100 ppm. Appears to be a mixed product.

In June 2015, a 545-gallon regulated UST near the southeast corner of the buidling was discovered.  Assessment revealed soil impacted by gasoline (430 mg/kg), diesel (3,100 mg/kg) and heavy oil (9,100 mg/kg) in boring 3 near the south end of the UST.  Following decommissining and removal of the UST, approximately 12.6 tons of contaminated soil was removed from the excavation. Confirmation samples were ND at the limts of the excavation.  
In December 2015, a 675-gallon HOT was encountered during parking lot renovation.  Assessment revealed diesel at concentrations up to 3,400 mg/kg in soil near the ends of the UST.  Following removal, approximately 300 tons of petroleum contaminated soil was removed from the excavation.  Confirmation samples collected at the limits of the excavation did not contain detectable diesel or heavy oil. Groundwater was not encountered to a maximum exploration depth of 11.5 feet bgs.  Site qualifies for closure under the Soil Matrix rules (JKS 4-26-16).",136282.0,22372.0,JSCHATZ,2016-04-26 09:43:26.413
