45395,17-15-1007,17,15,1007,,2015-07-08,2015-07-20 15:22:00.660,NW Highland LLC,702 NW 6th Street,GRANTS PASS,97526,907-264-6006,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"This is a Regulated site with two USTs that held Heating Oil Fuel for retail use.  Due to age (abandoned in 1970s) and empty of any contents, the tanks do not have to be registered.

9/19/18 Entered FIR date-J.Claussen",,"The site was developed by at least 1936 for use as an automotive repair and/or fueling station. At least two underground storage tanks (USTs) were used at the site to store gasoline and stove/heating oil. Currently the site is used as a radiator repair business. Two 1,000 gallon USTs and about 100 gallons of sludge and water from the tanks were removed from the site in 2015. Contamination appears to be the result of multiple holes in both of the tanks. No soil or groundwater cleanup was conducted at the site. Soil and groundwater contamination remains on the southern portion of the site and extends beneath the neighboring eastern property and beneath the 6th Street right-of-way. The remaining contamination is about eight to twelve feet below ground. All of the neighboring property owners and the Grants Pass Public Works Department were given an opportunity to comment on the proposed site closure. No comments were received. The City of Grants Pass owns a well (JOSE 568) about 150 feet south of the site which was sampled as part of the investigation at this site. While it does not appear the well has been impacted by this release, due to its proximity there is some risk. DEQ has recommended that the city sample the well for gasoline and diesel constituents prior to consumptive use.",136810.0,22538.0,GDECK,2018-12-07 16:39:32.810
