45441,26-15-1053,26,15,1053,,2015-07-27,2015-07-27 11:55:13.900,City of Troutdale UST,123 SW 21st Street,TROUTDALE,97060,503.475.6835,False,7.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"While no field indications of a release were observed during removal of the 12' by 4' tank, analytical results of samples collected beneath each end of the tank showed up to 60 mg/kg of diesel- and up to 524 mg/kg of oil-range hydrocarbons.  Because no holes or other field evidence (visual, PID, etc.) of a release were observed during removal, we suspect the detections are a result of tank scale in the samples.

Soil beneath the west end of the UST had the highest combined concentrations of diesel and heavy oil.  Delineation samples collected at 4.5 feet bgs showed that the pocket was extremely limited in magnitude and extent.  Contamination delineated to Matrix Level II standards. Groundwater was not observed during the decommissioning activities. (JKD 12-2-15)",,"While no field indications of a release were observed during removal of the 12' by 4' tank, analytical results of samples collected beneath each end of the tank showed up to 60 mg/kg of diesel- and up to 524 mg/kg of oil-range hydrocarbons.  Because no holes or other field evidence (visual, PID, etc.) of a release were observed during removal, we suspect the detections are a result of tank scale in the samples.

Soil beneath the west end of the UST had the highest combined concentrations of diesel and heavy oil.  Delineation samples collected at 4.5 feet bgs showed that the pocket was extremely limited in magnitude and extent.  Contamination delineated to Matrix Level II standards. Groundwater was not observed during the decommissioning activities. (JKD 12-2-15)",136893.0,22660.0,JSCHATZ,2015-12-02 08:51:45.443
