24-16-1549  A & R Spada Farms - 1k Gas Tank","The property was developed as a farm by at least 1923 with major commercialization in the 1960s. The site remains a large commercial nursery. The exact cause of contamination is unknown but may be the result of leaks at dispensers or remains from a previous release in the same tank pit (LUST #24-96-4052). Only soil is known to be impacted around the former tank pit. Groundwater is believed to be un-impacted and unlikely to be impacted based on sampling results. The nearest water well on the property was sampled and found to be un-impacted. The USTs were decommissioned by removal and no soil was excavated. The decommissioned USTs were sent to Marion Ag Service of Saint Paul to store water for fire suppression, in accordance with OAR 340-150-0166(1). Four areas of contamination remain around the former tank pit as shown on the attached figure. Remaining contamination is believed to be limited in extent and not more than about 20 cubic yards. The property is assumed to remain a commercial nursery that utilizes multiple onsite wells for irrigation and domestic use.",154089.0,22634.0,CRICHAR,2019-06-18 15:03:18.603
