45543,34-15-1155,34,15,1155,,2015-08-17,2015-08-17 15:52:04.847,Vickers Property,42185 NW Blossom Ln,BANKS,97106,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"42,480 ppm NTE

In August 2015, a 510 gallon diesel UST used to heat a swimming pool was deocommissioned in place. Diesel detected in soil near the north end of the UST. Contamination appears to be localized.  Deeper sample from this location was ND for diesel and heavy oil.  The sample containing the maximum detection of diesel was further analyzed for BTEX and PAHs.  No detections of these at levels of concern.

In December 2015, Soil Solutions advanced two borings in the area of the former UST to further delineate the extent of contamination.  Delineation samples were non-detect for diesel and heavy oil, indicating the pocket was limited in lateral and vertical extent (8 feet bgs).  

The site property is provided with drinking water by the City of Banks.  A use survey confirmed that water wells are present at properties in the vicinity of the site.  Based on information in WRD well logs, groundwater is located at a minimum depth of 80 feet bgs.  Based on the small footprint of the contamination pocket, limited depth and depth to groundwater. shallow soil contamination is unlikely to impact deeper producing aquifers. (JKS 2-23-16).",,"2,480 ppm NTE

In August 2015, a 510 gallon diesel UST used to heat a swimming pool was deocommissioned in place. Diesel detectedin soil near the north end of the UST. Contamination appears to be localized.  Deeper sample from this location was ND for diesel and heavy oil.  The sample containing the maximum detection of diesel was further analyzed for BTEX and PAHs.  No detections of these at levels of concern.

In December 2015, Soil Solutions advanced two borings in the area of the former UST to further delineate the extent of contamination.  Delineation samples were non-detect for diesel and heavy oil, indicating the pocket was limited in lateral and vertical extent (8 feet bgs).  

The site property is provided with drinking water by the City of Banks.  A use survey confirmed that water wells are present at properties in the vicinity of the site.  Based on information in WRD well logs, groundwater is located at a minimum depth of 80 feet bgs.  Based on the small footprint of the contamination pocket, limited depth and depth to groundwater. shallow soil contamination is unlikely to impact deeper producing aquifers. (JKS 2-23-16).",137089.0,22759.0,JSCHATZ,2016-02-23 15:57:44.657
