45621,20-15-1233,20,15,1233,12491.0,2015-07-22,2015-09-02 15:56:30.290,WEEE Acquisition #B3-096 /JOHN KHASFEDAI,904 W 6TH AVE,EUGENE,97402,(541)  513-1650,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Although new UST facility #12491 has the name of JOHN KHASFEDAI, we're going with the LUST name as submitted: WEEE Aquisition #B3-096,,, gdeck 9/23/15.",(10/31/17 MOTT) LTD not liable for remedial action costs under ORS 465.255(3)(a) since aquired property by eminent domain. Mr. John Khastedai is considered the RP.,"(MOTT 10/31/16) In July 2015, three USTs were removed from the site along with approximately 121 tons of soil. The excavation reached a total depth of approximately 12 feet and no groundwater was encountered. A total of 14 soil samples were collected, six of which indicated the presence gasoline. The highest TPH-G concentration (1,440mg/kg) was detected from beneath the USTs.  Impacted soil below 7 feet along the northern and western property boundaries and beneath the USTs was left in place due to site constraints which prohibited removal. Soil concentrations at the site exceed the Occupational Leaching to Groundwater RBC for TPH-G. (MOTT 06/02/17) In February 2017, two additional soil samples and one groundwater sample were collected at the site. TPH-G was detected above the construction worker RBC in one soil sample at a depth of 14 feet. Elevated concentrations of TPH-G and VOCs were detected in the groundwater sample.  Additional groundwater investigation/delineation is needed at the site; however, further work is currently on hold until the soil removal and supplemental investigation and the Astro #207 facility to the north is completed.",136722.0,0.0,MOTT,2017-10-31 14:28:16.180
