45770,21-15-1382,21,15,1382,,2015-09-21,2015-09-30 15:00:21.033,G&G Investments,2614 SE HIGHWAY 101,LINCOLN CITY,97367,,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"The tank was a 500 gallon metal tank and contained approximately 170 gallons of water at the time of decommissioning.  The tank had reportedly been out of service since before 1974.  Based upon the odor and piping configuration, K&S concluded that the tank was a former gasoline UST used to fuel vehicles from a former business(es) at the site.  One sample collected beneath the tank contained 110 ppm gas TPH and the other sample collected beneath the tank was ND.  Bill Knutson 9/30/2015",,,137619.0,22954.0,AGARCIA,2015-11-18 16:28:42.627
45771,20-15-1383,20,15,1383,3525.0,2015-09-28,2015-09-30 15:46:30.443,6th and Oak Parking,85 E 6th Avenue,EUGENE,97401,,False,7.0,,3.0,,True,False,False,3.0,False,False,False,False,False,"Low level of gasoline (0.152 mg/kg) detected in soil beneath north end of out-of-use 1,000-gallon UST.  No detectable levels of petroleum-range hydrocarbons identified in sample from south end of tank.... Mike Golden(PBS Engineering) 9/28/2015.  
UST will be registered....g deck 9/30/2015

Administratively closed 12/22/2015 (C. Rodda)",(C. Rodda 12/21/2015) see UST facility #3525 for addtl information.,"Two tanks were historically used for storing gasoline (1,000-gallon tank) and an unknown petroleum product (800-gallon tank) for the County’s fleet services. The tanks had not been used since at least 1991 when four other USTs were removed from the property. The two tanks were decommissioned by removal in September 2015. Each tank contained fill and sludge materials. Piping associated with the tank system was also removed Groundwater was not encountered during decommissioning and assessment work at the site. Confirmation soil samples were collected from beneath the tank cavity and piping. Gasoline was detected at 0.152 parts per million (ppm), below method reporting limits and DEQ “Soil Matrix” cleanup standards. Some gasoline constituents were also detected at low concentrations, and a petroleum release was reported to DEQ. All contaminants detected in soil sample T1-BN were below risk-based concentrations for receptors related to multi-family housing and commercial operations.",20356.0,0.0,CRODDA,2015-12-28 13:19:04.577
