45936,24-15-1548,24,15,1548,,2015-10-16,2015-11-04 13:14:26.980,Los Baez Restaurant,2920-2960 Commercial St SE,SALEM,97302,503-580-1756,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Release reported by representative of potential buyer who hired the consultant to do a phase II assessment.  Not hired by RP.  No info on a tank; just lab results of gas.  Therefore, calling this regulated until informed otherwise....gdeck 10/16/2015",,"From 1950 to approximately 1975, a gasoline station operated at the property and there was a commercial restaurant present. In 1975, both of those operations ceased and the present-day restaurant was constructed.  Historical records indicate there were four underground storage tanks (USTs) associated with the gasoline station operation, which have all been removed.  

Petroleum releases occurred from the gasoline containing leaking underground storage tanks.  Site assessments completed in 2015 and 2019 reported low levels of petroleum contamination remains beneath the site in soil and groundwater.  Soil contamination is limited to the site and the approximate areal extent of groundwater contamination appears to be limited to the parking lot of the subject property and the parking lot to the east.  See the Staff Memorandum in Web docs for figures.  The concentrations of remaining petroleum contamination in soil and shallow groundwater are below DEQ’s Risk Based Concentrations if the property remains in commercial use, and groundwater is not used for drinking water.

Following evaluation of sample results for soil, groundwater and soil gas, and considering the potential land and water use in the area, acceptable risk levels are not exceeded, and DEQ is issuing a No Further Action determination for this site.",138634.0,0.0,AFARRIS,2020-12-18 08:27:34.703
45937,20-15-1549,20,15,1549,,2015-10-21,2015-11-04 13:46:42.680,Cherie Babinec,28992 Summerville Rd,EUGENE,97405,541-868-6252,False,7.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Removed 1000-gal. farm-use tank.  Cleanup has begun.  -- Robert Despain 10/21/2015.

(CAR 7/8/16)Following excavation the pit bottom was ND and the bottom of the side walls were <10ppm.  Groundwater was not encountered.  I do not suspect GW to be contaminated.  They jackhammered out sandstone in the bottom of the pit and over time I would suspect the smear zone water to have transported some gasoline down which wasnt detected.",,"A 1,000 gallon gasoline tank was removed in October 2015.  Initial soil samples showed gasoline concentration in soil at 394 ppm (7' below ground surface).  Approximately 24 tons of soil was excavated and sent to the Coffin-Butte Landfill for disposal.  Confirmation samples from the bottom of the pit (12'6"" below ground surface) were below laboratory detection limits.  Confimration samples collected from the base of the excavation walls were all below 10 ppm.  Groundwater was never encountered and all confirmation samples are below the soil matrix cleanup standards.",143022.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2016-12-20 13:10:34.193
