46039,10-15-1651,10,15,1651,3467.0,2015-11-25,2015-11-30 14:56:49.300,BUY 2 @ CANYONVILLE,211 W 5TH,CANYONVILLE,97417,541-344-5983,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Jim Dirksen - 541-672-1667

Not sure at this time if this is an active system release or the exact source. RP says it could be other facilities nearby (offsite Shell might be upgradient; also historic onsite auto repair)... Lon Yandell at Geodesign, 11/25/2015.

Site address originally reported as 211 W 5th.  Updated to 211 SW 5th St. ... 3/3/20 gdeck",10-20-0183 Buy 2 @ Canyonville II,"Historically the site was a fueling station and automotive repair facility with three service bays and in-ground hydraulic lifts.
Soil and groundwater on the site are contaminated with petroleum products.
The cause of soil contamination is believed to be associated with the historic automotive repair facility.  Groundwater contamination is believed to be a result of the on-site soil contamination as well as groundwater flow from the up-gradient fueling station (LUST# 10-90-0093).
Four monitoring wells were installed on site as part of the site investigation.  Two rounds of groundwater samples were collected along with soil samples at the time of monitoring well installation.
All contamination on the site remains in place because the levels detected are below DEQ risk-based concentrations and does not pose a threat to human health or the environment, assuming continued commercial zoning and land use.
The property is expected to remain zoned C-3 (commercial highway related).  The City of Canyonville is expected to continue to supply water to all properties in the vicinity of the site.
Public notice was given to surrounding properties in the down-gradient direction and the City of Roseburg.  No substantive comments were received within the comment period.
Contaminated soil and groundwater are limited to the site and are not believed to extend beyond the boundaries of the property.",14679.0,0.0,GDECK,2020-03-03 16:18:39.580
