46062,26-15-1674,26,15,1674,3859.0,2015-12-03,2015-12-03 17:31:03.507,Comfort Auto,2653 NE MLK Jr. Blvd,PORTLAND,97212,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,,,"USTs from a former service station were removed from the site in 1987.  An investigation beginning in November 2015 identified gasoline and heavy oils in the soil in the northeast quarter of the site.  The gasoline appeared to extend beneath roadways to the north and east of the site.  Gasoline was also detected in on-site soil gas samples.  Gasoline and diesel were detected in sub-slab vapor samples south of the former UST pit.  The contamination does not present an unacceptable risk to current occupants of the site, or to future construction and excavation workers, but could pose a risk if the site is redeveloped for urban residential use.  A deed restriction was placed on the property prohibiting residential redevelopment unless additional actions are taken to mitigate the risks.  No further actions are necessary if the site remains in commercial use.",20590.0,0.0,KDANA,2017-05-02 09:46:00.767
