46150,26-15-1762,26,15,1762,,2015-12-22,2015-12-22 09:41:30.647,"Kohne, Cornelia",9148 SE Ankeny St,PORTLAND,97216,,False,0.0,,0.0,,False,True,False,0.0,False,False,False,False,False,,,,138506.0,23388.0,MJGILLE,2015-12-22 09:41:30.647
46151,03-15-1763,03,15,1763,,2015-12-22,2015-12-22 15:30:25.510,140 A Avenue,140 A Avenue,LAKE OSWEGO,97034,,False,7.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"In December 2015 during excavation related to construction at the site, three USTs were discovered in a common excavation near the east property boundary.  The tanks were found to contain a small amount of emulsified gasoline but primarily water.  Following decommissioning and removal, sampling near the ends of the USTs revealed gasoline at concentrations ranging from 103 mg/kg to 9,830 mg/kg.  Subsequently, as part of constructions, soil was removed across the site to a uniform depth of 25 feet bgs to faciliate construction of a parking garage.  Confirmation sampling beneath the west UST showed that contamination attenuated by a depth of 9 feet bgs, while contamination beneath the center and east USTs extended as far as 23 feet bgs.  Once the maximum soil removal depht was reached (25 feet bgs), sampling beneath the former center and east USTs did not reveal detectable levels of gasoline.  Based on the excavation depth, all soil associated with the former USTs has been removed.  Groundwater was not encountered at any time during the UST decommissioning and soil removal activities. (JKS 7-6-16).",,"In December 2015 during excavation related to construction at the site, three USTs were discovered in a common excavation near the east property boundary.  The tanks were found to contain a small amount of emulsified gasoline but primarily water.  Following decommissioning and removal, sampling near the ends of the USTs revealed gasoline at concentrations ranging from 103 mg/kg to 9,830 mg/kg.  Subsequently, as part of constructions, soil was removed across the site to a uniform depth of 25 feet bgs to faciliate construction of a parking garage.  Confirmation sampling beneath the west UST showed that contamination attenuated by a depth of 9 feet bgs, while contamination beneath the center and east USTs extended as far as 23 feet bgs.  Once the maximum soil removal depht was reached (25 feet bgs), sampling beneath the former center and east USTs did not reveal detectable levels of gasoline.  Based on the excavation depth, all soil associated with the former USTs has been removed.  Approximately 613 tons of contaminated soil was segregated, managed accordingly and disposed at Hillsboro Landfill.  Groundwater was not encountered at any time during the UST decommissioning and soil removal activities. (JKS 7-6-16).",65726.0,23392.0,JSCHATZ,2016-07-06 10:41:36.973
