46189,26-16-0001,26,16,0001,,2016-01-07,2016-01-07 17:22:17.100,JE Morrison Trust,25 NE 122ND AVE,PORTLAND,97230,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"The site includes three contiguous properties (Tax Lots 7800, 7900 and 8900).  The eastermost property (8900) was occupied by a retail fueling and service station from 1955 to the mid-1980s. The central property (7900) was developed with two buildings by 1955 but were demolished by 1990.  The west property (7800) has historically remained undeveloped. 
Geophysical surveys in 2008 and 2015 identified features associated with the former service station and a possible HOT on the south side of the former southern building on Tax Lot 7900.
In December 2015 Wohlers advanced borings on Tax Lot 8900 to evaluate if there were indications of contamination.  One soil sample collected at 18 feet bgs in the western portion of the former UST cavity contained gasoline at a concentration (350 ppm) exceeding urban residential RBCs for the vapor intrusion pathway.  However, levels of VOCs, PAHs and lead deteced in this sample did not exceed any applicable RBCs.   Samples from the same boring collected at 15 and 19 feet bgs did not contain detectable levels of petroleum hydrocarbons. The delineation data suggest that contamination deteted at boring DP-1 is not laterally or vertically extensive.  There were no detections in any of 18 other samples collected from the site. 
Groundwater is expected to be at a depth of 119 feet bgs and is not used as a source of drinking wate in the area of the site. 
Based on the depth of contamination, limited size and volume of pocket and lack of VOCs, DEQ does not believe this one detection poses unacceptable risks to future residents or employees. (JKS 4-7-16)",,,138668.0,0.0,JSCHATZ,2016-04-07 13:05:44.380
