File moved to Salem as Regulated tank - used as ""backup"" for blower for drying food... gdeck 1/21/2016",,"A 10,000 gallon fuel oil was reportedly removed in 1986 and backfilled with pea gravel to approximately 12 feet below ground.  A site assessment in 2015 rediscovered the tank pit and a limited Phase II investigation was performed.  •    During the tank decommissioning contaminated soil appears to have been excavated and backfilled with pea gravel to a depth of twelve feet.  Soil sample results indicate a thin layer of contamination exists at the bottom of the excavation. Soil concentrations exceed leaching to groundwater concentrations in one sample but were non-detect in another sample collected directly below the exceedance. The site is currently and expected to remain a commercial/industrial area that is connected to a municipal water supply.  Based on the available information, Kerr Concentrates is currently protective of public health and the environment.",138698.0,23449.0,CRICHAR,2017-01-18 09:52:21.373
