46302,20-16-0114,20,16,0114,,2016-02-03,2016-02-03 14:31:56.970,Littman Family Trust,3625 Glen Oak Dr,EUGENE,97405,510-504-2857,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Tank was removed and obvious soil contamination was encountered. Holes in tank. No Groundwater was encountered in the excavation.,,,138965.0,23549.0,MJGILLE,2016-05-24 10:25:11.467
46305,27-16-0117,27,16,0117,12499.0,2016-01-22,2016-02-05 15:06:53.670,Plaid Pantry / AZBAC Investments LLC,1089 EDGEWATER ST NW,SALEM,97304,(360) 574-3399,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"Four USTs (two 7,000-gallon gasoline, one 675-gallon heating oil, and one 340-gallon waste oil) were removed from the site in 2015. Approximately 31 tons of impacted soil was removed and transported offsite for disposal. Confirmation soil samples were collected from the bottom and walls of each excavation area. No Groundwater was encountered. All the confirmation soil samples indicated concentrations below the applicable soil matrix levels for the site. A NFA was issued on 12/14/2016.",137534.0,0.0,GDECK,2017-01-24 11:49:31.020
46306,21-16-0118,21,16,0118,8566.0,2016-01-22,2016-02-05 15:54:05.060,BEVENS MARKET & DELI,960 SW COAST HWY,NEWPORT,97365,(425) 681-1353,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,"THE TANK HAD 2 VISIBLE HOLES IN THE BOTTOM. IT APPEARED THE TANK HAD BEEN SCRATCHED AND THE COATING REMOVED EXPOSING THE BARE STEEL. THIS MOST LIKELY OCCURRED DURING THE INSTALLATION OF THE TANK.
SINGLE WALL FIBERGLASS WAS THE PIPING MATERIAL. CONTAMINATION FOUND UNDER PIPING NEAR THE DISPENSERS. APPEARS THE PIPE WAS LEAKING AT A FITTING.  ... Casey Michaels 1/22/16.",,"(MOTT 11/7/16) In January 2016, two 10,000-gallon gasoline and one 6,000-gallon diesel USTs were removed from the site. A hole was observed in one of the gasoline tanks and contamination was present in the soil and groundwater. The contaminated soil was excavated and transported offsite for disposal. A total of 422.28 tons of PCS was removed from tank pit and piping trench. New tanks (one 12,000-gallon gasoline, one 5,000-gallon gasoline, and one 5,000-gallon diesel) and piping were installed in same location. Four confirmation soil samples were collected from the bottom of the UST excavation. All four were ND for TPH-G, TPH-D, and TPH-O. The sidewalls of the excavation could not be sampled due to the shoring (excavation had to be shored due to sand). Water from the tank pit was pumped and treated onsite then discharged to the city system.  Eleven soil samples and eight groundwater samples were collected at the site following the excavation. In soil, the highest TPH-G concentration was 359ppm and the highest TPH-D concentration was 9,130ppm both from DB-1 @ 5-6’. In groundwater, the highest TPH-D concentration was 315ppb from B-4 located along the property boundary and downgradient of the USTs. TPH-G, TPH-O, BTEX, and PAHs were not detected in any of the groundwater samples. (MOTT 04/28/17) The site was issued a NFA on April 28, 2017",117387.0,0.0,MOTT,2017-04-28 12:23:49.670
