46325,34-16-0137,34,16,0137,11153.0,2016-02-08,2016-02-09 13:36:27.247,CARSON OIL COMPANY,4905 SW WESTERN AVE,BEAVERTON,97005,(503) 224-8500,False,4.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"CONTAMINATION WAS ENCOUNTERED WHEN REPLACING A GASOLINE SPILL BUCKET. THE CONCRETE WAS CUT TO REMOVE THE EXISTING SPILL BUCKET THAT HAD FAILED. 
SAMPLE B1 WAS COLLECTED BELOW BUCKET AND CONTAINED 5540 PPM GASOLINE.
AN AIR VACUUM VACTOR TRUCK WAS UTILIZED TO REMOVE THE CONTAMINATION DOWN TO THE TOP THE TANK. THREE SAMPLES WERE COLLECTED FROM THE WALLS AND A NEW SPILL BUCKET WAS REPLACED ON TOP THE TANK.
B2 = 1790 PPM GX
B3 = 272 PPM GX
B4 = 972 PPM GX

I spoke with Tim O’Gara with 4C’s today about the investigations at this site.   A gasoline release was found in association with a spill bucket.   Soil and gw sampling points were installed, but the full extent of gasoline contamination was not identified.  Diesel contamination was also noted in many monitoring points with no indication of what the source was.  A comprehensive subsurface investigation will need to be performed here to determine the source(s) of contamination and assess the risk to groundwater, soils and indoor and outdoor air.  8/29/18, Ash Desmond",LUST #34-92-0300,,3383.0,0.0,ADESMON,2020-10-13 16:41:24.100
