46397,26-16-0209,26,16,0209,,2016-02-24,2016-02-25 12:11:35.697,"Burger, Peter",4909 NE Alameda St,PORTLAND,97213,,False,2.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,9230 ppm north tank end,,,139159.0,23644.0,DGRANGE,2016-08-10 15:11:50.303
46398,24-16-0210,24,16,0210,2380.0,2016-02-11,2016-02-25 16:58:19.947,FORMER HONDA OF SALEM,686 COMMERCIAL ST NE,SALEM,97301,(971) 273-4341,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,"Salem First Baptist Church, ECSI 6161 - adjacent property","(MOTT 07/14/17) The site was formally used as an automobile dealership and auto repair facility which used one 1,000-gallon waste oil UST and one 5,000-gallon gasoline UST. The waste oil UST was removed from the site in 1998 and the 5,000-gallon gasoline UST was removed from the site in 2015.  TPH-G, TPH-O, PAHs, PCBs, and metals were detected in soil samples collected from 9 to 16 feet bgs in close proximity to the former waste oil UST (north side of building). No soil impacts were identified near the former 5,000-gallon gasoline UST (east side of building).  Although impacted soil remains near the former waster oil UST, contaminant concentrations are within the applicable RBCs or the accepted background metal values with the exception of TPH-G in one soil sample (B16@13-14’), which was above the urban residential vapor intrusion into buildings RBC. Soil gas samples collected from beneath the building slab did not indicate vapors above the urban residential soil gas RBCs. Arsenic, chromium, and lead were detected in groundwater; however, the City of Salem provides domestic water to the site and surrounding properties. A Contaminated Media Management Plan (CMMP) was prepared for the site and adjacent property to the east (Salem First Baptist Church, ECSI 6161) to help manage any impacted soil that may be encountered during future subsurface work at the site. (MOTT 11/3/17) The site was issued a NFA on November 3, 2017.",19590.0,0.0,MOTT,2017-11-03 08:47:20.253
