46440,24-16-0252,24,16,0252,12578.0,2016-03-02,2016-03-04 16:22:09.743,Industrial Property,2801 Valpak Road NE,SALEM,97301,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"3/5/18 CAR - During excavation of contaminated soil a cubic tank was discovered and is reported to contain gasoline/kerosine.  The tank will be registered and permitted. A previous soil boring showed the highest concentrations of gas next to the location of this tank.  The discovered tank appears to be the source of the gasoline contamination. Reported by Steve Omo of BBA.

Gasoline contamination was discovered at 2801 / 2803 NE Valpak Rd, during an investigation of an old bunker tank at 2805 NE Valpak Rd.  The source of the gasoline appears to be the north side of the buildings of 2801 / 2803 NE Valpak Rd.  Historical Sanborn maps make note of ""gas tank"" and ""gas pump"" in this area.  Geophysical work may be necessary to identify former UST Cavity location. ... Randy Boese, 3/2/2016

31-may-18 (Esc) - UST was discovered and decommissioned by removal with some spillage of tank contents on 5-March, Stephen Omo (BB&A) also indicated that bacteria and carbon (BOS?) were added to the open excavation to enhance natural attenuation, this LUST should be linked to UST #12578",LUST 24-15-1741 (State Investments) for HOT decommissioning. Ingrid Gaffney has sent HOT file to Salem office; both will be addressed under CRA for LUST#24-16-0252 and closed under one NFA letter.,"The Valpak Road site is composed of two tax lots located in an industrial use area of Salem. Two releases occurred at the subject property and were separately reported: one associated with a former heating oil tank (LUST 24-15-1741) and the second related to a historical gasoline underground storage tank (LUST 24-16-0252). Contamination remains in portions of the site that are below acceptable risk levels for general industrial property use. Gasoline, diesel, and oil and its constituents are located in soil and groundwater from approximately 8 to 20 feet. Restrictions to groundwater and residential use are in place through an EES filed with Marion County.",149587.0,23672.0,ACHAVEZ,2020-09-23 17:07:43.580
