46503,29-16-0315,29,16,0315,1511.0,2016-03-16,2016-03-16 14:37:34.630,BAYSIDE GARDENS SHELL & GROCERY,36453 HIGHWAY 101 N,NEHALEM,97131,503-842-2172,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Samples were collected when a modification was being completed at the fueling system. New piping, spill buckets, and sumps were being installed. Diesel was detected at 214 ppm at Sample B3. Sample B3 was collected below the piping at the diesel tank. The diesel tank was safe suction. There was no was visual staining or odor present in the soil.",,,0.0,23753.0,ADESMON,2020-10-13 16:39:22.873
46504,27-16-0316,27,16,0316,12508.0,2016-03-09,2016-03-16 16:28:58.580,GOODWILL INDUSTRIES,225 WALLACE RD NW,SALEM,97304,(503) 963-3200,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Discovered tank decommissioned 3/1/2016.... gdeck

Four tanks were removed fromt he property.  In one conversation with Tim OGara he mentioned there is likely a tank under the sidewalk.  In other conversations and in the Additional Drilling Report he says there is probably a tank in the middle of the road that is causing contamination.",,"In February of 2016, during demolition and construction activities four USTs were located.  One tank was 1,000 gal, two tanks were 6,000 gal and one tank was 8,000 gal. Three of the tanks had been abandonded in place with sand.  Before abandoning not all of the product was removed fromt he tanks.  A total of 3,400 gallons of liquid were removed fromt he tanks and recycled.  A total of 2184 tons of potenitally contaminated soil was removed fromt he site and disposed of at the River Bend Landfill.

Investigation of contamination included six soil samples from the tank pit excavation, the installation of twelve soil borings, and nine temporary monitoring wells.

Sample results indicate that contamination is present onsite and extending across Wallace Rd onto the Salem Tent and Awning property.  Contamination present does not exceed the applicable risk based screening levels and does not present unacceptable risk to human health.",139162.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2017-01-24 16:18:30.280
