46811,24-16-0623,24,16,0623,,2016-05-06,2016-05-17 11:25:35.300,Hammersly Property,22235 Butteville Rd NE,AURORA,97002,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"gasoline,diesel and oil detection.  The tank was an out of service unregulated tank approximately 700 gallons.  I would imagine that It was used for farm use at one point in time but per the owner, the tank has been out of service for at least 70 years.... Nick Thornton, Ecotech, LLC, 5/17/2016.",,"The site has historically been used as a private residence and small farm. The contamination was caused by a leak from a 700-gallon farm use diesel tank. An estimated ten cubic yard of soil is contaminated on the site.  Groundwater was not encountered during field work and the residential well was sampled and had no detections of petroleum. The tank was drained, triple rinsed, and filled in place with concrete slurry. Soil samples were collected from around and below the tank to delineate contamination. All contaminated soil, approximately ten cubic yards, remains on site below the tank and below surface soils. The property is expected to remain a rural residence that is connected to the onsite drinking water well which is cased to 145 feet below ground and sealed to 18 feet below ground. Only soils on site are believed to be contaminated within approximately five feet of the bottom half of the tank.",140261.0,24027.0,GDECK,2017-04-19 11:09:52.250
