46815,02-16-0627,02,16,0627,12563.0,2016-05-09,2016-05-17 15:59:51.073,Nusbaum Property,1348 MAIN ST,PHILOMATH,97370,541-929-3805,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"FORMER SERVICE STATION.  THREE (3) USTs WERE REPORTEDLY DECOMMISSIONED IN-PLACE IN THE 1980's, BY FILLING WITH SAND. SITE ASSESSMENT AND SUBSEQUENT LAB ANALYSIS IDENTIFIED GASOLINE-RELATED CONTAMINATION (DETECTED DIESEL WAS IDENTIFIED BY THE LAB AS OVERLAP FROM DEGRADEDGASOLINE)....

RP requested de-assignment on 1/12/17, RP says they cannot afford cleanup at this time. Do not charge to Q-time.

(MOTT 6/5/18) Site contact is Kim Brown 541-630-1004, kimnnbubba@gmail.com. Kim is handeling all site issues for the Nusbaums.",,"A Phase I and II were completed by the City of Philomath for the property in May 2016. The City was interested in redeveloping the property. Six soil borings were advanced at the site and five water samples were collected. Ethylbenznee and 1,2,4-trimethylbenzene were detected in soil samples at concentrations above the RBCs. Various compounds were detected in the groundwater samples at concentrations above the Occupational Ingestion and Inhalation RBCs and TPH-gasoline was reported at a concentration exceeding the Construction and Excavation Worker RBC in two of the groundwater sampling locations. Additionally, lead concentrations above the RBC were observed in soil samples collected along the eastern property boundary.",140271.0,24038.0,CRICHAR,2019-09-10 17:01:49.570
