8/2016:  Need some additional monitoring wells, 2 installed so far.  One other monitoring well exists on property north of subject property, which is being used for my Niemi Svenson site (04-00-0856, which is located just east of Hunt's).  The MW is MW-10.  I will suggest they get access to sample it.  Only on sample event from that well by Niemi, but is still there.  So far in soil: Vi for B and E.  TPH-Gx fails GW in Exc. 

ECI reports a suspected UST based on the geophysical survey conducted in June 2015 (under Envitech).  Field work by ECI was april 14, reported may 25.,  Please confirm that a UST is present and to what extent it was decommissioned in-place.   (RAH)

--
Envirotech identified petroleum-contaminated soil and groundwater in the vicinity of a gasoline UST following recommendations made in a Phase I ESA prepared for the property. Envirotech recommended additional subsurface investigation in order to verify the lateral and vertical extend of contamination. 

On April 14, 2015, EcoCon, Inc. (ECI) completed a Phase II ESA and collected five (5) soil samples and two (2)groundwater samples in the vicinity of the above mentioned UST. The soil and groundwater samples analyzed were reported in excess of their respective laboratory method reporting limit and/ or Oregon DEQ RBCs. ECI has recommended an additional ESA at the property.",,,140388.0,24137.0,RHOOD,2017-08-11 11:07:54.990
