46869,36-16-0681,36,16,0681,12513.0,2016-05-31,2016-05-31 13:45:37.230,Jackson Family Wines,3500 NE Three Mile Lane,MCMINNVILLE,97128,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,(MOTT) Release was origianlly reported with an address of 3500 SE Armory Way but the site address is actually 3500 NE Three Mile Lane,,"(MOTT 04/30/18) One 1,000-gallon waste oil UST was located at the southwest corner of the northern most building. Used oil from a mechanic pit inside the building would drain into the tank via a pipe that ran underneath the building. Additionally, water from a wash pad along the south side of the building drained into a catch basin which drained to an oil/water separator located above the southern end of the UST. Oil from the oil/water separator would also drain into this UST.  In 2016, the UST and oil/water separator were removed from the site and the mechanic pit inside the building was filled and covered with concrete. The wash pad was also removed and the catch basins were cleaned and connected to the City’s stormwater system. A total of six confirmation soil samples were collected from the tank pit. All the soil samples indicated concentrations below the applicable RBCs for the site.  Three soil samples were also collected from beneath the piping that ran from the mechanic bay inside the building to the UST. The three soil samples collected from beneath the piping were non-detect for TPH-G, TPH-D, and TPH-O.  Groundwater was encountered at approximately 12 feet in the UST excavation; however, no groundwater samples were collected.  In December 2017, a total of six grab groundwater samples were collected from in and around the former UST area. Petroleum compounds were detected in three of the six groundwater samples but at concentrations below the applicable RBCs for the site. Water is supplied to the site by McMinnville Water & Light. (MOTT 08/26/18) The site was issued a NFA on August 21, 2018.",140304.0,0.0,MOTT,2018-08-26 10:57:02.790
