46968,26-16-0780,26,16,0780,,2016-06-20,2016-06-20 15:17:43.370,"Hoch, Bridget",13624 SE Clay St,PORTLAND,97233,503-261-0109,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,140662.0,24249.0,DGRANGE,2016-08-02 09:58:00.707
46969,15-16-0781,15,16,0781,7331.0,2016-06-18,2016-06-20 16:56:53.473,Whites Midway Service,15 W Vilas Rd,CENTRAL POINT,97502,541-840-8853,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"From approximately 1950 to 1981 the site was used as an automobile fueling, repair, and maintenance facility which utilized two 3,000-gallon and one 6,000-gallon gasoline underground storage tanks (USTs). The USTs were emptied and filled with sand in 1981 and the fueling dispensers were removed in 1990. The exact cause of the release is unknown. All three USTs and dispensers were in close proximity which further complicates determining the exact cause of the release. Soil and groundwater are impacted in the northeast corner of the property and extending approximately 10 feet beneath the Table Rock Road right of way. Approximately 306 tons of soil was excavated and disposed of at Dry Creek Landfill. Four injections of microbes, nutrients, and hydrogen peroxide were completed in the former tank pit to reduce petroleum concentrations. Impacted soil and groundwater remain from approximately 9.5 to 18 feet below ground in the northeast corner of the property and extending slightly into the Table Rock Road right of way. In the impacted area, the property is expected to remain commercial and will be connected to the municipal water system. An opportunity to comment on the proposed closure was given to the neighbors and the public through letters, notices, and newspaper ads. No Comments were received. On March 19, 2019an easement and equitable servitudes document was recorded on the property that: prohibits groundwater use, requires engineering vapor barriers for future construction, and a Contaminated Media Management Plan must be followed during subsurface work in the impacted area.",154116.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2019-04-02 16:35:27.027
