47020,29-16-0831,29,16,0831,12525.0,2016-06-28,2016-06-29 10:17:22.577,Former Napa Auto Parts,114 IVY AVE,TILLAMOOK,97141,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,3.0,False,False,False,False,False,"RWA, 7/11/16 - Site discovery occurred following a request from the site owner to conduct Phase II sampling for a property redevelopment loan.  The presence of tanks and former site use as a gas station was not known until the end of June, when the release was reported to DEQ.  Additional assessment is planned using EPA Brownfield assessment funds.

RWA 12/12/2016 - Site Closure report submitted and approved by DEQ, December 12, 2016. Report includes Contaminated Media Management Plan as site development is expected within the building footprint in an area where elevated soil vapor (below applicable RBCs) were found.",,"The property received assistance from the EPA Tillamook County Salmonberry Corridor Brownfield Assessment grant to conduct a Phase II investigation associated three, underground storage tanks (USTs). A gas station operated on the property from the 1940s to 1950s. Soil, groundwater, and soil vapor samples collected in the summer of 2016 showed a release of petroleum. 
In September, 2016, the tanks were decommissioned by removal, and soil and groundwater samples were collected from the former tank nest and from locations up and downgradient from the tanks. 
Petroleum and petroleum constituents, including metals, were found at concentrations below applicable risk-based concentrations in the former tank nest. No contamination was found downgradient of the former tanks location.
A contaminated media management plan (CMMP) is included in the closure documentation for the site. DEQ issued the NFA determination in December 2016. The brewery tasting room was constructed over the former tank nest and opened for business in 2017.",140837.0,0.0,RWELLS,2018-07-23 11:07:27.797
