47156,20-16-0967,20,16,0967,8140.0,2016-07-25,2016-07-28 17:47:41.377,JACKSON FOOD STORES #551 R-O-W,86623 FRANKLIN BLVD,EUGENE,97405,(208) 888-6061,False,4.0,,3.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Free product was discovered in CentruyLink vault, located in the right-of-way on Jackson Food Stores property.

Potentially related to previous case.  Free product was not seen in previous case.

A site visit showed no free product in vault.  Have contacted Century Link and they have been updated.  The file will remain open for one year to allow for groundwater to fluctiate and allow century link to re-report the issue and let DEQ see the product if it reappears.","20-07-1374 Shell 121618
20-89-4034 Sunny LLC","On July 25, 2016, DEQ received a report of free product in a Century Link utility vault at the corner of the Jackson Food Stores #551 located at 86623 Franklin Blvd in Eugene. Previous investigations at the site (File 20-89-4034 and 20-07-1374) were completed and both issued letters of no further action.  Neither investigation sampled water from the utility vault.  However, groundwater samples were collected between the vault and areas of known high contamination, and concentrations were very low about thirty feet away from the vault. Sample results from the vault confirmed the presence of petroleum in vault water and concentrations that are much lower than DEQ’s risk based standards for excavation/utility workers. Based on the available information, Jackson Food Store #551 is currently protective of public health and the environment. It appears that the contamination present in the utility vault is associated with the former releases at your property and the concentrations have not increased indicating a new release.  Since there has not been a new release, this file (#20-16-0967) has been administratively closed. ",23515.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2018-03-22 08:45:13.553
