47279,10-16-1090,10,16,1090,12519.0,2016-08-05,2016-08-18 17:02:55.300,NEW PINE STREET SB,SE PINE ST AND SE OAK AVE,ROSEBURG,97470,(541) 957-3572,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Tank discovered on old parking lot, on SE Pine St between Oak and Washington.  Area now covered with newly re-routed Pine St Southbound.

phone call with Todd Paselk (ODOT) on 6-sep-16, decomm report & site assessment report will be submitted this week to Coos Bay (Esc)",,"On June 3, 2016 an ODOT contractor encountered an unknown 1,700 gallon used oil UST. Approximately 50 gallons of oil was spilled after the tank was ripped open by construction equipment. First Strike Environmental was contracted on June 3, 2016 to complete the tank decommissioning and environmental remediation. The tank was recycled and the remaining oil and sludge was disposed of through Thermo Fluids.  Approximately 26 tons of petroleum contaminated soil was excavated and disposed of at the Dry Creek Landfill. Soil samples were collected below the UST following tank removal and soil excavation and showed contamination below the applicable Level 2 soil matrix cleanup level. Tank decommissioning, soil excavation, and sampling all occurred on the same day on the release. No groundwater was encountered. Based on the available information, the New Pine Street SB site is currently protective of public health and the environment.",140603.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2017-02-13 08:37:25.337
