47308,20-16-1119,20,16,1119,2187.0,2016-08-12,2016-08-24 14:16:09.670,Conifer Products Inc.,85019 Parkway Rd.,PLEASANT HILL,97455,(480) 802-4035,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,phase 2 report with site assessment results was submitted to Coos Bay office on 2-aug-16 and sent to Chris Richardson via email (Esc),,"(MOTT 12/6/16) The property was previously used as a truck shop and utilized four USTs. According to the owner the USTs stopped being used in the 1980’s and were removed approximately 15-20 years ago. The property is currently being utilized as a remanufacturing mill. One single family home is located on the property and is used as a residence by the owner of the remanufacturing mill business. Water is supplied to the site via an onsite domestic well. In August 2016, a Limited Phase II ESA was completed for the site. A total of seven soil borings were advanced throughout the former UST area. One soil sample (B2) indicated a TPH-G concentration above the residential vapor intrusion into buildings and residential leaching to groundwater RBCs. Refusal was encountered between 10.5 and 13.5 feet. Groundwater was only encountered in one of the borings (B1) at a depth of approximately 10 feet. The groundwater sample collected from B1 indicated a TPH-D concentration of 307ppb; however, TPH-G was not detected.  The TPH-D concentration in B1 exceeds the Residential Ingestion & Inhalation from Tapwater RBC of 100ppb. A sample was collected from the onsite domestic well in November 2016 and analyzed for TPH-D, TPH-G, VOCs, PAHs, and lead. None of the compounds analyzed for were detected in the tapwater sample. (MOTT 2/13/17) An NFA was issued for the site on 2/13/17.",19433.0,0.0,MOTT,2017-02-13 08:23:05.527
