47430,15-16-1241,15,16,1241,,2016-07-22,2016-09-16 15:23:48.353,TerraMai,8400 Agate Rd,WHITE CITY,97503,541-944-4039,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Tanks removed in 1980s.  Registration will not be required at this time.,,"(MOTT 11/29/16) A Phase II was completed in 2011 and included soil sampling in four distinct areas of the site (three former UST locations and the former debarker area). Soil samples indicated TPH-D and benzo(a)pyrene concentrations above the soil ingestion, dermal contact, and inhalation RBCs for the construction worker pathway. Additionally, TPH-G, naphthalene, and benzo(a)anthracene were detected above the occupational leaching to groundwater RBCs.  Groundwater was encountered during the soil assessment; however, no groundwater samples were collected. Additional soil and groundwater sampling is still needed. Soil excavation in the former debarker area is scheduled for Spring 2017.


(Farris, 02/18/20) Soil and Groundwater investigation completed in 2019 that delineated the residual contamination.  Thorough description of results in both DEQ's  ""Staff Memo Recommending No Further Action, dated 12/30/19"" and the consultant's report ""Revised Focused Subsurface Investigation, dated 11/18/2019.""  Groundwater impacts remain so use of groundwater is restricted.  Soil impacts also remain that could be a risk to construction workers so any construction must follow the Contaminated Media Management Plan that is recorded with the Easement and Equitable Servitude (EES) on the property deed.",125195.0,0.0,GDECK,2020-05-06 18:51:52.360
