Contamination discovered during initial sampling.  Thhe tank has not been decomissioned and no soil has been moved.  They intent to dispose of it at the Dry Creek Landfill",,"One 502-gallon gasoline and one 502-gallon diesel tank were decommissioned and removed on 11/3/16. The tanks were for farm use and therefore non-regulated. Initial boring samples indicated soil contamination. Approximately fifteen cubic yards of contaminated soil was excavated and disposed of at Dry Creek Landfill. The tanks were taken to Schnitzer Steel for recycling. After decommissioning and soil remediation, additional soil samples were taken and confirmed to be within applicable soil matrix Level II amounts. No groundwater was encountered during decommissioning or excavation.",142271.0,0.0,GDECK,2017-06-22 15:40:58.610
