47642,26-16-1453,26,16,1453,3038.0,2016-10-31,2016-11-01 08:38:40.453,KIA OF PORTLAND,307 NE BROADWAY ST,PORTLAND,97232,(425) 821-7777,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"AN OIL DETECTION OF 83.2 PPM WAS REPORTED IN SAMPLE PL3-2.5. MSBA BELIEVES THAT THIS DETECTION IS NOT THE RESULT OF A RELEASE FROM THE UST SYSTEM SINCE OIL WAS NOT LIKELY CONTAINED WITHIN THE USTS. THE MINOR DETECTION OF OIL COULD POTENTIALLY BE FROM THE OVERLYING ASPHALT, OR DUE TO A WEATHERPROOF COATING SOMETIMES APPLIED TO PIPING, OR POSSIBLY RESIDUAL HISTORIC OIL FROM BEFORE ASPHALT WAS ADDED. OUR EXPERIENCE AT OTHER SITES WITHIN THESE VERY OLD COMMERCIAL/INDUSTRIAL AREAS OF PORTLAND INDICATES THAT LOW CONCENTRATIONS OF OIL NEAR THE SURFACE ARE NOT THAT UNCOMMON. ANOTHER CONSIDERATION IS THAT THERE WAS NO DISCOLORATION OR ODOR OF PETROLEUM OFTEN ASSOCIATED WITH POINT SOURCE RELEASES.",LUST #26-92-0186,,901.0,0.0,KDANA,2016-11-14 08:00:27.580
