47663,26-16-1474,26,16,1474,,2016-11-03,2016-11-04 07:00:32.630,"Bibleheimer, Rebecca",9339 N Geneva Ave,PORTLAND,97203,,False,2.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,143237.0,24953.0,IGAFFNE,2017-05-09 14:13:16.760
47664,24-16-1475,24,16,1475,11184.0,2016-11-03,2016-11-04 09:55:03.627,EVERGREEN STAGE LINES,854 FRONT ST NE,SALEM,97301,(503)378-0225,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Soil borings were competed around a former UST Excavation where the tank was removed in 1993. No recent excavation have been completed in the area.
Low concentrations of petroleum contamination remain in portions of the site and adjacent properties. Contamination consists of gasoline and gasoline related VOCs.
Soil contamination has been found between 15 and 35 feet below ground. The shallowest impacts are located around the bottom of the former UST pit and deeper impacts are generally found down gradient (west) of the tank pit, which correspond with increased depth to groundwater closer to the river.
Groundwater contamination is present beneath the entire property and laterally extends outward off-site as it moves down gradient towards the Willamette River.
Soil gases have very low concentrations of gasoline and gasoline related VOCs beneath the entire site. Soil gasses may also be impacted offsite but would be even lower in concentration as soil and groundwater concentrations decrease with distance offsite.A public notice was issued with comments received. Because the concentration within the LoF were below applicable RBCs an nonconditional NFA is issued.bcs.6.3.21",,"Soil borings were competed around a former UST Excavation where the tank was removed in 1993. No recent excavation have been completed in the area.
Low concentrations of petroleum contamination remain in portions of the site and adjacent properties. Contamination consists of gasoline and gasoline related VOCs.
Soil contamination has been found between 15 and 35 feet below ground. The shallowest impacts are located around the bottom of the former UST pit and deeper impacts are generally found down gradient (west) of the tank pit, which correspond with increased depth to groundwater closer to the river.
Groundwater contamination is present beneath the entire property and laterally extends outward offsite as it moves down gradient towards the Willamette River. 
Soil gases have very low concentrations of gasoline and gasoline related VOCs beneath the entire site. Soil gasses may also be impacted offsite but would be even lower in concentration as soil and groundwater concentrations decrease offsite. A public notice was issued with no comments received. Because the concentrations within the LoF were below the appicable RBCs an nonconditional NFA is issued. bcs.6.3.21",154085.0,0.0,GDECK,2021-08-16 17:40:24.453
