47680,15-16-1491,15,16,1491,,2016-11-08,2016-11-08 11:50:58.037,"Nash Holdings, LLC",1401 Center Drive,MEDFORD,97501,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"PCS found during site excavation in a presumed, previously removed, UST/piping location;
(ARL 10/22/2019) Site has been split into seperate tax lots since 2016 release report.",,"The site was originally developed by at least 1956 with a residential building and possibly a commercial automotive repair or maintenance building. Soil and groundwater have been impacted in a localized area in the north central portion of the property as shown on the attached figure. Impacted soil is located between 9 and 11 feet below ground. The cause of contamination from the tank system is unknown, as contamination was discovered following building demolition after the tanks or dispensers had been removed. However, because of the depth of the contamination, a leak or leaks from an underground tank is suspected. Prior to the excavation of contaminated soil, sample results indicated impacts of gasoline, diesel, lube oil, and gasoline related compounds in soil. In November 2016, about 480 tons of impacted soil were excavated and disposed of at the Dry Creek Landfill in Eagle Point, Oregon. Some contamination was left in place after the soil cleanup, around the eastern portion of the former excavation, where gasoline was detected in confirmation samples with gasoline concentrations as high as 350 mg/Kg. The site has been redeveloped for use as a shopping center and is connected to city water. Adjacent properties are also expected to be developed for commercial use and be connected to city water. This investigation was limited to the area of the excavation for petroleum contamination associated with this LUST, and did not investigate any other areas of the property.",143292.0,24970.0,CRICHAR,2020-06-29 09:39:29.833
