47692,03-16-1503,03,16,1503,,2016-11-10,2016-11-10 08:52:17.757,Linda Chang,13908 SE McLoughlin Boulevard,MILWAUKIE,97267,,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"Prior to 1978 the site operated as a gas station and in 1987 the station and tanks were decommissioned. Since that time the property has been used as a car sales lot. Contamination was caused by apparent leaks from the four onsite gasoline and diesel fuel tanks. The release has impacted subsurface soils, shallow groundwater in the vicinity, and soil gases. Excavation of contaminated soil was attempted, however, shallow groundwater was encountered before reaching impacted soils.  A total of three phases of investigation were performed to fully delineate contamination in subsurface soils, shallow groundwater, and soil gas. Contaminated soil remains on site in the vicinity of the former tank pits. Groundwater contamination also remains in the vicinity of the tanks pits and extends beneath the McLoughlin Boulevard right of way. The site is currently a paved lot.  Future development at the site is expected to be commercial or urban residential in nature and any structures are expected to connect to municipal water. Soil gas sampling did not reveal petroleum hydrocarbons or volatile organic compounds at concentrations posing unacceptable risks to current or future site occupants. On February 1, 2018, a public notice was sent to nearby property owners and underground utility operators requesting comment on the proposed No Further Action determination.  No comments were received.
