47709,30-16-1520,30,16,1520,,2016-11-14,2016-11-14 10:36:47.477,"Galenbeck, Catherine",903 SE Byers Ave,PENDLETON,97801,541-377-3787,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,,143337.0,25000.0,DGRANGE,2017-01-26 13:35:06.683
47710,09-16-1521,09,16,1521,9008.0,2016-11-05,2016-11-14 12:07:25.040,VALERO/BUTLER MARKET STORE,61396 S HWY 97,BEND,97702,(541) 312-6891,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,True,,,"Three steel USTs were situated immediately west of the dispenser island and connected via below ground piping were decommissioned on November 4, 2016.  The USTs were overlain by soil and sod approximately 19 inches thick.  The USTs were reportedly installed 30 years ago.   
Results of initial hydrocarbon identification sampling and analysis conducted during UST decommissioning on November 3, 2016, qualitatively indicated total petroleum hydrocarbons (TPH) in the gasoline range at approximately 10 feet below ground surface (bgs).  On November 16, 2016, additional soil samples were collected at the locations that initially tested positive for gasoline.  These soil samples had concentrations of gasoline ranging from 13.6 to 7,190 milligrams/kilogram (mg/kg).    
To accommodate new USTs, approximately 22 cubic yards of PCS was excavated and hauled to Knott Landfill for disposal on December 1, 2016.  The excavation extended to a maximum depth of 11 feet bgs, where laterally-contiguous basalt bedrock was encountered.  Groundwater was not encountered during excavation.",17923.0,0.0,TENGLAN,2017-02-23 14:06:37.353
