24-15-1072  A & R Spada Farms II","One 1,000-gallon gasoline tank was decommissioned and removed on 11/16/2016. The tank was for farm use and was non-regulated. Initial soil sampling indicated soil contamination. Approximately twelve cubic yards of soil was excavated and disposed of at Riverbend Landfill. The tank was taken to Cherry City Metals for recycling. After decommissioning and soil remediation, additional soil samples were taken and confirmed to be within applicable soil matrix Level II amounts. No groundwater was encountered during decommissioning or excavation. JClaussen 7/21/17",19384.0,25026.0,GDECK,2017-08-08 10:48:19.667
47740,04-16-1551,04,16,1551,5935.0,2016-11-21,2016-11-21 16:34:52.350,ASTORIA CITY SHOPS,550 30TH ST,ASTORIA,97103,(503) 325-3524,False,8.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"A 6,000-gallon diesel UST and a 2,000-gallon gasoline UST were removed from this site in November 2016.  A third UST (6,000-gallon gasoline) was filled in-place.  A total of 44.55 tons of PCS were excavated and removed from the site.  Additional contaminated soils could not be removed due to an adjacent building foundation.  Groundwater (at about 9 ft bgs) was also impacted.  However, the extent of residual soil and groundwater contamination appears to be minimal.",121.0,0.0,KDANA,2017-06-05 07:39:00.937
