47817,26-16-1628,26,16,1628,1919.0,2016-12-14,2016-12-14 13:36:22.633,JK Petroleum LLC,9138 SE Foster Rd,PORTLAND,97266,,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Site also addressed as 5959 SE 92nd Ave.,26-91-0207 Foster Mobil BP,"The site is a former gasoline/service station.   Underground storage tanks (USTs) of 12,000-, 8,000- and 6,000-gallon capacities were formerly located in a common tank pit west of the canopy.  In addition, two heating oil tanks and a 500-gallon waste oil UST were located adjacent to or beneath the former station building.  Between December 2016 and February 2017 the USTs were decommissioned and removed from the site. Compliance sampling in the area of the USTs did not reveal detectable concentrations of gasoline, diesel or heavy oil range hydrocarbons, however gasoline, diesel, and heavy oil range hydrocarbon contamination was discovered around the southeast fuel dispenser.  Sampling around the two heating oil tanks or the waste oil tank did not show detectable levels of petroleum in soils. Low level widespread gasoline, diesel, and heavy oil contamination was discovered in two contiguous areas through the center and northeast areas of the property that also extended offsite to the west. The offsite impacts cover an area of approximately 1,000 square feet. This widespread area of contamination is believed to be from controlled historic application of petroleum for dust control. Approximately 1,014 tons of contaminated soil was excavated and disposed of at the Hillsboro Landfill and all storage tanks were recycled through Metro Metals. Confirmations samples that followed the excavations showed that the remaining concentrations of petroleum are below the Soil Matrix Level II cleanup standards. Benzo(a)pyrene was detected in one soil sample at a concentration exceeding DEQ’s urban residential RBC for ingestion, dermal contact and inhalation.  However, the pocket of contamination is limited in volume and site employees are not likely to encounter contamination at depths equal to or greater than 3 feet below ground surface. No groundwater was encountered during the decommissioning or site assessment activities.",117315.0,25103.0,CRICHAR,2017-05-25 16:27:29.447
