47968,04-17-0108,04,17,0108,,2017-02-08,2017-02-08 10:53:53.920,Astoria Armory,407 17th St,ASTORIA,97103,503-936-5411,False,0.0,,0.0,,False,True,False,0.0,False,False,False,False,False,"TPH-Dx level of 97.9 mg/kg at 12"" bgs. Possible overspill.",,,144221.0,25256.0,DGRANGE,2017-02-08 10:53:53.920
47969,10-17-0109,10,17,0109,3674.0,2017-01-12,2017-02-08 11:15:44.060,KELLY'S KORNER CHEVRON,5146 OLD HWY 99S,ROSEBURG,97470,(541) 863-5268,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,,10-90-0021 KELLEY'S KORNER,"This site has operated as an automotive fueling and service station since the early 1900’s. The site has operated as a fuel station and convenience store in its current configuration since 1994. Contamination appears to be the result of a historic release and small leaks from diesel product piping. Soil at the site is contaminated with diesel and heavy oil. During piping upgrades in January 2017, storm water drained from the parking lot into pit areas and became contaminated with spilled diesel from the removed pipes. About six cubic yards of impacted soil were removed during piping upgrades.  At the same time about 12,500 gallons of impacted storm water runoff was treated and discharged to the Green Sanitary District water treatment system. Groundwater was not present in borings to 15 feet around the tank pit where the storm water was pumped from.  Therefore, there is no indication that groundwater has been impacted. Diesel contaminated soil remains onsite beneath the southern dispenser canopy.  Diesel and oil contaminated soil also remains at the northeast corner of the northern dispenser canopy. One sample exceeded the construction worker screening standard (for diesel) but this sample could not be repeated and it does not appear that there is unacceptable risk for construction workers.The site is expected to remain connected to municipal water.  Based on zoning, the property could be redeveloped for mixed use.",20464.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2018-05-22 13:41:34.050
47971,10-17-0111,10,17,0111,,2017-02-03,2017-02-08 14:48:52.567,Roseburg Senior Center,1614 SE Stephens St,ROSEBURG,97470,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"(MOTT 07/03/17) Two separate service stations operated along the southern property boundary (tax lots 05300 and 05400) sometime between 1939 and 1962. Roseburg Senior Center moved into the site building in January 2015. Between December 2016 and March 2017, a total of 36 soil borings were advanced at the site and a total of 52 soil samples were collected for laboratory analysis. Groundwater was not encountered within 25 feet of the ground surface; therefore, no groundwater samples were collected. Two distinct areas of soil impacts associated with the former service station locations were identified at the site, one just south of the site building and one along the southern property boundary.  Soil impacts generally extend from approximately 8 to 14 feet below ground surface (bgs) in both locations. Soil impacts were not observed above 5 feet bgs or below 15 feet bgs anywhere on the site.  Concentrations of petroleum related compounds were generally detected at concentrations below the applicable risk-based concentrations (RBCs) for the site, with the exception of one sample location (P17) located along the southern portion of the property. Concentrations of gasoline range hydrocarbons (TPH-G) were detected above the construction worker ingestion, dermal contact, and inhalation RBC and benzene and ethylbenezene were detected above the occupational vapor intrusion into buildings RBC at sample location P17. A soil gas sample collected near the south side of the site building indicates that vapor intrusion into the site building is not occurring; however, a soil gas sample was not collected near the area with the highest soil concentrations (southern portion of the property near sample location P17). If in the future a new building is constructed near this location an engineered vapor barrier should be installed. (MOTT 08/18/17) A CMMP was prepared for the site to address remaining soil with concentrations above the construction worker RBCs. A NFA was issued on 8/18/17.",144225.0,0.0,GDECK,2017-08-22 15:33:30.460
