48137,20-17-0277,20,17,0277,,2017-03-21,2017-03-23 17:47:34.760,Thompson's Properties,98 E 11th Ave,EUGENE,97401,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Phase I showed site was a gas station.  Phase II showed detections. 
C Richardson. 3/21/2017",,"(MOTT 06/07/17) The property was used as a gasoline service station from approximately 1933 to 1948 and then as an automobile sales facility from at least 1954 to 1968. According to the City of Eugene Fire Marshall Office, the former service station utilized one 4,000-gallon and four 1,000-gallon underground storage tanks (USTs). The USTs were reportedly removed from the site in 1951.  In February 2017, four borings (P1 through P4) were advanced at the site to a total depth of 19 feet. No visual or olfactory indications of contamination were observed in any of the borings. One soil sample was collected from the soil/groundwater interface (13-15 feet bgs) in each boring and analyzed for TPH-Gx, TPH-Dx, volatile organic compounds (VOCs), and polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs). Grab groundwater samples were also collected from each boring location and analyzed for TPH-Gx, TPH-Dx, VOCs, and PAHs.  TPH-G and TPH-O were detected in soil samples P3 and P4 but at concentrations below the applicable risk-based concentrations (RBCs) for the site. TPH-G, TPH-D, TPH-O, and VOCs were detected in the groundwater samples but at concentrations below the applicable RBCs for the site. PAHs were not detected in any of the soil or groundwater samples collected. (MOTT 10/13/17) The site was issued a NFA on October 13, 2017.",144879.0,0.0,MOTT,2017-10-13 11:03:02.643
