48395,24-17-0535,24,17,0535,1444.0,2017-05-09,2017-05-17 16:43:37.033,WOODBURN SHELL II,292 N PACIFIC HWY,WOODBURN,97071,(503)982-3511,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"two old tanks discovered beneath adjacent road/sidewalk by ODOT on 5-May-2016, tanks removed by 3 Kings but decomm report not submitted until March 2017 (?), soil sampling at that time found high levels of Gx and BTEX (Esc)",24-92-4061  Woodburn  Shell,"A partial no further action determination only applies to the current rights of way for Highway 99E and Highway 214. Additional investigation and delineation is necessary on Tax Lot 7900 prior to a complete no further action determination.The current service station building was built in the 1950s and underground storage tanks were installed by at least 1976 and decommissioned in 1992. Since 1992 the site has not sold fuel and is reportedly being used as an automotive repair shop. Two tanks were discovered north of the building and former dispenser island during roadway and sidewalk improvements in 2016. The tanks had been ripped open and filled with soil, apparently without being emptied of fuel. One of the tanks was found to be in the right of way and on tax lot 7900, making ODOT and the owner of tax lot 7900 jointly responsible for the investigation of contamination. Soil, groundwater, and soil gas near the tanks is impacted. ODOT has defined the extent of contamination into the right of way of both Highway 99E and Highway 214. After discovery of the USTs they were properly decommissioned by removal and a minimal amount of soil, about 3.5 cubic yards, was excavated. Contaminated soil and groundwater remain within about 20 feet laterally of the former tank pit into the right of way. Soil impacts are present between 5 and 17 feet below ground beneath the right of ways. All adjacent properties are expected to remain commercial and connected to municipal water for the foreseeable future.    An opportunity to comment on a proposed partial no further action determination was given to all adjacent property owners, the City of Woodburn, and underground utility providers. The public comment period was held for the month of January 2019 and no comments were received in that time. A partial no further action determination only applies to the current rights of way for Highway 99E and Highway 214. Additional investigation and delineation is necessary on Tax Lot 7900 prior to a complete no further action determination.",18918.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2019-03-12 14:21:31.963
