48675,21-17-0815,21,17,0815,,2017-07-11,2017-07-17 11:06:59.983,Oksenholt,316 SE HIGHWAY 101,LINCOLN CITY,97367,541-994-8626,False,7.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,True,False,False,False,False,"UST was discovered in the parkiing lot for Delake Bowl.  Based on the suction tube, condition of the tank interior and gasoline soil contamination,  the tank was probably an old gasoline UST used for residential, farm or commercial purposes.  Since it is partially under the sidewalk on Hwy 101 with no product (or odor) in it, I would say it has been out of service since well before1974.  It is a 300 gallon tank.  Hope that helps.  Bill Knutson",,"On June 27, 2017, K&S Environmental collected soil samples from beneath each end of the 300-gallon underground storage tank. Gasoline contamination was detected underneath the west end of the tank (11,100 mg/kg gasoline). No other constituents were detected on the west end of the tank.  No contamination was detected under the east end of the tank. On July 25, 2017, about 8.4 tons of contaminated soil was excavated to a depth of eight feet below ground. Five soil samples were collected from the walls and bottom of the excavation.  No contamination was detected in any of the confirmation samples. All excavated soil was disposed of at Waste Management’s Riverbend Landfill facility in McMinnville, Oregon. No groundwater was encountered during the remediation.",146369.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2018-03-26 16:16:11.280
