48698,20-17-0838,20,17,0838,,2017-07-12,2017-07-21 14:13:16.260,1535 Franklin Blvd,1535 FRANKLIN BLVD,EUGENE,97403,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"SITE WAS HISTORICAL SERVICE STATION. CONTAMINATION DETECTED IN FORMER TANK PIT AREA WITH A VERY HIGH READING ON A PID DURING A SITE ASSESSMENT. LABORATORY RESULTS ARE PENDING, WILL UPDATE CONTAMINANTS AND AFFECTED MEDIA WHEN RESULTS ARRIVE. ... SCOTT BRAUNSTEN (PBS), 7/22/2017.",,"The site had two gasoline stations operating from the 1960s until the late-1980s with the following underground storage tanks (USTs) noted:  
• One 10,000-gallon gasoline underground storage tank (UST)
• Two 4,000-gallon gasoline USTs
• One 6,000-gallon gasoline UST
• One 285-gallon fuel oil UST
Fire marshal records indicate these tanks were decommissioned by removal in 1987
The easternmost part of the site was also developed as a gas station in the late 1990s along with a fast-food restaurant.

In 2017 University of Oregon completed a Phase II excavation that identified soil and groundwater contamination.  During 2018, over 35,000 tons of soil was removed along with residual components of the gas stations.   All confirmation samples, except one at the easternmost edge of the site and 11.5 feet below ground surface were below cleanup levels.  
the groundwater is not a drinking  water source and was determined to not be reaching the Mill Race Creek so is not a risk.",146472.0,0.0,GDECK,2021-08-09 09:37:46.653
