48704,26-17-0844,26,17,0844,,2017-07-21,2017-07-25 10:20:21.073,Parks and Hill,4124 N Longview Ave,PORTLAND,97217,000-000-0000,False,0.0,,0.0,,False,True,False,0.0,False,False,False,False,False,"40,000ppm discovered on 7/21/2017 and reported on 7/21/2017 :)",,,146496.0,26006.0,CSALNAV,2017-07-25 10:20:21.073
48705,26-17-0845,26,17,0845,12552.0,2017-07-21,2017-07-25 10:30:19.333,Northbrook Village,22000 NE Halsey Street,FAIRVIEW,97024,503-742-1942,False,7.0,,3.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"We were contracted to provide emergency decommissioning of a suspected heating oil tank discovered during the ongoing soil remediation at ECSI site #6164. Excavation of the tank for cleaning and removal lead to discovery of a second tank. Based on the UST sizes and historical information from previous site operations indicated the tanks were likely agricultural diesel fuel tanks. The tanks were decommissioned by removal and confirmatory sampling was performed. Analytical results indicated a leak had occurred from one of the tanks. Impacted soil was excavated and additional confirmatory samples were collected. The residual diesel contamination is below the Level 2 soil matrix cleanup concentration for diesel.

We submitted discovered tank registration forms at the time of the discovery but could not file the release report until after the registration was complete. 

The decommissioning was initiated on 6/14/17. Analytical results indicating a release were received on 6/19/17. Notice was provided to Eric Clough on 6/21/17. Discovered tank registration and notice to decommission was submitted on 6/26/17. Remedial excavation and confirmatory sampling was completed on 6/26/17. 

Remediation of ECSI Site #6164 is ongoing. Contamination from the USTs is being referred to the Northbrook Village Cleanup File and this LUST release will be administratively closed.  (JKS 4-4-18)",ECSI #6164,ECSI #6164,146211.0,26019.0,GGAMOLO,2018-04-04 17:24:12.933
