48722,24-17-0862,24,17,0862,879.0,2017-07-24,2017-07-27 16:05:02.497,Klupenger Nurseries Inc II,24075 KLUPENGER RD NE,AURORA,97002,(503)682-2717,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Only one sample of groundwater collected (ND). Multiple drinking and irrigation wells are located within 200 feet on plumes. 1/22/18 CAR

HEAVY OIL - 227.  Andy Klopfenstein (Point Source) 7/24/17.

Two tanks: commercial HOT for warming greenhouses and a diesel tank for fueling vehicals.  ... c richardson 7/24/17.","24-13-0658 Klupenger Nurseries, Inc.","The site has been used for agriculture since at least 1952 and the onsite residence may have been constructed as early as 1916. Contamination is the result of leaks from an underground heating oil storage tank, an underground diesel storage tank, and leaking diesel and gasoline dispensers associated with a fueling area. Soil beneath the heating oil tank to a depth of about 19 feet is impacted with heating oil (diesel). No groundwater was encountered beneath this tank and it appears to be un-impacted. Groundwater is expected to be about 40 feet below ground, meaning there is about 20 feet of clean soil between impacts and groundwater. Soil beneath the diesel fuel tank, gasoline dispenser, and diesel dispenser is impacted with gasoline and diesel from 2 to 22 feet below ground. Groundwater was encountered in one boring and found to be un-impacted. The onsite domestic well, located about 150 feet south of the fueling area, was sampled and found to be un-impacted by the release. About 100 cubic yards of contaminated soil is estimated to remain beneath the former heating oil tank. About 250 cubic yards of impacted soil is estimated to remain beneath the fueling area. Both underground storage tanks were decommissioned and filled in place with pea gravel. The leaking dispensers were removed from service and replaced with tank-mounted dispensers on the new above ground storage tanks. The property is expected to remain a commercial nursery with no additional residential buildings constructed near the two areas of remaining soil contamination. The property is also expected to continue to use the existing domestic well and three irrigation wells on the property. This letter only applies to the two areas discussed above and shown on the attached figures. If contamination is identified, that is associated with other tanks or in other areas, it must still be reported to DEQ and addressed. Future construction of any buildings, including occupational, within 50 feet of the impacted fueling area is unlikely. DEQ must review and approve any future construction proposed in this area.",154580.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2019-06-25 09:41:52.477
