K Van Zandt 8/31/2017",,"On September 15, 2017, a 500-gallon gasoline tank was decommissioned by removal. Contamination was detected underneath the south end of the tank (631mg/kg). About 3.2 tons of soil were excavated and disposed of at Waste Management’s Riverbend Landfill facility in McMinnville, Oregon. Additional soil samples were collected in the excavation below the south end of the tank. All confirmation sample results were non-detect for gasoline. No groundwater was encountered during the cleanup.",147099.0,26241.0,CRICHAR,2018-05-24 12:59:43.127
