49017,34-17-1157,34,17,1157,,2017-09-27,2017-09-28 09:19:20.560,Butternut Creek,5095 SW 209th Ave,ALOHA,97078,,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"GeoPacific Engineering;  smorris@geopacificeng.com;  This tank appeared to have been decommissioned in place but records were not available.  No sign of a release was observed in the tank pit or soil samples and no petroleum odor was detected.  However, the lab results from one of the confirmation soil samples detected diesel range hydrocarbons at 104 ppm.  This appears to be a diminimis amount of contaimated soil as no signs were detected via visual, olfactory or with the MiniRaePhoto Ionization Detector (PID) employed in the field for all soil samples.",,,0.0,26352.0,CSALNAV,2017-10-11 16:16:38.810
