49019,20-17-1159,20,17,1159,,2017-09-22,2017-09-28 15:15:01.380,Former Auto Station,947 Franklin Blvd,EUGENE,97403,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"(MOTT 05/09/18) The site was used a gas station and/or auto service facility from at least 1938 to 1958. According to the Eugene Fire Marshall, one underground storage tank (UST) was installed at the site in 1956.  No records relating to the size or contents of this UST were available, nor where there any records of this UST being removed. A GPR survey was completed at the site in 2016 and did not indicate the presence of a UST at the site. It is likely the UST was removed during site redevelopment activities in 1958. Multiple soil and groundwater samples were collected at the site in 2016 and 2017. TPH, benzene, and lead were detected in soil; however, all concentrations were below the applicable RBCs. No petroleum related compounds were detected in groundwater at the site. In 2018, the majority of the site was excavated to prepare for site redevelopment activities. Two areas of PCS were identified and approximately 157 tons of PCS was removed and taken to Short Mountain landfill. (MOTT 06/14/18) The site was issued a NFA on June 14, 2018.",147347.0,0.0,MOTT,2018-06-14 14:57:39.727
49020,06-17-1160,06,17,1160,12562.0,2017-09-23,2017-09-28 16:34:01.013,Former Gasoline Station Bayshore,595 N Bayshore Dr,COOS BAY,97420,,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"RYS Environmental LLC;  rysenvllc@gmail.com;  Groundwater reported to DEQ on 9/18/17 via phone call.

Three 7500-gal USTs discovered, registered, and decommissioned 9/18/2017. ...gdeck

dissolved gasoline contamination extends well off-site towards Coos Estuary, subsurface utilities may be acting as preferential pathways, upgradient source(s) may be impacting this property (Esc)

3 tanks discovered and registered.",,,147067.0,26340.0,ECLOUGH,2018-04-13 11:00:52.017
49021,14-17-1161,14,17,1161,12567.0,2017-09-25,2017-09-29 10:33:55.090,Ken Jernstedt Airfield,3608 AIRPORT DR,HOOD RIVER,97031,541-386-1645,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Ken Jernstedt Airfield is located at 3608 Airport Drive, Hood River, Hood River County, Oregon.  The subject property is identified as tax lot 2600, Township 02 North, Range 10 East, Section 11BD.  The area of investigation is located at approximately Latitude 45.672o North, Longitude 121.540o West.  The elevation at the site is 638 feet above sea level.

The 115-acre Ken Jernstedt Airfield is located in the lower Hood River Valley in an area known as the Hood River Heights.  The topographically flat facility includes a 3,040-foot asphalt runway, associated taxi-ways, paved plane parking areas, and several hangers.  The locality of facility (LOF) is an area surrounding the decommissioned waste oil tank (WOT) and is located in the southern portion of the property.  Surrounding properties are predominantly orchard and pasture land and associated dwellings with the nearest residence approximately 650 feet west-northwest of the LOF.",,"A waste oil underground storage tank (WOT) was discovered during grading activities for resurfacing of the tarmac. The tank contained approximately 242 gallons of waste oil and is believed to be associated with the aircraft repair facility located south of the WOT.   The tank was decommissioned on September 27, 2017 in accordance with Oregon UST rules.
Contamination was discovered on the south end of the excavation and additional contaminated soil removal occurred on September 29, 2017.

Following removal of contamination, and based on sample results for soil, acceptable risk levels are not exceeded and a No Further Action determination is recommended for this site.",147349.0,0.0,TENGLAN,2018-01-23 10:07:46.400
