49233,15-17-1373,15,17,1373,566.0,2017-11-28,2017-11-28 13:35:57.090,Crater Lake Ford,2611 Biddle Road,MEDFORD,97504,541-770-3600,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Reported by: Pump Pipe & Tank Services;  Bob@pumppipetank.com,15-96-0063 Crater Lake Motors,"On November 11, 2017, Pump Pipe & Tank Services collected soil samples from beneath the three underground storage tanks (one gasoline, one diesel, and one used oil) after they had been removed.  Contamination was only detected underneath the used oil tank (1,010 mg/kg); no contamination was detected underneath the gasoline and diesel tanks. The maximum concentration is within the laboratory margin of error and was detected as lube oil while diesel was not detected.  Additional analysis found no detections of VOCs or SVOCs. Waste-oil tank sampling also indicated elevated levels of lead and chromium that exceed background concentrations and leaching to groundwater standards. No soil was excavated beyond what was immediately around the tanks. No groundwater was encountered.  The Medford Water Commission was able to confirm that all immediately adjacent properties are connected to municipal water. Only one property relatively nearby may have a well, and it is over 700 feet away.",162.0,26568.0,GDECK,2018-03-16 15:10:45.057
