While performing an assessment of the waste oil tank, found evidence of soil contamination. Highest detection was 610mg/kg heavy oil. Recommended decommissioning tank if no longer in use. Per Lynn Green 1/11/18.",,"Since 1982, the Port of Bandon operated a waste oil tank in a three-sided concrete vault filled with gravel on the southern rip-rap shoreline of the Coquille River marina in old town Bandon for waste oil disposal by tenents of the boat slips.  The tank was taken out of use and decommissioned in May 2018.  Soil contamination was discovered that appeared to be the result spills/overfills.  

