Groundwater impact confirmed by email from Andy Klopfenstein (PSS) 12/21/2017

UST Facility # 1727 in the DEQ record is located at 1870 Lana Ave NE (next door) had only one tank registered and filled with sand in the 1970-80’s, according to the paperwork. We're still trying to figure out if the two tanks associated with this new release at 1880 Lana are a different UST system or the same as UST Facility # 1727... gdeck 12/26/2017.

New tank registered; Facillty address for UST # 1727 changed to 1880 Lana.  I added the UST number to the LUST database to connect them. ....gdeck 9/5/2018",,"This site was used as gas station from approximately 1960 to 1975.  In 2018, two 4000-gallon gasoline underground storage tanks and associated piping from the former gas station were identified as still in place so, in the fall of 2018, both tanks were decommissioned, one via removal and the other in-place. Also, 200 tons of impacted soil was removed for disposal at Hillsboro Landfill. Sampling after the tank decommissioning indicated there is still petroleum-related soil and groundwater contamination at the site at depths ranging from 12 to 28 below ground surface (See the NFA letter for the figures.)  The site, however, is zoned for general commercial use and there are no water wells in the vicinity.  The property and neighborhood are provided municipal water from the City of Salem.  Therefore DEQ is issuing a conditional NFA with a Contaminated Media Management Plan.  The EES also restricts gw use and requires a passive vapor barrier liner on new building construction if people are to occupy the building.",148668.0,26657.0,GDECK,2019-10-29 17:50:36.663
