This site was a commercial gasoline station that went out of service in the early 1980s. Six regulated underground storage tanks were decommissioned on January 8, 2018. The soil in the backfill materials of the 5,000 gallon tank was contaminated with petroleum products. Confirmation soil sampling indicates that all petroleum-contaminated soil was removed from the property relating to this release. Groundwater was not encountered at any time during the UST decommissioning and soil removal activities. Waste from the waste oil tank and contaminated soil went to the Waste Management Hillsboro Landfill Inc. Waste from the other tanks were recycled at ORRCO. The tanks were recycled at Metro Metals Northwest, Inc. [KMH 6/4/2018]",,"This site was a commercial gasoline station that went out of service in the early 1980s. Six regulated underground storage tanks were decommissioned on January 8, 2018. The soil in the backfill materials of the 5,000 gallon tank was contaminated with petroleum products. Confirmation soil sampling indicates that all petroleum-contaminated soil was removed from the property relating to this release. Groundwater was not encountered at any time during the UST decommissioning and soil removal activities. Waste from the waste oil tank and contaminated soil went to the Waste Management Hillsboro Landfill Inc. Waste from the other tanks were recycled at ORRCO. The tanks were recycled at Metro Metals Northwest, Inc. [KMH 6/4/2018]",148763.0,26706.0,KHACK,2018-06-04 14:23:46.573
