49458,10-18-0110,10,18,0110,9247.0,2018-01-31,2018-02-05 10:20:13.630,Rodeway Inn Rice Hill,621 John Long Rd,OAKLAND,97462,541-849-3335,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"The site was operated as a Mobil branded gasoline station from approximately 1968 until 1990 when the fueling system was decommissioned. In 2000 the current hotel buildings were constructed. Contamination was apparently caused by leaks from the underground storage tanks and product piping to the former dispenser area. Soil and shallow perched groundwater has been impacted with gasoline and related constituents. Deeper groundwater, which is used for consumption at this site and in the immediate area, appears to be un-impacted. It is unknown if any contaminated soil or water were removed or treated at the time of the fuel system decommissioning. Contaminated soil and some shallow perched groundwater exists in an approximately 85 foot by 35 foot area on the western end of the property at the location of the former tank pit and dispenser area. This determination is based on the expectation that the property will remain a hotel or other occupational use, and not be used for longer term residential uses. Two existing drinking water wells are expected to remain in use on the site. While the onsite water wells are unlikely to become impacted in the future. DEQ recommends periodically sampling the water for petroleum related volatile organic compounds (benzene, toluene, ethylbenzene, xylenes) when conducting routine water sampling as required for the public water system.  Any new water supply wells installed in the future should be constructed outside of the area of contamination described above and shown on the figure included with the No Further Action Letter.",17726.0,0.0,GDECK,2018-07-16 13:50:51.433
