49592,24-18-0244,24,18,0244,,2018-03-06,2018-03-09 15:21:46.290,St Paul Elementary School,20449 Main St NE,SAINT PAUL,97137,,False,,,,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,,24-00-5686  ST PAUL SCHOOL DIST 45,"(MOTT 04/03/2018) The return line on the school’s 8,000-gallon HOT was damaged in July 2017. The leak went unnoticed until January 1, 2018 when heating oil was observed in an unnamed tributary of Mission Creek. The St. Paul Fire Department traced the release through the storm water system back to St. Paul Elementary School. Heating oil from the leaking return line ran down into the pea gravel and flowed into the bedding around the tank. A subsequent investigation revealed that a segmented concrete drain line passed through the tank nest area. When runoff from the roof of the school drained through downspouts into the concrete line, it leaked out at the joints, filling up the tank nest with water and floating the heating oil up around the concrete line, where it entered the storm water system. The fuel traveled 1,600 feet underground via the St. Paul storm water system to an open ditch line located in a residential area to the southeast of the school. A total of 2,400 feet of storm water system was affected by this spill.  Cleanup efforts both onsite and offsite are ongoing.",149651.0,0.0,GDECK,2018-04-03 11:19:24.097
