49632,24-18-0284,24,18,0284,5513.0,2018-03-19,2018-03-19 13:17:12.330,Future Salem Police Station,745 Liberty St NE,SALEM,97301,503-588-6255,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"ENW;  lynng@evren-nw.com. Discovered tank, empty = Regulated but not permitted. 1 HOT, 1 UST (Gx) and 18 hoists decommissioned.

UST # 5513, Delon Auto Center, 750 Commercial St NE.  Facility was large and located between Liberty and Commercial.

HOT also discovered during excavation; is being handled along w/LUST site.","24-94-4112, Delon Auto Center","The site had been historically developed as a mix of residential and commercial use.  The western half of the site was residential and the eastern half was a variety of used car lots until sometime in the 1970s.  The 1978 Sanborn map shows the former DeLon Oldsmobile dealership with sales, service, parking and paint booth on the east side of the site and apartments on the west.  In 1984, the former DeLon Honda dealership was developed on the western half of the site.  Tom DeLon sold his dealerships to O’Brien Auto Group in 2007, but retained ownership of the property.  The site operated as Honda of Salem on the western portion of the property and as Volkswagen of Salem on the eastern portion of the property (Figure 2).  Lithia Motors, Inc. purchased the dealerships in 2013 and moved the dealerships in 2016 to another location in Salem. The City of Salem purchased the property on December 27, 2017 and the buildings were demolished in 2018.
A Phase I Environmental Site Assessment in 2017 identified 16 hydraulic hoists, two underground storage tanks (USTs), two above ground storage tanks (ASTs), and a potential former fuel pump island as well as floor drains associated with historic site use. 
In 2018, the buildings were demolished making way for the future Salem Police Station structure.  Between 2017 and 2018, all 16 hydraulic hoists, two USTs, and two ASTs, floor drains and related piping were decommissioned by removal.  
A total of 950 tons of petroleum-contaminated soil (PCS) was removed during the decommissioning field activities.  Confirmation soil sampling at the site reported concentrations of all petroleum related hydrocarbons and RCRA 8 metals were below DEQ’s applicable Risk Based Concentrations (RBCs).  No residual soil or groundwater contamination has been left in place at the site.
The property is zoned commercial-general business district (CB) and will likely remain as this zoning designation for the very distant future.  Surrounding properties are also zoned commercial to the west, south, and east.  To the north and northeast properties are zoned high rise residential RH across Mill Creek and will likely remain as such in the distant future.  
There is no current or likely anticipated beneficial use of groundwater and city water is provided by the City of Salem Public Works Department to the site.",149815.0,26985.0,GDECK,2019-08-07 15:50:52.340
