49711,34-18-0363,34,18,0363,,2018-04-06,2018-04-09 08:45:06.370,"Robbins, Scott",17258 SW Meinecke Rd,SHERWOOD,97140,,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Soil Solutions;  emily@soilsolutionsenvironmental.com;  65,000 ppm",,,150204.0,27070.0,LDIMOCK,2018-09-06 09:07:48.680
49712,03-18-0364,03,18,0364,,2018-03-22,2018-04-09 17:10:19.170,Willamette Falls Legacy Site,427 MAIN ST,OREGON CITY,97045,,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"(RWA 4/26/2018)Rebecca Wells-Albers participates on the Brownfield Advisory Committee for the Metro/Oregon City/Clackamas County (Coalition) McLoughlin Corridor EPA Brownfield grant. Part of Rebecca’s role on the advisory committee is to review information for sites that may be eligible to use the Coalition’s EPA grant funding to determine if the objectives of the grant funds are met (public benefit, addressing a community need, etc). Rebecca also provides technical assistance and issue eligibility determinations, which are required by the grantor (EPA).

In late February (2/23/18), Brian Harper (Metro’s Coalition grant project manager) contacted Rebecca to discuss preliminary sample results collected from the Willamette Falls site in Oregon City. Metro used their brownfield grant funds to conduct due diligence (soil and groundwater sampling) in areas at the Willamette Falls, which are proposed for a public easement. Note that Metro does not own or operate on the Willamette Falls site. George Heidgerken owns the property and granted access to Metro to conduct the sampling but was otherwise not involved in the sampling activities.

Maul Foster and Alongi (MFA) are Metro’s environmental consultants who conducted the sampling.  MFA is not a licensed UST service provider or a Responsible Person as defined under OAR 340-122-0210, and is therefore not required to report a release to DEQ. Although the property owner, Mr. Heidgerken, is required under OAR 340-122-0220 to report the release within 24 hours of confirmation, he was not informed of the sample results by MFA until the release was officially reported to DEQ shortly before March 22, 2018.  As a result, DEQ will not pursue Enforcement against Mr. Heidgerken.",,,61088.0,0.0,RWELLS,2019-06-27 12:22:00.927
49713,15-18-0365,15,18,0365,,2018-04-09,2018-04-10 11:02:34.973,"Brian, Michael",922 S Oakdale Ave,MEDFORD,97501,,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"R & D Environmental Solutions LLC;  rick-dan@r-d-environmental.com;  The HOT was reportedly previously filled in place.  Tank length and orientation established with probe rod.  Auger boring was advanced at either end of HOT. Stained soil encountered at 6.0 feet.  Soil samples collected from 6.0 to 6.5 feet.  Lab report indicates diesel range petroleum hydrocarbons at 5,090 mg/Kg and 6,600 mg/Kg.",,,150231.0,27072.0,CSALNAV,2021-07-14 10:31:15.550
49714,26-18-0366,26,18,0366,,2018-04-09,2018-04-10 11:06:00.477,Emily Lewis PR,10225 SE Market Dr,PORTLAND,97216,,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"EcoTech, LLC;  tanks@ecotechllc.com;  18,400 PPM on north side and 302 PPM on south side of tank",,,150232.0,27074.0,CSALNAV,2018-07-23 14:11:28.653
