49728,03-18-0380,03,18,0380,,2018-04-11,2018-04-12 08:53:43.997,Pickett Property,905 N Juniper Street,CANBY,97013,,False,7.0,,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,Alpha Environmental;  zachary@alphaenvironmental.net,,"[KMH 10/16/2018] This site is residential and contained an unregulated gasoline tank and a heating oil tank (HOT). The 340-gallon gasoline underground storage tank (UST) and the 500-gallon HOT were decommissioned by cleaning and filling with sand. The tanks were found to be empty. Two soil samples were collected on opposite ends of each tank. The attached Sampling Plan shows the locations of these samples. The soil samples for the HOT were non-detects. The north sample of the former gasoline tank had a result of 42.7 parts-per-million (ppm) of gasoline. This is below the Soil Matrix Level 2 Cleanup Level of 80 ppm of gasoline. Petroleum contaminated soil was not removed from this site. Groundwater was not encountered at any time during the gasoline UST and HOT decommissioning. A No Further Action was issued on October 16, 2018. ",150271.0,27088.0,KHACK,2018-10-16 11:14:08.030
