49795,10-18-0447,10,18,0447,9093.0,2018-04-10,2018-04-26 09:51:52.150,C & D Lumber Company,1182 Pruner Road,RIDDLE,97469,541-874-2281,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Western States Environmental Services, Inc.;  searly@wsenvironmental.com;  soil is non detect
Low groundwater detection of TPH as Gasoline",ECSI # 3848.,"On March 19, 2018, gasoline contamination in soil and groundwater was discovered during the decommissioning by removal of a 2,000-gallon UST and dispenser from the C&D Lumber site located near the northwest corner of tax lot 00100 at 1182 Pruner Road in Riddle, Oregon. Gasoline in soil was not detected above lab reporting limits in four UST sidewall samples but was identified at 8.35 ppm from beneath the dispenser. Water entered the UST excavation and was sampled. The pit water sample contained gasoline at 768 ppb, lead at 33 ppb, benzene at 16.3 ppb, ethylbenzene at 14.3 ppb, and naphthalene at 3.27 ppb. Pit water detections were above DEQ risk-based concentrations for ingestion of groundwater. In August 2018, four temporary wells were installed in all four directions surrounding the former UST area. Water samples from the wells were collected and analyzed for gasoline and gasoline-related VOCs. None of the samples contained gasoline above lab reporting levels. Trace levels of toluene and xylene were identified in one of the wells at 1.7 and 2.32 ppb, respectively. The property is zoned Rural Industrial and located in an industrial area within the City of Riddle’s Urban Growth Boundary. The site and surrounding area are connected to the City of Riddle’s municipal water supply. Shallow groundwater is currently not used at the site nor is it expected to be used in the future. Soil and groundwater containing low levels of contamination remains near the northwest portion of the tax lot and appears limited to the immediate area of the former UST. The concentrations of contaminants should not present an unacceptable risk to workers at the site. Based on findings, this LUST file is anticipated to be closed during December 2018.",150485.0,27080.0,GDECK,2019-05-02 18:32:12.600
