49844,06-18-0496,06,18,0496,,2018-04-26,2018-05-04 15:51:48.723,Commercial Property,1845 Sherman Ave,NORTH BEND,97459,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,False,False,"EVREN Nortwest;  lynng@evren-nw.com;  Source of impacts are not currently known, but suspected to be associated with former USTs removed previously (no records of removal).  Owner decided to report impacts as a release from a UST system so that State oversight can be provided on this project. Note, client does not have email - email address provided is for client's contractor.","06-15-0390 Boshears, Ken HOT closed 5/19/15 JClaussen","The site appears to have been first developed in the 1960s for use as an automotive fueling and repair facility.  The service station had at least two and up to four underground storage tanks and a single dispenser island to the west. More recently the building has been used by an automotive repair and painting business. The cause of the release is unknown; however, it is likely a result of a leak from one or both tanks that were located south of the former station building. The investigation evaluated soil and groundwater around the former dispenser and tank pit areas. Contaminated soil remains on the property between 14 and 17 feet below ground in a roughly 60-foot diameter circular area at the south central portion of the property. A small amount of impacted groundwater was also discovered near the southwest corner of the former tank pit. It appears that this groundwater is perched and discontinuous, and does not appear to represent a useable aquifer. General land use in vicinity is expected to remain commercial and/or light industrial. Zoning does allow for urban residential use of the site. Municipal water is provided to the entire area and is expected to continue for the foreseeable future.  Groundwater is not expected to be used at or in the vicinity of the site.  Two soil samples exceeded the gasoline vapor intrusion into buildings screening level for future urban residential occupants of the site. Soil gas sampling showed concentrations are about half of the residential standard. An opportunity to comment on the proposed closure was given to all neighbors as well as the City of North Bend. The comment period was for a proposed conditional closure, with a restriction on residential use. No comments were received; however,  after further discussion with the property owner and additional investigation, DEQ determined that residential use, while unlikely, would be safe, and should not be prohibited.",135544.0,27155.0,CRICHAR,2019-02-19 13:58:15.007
