49873,24-18-0525,24,18,0525,8963.0,2018-05-11,2018-05-11 14:21:10.340,DEL WEB/INDUSTRIAL DRIVE,1190 SALEM INDUSTRIAL DR NE,SALEM,97303,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,,LUST#24-06-0947 Del Web Cardlock NFA 7/8/09,"Historically the site was part of a lumber processing or storage facility including a log pond. By 1981, the log pond had been filled in and the site was developed for commercial fuel sales in 1987. In 2006 a release was reported (LUST #24-06-0947) at the site which was investigated and received a No Further Action letter in July 2009. In May 2018, a diesel turbine failed causing a release of fuel to the subsurface. The pump was replaced and the Underground Storage Tank was put back into service. Soil concentrations of diesel and lube oil range petroleum remain consisted with the 2006 release. Groundwater southwest of the USTs has been impacted by diesel from this release. Further investigation has shown that the extent of the groundwater impacts are not likely to migrate significantly offsite. Contamination remains across much of the site consistent with the historical release. This contamination is present from about five feet below ground down to 13 feet. The site and surrounding properties are all expected to remain zoned for general industrial use and occupied buildings connected to the municipal water supply. An opportunity to comment on the proposed closure was mailed to neighboring property owners. No comments were received. This investigation looked at the increased diesel concentration found southwest of the UST pit. Other sampling showed concentrations consistent with the historic release and were not evaluated further.",24087.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2020-07-23 13:36:55.067
