Contamination discovered on this property (2290 Front St NE) by DEQ while doing off-site assessment for The Arsenal site.  Contamination found on this property determined to be from historic source onsite (not from the Arsenal).",,"The site was developed by at least 1926 and has been used as an automotive repair shop, automotive junk yard, fueling station and currently as a tavern. The exact causes of contamination are unknown but appears to be related to the historical use of the property for automotive repair and fueling. Soils between about 8 and 17 feet below ground are impacted with low levels of gasoline and diesel. Groundwater is also impacted on the site and was encountered as shallow as 17 feet below ground. No remedial actions are known to have occurred other than soil and groundwater sampling. Soil and groundwater impacts remain in two areas corresponding to former buildings on the site. Impacted areas are located at the northwest and southeast corners respectively and are generally circular in nature and approximately 40 feet in diameter. The site is assumed to remain an occupational facility that is connected to city water. Prior to any future residential use further investigation and/or remediation is required and must have DEQ’s approval. An opportunity to comment on the proposed closure was given to the City of Salem and no comments were received.",151700.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2019-01-22 13:14:58.090
