50202,27-18-0854,27,18,0854,,2018-07-16,2018-07-23 11:14:31.593,Coe Property,1330 E ELLENDALE AVE,DALLAS,97338,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,True,False,False,False,False,"Soil Solutions;  gabby@soilsolutionsenvironmental.com;  1,800 ppm diesel 680 ppm residual range

Please use email: nick@soilsolutionsenvironmental.com --> this email has to many characters to fit in the provided email box

Note: I'm re-reporting this release to confirm that it is an unregulated UST rather than a heating oil tank, please email myself with any questions.

Farm and personal use.  It has not been in use for over 40 years, since our client bought the property.  Given the area, it seems a reasonable assumption that it was used to fuel vehicles and farm equipment but we don’t know too much about it. ... Tess Chadil, Soil Solutions Environmental",,"The site is a residential property located on East Ellendale Avenue in Dallas, Oregon.  It had a 275-gallon unregulated underground storage tank for fueling farm equipment that was decommissioned in-place in July 2018.  During decommissioning a soil sample collected through the bottom of the tank indicated diesel contamination at 1,800 parts per million, but no other contaminants of concern.  The tank was emptied, cleaned, and filled with sand to decommission in place.  
Soil contamination remains beneath the tank at approximately four feet below ground surface.  The contractor drilled a groundwater assessment boring to a depth of 22 feet below ground surface, but did not encounter any water. 
Two irrigation wells, one on-site and one on the neighbor's property were sampled for diesel, heavy oil, and the constituents benzene, toluene, ethylbenzene, and xylene.  All results were non-detect. 
