50385,26-18-1037,26,18,1037,,2018-09-04,2018-09-10 15:33:20.830,Performance Properties Inc,2625 SE 35th Pl,PORTLAND,97202,,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Environmental Works LLC;  Andy@eworksnw.com;  Tank was sampled and certified under the Voluntary status in 2007 by another company. We got contracted to remove tank for remodeling of the foundation. Found contamination after tank was removed that shows the tank had leaked. The HOT ID from the LIST is 19087,,,154539.0,27793.0,CSALNAV,2019-04-17 14:44:46.327
50386,03-18-1038,03,18,1038,,2018-09-10,2018-09-10 15:59:35.170,Zigzag Ranger Station,70220 E HIGHWAY 26,ZIGZAG,97049,(503) 622-3191,False,,,3.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,,,"DEQ understands that during the installation of a yard hydrant and waterline, petroleum was discovered in the soil and subsequently reported on September 10th, 2018. Three samples were collected and analyzed for gasoline, diesel, lube oil, benzene, toluene, ethyl benzene, and xylene. The highest sample result for gasoline was 4,500 parts per-million (ppm) for sample S1 collected at a depth of 2.5 to 3 feet.

Less than 1 cubic yard of contaminated soil was removed. No tank was discovered. Confirmation sampling did not detect benzene, toluene, ethyl benzene, xylene, or gasoline. There were detections of barium, cadmium, chromium, and lead in the samples. The highest detection of these metals were 39 ppm, 1.3 ppm, 20 ppm, and 160 ppm, respectively. These are below DEQ’s generic risk based concentrations for residential receptors via soil ingestion, dermal contact, and inhalation. The area is currently used as a parking lot and is completely paved over.

DEQ is in agreement that the discovered petroleum contamination is not from a new underground storage tank release, but represents known contamination from an older release (LUST#03-92-0019). The previous incident received a No Further Action Determination on March 5, 1992. Based on a lack of evidence for a new release, DEQ is issuing an administrative closure for LUST# 03-18-1038.",66809.0,0.0,KHACK,2019-03-26 16:52:52.740
