50419,10-18-1071,10,18,1071,11484.0,2018-08-17,2018-09-13 10:10:35.557,ROSEBURG URBAN SANITARY AUTHORITY,3485 W GOEDECK AVE,ROSEBURG,97470,(541) 673-6570,False,7.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,True,False,3 USTs decommissioned by excavation and removal. Approx. 10 cubic yds PCS disposed at Dry Creek Landfill. Dx=528 and 95.9 and 64.5 mg/kg.,,(NAS 3/25/19) First Strike Environmental removed three petroleum underground storage tanks (USTs) from the site for the Roseburg Urban Sanitary Authority between May and August 2018.  About 8 tons of contaminated soil was removed and disposed of at Dry Creek LF in Eagle Point.  Confirmation soil samples were taken from the excavation pit.  These samples indicated that remaining soil contamination was below DEQ's applicable Soil matrix cleanup goal for gasoline of 80 ppm and diesel of 500 ppm. No groundwater was encountered. DEQ determined that no further action was needed and the site could be closed using the soil matrix rules since contamination was removed to below the cleanup goals.,13333.0,0.0,NSAWKA,2019-05-16 13:11:09.503
