50458,36-18-1110,36,18,1110,,2018-09-21,2018-09-21 11:47:10.860,Schrepel Residence Gas Tank,15005 NE Yamhill Road,YAMHILL,97148,,False,1.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"9/21/18 Tank was used for fueling residental vehicles; installed ~1976. When removed, saw pitting in tank, less than 1"" product in tank. No GW encountered per Jim Cooper-Alpha Env. JClaussen

Alpha Environmental Services;  jim@alphaenvironmental.net",,"The site is the location of an operating vineyard with a residential home. A 500-gallon gasoline UST was removed from the site in Sept 2018. Alpha Env assessed the area of the UST after it was removed and found elevated levels of petroleum contamination in the soil including gasoline up to 18,900 ppm and diesel up to 3,700 ppm. Based on this, Alpha reported a release of petroleum to DEQ on Sept 21, 2018. In Oct 2018, Alpha excavated and removed about 33 tons of contamianted soil from the area and disposed it at Hillsboro Landfill. Confirmation soil samples collected from the bottom and sidewalls of the excavation prior to backfilling indicated gasoline up to 13.3 ppm remained in the soil.  Diesel was not detected. Several VOCs were also detected: benzene at 0.528 ppm, ethylbenzene at 0.127 ppm, toluene at 1.02 ppm, xylenes at 0.934 ppm and 1,2,4-trimethylbenzene at 0.146 ppm. Because benzene was above DEQ’s residential vapor intrusion risk concentration of 0.16 ppm, Alpha collected a soil gas sample between the tank area and the home. Gasoline and VOC concentrations in the soil gas sample were several orders of magnitude below the DEQ’s residential risk concentrations for soil gas inhalation. 
Groundwater was not encountered in the excavation during the soil cleanup activities.    Confirmation sample results for diesel and gasoline were below the most stringent soil matrix cleanup goal of 40 ppm for gasoline and 100 ppm for diesel.
Soil gas results were well below the residential inhalation risk level.  DEQ determined that remaining contamiantion did not pose and risk to the site or residence and is proposing a no further action and closer of the petroleum release.  The NFA will be issued once final approval is given.",152391.0,27875.0,GDECK,2019-07-02 10:51:55.293
