ND for HCID",,"<div>On October 26, 2018, XEI performed a limited subsurface investigation to determine if petroleum product is present near the 675 gallon UST or 1,000 gallon HOT. Diesel and oil detections were found beneath the south end of the UST, five feet bgs. Further analysis measured diesel at 190 ppm and oil <50 ppm.  The west roll of the UST, five feet bgs, measured diesel at 190 ppm.</div><div>Further sampling performed by Bill Goff Construction on January 11, 2019 found diesel concentrations as high as 11,500 ppm near the north end of the UST and 8,300 ppm near the south end of the UST, all at five feet bgs.</div><div>The UST was fully removed and the excavation pit was excavated to ten feet bgs. Four samples were taken at the north, south, west, and east sides of the floor/sidewall. All samples returned ND for diesel and oil.</div>",152877.0,28013.0,ALEIDEL,2019-12-10 13:28:13.863
