50717,24-18-1369,24,18,1369,10896.0,2018-11-30,2018-12-11 17:48:22.653,SCC Properties II,3710 Portland Rd NE,SALEM,97301,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Alpha Environmental Services;  jim@alphaenvironmental.net;  Rob Hood was previously contacted in response to the discovery.,24-91-4290 SCC Properties,"The site was developed as a gasoline fuel station sometime between 1954 and 1967. It was reportedly demolished and the underground storage tanks removed sometime between 1982 and 1994. Since that time the site has been a paved parking lot. The exact cause of contamination is unknown but impacts were found at the bottom of the former tank pit and in what appears to be former product piping trenching. Soil at the bottom of the former tank pit, roughly nine feet below ground and along the bottom of product piping about three feet below ground are impacted with gasoline and related components. Soil impacts do not extend laterally a significant distance from the historical fueling infrastructure and do not extend offsite. Groundwater was not assessed because borings completed as deep as 35 feet (refusal) did not encounter groundwater when left open for several hours. Soil gas samples were collected near the impacted areas and indicate there are low levels of impacts that should not affect any future construction. Other than the historical removal of the USTs no other remediation such as excavation or soil treatment is known to have occurred. The site is zoned for commercial retail but a special overlay allows for urban residential use. Commercial or urban residential property use is acceptable based on the available sampling results. Any future development of the site is expected to connect to the municipal water system and there are no known beneficial uses of groundwater in the area.",153226.0,28106.0,CRICHAR,2019-08-21 08:12:39.117
