50877,24-19-0119,24,19,0119,,2019-01-26,2019-02-08 13:16:50.797,Northcore USA (Diesel),1881 WILTSEY RD SE,SALEM,97306,,False,7.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"ENW;  lynng@EVREN-NW.com;  Soil matrix cleanup.  Tank located at same site as HOT that also was source of release and previously reported. Farm tank, 500 gal. HOT closed by HOT program in February 2019 - refer to LUST 24-18-1405.","24-18-1405, Northcore USA LLC (HOT)","(NAS 4/29/19)The site has been used for residential and agricultural purposes since at least 1936. A partially buried 500 gallon UST was discovered on the east side of the property during a Phase I Environmental Site Assessment in October 2018. The tank stored diesel fuel for farm equipment. A dispenser was located on top of the UST. The tank and approximately 42 tons of petroleum-contaminated soil were excavated and removed on December 26, 2018. The soil was disposed of at Coffin Butte Landfill in Corvallis.    Confirmation soil samples were collected from each sidewall and the bottom of the excavation. All samples were non-detect for diesel contamination.No groundwater was encountered in the excavation during the decommissioning activities.The site is currently vacant and zoned for Multiple Family Residential 2 use. Future development of the property is for multi-family apartments. Future development will be hooked up to municipal water from the City of Salem.The site meets the requirements for closure under DEQ's Soil Matrix rules.",153657.0,28250.0,GDECK,2019-05-02 17:09:20.430
