50929,19-19-0171,19,19,0171,11228.0,2019-02-22,2019-03-01 11:04:35.840,Hunters RV,18020 Highway 395,LAKEVIEW,97630,,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Ed Staub & Sons, Inc.;  jared.staub@edstaub.com;  Very little contaminated soil was found. The job write-up in 2015 can be provided if needed. The contaminated soil appeared to be very old and most likely caused from tank overfill in years past. More than likely the fuel spilled was before the spill buckets were mandated in 1998. Tank integrity was very good. No corrosion or pitting.",,"DEQ has determined that remedial action to address environmental contamination at Hunters RV (now known as Base Camp RV Park) is complete, and no further action is required. This determination is based on the DEQ regulations and the facts as we now understand them including, but not limited to the following:

•Past site use includes retail fueling utilizing Two (2) 6,000 underground storage tanks (USTs) and One (1) 10,000 gallon UST.

•Cause of contamination is apparently minor releases of gasoline and diesel, possibly prior to regulatorily mandated spill buckets.

•Affected media includes subsurface soils

•Remedial actions taken include removal of 3 USTs, excavation of contaminated soils, and confirmation sampling of remaining soils. Per Jared Staub: Tank integrity was very good. No corrosion or pitting.

•Contamination left in place include low levels of gasoline ranging from non-detect to 44.6 milligrams per kilogram (mg/kg) and low levels of diesel ranging from non-detect to 149 mg/kg.",153912.0,28346.0,CKENNED,2019-05-02 10:34:13.580
50930,17-19-0172,17,19,0172,12605.0,2019-02-21,2019-03-01 17:16:41.910,Sukhwinder Rai Property,2476 Williams Hwy,GRANTS PASS,97527,,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"R&D Environmental Solutions;  rick-dan@r-d-environmental.com.  3 abandoned tanks decommissioned.  all about 12'x44"", 1000 gal.  Pumped 660 gal oily water total. Sample: 8-12 ppm lead in soil samples under one pump; almost ND under other pump. ... per phone conversation with Danny Boone 2/21/19.  gdeck

3/27/19 J.Claussen; per 20 day report, water pumped from excavation was from stormwater runoff. Sampling shows no Gx or BTEX and City of Grants Pass allowed water to be discharged to sewer. Water did not recharge in excavation after pumping.",,"A gas service station was constructed on tax lot 1800 prior to 1950 and closed prior to 1969. This site contained three UST used during gas station operation. During UST decommissioning, soil sampling was performed from the excavation pit and measured detectable levels of TPH-G, TPH-Dx, VOCs, Pb. Groundwater was not encountered during excavation. No indications of pertroleum was noticed during decommissioning activities. This site has submitted a work plan covering additional work that needs to be performed in order to determine the extent of contamination. ",153915.0,28341.0,ALEIDEL,2019-09-06 11:00:09.020
