4/11/19 per UST Compliance, all three tanks will be filled with concrete and left in place; one tank is under building, other two tanks are near natural gas line and billboard footings.

4/5/19 J.Claussen: lab reports 12,300mg/kg Oil
6,170 mg/kg Diesel
73,700 ug/L Diesel
12,200 ug/L Oil
10,900 ug/L Gas
1,190 mg/kg Gas
166 ug/L Benzene & other VOCs, PAHs
Trace VOCs in soil
64.8 ug/L Zinc (all other metals ND)",,"The site was operating as an automotive repair shop by at least 1965 and DEQ’s UST database indicates that petroleum underground storage tanks were installed in 1950. Three USTs were decommissioned in place and about 6 tons of impacted soil were excavated in March 2019. Three in-ground vehicle lifts were decommissioned by removal including the excavation of about 2 tons of impacted soils. Contamination is the result of repeated overfills of a waste oil tank and corrosion holes in vehicle lift hydraulic cylinders. Soils in the immediate vicinity of the former USTs and vehicle lifts are impacted with waste oil and hydraulic oil. There is the potential for construction or excavation workers to encounter free phase hydraulic or lube oils in soils remaining immediately around the decommissioned USTs. It may also be found immediately around the historic locations of the vehicle lifts to a depth of eight feet. Groundwater beneath the northern half of the site and beneath Hayes Alley is impacted by heavy/hydraulic oil. An approved Contaminated Media Management Plan dated, May 17, 2019 was prepared to describe how future subsurface excavation work should be carried out to reduce exposures and protect construction and excavation workers that may be exposed to the remaining contamination, including free product. Impacted areas are currently developed for occupational use. Future property use is expected to remain commercial. All properties in the area are connected to municipal water and are expected to remain so in the future. An opportunity to comment on the proposed closure was given to impacted parties and utility operators. No comments were received within the comment period  .",154068.0,28402.0,CRICHAR,2019-06-21 10:35:17.283
