51264,20-19-0506,20,19,0506,279.0,2019-05-21,2019-06-05 16:51:28.837,LOWELL GAS AND GROCERY,113 E MAIN ST,LOWELL,97452,,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,True,False,,"See Also 20-89-4097, Lowell Union Service; 20-95-7016, Lowell Union Service II","The site has operated as an automotive fueling station since at least 1975, but fueling activities may have started as early as 1945. The site has most recently operated as a coffee shop. Previously, in 1996, DEQ issued a No Further Action (NFA) letter for this site, for leaking underground storage tank (LUST) files 20-89-4097 and 20-95-7016. In August 2019 the most recently used underground storage tanks (USTs) were decommissioned and it was determined that a new gasoline release had occurred, resulting in the opening of LUST # 20-19-0506, which is the focus of this letter. The USTs were decommissioned in place by filling with a concrete slurry and the remainder of the fuel system components were decommissioned by removal. The exact cause of contamination is unknown; however, the highest concentrations were detected at the corner of the UST pit, where product lines were located. Soil and groundwater at the site have been impacted with gasoline and related constituents. This contamination remains under the site, between about 6 and 17 feet below ground. The soil contamination is focused beneath the southeast corner of the onsite building, and sample results indicate that concentrations drop by an order of magnitude within several feet of the remaining contamination. The levels of remaining soil contamination are below DEQ’s acceptable risk levels based on the depth of the contamination and the use of the property. Groundwater impacts remain around the southeast corner of the building and extend south about 30 feet to the property line, but do not appear to leave the property. The site is expected to remain commercial and connected to municipal water. This determination assumes that groundwater wells will never be installed or used at this site. An opportunity to comment on the proposed closure was given to the neighboring property owners, the Lowell School District, and the City of Lowell. No Comments were received.",18139.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2019-12-23 11:21:10.430
