51294,26-19-0536,26,19,0536,,2019-06-05,2019-06-11 14:16:13.300,SE Construction Inc.,2539 SE 34th Ave,PORTLAND,97202,5032911454,False,1.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"K&S Environmental, Inc.;  ksenvironmental@yahoo.com",,,155451.0,28740.0,MCOBB,2019-07-02 11:56:04.467
51295,26-19-0537,26,19,0537,12608.0,2019-06-11,2019-06-12 09:23:03.450,Ellis Apartments LLC,5603 SE Milwaukie Ave.,PORTLAND,97202,,False,7.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Five underground storage tanks were decommissioned by removal from this site in June 2019: two 10,000-gallon gasoline USTs and three 250-gallon gasoline USTs.  Approximately 135 tons of soils were excavated and removed from around the tanks in June 2019, followed by an additional 84 tons in September 2019.  Confirmation soil sampling found virtually no residual contamination.",,,155194.0,28769.0,KDANA,2021-02-17 10:14:29.410
51296,24-19-0538,24,19,0538,,2019-06-06,2019-06-12 10:27:42.880,NAPA AUTO PARTS,105 - 145 N 3rd Ave,STAYTON,97383,,False,1.0,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"BB&A Environmental;  smomo@bbaenv.com;  A site assessment was conducted at the Stayton Napa Auto Parts.  A boring was placed next to an aboveground storage tank (AST) at southwest corner of the building.  The boring was also placed next to an 8' by 12' asphalt patch in the parking lot, next to the AST.  This is the location of a SUSPECTED Underground Storage Tank (UST), although it has not been confirmed that a UST was ever at this location.  Analytical results for soil and groundwater samples identified heavy oil, diesel, gasoline, and individual constituents.  Chlorinated solvents were NOT detected.",,"The property operated as an auto parts store since 1964 and as NAPA Auto Parts from 2010 to present. Petroleum, lead and polychlorinated biphenyls contamination related to a used oil AST and UST formerly located on the southwest exterior side of the NAPA building was found in soil and groundwater during investigations completed between May 2019 and May 2020.  The contamination extends beneath the southwest section of the site and has also migrated offsite along the alley way and vacant lot to the west. DEQ determined that the contamination beneath the alley and vacant lot does not pose a current or future human health or environmental risk to these areas based on the uses of these properties.  The contamination does not pose a risk to the NAPA Auto site as long as the following conditions are maintained on the NAPA property: the property is not developed for residential use, the groundwater beneath the property is not used for drinking and a Contaminated Media Management Plan is implemented for any subsurface work in the area of contamination.  The property owner has agreed to these conditions which are being implemented through an Easement and Equitable Servitudes that was recorded with the County in January 2021.  With the recording of the easement, DEQ plans to issue a no further action for the site investigation and cleanup.",155412.0,28747.0,GDECK,2021-05-21 16:11:11.360
