24-19-0517 City of Woodburn R-O-W","On 6/17/2019, 1-1,000 and 1-300 gallon underground storage tanks discovered during utility improvements at location. Tanks appeared to have been pumped out, with one empty and one containing dirt. In the 1950-1960 era, a former gas station was located 50 feet from this location, same side of street, approximately 50 feet north of where tanks were. UST's were removed by licensed service provider and petroleum contaminated soil removed from utility area and transported to Hillsboro Landfill so utility work could resume. However, the Consultant estimates that contaminated soil remains approximately two feet below utility lines.",154093.0,28803.0,JCLAUSS,2019-10-17 13:58:35.067
