Site name originally reported as CCCU Property.  RP asked that it be changed to Harvard Drug. Site name changed to HARVARD DRUG 9/18/2019... gdeck","(ARL 01/14/2020) Also in HOT program, LUST #10-19-1072","(ARL 4/12/2020) The site consists of three buildings across the 0.68-acre tax lot. Two gasoline underground storage tanks (UST), two diesel USTs, and one waste oil UST were decommissioned and removed from the tank nest located in the southeastern portion of the site. During this decommissioning, one heating oil tank (HOT) was also removed. Excavation efforts removed approximately 733.3 tons of petroleum-contaminated soil (PCS) and overburden from the excavation through October 1 to October 28, 2019. The locality of facility (LOF) defines the area where contamination can be in contact with human and ecological receptors. Therefore, the LOF is bound to the southeastern portion of the lot according to the groundwater and soil samples which were taken around the tank nest during the Focused Subsurface Investigation, finished on July 24, 2019 and the clearance samples taken on October 7 and 17, 2019. On October 7, 2019, diesel, gasoline, and heavy oil contamination was found below the tank nest, around three to thirteen feet (ft) below ground surface (bgs).  Additional excavation of PCS was performed and an additional eight clearance samples were taken below the tank nest, around 12 to 13 ft bgs. The October 17, 2019 clearance samples measured all contaminants of interest (COI) below all applicable Risk-Based Concentrations (RBCs).",156274.0,28943.0,ALEIDEL,2020-07-15 11:02:23.333
