10K diesel UST decom'd in place July 2019... gdeck",27-90-4006 Central School District,"(01/23/2020 ARL) During in-place decomissioning of one 10,000 gallon diesel underground storage tank (UST) on July 23, 2019, regulatory soil samples were taken. These include one soil sample under the UST, one soil sample collected at the soil/groundwater interface - approximately eight feet (ft) below ground surface (bgs) - from each side of the excavation pit, one groundwater sample from the excavation pit water, one soil sample below the product piping lines, approximately two ft bgs, and one soil sample below the dispenser, about two ft bgs.  The soil samples taken under the dispenser and product piping measured total petroleum hydrocarbons (TPH) in the diesel range at 564 and 748 parts per million (ppm). The soil sample taken under the dispenser also measured TPH in the gasoline range at 17.6 ppm. The soils samples from each wall of the excavation pit, soil sample below the tank, and the pit water sample were all NDs for TPH and BTEX+N. Further excavation was performed to remove 0.81 tons of petroleum contaminated soil. Clearance samples taken on August 29, 2019 were analyzed for TPH as gasoline, diesel, and heavy oil, as well as BTEX+N. One soil sample, located on the southern sidewall, detected TPH in the heavy oil range at 55.2 ppm. This measurement is below all Oregon risk based concentrations. The excavation area was backfilled and resurfaced with concrete on September 9, 2019.",16996.0,28970.0,ALEIDEL,2020-06-22 15:24:34.230
