51761,26-19-1003,26,19,1003,,2019-10-07,2019-10-07 16:13:06.903,42nd and Prescott School,4212 NE Prescott Street,PORTLAND,97218,,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Terracon Consultants;  rick.rodriguez2@terracon.com;  Property is a former gasoline fueling station and auto repair, redeveloped in 1991. Soil Impacts (diesel) have been identified in subsurface soils. Site is currently a unoccupied commercial/school space.  Impacts were identified at depths of 17  to 22 feet below ground surface along the south side of the property. Site investigations have been completed during property transaction due diligence.",,"MTPThe Property was developed in 1950 as a retail fueling station, with the station building, pump islands and underground storage tanks (USTs) located in the northwest area.  Reportedly three 7,000-gallon gasoline and one 500-gallon waste oil tank were present.  By 1970 the Property was redeveloped with a different fuel station configuration in the southeast area of the Property, with a new station building, three fuel USTs and two waste oil USTs of unknown size.  As reported in a 2018 Phase I Environmental Site Assessment prepared by Hahn and Associates Inc. dated July 26, 2018, the City of Portland Fire Department issued a permit for removal of three USTs in 1984. No removal reports or other documentation are available for any of the USTs.  Subsequent investigatory work summarized below found no indication that any of the USTs remain at the Property. In 1992 the site was redeveloped with the current structure.  

golden Iris, LLC entered into an Agreement to faciliate cleanup and productive use of the Property with DEQ in January 2020.  Under the Agreement Golden Iris prepared a DEQ-approved contaminated media managment plan, and agreed to implement it during future work in areas of residual contamination.   ",157125.0,29241.0,MPUGH,2020-02-25 08:03:23.667
