51827,04-19-1069,04,19,1069,,2019-10-28,2019-10-28 10:10:02.070,"Mangan, John",234 S Ocean Ave,GEARHART,97138,,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Clarke Construction, LLC;  bclarket800@hotmail.com;  HOT decommissioned by removal 10/22/19.  No indications of contamination in field tests.  Lab (Apex) confirmed 56.4ppm concentration of diesel under west end of HOT.  Level remains below Level 1 soil matrix standards",,,157319.0,29316.0,MCOBB,2020-01-08 11:26:12.297
51828,27-19-1070,27,19,1070,,2019-10-21,2019-10-28 11:52:09.747,Oregon Fruit Products II,809 Edgewater St NW,SALEM,97304,971-645-2331,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Anderson Geological, Inc.;  erik@andersongeo.com;  Contaminant source is a former gas station that was demolished in the 1980's. Exact source of contamination is not known.",,"The site is owned by PDQ Investments, LLC and is currently occupied by a vacant warehouse that used to be part of the Oregon Fruit Products facility.  The site was formerly occupied by a fueling station and auto repair shop from the 1940’s through the mid-1980’s. 

Petroleum contamination was found in soil, groundwater, and soil gas beneath the site during environmental investigations completed in October 2019. This contamination is likely related to past operations of the fueling station. The contamination has migrated a short distance off of the site to the east beneath Murlark Avenue NW and to the south beneath Edgewater Street NW (see attached figure). The site is currently zoned Edgewater/2nd Street Mixed-Use Corridor by the City of Salem. There are no water supply wells on the site or near the contaminated area. Remaining contamination does not pose a threat to the current land or water uses of the property or surrounding area, but could pose a threat to future construction workers doing subsurface work onsite in the contaminated area or to future residents if the site were converted to residential use.  DEQ determined that the site could be closed as long as the following conditions were required that would protect potential future site uses from contaminant risks:
•No residential use or development allowed on the property without prior approval from DEQ.
• Prohibit the installation or use of groundwater wells on the property.
• Have a contaminated media management plan prior to any subsurface excavation work in the area of remaining contamination.

These conditions were implemented through a deed restriction that was recorded with the property on 10/19/2020.  DEQ plans to issue a No Further Action Determination for the site as soon as administrative closure tasks are finalized and remittance of a final invoice.",157302.0,29291.0,GDECK,2021-04-23 15:43:50.770
