51945,36-19-1187,36,19,1187,,2019-11-26,2019-12-03 12:15:11.703,Rural Home Property,17901 NE Baker Trail Lane,NEWBERG,97132,,False,7.0,,4.0,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Reported by BBA ENVIRONMENTAL; rjboese@bbaenv.com

2-500gal gas tanks located adjacent to N side of shop on rural residential property. Product piping, dispensers, and vent lines were located immediately above and adjacent to the USTs.",,"On November 25, 2019, BB&A Environmental decommissioned two 500 gallon gasoline underground storage tanks by removal. A soil sample analyzed by method NWTPH-HCID indicated only gasoline contamination was present. During the decommissioning six confirmation samples were analyzed for gasoline and resulted in concentrations between 51.3 parts per million and below laboratory detection limits. The decommissioned USTs were recycled at Schnitzer Steel in Eugene. Contamination was present above and below the tanks due to visible holes in the top of the tanks. On December 20, 2019 approximately 21 cubic yards of impacted soil was excavated from the south and southeastern walls of the tank pit. Two additional confirmation soil samples were collected following over excavation of contaminated soil. All confirmation samples were below the Level 2 soil matrix cleanup standards. All excavated soil was disposed of at the Hillsboro Landfill facility in Hillsboro, Oregon. No groundwater was encountered during the decommissioning or over excavation.",157757.0,0.0,CRICHAR,2020-12-07 08:29:02.340
