52141,34-20-0139,34,20,0139,12645.0,2020-02-17,2020-02-18 17:44:33.047,Beaverton 2002 LLC,12990 SW Canyon Road,BEAVERTON,97005,5034525561,False,1.0,,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"


4.21.2021: Received recorded EES (RAH)

EVREN Northwest, Inc.;  pault@evren-nw.com

Site assessment performed in 2019 in response to request from ODOT for access related to planned ROW realignment work.  A February 2019 geophysical survey revealed anomalies that could be tanks, piping and vent lines. In April 2019 soil and groundwater samples were collected near the proposed ROW footprint. Gasoline and diesel-range hydrocarbons were detected in the samples. In a May 2019 site assessment report EVREN NW Inc. recommended that if the presence of USTs was confirmed, then a release should be reported and the USTs decommissioned. EVREN reported that a test pit evaluation was performed in November 2019. At least one UST was confirmed to be present and the likely source of site contamination. The release was not reported until February 2020. The May 2019 report was not provided to DEQ until April 2020 (JKS 4-24-20).",,"Site assessment performed in 2019 in response to request from ODOT for access related to planned ROW realignment work.  A February 2019 geophysical survey revealed anomalies that could be tanks, piping and vent lines. In April 2019 soil and groundwater samples were collected near the proposed ROW footprint. Gasoline and diesel-range hydrocarbons were detected in the samples. In a May 2019 site assessment report EVREN NW Inc. recommended that if the presence of USTs was confirmed, then a release should be reported and the USTs decommissioned. EVREN reported that a test pit evaluation was performed in November 2019. At least one UST was confirmed to be present and the likely source of site contamination. The release was not reported until February 2020. The May 2019 report was not provided to DEQ until April 2020. (JKS 4-24-20)",0.0,29635.0,RHOOD,2021-04-21 11:13:15.320
