4/28/2020 J.Claussen: Spoke w/Dan Boone. Western States initially hired to decom HOT, also discovered 1,000 gal. diesel fuel tank (Tank A) w/some low-level contam. HOT (Tank B) had high contam. R&D Environmental has been hired by property owner to decom both tanks and do risk-based closure.

5/19/20 GDeck: originally reported as HOT site.  Switching file from HOT to LUST program to be closed under one NFA letter.  Changing from HOT to Non-Regulated.",,"The site was originally developed as a single family residence in 1959 and it is likely that the two underground storage tanks were installed at that time since one of the tanks was used to store heating oil. In Mach 2020 the two underground storage tanks were decommissioned by removal and about seven cubic yards of contaminated soil was excavated and disposed at the Dry Creek Landfill. Contamination is believed to be the result of small holes, spills, or overfills of the heating oil tank. Only soil is known to be impacted and it appears unlikely that groundwater at the site has been contaminated due to the depth of groundwater in nearby wells and sampling results following excavation. Low levels of contaminated soil remains in a roughly 20 foot circular area beginning about 7 feet below ground and extending down to about 15 feet below ground. The remaining contamination should not present a risk to residents or the groundwater. The site and surrounding properties are expected to remain residences that rely on private drinking water wells. An opportunity to comment on the proposed closure was given to the down gradient property owner who did not comment on the proposed closure.",160112.0,29722.0,CRICHAR,2020-11-17 10:46:01.167
