52349,30-20-0346,30,20,0346,,2020-05-01,2020-05-04 13:20:33.550,"O'Gorman, Dave & Marilyn",2240 W Highland Ave,HERMISTON,97838,541 567-5964,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Sprecher Group;  terry.sprecher@sprechergroup.com;  Eastern Oregon Environmental Recovery, LLC, Dave Ammons, is the HOT Service Provider. LIcense # 26951. Phone 541 571-3530. email: eoerdave@gmail.com",,,0.0,29854.0,CSALNAV,2020-06-02 09:53:48.010
52350,36-20-0347,36,20,0347,7147.0,2020-05-04,2020-05-05 17:29:46.883,Road Runner 2 # 512,1500 Portland Rd,NEWBERG,97132,415-328-7209,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,True,False,False,True,False,"CCS, a division of PNE Co. LLC;  scottg@ccs-pneco.com; was replacing USTs at this site when extensive water was detected in pit.  The required soil samples from dispensers, piping and tank excavation (sidewalls and beneath tanks were collected after USTs were decommissioned for a total of 19 samples.  These were non-detect for gas and diesel. The pit water had a detection for diesel, but no gas or benzene.  There were slight detections of ethylbenzene, xylene, toluene in the water.  Approx. 40,000 gallons of water was removed during the decommissioning and taken to Oil ReRfining Company (ORRCO) in Portland.  No water recharged into the pit and the new USTs were installed.  DEQ believes the pit water was not groundwater and there are no unacceptable risks at the site.  DEQ is recommending an NFA for these tanks.  August 2020.",,"CCS, a division of PNE Co. LLC was replacing USTs at this site when extensive water was detected in pit.  The required soil samples from dispensers, piping and tank excavation (sidewalls and beneath tanks were collected after USTs were decommissioned for a total of 19 samples.  These were non-detect for gas and diesel. The pit water had a detection for diesel, but no gas or benzene.  There were slight detections of ethylbenzene, xylene, toluene in the water.  Approx. 40,000 gallons of water was removed during the decommissioning and taken to Oil ReRfining Company (ORRCO) in Portland.  No water recharged into the pit and the new USTs were installed.  DEQ believes the pit water was not groundwater and there are no unacceptable risks at the site.  DEQ is recommending an NFA for these tanks.  August 2020.",22824.0,29860.0,GDECK,2021-04-27 17:39:27.173
