52515,20-20-0512,20,20,0512,12640.0,2020-06-22,2020-06-23 11:04:25.790,Market District Commons,560 Oak St,EUGENE,97401,1-541-484-9484,False,1.0,,4.0,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"BB&A Environmental;  jakooiman@bbaenv.com;  A abandoned heating oil UST was discovered during site redevelopment. The UST was decommissioned by removal in June 19, 2020, by Delta Construction under the supervision of BB&A Environmental (licensed service provider). The property is owned by Lane County. Lane County's contact person is Jeff Turk (Property Management Office (541-682-3859). Upon removal of the UST obvious odors were observed.

Site address originally reported as 540 Oak St.  Corrected to 560 Oak St per consultant 7/1/2020.
Originally reported as HOT release.  After decommissioning, results showed gasoline and diesel.  Site changed from HOT to Regulated site and moved to the LUST program.... gdeck 7/1/2020",,"•    A fuel station operated at the site from the 1950s until the station was decommissioned in 1991.  Lane County purchased the property in 1991 and used it as a parking lot until 2019.
•    In 2019, the site was developed by Homes for Good as a low-income residential housing development.  The housing development provides 50 residential units for low-income residents and military veterans.
•    The site is currently zoned commercial and expected to stay that way well into the distant future, including the current use as low income housing (urban residential).
•    In June 2020 during site development activities, an underground storage tank (UST) was discovered.  The UST was determined to be approximately 300 gallons with dimensions of three feet in diameter by five feet in length.  The tank was retroactively registered with the Department of Environmental Quality Underground Storage Tank program as UST #12640 on June 17, 2020.
•    Gasoline and diesel range hydrocarbons were reported at low concentrations in soil samples collected during the decommissioning activities. Approximately 5 tons of contaminated soil were removed from the site and disposed off-site during redevelopment.",161360.0,30023.0,CJACOBS,2021-02-25 15:31:31.663
