53072,20-20-1069,20,20,1069,,2020-11-18,2020-11-24 16:07:27.680,City of Eugene - EWEB,500 E 4th Ave,EUGENE,97401,971-707-2219,False,,,,,False,False,True,,False,False,False,False,False,"Bill Goff Construction;  goff1@pacifier.com;  We found the tank when excavating for other lines.  We were following the other lines to determine the location they were headed from & to.    We reported this to Dylan Eckert of the Eugene DEQ Office. 
Mr Eckert came to the site to look at the excavation.","LUST # 20-12-0026 EWEB
ECSI # 3808
Use Qtime number 46214 for DEQ charges associated with LUST # 20-20-1069.","During the City of Eugene's work to redevelop the riverfront property that was formerly EWEB's headquarters complex,there contractors encountered a set of fiberglass fuel distribution product lines, one 10,000 underground storage tank (UST),
one 500-gal heating oil tank (HOT), and one concrete vault, capacity of roughly 3,000-gal, that was a junction for fuel lines.  All of these items were removed during the excavation process at the site in summer of 2020.  Small releases from a puncture in the HOT occurred and the soil was overexcavated.  The vault was also overexcavated to get as much impacted soil as possible.  Confirmation samples were collected.  Some contaminated soil remained at the vault so oxygen-releasing compound was place at the soil/gw interface and subsequent gorundwater samples were collected.  No contaminants were detected in the groundwater.  residual soil concentrations were below urban residential cleanup levels. ",48463.0,30582.0,AFARRIS,2021-07-07 14:46:04.277
