53830,20-21-0672,20,21,0672,,2021-07-13,2021-07-14 10:02:00.077,"Standifer, David",2360 Douglas Dr,EUGENE,97405,15417297389,False,7.0,,1.0,,False,True,False,,False,False,False,False,False,M Carlton Construction;  Madeline@mcarltonconstruction.com;  80 ppm,,,165826.0,31398.0,CSALNAV,2021-07-26 16:14:34.597
53831,26-21-0673,26,21,0673,,2021-07-14,2021-07-14 10:03:18.513,"Fitzpatrick, Buford",9717 SE Stephens St,PORTLAND,97216,,False,0.0,,0.0,,False,True,False,0.0,False,False,False,False,False,Alpha Environmental Services;  erick@alphaenvironmental.net,,,,31399.0,MCOBB,2021-07-14 10:03:18.513
53832,24-21-0674,24,21,0674,,2021-06-21,2021-07-14 14:28:32.820,Eisenbahn Apartments,200 Railroad Ave,MOUNT ANGEL,97362,,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,OGI Environmental LLC;  rthompson@ogienviro.com;  OGI performed a Phase II investigation as part of due diligence for the site (currently an apartment building).  The Phase II was in response to the discovery of a gasoline dispenser in a 1922 fire insurance map during a Phase I ESA conducted earlier this year. One boring advanced in the vicinity of where the dispenser was reportedly located came back with TPH impacts at concentrations exceeding DEQs RBCs.  The quantity of impacted soil is unknown and age of the release is likely over 80 years.  Groundwater samples collected from same boring did not contain VOC impacts at concentrations exceeding RBCs.,,,157338.0,31308.0,GDECK,2021-07-14 15:03:14.403
53833,26-21-0675,26,21,0675,,2021-07-12,2021-07-15 10:53:54.700,"Mitchell, Jill & Stephen",7105 SE 19th Ave,PORTLAND,97202,,False,0.0,,0.0,,False,True,False,0.0,False,False,False,False,False,Environmental Works LLC;  conrad@eworksnw.com;  contamination discovered during decommissioning,,,,31390.0,MCOBB,2021-07-15 10:53:54.700
53834,26-21-0676,26,21,0676,,2021-07-12,2021-07-15 11:05:11.390,"Carlson, Errol",7525 SE Salmon St,PORTLAND,97215,,False,0.0,,0.0,,False,True,False,0.0,False,False,False,False,False,Soil Solutions;  paul@soilsolutionsenvironmental.com,,,,31393.0,MCOBB,2021-07-15 11:05:11.390
53835,26-21-0677,26,21,0677,,2021-07-15,2021-07-15 11:07:21.327,"Jacobs, Barbara",7714 NE Tillamook St,PORTLAND,97213,,False,0.0,,0.0,,False,True,False,0.0,False,False,False,False,False,Environmental Works LLC;  conrad@eworksnw.com;  Leak discovered during decommissioning,,,,31400.0,MCOBB,2021-07-15 11:07:21.327
53836,15-21-0678,15,21,0678,7869.0,2021-06-25,2021-07-16 11:56:44.600,RB Browns Trucking Inc,5758 Crater Lake Avenue,CENTRAL POINT,97502,(541) 826-7420,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"Point Source Solutions;  kyle@pointsourcesolutions.com;  Discovered suspected 10,000 gal UST during geophysical & phase II site assessment. Consistent drilling refusal at 9 ft prevented probe from advancing below tank bottom, estimated at 11.5 ft. West tank end sample at 9 ft. returned Dx results at 1060 mg/kg and Gx results at 71.3 mg/kg; south tank end sample at 4 ft. returned Dx at 115 mg/kg and Gx at 16.8 mg/kg. UST is full of what appears to be diesel contaminated sand and water.",,,20111.0,31330.0,GDECK,2021-07-16 14:52:33.170
53837,24-21-0679,24,21,0679,1366.0,2021-06-30,2021-07-16 15:35:21.283,Marc Nelson Oil Prod Crdlck,2010 W Washington St,STAYTON,97383,503-363-7676,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,Petroleum Compliance Services LLC;  jpike@pcsnw.net;  Samples were obtained during change in service project. The UST is being converted from a diesel tank to a water tank. Holes were cut in the bottom of the tank to collect samples. Two of the samples had hits on diesel. one was 39.7 ppm and the other was 77.8 ppm. Lube oil was also found at 163 ppm. Care was taken during the collection of the samples but the lube oil could have been from the cutting process. No ground water was found. Photos will confirm this.,24-98-4084 Stayton Pacific Pride,,18851.0,31345.0,GDECK,2021-07-16 16:12:18.450
53838,26-21-0680,26,21,0680,,2021-07-15,2021-07-18 18:47:14.127,Hazelwood Manor Apartments,2605 SE Division Street,PORTLAND,97202,,False,,,,,True,False,False,,False,False,False,False,False,"PBS Engineering and Environmental Inc.;  bret.waldron@pbsusa.com;  Visual and olfactory impacts to soil encountered below the USTs during decommissioning. Decommissioning was undertaken by Raimore Construction, who is contracted to TriMet. Work was completed in conjunction with transit stop improvements along SE Division Street. One tank was empty, and another contained approximately 300 gallons of water. The empty tank was treated as unregulated, and the one with water as regulated, and registered with DEQ. The tanks appear to be associated with a former service station decommissioned prior to the apartments on the NE side of SE 26th and Division by the early 1980s.",,,165709.0,31404.0,KDANA,2021-08-16 07:34:27.353
